{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy","id":158192,"title":"What's YOUR custom Legacy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T13:18:38-07:00","id":158192,"title":"What's YOUR custom Legacy?","content":"(I made one for Shifters, Bloodlines, now its time for Legacies!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Great Masters:</b> A legacy of Obrimos martial artists who despite their functionality, originated in the west. By combining magical properties with martial arts, they attempt to recreate legendary techniques only witnessed in myths, video games, and the movies. Sometimes called Fanboys, they strive to imitate Asian masters, whether they are real or fictional. In addition to the Arcana of Forces and Prime, they have also begun to study the power of Space as well. They are most commonly found as members of the Free Council, but have occasionally joined the Adamantine Arrow if they are eager to test out their training.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Skinless Hand:</b> A Left-Handed Moros legacy of militant necromancers. They refine their study of raising the dead in order to produce more effective soldiers for both offensive and defensive purposes. They operate like a mercenary company, hiring themselves out to other supernatural creatures (or those who are aware of the supernatural), commanding squads of heavily armed zombies to provide security detail or assault strikes. Their insignia is a blood dripping hand with clenched fingers and the skin hanging off it in tattered strips. Because dead bodies are prone to decomposition and rigid movements, The Skinless Hand has begun to study the Arcana of Matter in an effort to make them more flexible and attract less attention from onlookers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast Channelers:</b> A Right and Left-Handed legacy of Thyrsus who combine magic with barbaric hand to hand combat. They harness the powers of the animal kingdom to perform feats normally impossible for the human body. Such powers they have demonstrated includes inflicting lethal damage with one's bare hands (as if they were claws), overturning a car with a head on tackle (like a charging rhino), or crushing a man's bones with a vice-like squeeze (like a giant snake). They are typically found within the Adamantine Arrow, but due to the savage fighting styles they specialize in, they often instill distrust and unease in the other members.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't own the Mage Book, so I'm not sure if these would be acceptable or not. I scraped them together after reading about the game on the Wiki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-03-2014, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:47:33-07:00","id":158229,"title":"","content":"They are. There's already a zombie-making Legacy called the Bokor. I guess yours could be based on that one but with optional Attainments based on Matter to further weaponize the reanimated corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T19:52:11-07:00","id":158585,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. From what I read about them, they seem to create zombies based on their idea that a dead body is just a tool to be used. The idea I had for TSH is that they are hired to create zombies as part of some kind of supernatural defense contract, except they don't exactly work for the good guys. After all, what morally upstanding citizen is going to pay a bunch of death mages to fill their halls with gun toting corpses?<br /> <br /> In other words, The Skinless Hand are Necromancers who decided to become mercenary soldiers, instead of researching in a crypt all day. Kind of awesome when I think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:20:29-07:00","id":158614,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Supremely Focused:</b> A powerful (though foolish) legacy of the Obrimos who have chosen to specialize in an extremely narrow focus of magic. Students of Forces, they select one particular force in the universe (Electricity, Heat, Gravity, Kinetic, Light, Radiation, est) and devote ALL of their magical training exclusively towards that focus. In doing so, they become the undisputed masters of their particular specialization, but at the cost of being limited in what kind of spells they can do. A member of The Supremely Focused can in theory accomplish any feat that is within their specialization, however.<br /> <br /> The goal of The Supremely Focused is to become so in tuned with their chosen Force, that it becomes like an extension of their own body, and they can wield its power as naturally as breathing. Most outside this legacy consider them to be rather foolish, sacrificing flexibility in exchange for raw power.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-22-2014, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T04:22:40-07:00","id":158897,"title":"","content":"The Skinless Hand do nothing that the Bokor don't already do, have no incentive for material wealth, being Moros capable of transmuting their every wish, and would be better served bartering more benign services with other supernaturals than making enemies everywhere they go. They might be an interesting *cabal* of Bokor, but seem both too out in the open for a left-handed legacy to survive, and offering too little to the adherents for the risk to create an entire legacy. <br /> <br /> As for the CoHD... I think they would unequivocally damage any game they were a part of. In a PC, they reflect the very worst of Male Gamer stereotypes and I personally would leave any game with a player that seriously suggested the legacy. As an antagonist, they're just so... petty. Vile, disguisting, and petty. Either the themes are approached maturely, and they make me gag, or they are played off as a joke, which makes me want to gag equally and for different reasons. Might they exist in the WoD? Maybe, but if I were a mage I would immediately murder any that I came across... and I suspect most other mages would as well. Being a member of a legacy requires being at least Gnosis 3 and is irreversable, any mage of that power and in that legacy is either deranged or sociopathically evil, having made the concious decision to change their soul into such a disguisting, wretched thing. ...and the way you described them, I have a hard time seeing them as being wise and cautious enough to evade the Guardians *and* Seers that would hunt them long enough to acquire likeminded apprentices to induct into the legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T04:52:04-07:00","id":158913,"title":"","content":"Yep, they would never became an actual Legacy, the first one will be quickly dispossed of before he can pass it along. Its also quite juvenile and offensive because of that. Rape is a very, very serious matter, not something to happily joke about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T06:32:51-07:00","id":158974,"title":"","content":"I thought about a Legacy, that belevies that things are the most &quot;true&quot; and the most &quot;themselves&quot; the moment they break/die/are destroyed. They're theory is that sth ceases to exist it remains existing on the concept level via people's recognition, so the moment on &quot;death&quot; is the time when things are closest to their Supernal Ideal (the Supernal being the realm of concept). Moros legacy with main arcana being Death and Prime, but i don't quite have the attainments thought up. I thought about sth regarding pattern scouring but i dont know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T06:35:49-07:00","id":158976,"title":"","content":"I was about to delete them when I woke up this morning, thinking &quot;maybe this is a tad too extreme&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, the hatred that's targeted towards them is kind of the point. They're typically immature and disrespectful mages who most likely Awakened before they were old enough to truly comprehend what that entails. And no, it wasn't intended to be a joke, just like the Malkavian's weren't intended to be the jesters of Vampirism. This is a Gothic Horror game, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wasn't aware of the requirements needed to create / join a Legacy, but now that I do, I may be able to come up with better ones in the future. Though why do you say that The Supremely Focused wouldn't survive long enough to pass it on?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I apologize if the content I came up with was too extreme. I'm not sure the exact limits of what most player considers to be over the line when it comes to the mature themes of this game. I watched a gaming session for Werewolf, in which the PC's are attacked during a high-school shooting by spirit ridden assailants. I've also seen a Sabbat game session involving stuff that was straight up twisted, which I won't be repeating here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-04-2014, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T07:41:24-07:00","id":159036,"title":"","content":"Nah, the supremly focused are actually ok, I was refering to the CoHD. Thing is, it takes a member with at least the second Attainment (Gnosis 5 and Arcanum 3) to pass the Legacy along. I don't see those getting that far before being executed.<br /> <br /> Regarding the content, thing is, this is an open forum. There's people here that had suffered abuse (sexual or otherwise) that could do without the gratuitous use of such as a shock element. At the very least a warning would be nice. This stuff is triggery for a lot of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:21:33-07:00","id":159135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159036#post159036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, the supremly focused are actually ok, I was refering to the CoHD. Thing is, it takes a member with at least the second Attainment (Gnosis 5 and Arcanum 3) to pass the Legacy along. I don't see those getting that far before being executed.<br /> <br /> Regarding the content, thing is, this is an open forum. There's people here that had suffered abuse (sexual or otherwise) that could do without the gratuitous use of such as a shock element. At the very least a warning would be nice. This stuff is triggery for a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, there is a legacy that is dedicated essentially to BDSM... It is called the whipping boys (from the supernal tarot. Their whole thing is overcoming the barriers of society: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Whipping_Boys\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Whipping_Boys</a><br /> <br /> Code name is the Perverts. So it could be an example of how to do such a legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:52:17-07:00","id":159155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=158614#post158614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Cult of Hentai Demons</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I stopped reading RIGHT THERE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":1642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","user":"Paddon","date":". 06-04-2014, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:10:51-07:00","id":159175,"title":"","content":"I'm slowly trying to put together a Legacy based around forming the local spirits in the mage's area into a court through the imposition of laws and customs (with the mage having significant influence in the court, natch). The basic idea came from the Wu-Leng from oMage; the Legacy might be called the Mandarins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T11:00:47-07:00","id":159209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159175#post159175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm slowly trying to put together a Legacy based around forming the local spirits in the mage's area into a court through the imposition of laws and customs (with the mage having significant influence in the court, natch). The basic idea came from the Wu-Leng from oMage; the Legacy might be called the Mandarins.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would likely want to make it spirit and fate: Spirit naturally to elicit the ordering and interaction with spirits, and fate to simulate the feudal oaths and nature of the courts. The biggest question is how to avoid pissing off any courts who lay claim to the local spirits already... Maybe make part of the legacy receiving blessings from the regional spirit lords to receive a fiefdom over your local area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T14:41:38-07:00","id":159363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, there is a legacy that is dedicated essentially to BDSM...</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, the Whiping boys. Excellent Legacy by the way, pretty cool. That said, apples and oranges, rape and BDSM aren't the same thing in the least. The problem is not the sexual themes, sex is good after all, is the (non consensual) victimization and abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T15:30:56-07:00","id":159405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159363#post159363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I know, the Whiping boys. Excellent Legacy by the way, pretty cool. That said, apples and oranges, rape and BDSM aren't the same thing in the least. The problem is not the sexual themes, sex is good after all, is the (non consensual) victimization and abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div> I understand the difference quite clearly, having worked as a counselor for rape victims. My point was to highlight how you could do a legacy that worked outside of the norms of mainstream ideas of human sexuality, without going into the realms of abuse or rape. The only way I could see a rape based legacy ever possibly existing would be if it was a truly an abyssal creation, simply because such a concept is so destructive and dehumanizing to act as the basis of how you mold your soul.and I do not think I would use such a legacy in my game ever, especially since one of my players significant others was a victim of sexual abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T15:38:50-07:00","id":159412,"title":"","content":"that said, I understand that my original post did not convey that sentiment, &amp; I apologize that I wasn't that clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T15:39:14-07:00","id":159413,"title":"","content":"<b>Seekers of Perfection:</b> A legacy of Mastigos who believe that Lichdom is too extreme of a path towards immortality, and who's cost outweighs the benefits. Instead, they believe the limitations of the physical body can be overcome by transferring their minds into immortal constructs. By transcending their bodily functions, they can devote the rest of their time to honing their minds! In exchange for sacrificing their talent in Space, they have replaced it with Matter, the previous weakness of the Mastigos. By combining Mind and Matter, they strive to create the perfect Golem host for them to transfer into.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Spinners of Fate:</b> A Left-Handed (and exclusively female) legacy of Arcanthus who operate in teams consisting of no more or less than 3 members. They believe that their powers entitle them to play goddess with the lives of others (primarily Sleepers who can't fight back), and use their power over Fate to shape the events of those around them, severing their threads once their usefulness has run out. Their organization is modeled after the Sisters of Fate from Greek mythology. Their cabals have one member dedicated to controlling each period of the time line (past, present, and future).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Magical Restoration Agency:</b> A legacy of Thyrsus who dedicate their powers to helping the world heal from the destruction imposed on it by human society and supernatural disasters. They rejuvenate burned and rotting forests, cleanse polluted lakes, and basically seek to heal the world and its creatures from the various maladies that plague it. Sleepers take notice of a charred forest springing back to life overnight, however, so their magic is a slow process that will not draw too much attention. It may take longer than they wish it to, but their magic can bring hope back to what was previously a lost cause. In addition to the Arcana of Life and Spirit, they also study the Arcana of Matter, giving them the most effective means of healing magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-05-2014, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T16:10:38-07:00","id":159427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">that said, I understand that my original post did not convey that sentiment, &amp; I apologize that I wasn't that clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to. I'm glad that there are people like you helping people out. That rocks.<br /> <br /> <br /> So..., custom Legacies, I may have written a bunch of them over the years, in no particular order:<br /> <br /> <b>Exemplars</b>: Arcana specialists created by a very special type of Auctoritas Arcanum. They get better at one side of their Path by sacrifying their conection to the other.<br /> <br /> <b>Horizon Seekers</b>: a Legacy of travelers and explorers.<br /> <br /> <b>Tamers of Iron</b>: a Mastigos Legacy with a will as sharp as their blades.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnamed Astral Legacy</b>: summoners of platonic elementals from the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pack</b>: werewolf-like shapeshifter mages<br /> <br /> <b>Liches</b>: clasic &quot;hide my soul in a phylactery and reanimate my own corpse&quot; type of mage.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cult</b>: an infernalist Legacy that gets infernal powers (mimicking Castigation Endowments) but that show their corruption by hellish telltales.<br /> <br /> <b>Hematomancers</b>: mages that get power from the blood and tap into its sympathetic properties.<br /> <br /> <b>Verbena</b>: a variant of the Hematomancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T18:07:48-07:00","id":159575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159413#post159413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Seekers of Perfection:</b> A Left-Handed legacy of Mastigos who believe that Lichdom is too extreme of a path towards immortality, and who's cost outweighs the benefits. Instead, they believe the limitations of the physical body can be overcome by transferring their minds into immortal constructs. By transcending their bodily functions, they can devote the rest of their time to honing their minds! In exchange for sacrificing their talent in Space, they have replaced it with Matter, the previous weakness of the Mastigos. By combining Mind and Matter, they strive to create the perfect Golem host for them to transfer into.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure why these guys are Left-Handed as described. I mean, sure, they're probably not the Wisest on the whole, but unless they are harming those around them for their power they just seem a bit short-sighted. <br /> Unless this is one of those &quot;they didn't tell you everything about your legacy&quot; situations. Which could be really cool if explored more. Maybe the process inherently drives the mages towards a cruel and dispassionate mindset without the hormones of a physical body to encourage emotions, and as such they effectively turn themselves into irrevocable monsters? Perhaps they actually become linked into and subsumed by a hive-mind intelligence upon achieving their final attainment, and that intelligence has an ancient grudge against the Pentacle orders (Thanks to DaveB's excellent Actual Play, the Soul Cage for that idea)?<br /> <br /> All in all, I like the idea, but it needs a bit more articulation of why it's left-handed. Also perhaps it links into the tick-tock ghost known as the Schafer Movement from page 108 of Night Horrors: The unbidden. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159413#post159413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spinners of Fate:</b> A Left-Handed (and exclusively female) legacy of Arcanthus who operate in teams consisting of no more or less than 3 members. They believe that their powers entitle them to play goddess with the lives of others (primarily Sleepers who can't fight back), and use their power over Fate to shape the events of those around them, severing their threads once their usefulness has run out. Their organization is modeled after the Sisters of Fate from Greek mythology. Their cabals have one member dedicated to controlling each period of the time line (past, present, and future).</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, I'm not seeing why these gals would be necessarily left-handed. A fair number of Acanthus already do that sort of thing, it's sort of par-for-the-course for powerful characters with control over time and fate. Sure I can definitely see crazy cabals of this legacy causing problems, but it takes more than a few bad apples to get an entire legacy declared left-handed... typically it requires an element of the attainment itself to be damaging to the soul, morality, or sanity of the mages entering it.<br /> Though its certainly true that a legacy of entirely Evil-with-a-capital-E mages can be declared left-handed even if their legacy is all about ponies. Everyone will just go &quot;Erm, everyone who's ever been in that legacy killed toddlers for a hobby. And they're all in that legacy. Best not to take chances, maybe there's something sinister about the Supernal symbol for ponies that we haven't discovered yet.&quot; <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159413#post159413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Magical Restoration Agency:</b> A legacy of Thyrsus who dedicate their powers to helping the world heal from the destruction imposed on it by human society and supernatural disasters. They rejuvenate burned and rotting forests, cleanse polluted lakes, and basically seek to heal the world and its creatures from the various maladies that plague it. Sleepers take notice of a charred forest springing back to life overnight, however, so their magic is a slow process that will not draw too much attention. It may take longer than they wish it to, but their magic can bring hope back to what was previously a lost cause. In addition to the Arcana of Life and Spirit, they also study the Arcana of Matter, giving them the most effective means of healing magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> I hope it doesn't come across as if I have a vendetta against your ideas. I actually quite like this one... though what if it was actually a Moros legacy? Necromancers focused on fighting their reputation as death obsessed and exploring the intricate dance of life and decay through nature with Matter and Life as the Legacy's primary Arcana.<br /> I could even see a similar Acanthus legacy with Life and Time to rewind pieces of nature to an earlier time, or to undo the damages of man in a way that is perfectly in line with what once was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T18:20:02-07:00","id":159580,"title":"","content":"As for the original topic of the post, so as to actually contribute something other than analysis: <br /> <br /> <b>The Scavengers of the Farthest Shore:</b> A legacy of skilled Astral Travelers that is currently under scrutiny for left-handedness, the Scavengers of the Farthest Shore are fascinated by the various creatures and objects that wash up on the shores of the Ocean Oroboros. They believe that the twisted things that wash up on the shores are actually abyssal reflections or permutations of what has been lost within the Ocean's black depths over the ages - and that with proper study, fragments of the time before the abyss can be seen within their twisted forms.<br /> Obviously this legacy is prone to low-wisdom madmen who are easily tempted by the Abyss they study, but the legacy is difficult to detect... as part of their first Attainment is casting away the magical signs of their legacy into the Ocean Oroboros. Later attainments also involve casting parts of themselves into that same devouring ocean, but make them incredibly skilled Astral Travelers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:12:46-07:00","id":159604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159427#post159427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No need to. I'm glad that there are people like you helping people out. That rocks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Worked for a college health center for a bit, doing general counseling and specific to sexual abuse, assault and rape. Part of what pushed me further down the path of medicine, looking back at it. Hopefully I made some impact for the short time I worked in that role. <br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159575#post159575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I hope it doesn't come across as if I have a vendetta against your ideas. I actually quite like this one... though what if it was actually a Moros legacy? Necromancers focused on fighting their reputation as death obsessed and exploring the intricate dance of life and decay through nature with Matter and Life as the Legacy's primary Arcana.<br /> I could even see a similar Acanthus legacy with Life and Time to rewind pieces of nature to an earlier time, or to undo the damages of man in a way that is perfectly in line with what once was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about Moros for this, simply because one of the keys in the description of most Moros is that their awakening imparts on them the idea that everything is base and doomed to death and entropy except the human soul, and that even their own life is just a serious of processes meant to hold a human soul to this world... so the idea they would shift their world view to fighting such a thing is odd. I do like acanthus though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:25:26-07:00","id":159627,"title":"","content":"That's fair about the Moros... though I could see a Moros whose goal is to increase the life in the world and thereby also increase the number of things that do pass away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:33:50-07:00","id":159651,"title":"","content":"I am not going to list the full legacy idea unless people want, but just give the overview:<br /> <br /> <b>Legionem vigilent custodes (Legion of the Vigilant Watchmen): </b>An order of watchmen who are beholden only to the Supernal Truths of Law, Justice, and Mercy. They claim descent from the original police force of the Awakened City, and now are drawn only from Obrimos and Thyrsus mages who belong to the Adamantine Order. They are the equivalent of SWAT and a detectives, their purpose to track down those whose use of magic has endangered the safety of both reality and its denizens. They develop their soul to let them suppress the magic of others, while also fortifying their bodies to allow them to physically overcome and detain them. Those with sufficient skill can track their prey no matter where they flee.<br /> <br /> Only available to Obrimos and Thyrsus of the adamantine order.<br /> Requires Oath 2 (Adamantine Arrow only merit), with all 2 dots dedicated to the oath taken upon swearing into the order. The mage does not get any benefit beyond admission to the legacy, but still suffers all penalties for breaking the oath. Each additional attainment after the first requires an additional dot of the merit dedicated to it (i.e. two attainments rquires at least oath 3 with all dots dedicated to the legacy oath) with the negative penalty still intact.<br /> Nickname: Watchmen, Coppers<br /> <b>Prime Arcana:</b> Life and Prime (Obrimos get life, Thyrsus get Prime);<b>Optional Arcana: </b>Space <b>Conjunctional Arcana:</b> Mind<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> It is a powerful legacy in our game (not Celestial Masters bad, but definitely dangerous) but the Oath component acts as a way to balance it out. The reason we went AA vs GotV was because the player who suggested it wanted to base the personality of the legacy off of Sam Vimes from Discworld. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T21:05:13-07:00","id":159709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159575#post159575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure why these guys are Left-Handed as described. I mean, sure, they're probably not the Wisest on the whole, but unless they are harming those around them for their power they just seem a bit short-sighted.<br /> Unless this is one of those &quot;they didn't tell you everything about your legacy&quot; situations. Which could be really cool if explored more. Maybe the process inherently drives the mages towards a cruel and dispassionate mindset without the hormones of a physical body to encourage emotions, and as such they effectively turn themselves into irrevocable monsters? Perhaps they actually become linked into and subsumed by a hive-mind intelligence upon achieving their final attainment, and that intelligence has an ancient grudge against the Pentacle orders (Thanks to DaveB's excellent Actual Play, the Soul Cage for that idea)?<br /> <br /> All in all, I like the idea, but it needs a bit more articulation of why it's left-handed. Also perhaps it links into the tick-tock ghost known as the Schafer Movement from page 108 of Night Horrors: The unbidden. Again, I'm not seeing why these gals would be necessarily left-handed. A fair number of Acanthus already do that sort of thing, it's sort of par-for-the-course for powerful characters with control over time and fate. Sure I can definitely see crazy cabals of this legacy causing problems, but it takes more than a few bad apples to get an entire legacy declared left-handed... typically it requires an element of the attainment itself to be damaging to the soul, morality, or sanity of the mages entering it.<br /> Though its certainly true that a legacy of entirely Evil-with-a-capital-E mages can be declared left-handed even if their legacy is all about ponies. Everyone will just go &quot;Erm, everyone who's ever been in that legacy killed toddlers for a hobby. And they're all in that legacy. Best not to take chances, maybe there's something sinister about the Supernal symbol for ponies that we haven't discovered yet.&quot; I hope it doesn't come across as if I have a vendetta against your ideas. I actually quite like this one... though what if it was actually a Moros legacy? Necromancers focused on fighting their reputation as death obsessed and exploring the intricate dance of life and decay through nature with Matter and Life as the Legacy's primary Arcana.<br /> I could even see a similar Acanthus legacy with Life and Time to rewind pieces of nature to an earlier time, or to undo the damages of man in a way that is perfectly in line with what once was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Spinners of Fate were considered to me to be a Left-Hand, because they feel their powers give them a right to mess with people's lives and sculpt them however they desire. Sure, there are plenty of Arcanthus who manipulate fate, but how often do they do it simply because they can, and not because they should? The Spinners twist the lives of others for entertainment or for personal gain, and they believe they are above reproach for doing so. Somebody criticizes their work? Make them go bankrupt when they forget to file their taxes this year. Somebody attempts to stop them, make their family contract a tropical disease while they're on vacation overseas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Seekers of Perfection are considered Left-Handed, because I think that a group of mages looking to achieve immortality by transferring into soulless bodies would probably raise a few red flags. After all, the Tremere sought to become immortal and look how they turned out; now we've got a legacy of undead mages devouring the souls of everyone they meet! I do like your ideas to the Legacy, however. Maybe I could inflict them with a powerful, gripping fear of death that drives them to sacrifice just about anything (including their own bodies) to escape it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I thought Thyrsus was the most fitting for The Magical Restoration Agency. Their name was intended to be a joke on various environmental protection agencies in the real world. They're sort of like magic wielding hippies (hey, they use crystals, it's a possibility!) who are trying to save the planet. When Sleepers are watching them, they focus on natural damages such as pollution and fires, but when they're in private, they turn their attention to fixing supernatural disasters. Think Ferngully (if you've ever seen that movie). They take a seed, plant it, and use their magic to care for its growth to the point where it can survive where otherwise it could not. Give it a few years and soon that decimated forest will be lush once more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-05-2014, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T21:25:14-07:00","id":159721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159709#post159709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seekers of Perfection are considered Left-Handed, because I think that a group of mages looking to achieve immortality by transferring into soulless bodies would probably raise a few red flags. After all, the Tremere sought to become immortal and look how they turned out; now we've got a legacy of undead mages devouring the souls of everyone they meet! I do like your ideas to the Legacy, however. Maybe I could inflict them with a powerful, gripping fear of death that drives them to sacrifice just about anything (including their own bodies) to escape it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere aren't Left-Handed because they seek immortality; they're Left-Handed because they consume souls! Any Legacy that requires a Wisdom 1 sin every few months/weeks is going to be branded as Left-Handed, because the councilii don't want a bunch of Wisdom 0 mages running around!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159709#post159709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Thyrsus was the most fitting for The Magical Restoration Agency. Their name was intended to be a joke on various environmental protection agencies in the real world. They're sort of like magic wielding hippies (hey, they use crystals, it's a possibility!) who are trying to save the planet. When Sleepers are watching them, they focus on natural damages such as pollution and fires, but when they're in private, they turn their attention to fixing supernatural disasters. Think Ferngully (if you've ever seen that movie). They take a seed, plant it, and use their magic to care for its growth to the point where it can survive where otherwise it could not. Give it a few years and soon that decimated forest will be lush once more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also see the newest Maleficent movie for why not to dismiss these people as &quot;magic wielding hippies&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T21:37:29-07:00","id":159729,"title":"","content":"The thing is though that it normally takes more than just a mindset to make a Legacy Left-Handed. It *can* happen in the case of particularly monstrous individuals and the legacies they create, but in most circumstances Left-Handedness requires the Legacy itself, not merely the philosophy of its constituent members, to be significantly damaging to the Wisdom of its members. It takes a fairly strong consensus among Mages of many Conciliums for a group to be declared Left-Handed on a large scale, and the burden of proof has to be more than just anecdotal. &quot;The Tremere EAT SOULS&quot; is pretty easy, but &quot;Those Acanthus are slightly more prone to being dicks than other Acanthus&quot; is much harder and would take blatant and public disregard for the Lex Megica for Mages as a whole to shun the entire Legacy as inherently evil.<br /> <br /> TLDR - If the Legacy Attainments themselves encourage or require morality checks, it's likely Left-Handed. Otherwise, it's likely not.<br /> <br /> On the topic of the Seekers of Perfection, I like the idea, I just think they also need something more clear cut for them to be considered necessarily Left-Handed. Seeking immortality alone is not a Mage taboo, there are more than a few well-respected Legacies within mage society that already grant eternal life... and any mage with an advanced grasp of the Life Arcana can maintain eternal youth with ease.<br /> I especially have a hard time seeing that inclination alone as being a problem for mages because unless there's something else about the Legacy other than written, they aren't even risking harm to others around them. It's a common and understandable thing to want to live forever, the fact that they are choosing not to eat souls to achieve endless life would be a check in their favor if anything.<br /> <br /> As for the Thyrsus... which abbreviates comically down to the MRA, I just like subversions of expectations more than fulfillment of stereotypes; that's just personal preference though. It's easy to envision a Thyrsus as a hippie environmentalist, but harder and more compelling to explain how another Path might use their abilities and shape a Legacy for those same goals.<br /> If I were going to have a game with that Legacy in a prominent place (whether they are Thyrsus or otherwise), I'd almost certainly have an antagonistic legacy that opposes the Restoration Agency. Their stance would be that by undoing humanity's damage to the environment, the Agency is protecting humans from ever facing the consequences of their own actions, and therefor encouraging the very behavior that caused the damage in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:08:17-07:00","id":159745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159721#post159721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tremere aren't Left-Handed because they seek immortality; they're Left-Handed because they consume souls! Any Legacy that requires a Wisdom 1 sin every few months/weeks is going to be branded as Left-Handed, because the councilii don't want a bunch of Wisdom 0 mages running around!.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant there is the potential for their immortality to go horribly, horribly wrong once they achieve it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The point I'm trying to make is that they are, essentially, trying to follow in the footsteps of one Legacy that already fucked up horribly. Sure, they may be trying a new approach to fulfilling that goal, but people have been trying for thousands of years to cheat death. Usually there's a good reason why only a handful of people have succeeded (in game terms, not RL).<br /> <br /> <br /> But it seems being risky isn't enough to actually warrant being evil, as Jam pointed out. If we didn't have the Immortals book describing the function of Body Snatchers, I could have made them cheat death by jumping to a new host. I imagine that would qualify as Left-Handed, but sadly it's already taken. D:<br /> <br /> <br /> Seems they don't fit the bill, so I'll edit them no longer be Left-Handed. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:21:47-07:00","id":159761,"title":"","content":"Pointed reminder to all that Left-Handedness is a political category, not a metaphysical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T23:30:57-07:00","id":159781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159761#post159761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pointed reminder to all that Left-Handedness is a political category, not a metaphysical one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Right. Which is exactly why a legacy has to be pretty much unquestionably dangerous to the Mages in question or those around them for entire groups of often conflicting Mages to come together in a political movement to decry a Legacy as a whole.<br /> It's not one Council that is responsible for declaring a Legacy Left-Handed. It's entire groups of mages. How hard is it to get any group of people to all come together and agree that one specific mentality is not only bad, but punishable by death on sight? Right. It's almost impossible. Now get a majority vote from disparate super-humans that have almost all likely tampered with Things Man Should Not Know that any specific legacy is Evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T06:48:34-07:00","id":159960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159135#post159135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>That said, there is a legacy that is dedicated essentially to BDSM...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. There's a ton of precedent for self-harm as a spiritual practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortification_of_the_flesh\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Thwack.jpg/1280px-Thwack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortification_of_the_flesh\" target=\"_blank\"> Mortification of the flesh - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortification_of_the_flesh\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortification_of_the_flesh </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T07:15:12-07:00","id":159969,"title":"","content":"If the Daione aren't left-handed, I don't see why your spinners of fate would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T07:48:09-07:00","id":159982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159960#post159960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda. There's a ton of precedent for self-harm as a spiritual practice.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortification_of_the_flesh\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortif...n_of_the_flesh</a></div> </div> </div> </div>See my follow up post. There is a huge history, as you pointed out, of pain being a path to spiritual purity (Flagellants in Christianity, fasting in most, etc). The comment was more about how you can base a legacy outside of mainstream human sexuality, involving physical harm, without resorting to rape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T11:44:18-07:00","id":160116,"title":"","content":"<b>The Tamers of Radio</b> - a Free Council legacy that took the concept of the Elemental Tamers and gave it a modern spin. They are Obrimos who develop ways of manipulating both broadcast frequencies (actually going beyond radio) and the 'wavelengths' of the human mind.<br /> <br /> <b>The Gloaming -</b> a mysterious cult of Acanthus who manipulate shadows and time in an attempt to defeat a bizarre apocalypse (the 'True Night'). They are dark prophets who can see the future by cutting off their senses, but their predictions are always about upcoming disaster.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ancient and Puissant First Chapter of Spellmasons </b>- an odd bunch of sacred architects and monolith-builders, who are masters of weaving magic into structures they build or manipulate and channelling leylines for useful effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T12:36:00-07:00","id":160146,"title":"","content":"Hey, I like the Tamers of Radio, very original!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T00:57:08-07:00","id":160641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159580#post159580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Scavengers of the Farthest Shore</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Really like these guys. Very original and interesting idea. Would love to see the full writeup with attainments if you could submit it.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160116#post160116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Tamers of Radio</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I concurr with Thorbes on this one. Another very original idea.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160116#post160116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Gloaming</b></div> </div> </div> </div>There really should be more apocalyptic Acanthus groups. I would definitely love to see the full writeup of this one too.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160116#post160116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Ancient and Puissant First Chapter of Spellmasons</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that these are too much like the Tamers of Stone and the Tellurians to warrant a separate existence, but I'm always for sacred architect mages either way.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for my own contributions:<br /> <br /> <b>Wenen-Nefru-Kau</b>: Moros and th\u00e9arch Ascension seekers with roots in ancient Egypt and its mysticism of the soul. They believe that the true road to the Supernal is by exaltation of the soul through magical alchemy. Their attainments guard their souls against outside tampering and grant them greater puissance in using magic related to soul manipulation. They are protected from Reaper status by the simple fact that their attainments are suppressed while their souls are too wounded (i.e. their Wisdom is low).<br /> <br /> <b>Eaters of the Void</b>: Mastigos and Guardian mages who uphold the traditionally Guardian creed of sullying one's soul for the good of other mages. Their attainments allow them to purge other mages of magical impurities by taking them unto themselves, and at higher levels can even &quot;eat&quot; the Paradoxes and Wisdom sins of others. Their gifts are not freely given, however, and their charges are subjected to harrowing mental and physical trials before they are cleansed of their sins.<br /> <br /> <b>Circle of the Outer Light</b>: Seer of the Throne priests who belong to the Obrimos Path and the Paternoster Ministry. They use their abilities with the Mind Arcanum to sway or break others to worshiping the Exarchs, and can even grant their &quot;congregants&quot; prophetic, though maddening, dreams of the Exarchs' commands.<br /> <br /> <b>Court of Discord</b>: Left-handed Acanthus saboteurs shamefully associated with the Free Council. They believe that true enlightenment only exists when all rules are broken and utter chaos descends upon everything. To this end, they spread strife among people and topple organisations using their causality-breaking attainments, all to bring about their mad vision of absolute freedom from any supposed restraints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T01:17:33-07:00","id":160644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wenen-Nefru-Kau</b>: Moros and th\u00e9arch Ascension seekers with roots in ancient Egypt and its mysticism of the soul. They believe that the true road to the Supernal is by exaltation of the soul through magical alchemy. Their attainments guard their souls against outside tampering and grant them greater puissance in using magic related to soul manipulation. They are protected from Reaper status by the simple fact that their attainments are suppressed while their souls are too wounded (i.e. their Wisdom is low).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I remember these guys from the old forum, I had them saved in my laptop. I loved them. Can't remeber the part about the Attainments being supressed on low Wisdom, did you update them?<br /> <br /> I'd remember a couple more:<br /> <br /> <b>Body Thiefs:</b> Seer Legacy asociated with the Prelates of the Unity that achieve a sort of inmortality by living inside the bodies of slepers.<br /> <br /> <b>The Most Sacred and Exalted Lodge of the Midnight Sun:</b> both parts Legacy, Mystery Cult and proto-Order, these Obrimoi study and conduct ritual death to help the souls along in its cycle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":"right the first time around 06-06-2014, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T01:20:57-07:00","id":160645,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, are some of them fully stated or are only some cool ideas? Because we should totally resurect the old Legacy Thread as it was in the old forum and post them. I at least want to see a lot of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T01:50:40-07:00","id":160658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160644#post160644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I remember these guys from the old forum, I had them saved in my laptop. I loved them. Can't remeber the part about the Attainments being supressed on low Wisdom, did you update them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep: <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default5783-2.html?g=posts&amp;m=1173580#post1173580\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160644#post160644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, are some of them fully stated or are only some cool ideas? Because we should totally resurect the old Legacy Thread as it was in the old forum and post them. I at least want to see a lot of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES TO ALL OF THIS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T02:28:55-07:00","id":160670,"title":"","content":"<b>Supernal Technologist</b>: Supernal Technologists take the typical Libertine view of technology approaching magic and run with it; where a normal Libertine will encourage sleeper technological advances a Supernal Technologist will be developing new technologies from Supernally inspired designs and using magic to &quot;bridge the gap&quot; on developing or futuristic technologies, often then attempting to reverse engineer the devices to discover &quot;mundane&quot; ways of building them. See my sig for more details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T03:42:11-07:00","id":160706,"title":"","content":"<b>Disciples of Rathma</b>: Free Council Legacy based around the wheel of life and death and Darwin's theory of evolution. Members of the Legacy are Moros and Thyrsus, who believe evolution is driven by the cycle of life and death and try to apply those principles to their own bodies. Basically becoming able to evolve themselves. They came around the same time as the Free Council and are a bit more hidebound than the average. They take often appearance and rituals from sleeper religions that look at this cyclical relationship between life and death.<br /> <br /> <br /> After I made the first drafts of the legacy my ST pointed out that they are basically trying to transform themselves into biological Seed AIs. Which I realized is actually a pretty good description. Now I have fun imagining how the legacy is slowly getting traction among thechnologically minded, tranhumanism affine libertines. to the great consternation and disgust of some of the old guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-06-2014, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:08:44-07:00","id":161335,"title":"","content":"<b>The Secluded Mystics:</b> An Obrimos + Arcanthus legacy comprised of isolationists who live in temples high atop the peaks of snow covered mountains. Disconnected from the troubles of the world, they refine their magic and contemplate the mysteries of the universe. They accept new members from the Awakened, but only if they can pass their test, they must be able to scale their mountain without the use magic. Unfortunately most end up freezing to death in a blizzard or being crushed by an avalanche before they even see the temple. Sleepers who accomplish this feat are permitted to ask one question of the temple's leader, which he or she will answer truthfully to the best of their ability.<br /> <br /> (Premise for this Legacy is based on Tibetan Monks, as well as the Doctor Strange movie.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T22:06:42-07:00","id":161412,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Pattern scouring is base-book stuff for a reason, Strill; it could stand some further elaboration, in fact, given the Thyrsus and Mastigos emphasis on the topic of extreme experiential enlightenment. There are also multiple Ecstatic legacies, like the (mediocre) example from <i>Legacies the Sublime</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've had plenty of legacy ideas over the years, only a few of which I posted. I'll list some that I've not mentioned before:<br /> <br /> <b>Fire Tenders</b>: These are keepers of the Eternal Flame. They make pilgrimage to the Well of Knowledge, and strive to keep the supernal light alive in the Fallen World. They have attainments to use literal fire (and possibly sunlight) as metaphorical enlightenment. A sacred fire can be used to reveal secrets or destroy things. Prime primary, Forces secondary. Spirit optional.<br /> <br /> <b>Shinobi</b>: A warrior legacy that focuses on fighting from the shadows. They manipulate shadows and ultimately become one with it. Death primary, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Digitus Medius</b>: They claim to be the &quot;Finger of the Oracles&quot; and that they are each specifically selected by them, but essentially no one believes them. They consider themselves the harriers in the Ascension War. They know their place. This is a Free Council legacy (in fact, more specifically, Freedom Fighter) open to anyone who is willing to pass their tests. Willingness to fight the Lie is the most critical. Their attainments are Fate (primary) and Mind based and represent an awareness of the Lie and how it affects perceptions. They study a phenomenon or system and then use their supernally-granted knowledge to break it or subvert it.&quot;Cosmic Judo&quot; is a fun description they sometimes use to describe it.<br /> Rumor holds that their Grand Master is actually a Guardian plant and they know it... he's effective, so why should they care? True or not, that describes their attitude quite well.<br /> <br /> <b>Pearl Sages</b>: They fashion, wear, and eventually integrate as a third eye a large pearl filled with the wisdom of the lunar dragon. The Dragon's Eye provides great perception and even understanding. Ultimately, even authority over spells is granted the sage. Prime primary, Mind conjunctional, and Spirit optional.<br /> (Dark sages could use a Death/Mind variation and be able to capture souls in their eyes)<br /> <br /> <b>Pit Baiters</b>: These are Fate workers who attempt to curse the Abyss, tying it up in Supernal Mandates and driving it back. If the Supernal defines 'What Is' then the Loom of Fate defines the patterns of everything. Paradox is where 'What Cannot Be' is getting tangled up in the Loom. Baiter attempt to fix that by cursing the darkness--thus binding it. Paradox rolls are manipulated as these magi try to weave them out of the world. Fate primary. Considered reckless, at best, but they do have their successes. For now, they are not deemed Left Handed.<br /> <br /> <b>Living Spectre</b>: Learning the Atlantean model of ghosts is one thing, but these fellows apply it to their own minds while living. At first, they have to &quot;die&quot; to call up their Shade, but eventually, they can send it to act out their will without them. Death primary, Mind conjunctional<br /> <br /> <b>Barren Souls</b>: Members find their feelings of loss and isolation from what <i>should </i>be so great that they begin to hunger for anything real. Having tasted the sky, the earth is a truly dank prison. As they progress, their requirements deepen: The strongest ties to supernal concepts like love are unaffected, but the weakest become meaningless, and that cut-off grows as they do. They cling to anything that remains with desperation. They need mana and magic to feel like a normal human being any more. They consume mana and, eventually, spells. Like calls to like, and they are also adept at locating others who feel isolated or desperate. Declared Left-Handed, but the ruling is in appeal. Their powers work exceedingly well against mage threats; rumors hold that Seers are destroyed by taking the legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Dolor</b>: (Edit: Ah, yes, <b>The Daimonic Lance</b>) They are a damaged legacy who cannot escape pain unless they share it with others. Their curse is the pain that will not quit, but they can share more pain than just that, making them dangerous to attack. Eventually they learn to cope by walling their pain off from their consciousness and eventually gain the ability to precisely target the release, rather than generally sweep up all around them in diffused pain. Mind.<br /> <br /> (Wrote the last one up during a migraine, if you couldn't guess.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 08-29-2015, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T22:21:35-07:00","id":161419,"title":"","content":"<b>The Tenants of Gaia:</b> A Thyrsus Legacy who have formed an alliance with the Werewolves and dedicate their magic to assisting them in their duty to safeguard the physical and spiritual realms. Often referred to as Druids by those outside this Legacy, the Tenants of Gaia have grown quite fond of shapeshifting into various animal forms both in and out of battle (though almost never as powerful as a true Lupine). In addition to their specializations in Life and Spirit, they have also taken up training in the Arcana of Matter, granting them nearly total control over the environment and its inhabitants both physical and spiritual. The Tenants of Gaia prefer to live in the wilderness and rarely interact with major human civilizations unless there is a serious threat to the environment that must be addressed. Occasionally they have also been known to sent a &quot;recruiter&quot; into town, looking for worthy Thyrsus who might be willing to join their Legacy and ensure the world continues to be preserved from those who would see it destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-07-2014, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T19:58:22-07:00","id":177577,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see some of these Legacies fleshed out. Not sure if I should resurrect the old Legacy thread on the previous forum given that I haven't come up with any Legacies myself but I'd be ecstatic if one of you folks did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160706#post160706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Disciples of Rathma</b>: Free Council Legacy based around the wheel of life and death and Darwin's theory of evolution. Members of the Legacy are Moros and Thyrsus, who believe evolution is driven by the cycle of life and death and try to apply those principles to their own bodies. Basically becoming able to evolve themselves. They came around the same time as the Free Council and are a bit more hidebound than the average. They take often appearance and rituals from sleeper religions that look at this cyclical relationship between life and death.<br /> <br /> <br /> After I made the first drafts of the legacy my ST pointed out that they are basically trying to transform themselves into biological Seed AIs. Which I realized is actually a pretty good description. Now I have fun imagining how the legacy is slowly getting traction among thechnologically minded, tranhumanism affine libertines. to the great consternation and disgust of some of the old guard.</div> </div> </div> </div>These seem like a perfect fit for Dataweavers Palinoros, an alternate Watchtower with Life and Death as it's Ruling Arcanum. He's actually looking for appropriate Legacies so here's the relevant thread if you're interested: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/142305-the-other-five-paths\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...her-five-paths</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T21:23:25-07:00","id":177654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159745#post159745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> But it seems being risky isn't enough to actually warrant being evil, as Jam pointed out. If we didn't have the Immortals book describing the function of Body Snatchers, I could have made them cheat death by jumping to a new host. I imagine that would qualify as Left-Handed, but sadly it's already taken. D:...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd point out that this is actually not a problem at all. You can either make this a legacy that was created by such a figure Awakening, a mage who researched them enough to discover a way to tap the same mystical properties, or could simply be an unrelated way of doing something similar. <i>Any</i> of those takes on the subject could make for an interesting Legacy.Oh, and these <i>would</i> be left-handed if they were known about...<br /> <br /> Actually, imagine a legacy who can (in effect) meditate to his Oneiros, activate an attainment to up stakes, and astrally travel via the Temenos to another Oneiros to make camp. Death of the current host kills the mage, but this would make a really slippery devil. The former mind could remain intact and uninjured in this process, rendering the mage a passenger. This could be developed into something interesting and not necessarily left-handed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:10:42-07:00","id":183092,"title":"","content":"<b>Bardic Circle</b> Bard's are social and political creatures. they usually play a heraldic role in the cities Consilium and tend to be behind the scenes manipulators of awakend politics. As such, the legacy responds most strongly with members of the Silver Ladder and Mastigos mages. The Attainmemts of this legacy all involve enhancing the characters social abilities. As bards are famed for their prowess at singing and oratory, thier attainments are always directly linked to their voices and require that at Target hear them speak or sing before taking effect. the primary Arcanum is Mind. <b>1: How Do You Do? </b> this attainment basically replicates the effects of the spell first impression which is always active. <b> 2. Voice of an Angel </b> the second attainment allows the mage to add his dots in Mind to either his presence or manipulation stat for up to one hour. with optional life, the mage can also simulate the spell Image of Striking Beauty with successes equal to dots in LIFE but the beauty it creates applies to the mages voice rather than physical appearance adding a bonus equal to life to any Expression, Persuasion, or Socialize rolls where he uses his voice to influence someone. <b> 3. Pied Piper </b> this a attainment allows the mage to raise the other of Presence or Manipulation by his mind dots when using his voice in some way to influence others. With optional Life, the name age can also create an effect similar to this spell Trigger the Lizard Brain with a prolonged duration and an area of effect equal to those who can hear the mages on unaugmented and unamplified voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3389-druid","name":"Druid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3389_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T12:13:39-07:00","id":183142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Druid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=183092#post183092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bardic Circle</b> Bard's are social and political creatures. they usually play a heraldic role in the cities Consilium and tend to be behind the scenes manipulators of awakend politics. As such, the legacy responds most strongly with members of the Silver Ladder and Mastigos mages. The Attainmemts of this legacy all involve enhancing the characters social abilities. As bards are famed for their prowess at singing and oratory, thier attainments are always directly linked to their voices and require that at Target hear them speak or sing before taking effect. the primary Arcanum is Mind. <b>1: How Do You Do? </b> this attainment basically replicates the effects of the spell first impression which is always active. <b> 2. Voice of an Angel </b> the second attainment allows the mage to add his dots in Mind to either his presence or manipulation stat for up to one hour. with optional life, the mage can also simulate the spell Image of Striking Beauty with successes equal to dots in LIFE but the beauty it creates applies to the mages voice rather than physical appearance adding a bonus equal to life to any Expression, Persuasion, or Socialize rolls where he uses his voice to influence someone. <b> 3. Pied Piper </b> this a attainment allows the mage to raise the other of Presence or Manipulation by his mind dots when using his voice in some way to influence others. With optional Life, the name age can also create an effect similar to this spell Trigger the Lizard Brain with a prolonged duration and an area of effect equal to those who can hear the mages on unaugmented and unamplified voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea, but think it'd actually fit Acanthus better than Mastigos, at least as described (the Acanthus fit the gregarious nature of bards better, imo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T12:31:27-07:00","id":183147,"title":"","content":"that's a very good point and something to consider as I fully flesh out this legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3389-druid","name":"Druid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3389_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T02:15:30-07:00","id":183665,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Mastigos themes are usually all about pushing through limits, purging weakness, mastering one's self, and suchlike. Mind makes perfect sense for these guys as a primary arcana, but not so much the Path of Scourging. You <i>could</i> work up a bardic legacy that pushes the limits of what the voice can do, perfecting the art and the attainments would follow that. You certainly don't need to, but if you wanted to shift the theme over, I'd go something along the lines of the following,<br /> <br /> <b>1st: Support of Breath - reqs. Perform 3, Specialty in some vocal art, Life 2, Mind 1</b><br /> Character adds Life to Stamina for purposes of breath and voice. This helps with endurance and holding one's breath, but it's a result of refined breath support. This also grants 9-again to performances in a vocal specialty. (All Bards develop at least one specialty, but most develop all facets of their voice.)<br /> The character gains the ability to read an individual or a crowd's moods as a reflexive mental action once a round. (The information is per Aura Perception, but is often received through smell or hearing)<br /> Finally, the character gains the ability to purchase Eidetic Memory with experience points.<br /> <b>2nd: reqs. Perform 4, Life 3, Eidetic Memory</b><br /> The character can perfectly pronounce anything they hear within the realm of natural capacity. (That is, they must obey the physical limits of their natural voice.) All words and notes in anything heard are perfectly stored, and retrieval takes a reflexive thought. If something is difficult to remember, the number of mental actions to retrieve it are equal to the normal level of penalty assessed, reduced by one per level of Mind. (If the mage has Mind 2 and the thing recalled is so complex it would have a penalty of -4, it would take 4-2=2 actions to grab. Taking the reflexive action and the characters instant action for the round suffices.) These rules only apply when they improve Eidetic Memory.<br /> This grants their voice a magical quality, which grants 8- and 9-again to any vocal efforts that apply to a vocal specialty or would be aided by Striking Looks.<br /> <b>Optional Mind 3:</b><br /> The character may speak and understand any language. This includes flawless idomatic understanding and usage, as well as perfect tone and voice.<br /> <b>3rd: Silvered Tongue reqs. Perform 5, Life 4, Mind 2</b><br /> The character can make any noise that a human can hear, using just their voice. For a willpower, the bard may add Life to any vocal rolls.<br /> Further, the character may use his superlative voice to manipulate a crowd. The effects are essentially the same as Emotional Urging.except the activation roll is Presence + Performance or Persuasion (As most appropriate) and the Potence is equal to successes. Ranks in Mind set the levels of Area on the Advanced Area of Effect chart for a ritual casting. Anyone within this area is affected by the spell. Target factors can be added to include anyone within earshot or exclude anyone in the area, but the bard must specifically interact with any of these. This means the target factors come out of the mundane roll. Attempts to conceal this apply further penalties.<br /> <b>Optional Mind 4</b><br /> The character can <i>force</i> an audience to see the images conveyed. When using their superlative vocal specialty, a bard can impress information into the minds of the audience. The effects end up as per the spell Hallucination (Duration and Potency are set by the character's Mind, but detail and quality are defined by the mundane roll) or a perfect mnemonic can be implanted. (This is almost like Psychic Reprogramming, except it can only set a piece of the performance to be unforgettable.) The performance puts the image in the mind, while the attainment locks in the pieces desired. Only one mental scene or concept can be placed in the mind per performance, but this can draw on any or all of the performance to create the image. This is simply an image or idea that keeps popping up. A song becomes an ear-worm, or the phrase echos in their mind. It doesn't force them to accept the idea or like the image.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the version you got there, some thoughts:<br /> First Impressions is actually a really nice fit. Might toss in something further about his natural blessed charm and apply a shielding effect or even a fate sight like Sybill's or Interconnections which allows a bard to find the things he needs to witness and record.<br /> Voice of an Angel --Want a mystical voice, here? How about just adding Mind to all vocal rolls or something. A willpower to gain rote quality on any vocal action. something like that, perhaps? Works especially well with a Mind/Fate combo.<br /> Pied Piper--Don't get me wrong, stat boosts can be sweet, but I just think that this should get something more specifically bardic... I like the optional Life side more than the main part, here, accordingly. I point out that Mind can certainly do that same effect.<br /> An Optional Fate component could allow for a Gaes/prophecy/oath, by the by. (The ability to fling out a curse in death would seem appropriate, potentially.)<br /> Curses entirely devoted to a person's story would be especially fitting. &quot;You will be forgotten by any who would revere you. Your name will become a joke.&quot; or &quot;No one will ever forget your sacrifice. Your story will become common in lorehouses the world over.&quot; would be the sorts of blessings or curses I'd allow here, with a requirement to craft an appropriate story or something to charm the Fates with and seal the deal.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, some thoughts to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:22:35-07:00","id":184989,"title":"","content":"I really like your alternate idea for attainments but for another legacy not for mine. I do see your point with regards 2 the attribute boost however I feel that increasing your presence and manipulation by your dots in mind based on vocal quality is only is exactly the feel I was looking for. I do see the point that you both made about Mastigos possibly not being the best fit. Acanthus is much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3389-druid","name":"Druid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3389_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T12:41:06-07:00","id":185729,"title":"","content":"There also happens to be a bardic Legacy already, the Skalds from one of the two legacy books. You probably already considered it, but if not it might be worth mentioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T13:15:09-07:00","id":185748,"title":"","content":"One idea I'm fiddling about with is based on the idea of a karmic debt turning someone into a dark immortal. In particular, I figure the character should be, in essence, hosting the formation of a really destructive spirit, but one that emerges from the character's soul. In other words, metaphysically, this is a specific form of Spirit Claiming. Mechanically, it's a legacy.<br /> The three levels currently kinda look like:<br /> <br /> Akuma<br /> 1st: Dark Aura - The aura of death makes the Akuma fearsome and frightening. Social penalties and so forth are offset by huge benefits to intimidation and combat.<br /> 2nd: Shadow Self - The Demon Self grows enough to take over and enhance the Akuma's combat abilities. Downside is that they become dangerously volatile. (Maybe move this up to the third) This isn't a stupid and beast-like rage, though. The demon doesn't lag the normal mind as clever. In fact, it enhances that. It just removes the safeties and uses whatever martial and magical skills are most effective. Not sure how this ought to interact with Wisdom.<br /> 3rd: Dark Awakening - The Akuma has merged with their Demon Soul, to become something more dangerous. May allow access to Harrowing or Blast numina and an Essence pool.<br /> <br /> Mechanics are the hard part, since I want the progression to be balanced and reasonable throughout.<br /> I'm thinking that, given the death and human suffering essence that causes this condition, this should be a dangerous form of geist that forms. That geist could be treated as an immaterial familiar in most ways, and the attainments simply grant it further powers, perhaps. I dunno. Once the third attainment is known, the mage isn't immortal, but they will merge further with their Demon Self. <b>That</b> could be what converts the spirit into a geist... and also explain the whole &quot;becoming immortal&quot; idea. (Especially if this thing can restore the body in some way.)<br /> Thoughts are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T13:56:01-07:00","id":185778,"title":"","content":"Will this artificial self-Claimed still had access to Arcana? I ask because the rule about not stacking Templates is there for a reason (plus, on top of that general rule, there is the specific one about supernaturals being incapable of being claimed). So, is this a &quot;I stop being a mage and become an inmortal Claimed&quot; (or claimed-like) thing, or is I am an inmortal Claimed and a mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T15:46:11-07:00","id":185822,"title":"","content":"Living mage with a legacy (claimed-like-thing) until death.<br /> Then they become some unholy ghost mage/spirit hybrid. (Kinda like a nasty variation on the Bene whatsit)<br /> <br /> That rule against template-stacking was <i>specifically stated</i> to be a rule of the game and not the world the game is set in, so fluff is fair game. That said, this is not a rule I consider well-planned or stated, so I've never considered it particularly binding. Expect me to heed it only so far as to avoid major arguments on the point. (Best advice I've seen was to consider it the training wheels for STs. Take 'em off when you know what you're doing or leave them on if you're having fun. Your call.)<br /> <br /> Honestly, the thing would probably be best as a generic supernatural template, but I'm a mage player/ST. With a legacy, the change is directly through/by/to the soul, and fits the balance of Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T17:17:40-07:00","id":185861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=185778#post185778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will this artificial self-Claimed still had access to Arcana? I ask because the rule about not stacking Templates is there for a reason (plus, on top of that general rule, there is the specific one about supernaturals being incapable of being claimed). So, is this a &quot;I stop being a mage and become an inmortal Claimed&quot; (or claimed-like) thing, or is I am an inmortal Claimed and a mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's already a spirit/life legacy that gives you influence and an arcana. I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T19:30:12-07:00","id":185945,"title":"","content":"After encountering members of <b>the True Soul</b> legacy (from Grimore of Grimores) and figuring out what was actually happening to them, my Mastigos took the basic idea and ran with it. Reasoning that it was by encoding his personal memories and personality into a legacy that had allowed its creator to survive the fall, and that by doing the same with his own memories and personality, he might be able to withstand other cosmic cataclysms that he'd otherwise have no defense against. Since the Legacy only ever turns students into copies of him, and he doesn't want to multiply himself like that, it isn't a Legacy he intends to pass on conventionally, so much as teach other students how to shape similar legacies for themselves. (Meanwhile, keeping a Daimonicon back at his Sanctum as a final backup plan for cheating death should the worst happen.)<br /> <br /> He's trained one cabal-mate so far, but has been avoiding explaining exactly what's involved to the local consilum out of fear of being branded left-handed.<br /> <br /> Among the things he's hoping it'll help with is if a major expansion of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves' foothold takes place, the legacy will allow him to basically possess his other self from the newly asserted timeline, and from there maybe take action to try and set things right. So far, he hasn't gotten the chance to test his theory. If it proves effective, he'll likely start aggressively promoting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","user":"Cesario","date":". 07-01-2014, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","name":"Cesario","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T02:34:44-07:00","id":186136,"title":"","content":"It occurred to me that the karmic burden might pervert the Akuma's <u><i>Daimon</i></u> into the spiritual force driving improvement of his killing arts. That grants it all sorts of drawbacks automatically, and it's already part of the mage's pattern. Something akin to:<br /> <br /> Some mages perfect their killing arts. The burden of all the killing can have a grave effect even if the mage's Wisdom doesn't shatter under the strain. Each attainment requires a dramatic amount of killing on the Akuma's part. Rarely, only one or two deaths are needed, but that's only when the fights <i>themselves </i>are exceptionally flawless or the slain are especially skilled. All the essence and killing stain the character's soul... and eventually spawn something dark.<br /> <br /> <b>1st: Demon Aura</b> -- Spirit 2, Death 1<br /> The Akuma's Daimon has become tainted by the killing. Perfecting the ability to kill becomes an important part of the self improvement it promotes. It now, also, actually considers survival of the Akuma an active priority. A consequence is that the Akuma's aura becomes tainted with blood red blotches and black flames. This interferes with the ability to examine the character's aura, as if a 2 Potency shielding effect. This signifier is perceived before anything else, if order matters. The Akuma's Nimbus is also altered by this taint in a manner appropriate to the mage's former Nimbus.<br /> The effect grants Unseen Shield at Spirit potency.<br /> <b>Optional Mind 2</b><br /> The aura makes people uneasy. As an Instant mental action, the mage can impose a fear of himself into any target in sensory range. Potency of the effect is equal to Mind. This can be reflexively used as part of any mundane Intimidation attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd: Demon Shadow</b> -- Spirit 3 Mind 3<br /> The Akuma's Daimon now considers the Akuma's killing art to be the most important aspect of his being to improve. This attainment grants it the ability to extend part of itself into Twilight while remaining inside the Akuma's Oneiros. This is known as the Shadow. The form it takes is part of the Akuma's Aura. Manifesting this is reflexive with a Indefinite duration, and does not count as an action taken by Akuma. This also means it is not an action the Akuma retains any control over.<br /> <br /> Create the Daimon's Shadow as a normal disembodied familiar, including the familiar bond. The actual Daimon is an astral being of much greaeter power than this projection, and can act utterly independently of it. This Shadow has access to the Akuma's skills and most merits, whenever appropriate. When using the Akuma's body, the Shadow uses the Akuma's attributes. Unlike normal possession, the Shadow <i>does</i> have access to the Akuma's complete powers unless the Akuma is actively resisting it.<br /> <br /> If the Akuma's mind is outside of his body or inside the Inner Realms, the Shadow can control the body uncontested. For a willpower, the Akuma can grant the Shadow control of his body for a scene. The Akuma can give it goals and restrictions, which it will follow unless they directly conflict with the Daimon's goal of improving the Akuma's art. One of these restrictions can be to relinquish control when something is accomplished. &quot;Kill these three attackers and relinquish control&quot; is perfectly valid, for example. (Add rules linking Composure to control?)<br /> <br /> The Shadow, Daimon, and Akuma are linked tightly. Any skill training done by one aspect is affects all. They share an experience point pool. It's not uncommon for an Akuma to use this to train while doing other things, like meditating.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Death 3</b><br /> The <i>Daimon</i> can use Sculpt Ephemera at will.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd: Demon Soul</b> -- Spirit 4<br /> The Daimon now considers the improvement of the Akuma's killing arts to <i>be</i> improving the Akuma. (As part of that, the Daimon remains focused on self-preservation.)<br /> <br /> The Rank of the Shadow is now set as the lesser of the Akuma's Death and Spirit. Influences and Numina are normal for the rank, but then add Numina: Blast, Harrowing, and Materialize. Its Influence remains the primary killing art of the Akuma.<br /> <br /> (strike: At this level of attainment, the Daimon can begin the process of claiming the Akuma as a more normal spirit might claim a human.)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Mind 4</b><br /> (strike: The Daimon can act inside the Inner Realms as well as the physical simultaneously. If so desired, the Daimon can externalize the inner eye as a mental projection. Both of these can process mental actions independently. Also, the Daimon has more than just a Familiar bond, now, and can fully communicate with the Akuma.)<br /> <br /> Maybe something along these lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 07-02-2014, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T02:35:55-07:00","id":186137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's already a spirit/life legacy that gives you influence and an arcana. I don't see why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing is getting an Influence, and other way different is getting Claimed, with among other things gives free Attribute's dots, Aspects (more Paradox-free supernatural powers), another supernatural tolerance trait, another energy pool (Essence) and yes, Influences. Compare to any other Legacy that gives 3-6 Paradox-free powers and tell me that's internally balanced.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wich this Legacy, now fleshed out, doesn't seem to do. That's not spirit claiming, it seems more like a sort of goetic manifestation than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 07-02-2014, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T14:19:57-07:00","id":186516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=186137#post186137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing is getting an Influence, and other way different is getting Claimed, with among other things gives free Attribute's dots, Aspects (more Paradox-free supernatural powers), another supernatural tolerance trait, another energy pool (Essence) and yes, Influences. Compare to any other Legacy that gives 3-6 Paradox-free powers and tell me that's internally balanced.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wich this Legacy, now fleshed out, doesn't seem to do. That's not spirit claiming, it seems more like a sort of goetic manifestation than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough, this later version actually <i>is</i> the one that uses the claiming mechanics. (Admittedly, this was mostly a shortcut. Rather than, as I <i>was</i> doing, play around with various bonuses and abilities, I took the lazy out and just did that.) The previous idea was to leave that concept exclusively in the fluff as a way of explaining the abilities and theme. Obviously, it could be edited out in refinement. (This is a very rough draft. In fact, it's more of an outline.)<br /> <br /> What the heck <i>is</i> an &quot;Aspect,&quot; anyhow? Is that from another translation or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T14:21:07-07:00","id":186518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=186516#post186516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the heck <i>is</i> an &quot;Aspect,&quot; anyhow? Is that from another translation or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from the actual Claimed mechanics in Werewolf: the Forsaken - Predators and WoD: Skinchangers. Basic supernatural powers and &quot;mutations&quot; and such, like Longevity or Natural Weaponry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T15:34:10-07:00","id":186560,"title":"","content":"Now they seem to be going to be called Dread Powers, but yeah, as Satchel said, any supernatural power that you get from the Claiming is an Aspect (like a venomous bite from being claimed by a snake spirit or some armor if claimed by a rock one).<br /> <br /> Anyway, I may have missed it the first time around or it may have been edited after my own edit, but I didn't remember that line about the Daimon actually claiming the mage in the 3rd Attainment. Also, everytime I read &quot;killing art&quot; I cringe a little.<br /> <br /> Why is Claiming needed for the Legacy? How are its objectives not already attained with other methods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T18:13:32-07:00","id":186669,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks, Satchel &amp; Thorbes. It's been a while since I actually read through all of that section. Clearly need to... heh.<br /> <br /> The objectives are a loss of control and shift of purpose as they gain ever greater strength. Claiming does all of this. It's obviously not something I'm committed to. Nor am I opposed to it. The trade-offs need to be such that the legacy is rather objectively a bad thing, but, boy-howdy, is it strong.<br /> <br /> Any ideas for improvements are welcome. This means completely retooling it if you got a cool notion that fits the theme would be spiffy; by all means. That's what I meant by calling it an outline.<br /> <br /> Also feel free to suggest a better way of describing someone's techniques for killing. I was attempting to convey the entire process of killing, so an assassin, terrorist, or spy might end up with this, too. The point is that these jokers get significantly better at what they do and<i> how they already do it</i>. Even a broad understanding of &quot;martial arts&quot; conveys the wrong idea.<br /> <br /> (edit: Heh: &quot;marital arts&quot; sexy sexy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 07-04-2014, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T03:50:06-07:00","id":187798,"title":"","content":"Yep, martial arts probably brings to mind an image too specific that may not apply to the combat/killing methods of all the members of the Legacy. &quot;Combat prowess&quot;, perhaps? Or is the fact that if you get into a fight with one of these guys you either win or die a key aspect of the Legacy? They'll probably be branded Left Handed in some places, turning your soul into a killing tool could be seen as less than Wise by most mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T04:38:58-07:00","id":187813,"title":"","content":"I've always conceived of this as pretty clearly sinister. If I go with the twisted Daimon aspect, <i>especially </i>so.<br /> &quot;Combat prowess&quot; might work. I suppose a line explaining that the specific form is anything (and only) lethal would suffice. The thing that causes this is the ending of lives, however that gets accomplished.<br /> <br /> This twists the mage into something that <i>intuitively </i>kills. So, I wasn't thinking so much that you <i>have</i> to kill or be killed, but that this would be the normal outcome. As in, at least by the end, it would require Willpower to <i>avoid</i> killing a foe in most cases. (With the daimon approach, only those who are sufficient challenge to teach and improve the skills would be left alone. I could see an assassin leaving the inspector hunting him alive because &quot;he keeps me sharp,&quot; for example.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:04:43-07:00","id":188015,"title":"","content":"One thing I\u2019ve always wanted to try is to come up with a set of \u201ccrossover Legacies\u201d \u2014 that is, Legacies that draw on another gameline\u2019s themes and which would be at home in a crossover involving <b>Mage</b> and that other gameline. I know that this isn\u2019t everyone\u2019s cup of tea, and that some of you will in fact hate this notion with a passion. Your concerns are preemptively noted; but I still want to see what I can come up with. <br /> <br /> \u2022 The Tremere Liches are an official example of this, providing a bridge of sorts between <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Mage</b>. <br /> \u2022 The Sons of the Aether were conceived to serve as a similar bridge between <b>Mage</b> and <b>Promethean</b>: their founding belief is that all <b>Promethean</b>-related phenomena are in fact linked to the Aether (they point to Firestorms and <i>qashmallim</i> as evidence that the Supernal Realm of Prime and Forces, and the abode of Angels, is somehow connected to the Divine Fire); and as wrong as that premise <i>is</i>, they\u2019ve nevertheless managed to forge some useful Attainments centered around coping with and exploiting Pyros-based phenomena as they pursue their obsession. <br /> \u2022 In much the same way that the Sons of the Aether drew inspiration from cWoD\u2019s Sons of Ether, I could see a (Mastigos-based?) Legacy designed to bridge <b>Demon</b> and <b>Mage</b> that draws inspiration from cWoD\u2019s Iteration X: a Legacy that has developed around an (unhealthy) interest in the God-Machine, with Attainments designed to give the mage \u201cgadgets\u201d and \u201cimplants\u201d (the latter of which mimic features of a Demonic Form, turning the mage into a cyborg; think HIT Marks). They may even worship the God-Machine, in direct analogy to how cWoD\u2019s Iteration X worshipped the Computer, a god-like machine spirit from Autochthonia. <br /> \u2022 For <b>Geist</b>, I\u2019m thinking maybe a Moros-based Flatliners Legacy (nickname: Orpheans), with Attainments designed to interact with ghostly Twilight and the Underworld, including projecting one\u2019s soul into Twilight in a ghost-like manner, opening Avernian Gates, and crossing the Underworld\u2019s Rivers. They share the Sin-Eaters\u2019 status as having one foot in the realm of life and one in the realm of death. <br /> \u2022 For <b>Mummy</b>, I\u2019d want something that imitates the \u201cmaterial magic\u201d paradigm that the Arisen feature, with a heavy emphasis on the ability to make and use relics. This Legacy would not have a single Parent Path, but would customize its Attainments according to the mage\u2019s Path (largely in terms of what kinds of relics the mage is best with). It would be ugly in that sacrifices would be a big part of their magic. <br /> \u2022 The aforementioned Akuma might serve as a <b>Werewolf</b> bridge, though I\u2019d be inclined to base them on being \u201cClaimed\u201d by a Supernal Beast. <br /> \u2022 I\u2019m not sure what to do with regard to <b>Changeling</b>. Maybe an Acanthus-based Legacy with a talent for oneiromancy? <br /> <br /> Note that most of these are intended for use as antagonists, for the most part (though not exclusively so). The Flatliners and Inception-derived Legacies appear to be among the most benign at first glance; but even they should have justification for being classified as Left-Handed Legacies \u2014 I\u2019m just not sure what to do to darken them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:20:21-07:00","id":188022,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely love a mage legacy based around Guardian Masques and Demon Covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T11:21:13-07:00","id":188138,"title":"","content":"i\u2019m not quite sure how that would work: Covers are defined in terms of their fragility, and don\u2019t define any strengths that Masques lack which a Legacy could emulate. OTOH, I could definitely see adapting something like the Guardians\u2019 Masques as Demon-specific Merits that let you enhance a Cover. But that\u2019s a Demon thing, not a Mage thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T11:23:39-07:00","id":188139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=188138#post188138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i\u2019m not quite sure how that would work: Covers are defined in terms of their fragility, and don\u2019t define any strengths that Masques lack which a Legacy could emulate. OTOH, I could definitely see adapting something like the Guardians\u2019 Masques as Demon-specific Merits that let you enhance a Cover. But that\u2019s a Demon thing, not a Mage thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>He means basically sidereal resplendencies where a mage can adopt a whole new identity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T11:26:26-07:00","id":188140,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m still familiarizing myself with Masques. How would Masques and \u201cresplendencies\u201d differ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T14:49:26-07:00","id":188264,"title":"","content":"If I was going to blend the themes of Promethean into Mage, I figure the Moros are the best place for it, given their natural tendencies towards alchemy. Just a thought. Still, a Moros legacy that gains Internal Alchemy with Prime as its primary arcana seems quite workable.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to merge Demon's Cover into a legacy, you could make it a separate thing the legacy creates, reinforces and bolsters, but can be shattered sans magic. IOW, they could literally <i>get</i> covers. Depending how dark you want to get, the legacy could create these covers using supernal truth or using the supernal link built into a human soul. (Thus sacrificing a person ala Demon) The mechanics could work all sorts of different ways, even with those notions fixed.<br /> <br /> If I remember to find it, I actually have a legacy or two already fairly worked out that fits your Orphean legacy description quite well. One version was a Mastigos legacy that focused on the image of the Iron Key, which could open Avernian gates and defy some of the laws of realms. Death primary, Space. Fate/Mind optional to read the realms' laws and such. Don't think I finished that particular one. I delve into my list and see if I can find it.<br /> <br /> (edit: Not finding it. It's possibly a casualty of my harddrive crash several months ago. Phooey.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 07-04-2014, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T17:41:34-07:00","id":188332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=188264#post188264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was going to blend the themes of Promethean into Mage, I figure the Moros are the best place for it, given their natural tendencies towards alchemy. Just a thought. Still, a Moros legacy that gains Internal Alchemy with Prime as its primary arcana seems quite workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that all you need for Supernal Alchemy is Matter, adding Matter to an Obrimos works reasonably well, too. Plus, the parallels between pure Pyros phenomena (e.g., <i>qashmallim</i> and Firestorms), the fact that lightning acts as a conductor for Pyros, and \u201cSons of <i>the Aether</i>\u201d\u2026 (The only downside is that Death is Inferior for the Obrimos, whichis at odds with the \u201canimated dead flesh\u201d thing; but that\u2019s mainly a technicality.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=188264#post188264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to merge Demon's Cover into a legacy, you could make it a separate thing the legacy creates, reinforces and bolsters, but can be shattered sans magic. IOW, they could literally <i>get</i> covers. Depending how dark you want to get, the legacy could create these covers using supernal truth or using the supernal link built into a human soul. (Thus sacrificing a person ala Demon) The mechanics could work all sorts of different ways, even with those notions fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I\u2019m more interested in the \u201cSupernal cyborgs\u201d thing than the Cover thing. If I <i>were</i> to go with a Cover-mimicking Legacy, I\u2019d want to avoid the Demonic soul-pact thing. Which is probably why I wouldn\u2019t want to do the Cover thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=188264#post188264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember to find it, I actually have a legacy or two already fairly worked out that fits your Orphean legacy description quite well. One version was a Mastigos legacy that focused on the image of the Iron Key, which could open Avernian gates and defy some of the laws of realms. Death primary, Space. Fate/Mind optional to read the realms' laws and such. Don't think I finished that particular one. I delve into my list and see if I can find it.<br /> <br /> (edit: Not finding it. It's possibly a casualty of my harddrive crash several months ago. Phooey.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh; that\u2019s an unexpected direction to go. I\u2019d be more likely to go either with Moros or Thyrsus: Moros because, well, necromancy; Thyrsus because of the Sin-Eaters\u2019 \u201ccelebrate life\u201d thing. Probably Thyrsus, now that I think of it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T08:40:44-07:00","id":193662,"title":"","content":"<b>Fairy Tale Wizards: </b>Desiring to further their understanding of their magic's origin, this left handed legacy of Acanthus have formed a contract with the Gentry. In exchange for their obedient servitude, they are taught the secrets of Fae magic, and are protected against the warping powers that would normally turn them into Changelings. Their dealings with the Fae have taught them the Arcana of Mind, in addition to Fate and Time which they already possessed.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T08:49:09-07:00","id":193670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=188138#post188138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i\u2019m not quite sure how that would work: Covers are defined in terms of their fragility, and don\u2019t define any strengths that Masques lack which a Legacy could emulate. OTOH, I could definitely see adapting something like the Guardians\u2019 Masques as Demon-specific Merits that let you enhance a Cover. But that\u2019s a Demon thing, not a Mage thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>coughcough(Legion)cough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:04:42-07:00","id":193680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=193670#post193670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">coughcough(Legion)cough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Need a ricola for that cough?<br /> <br /> (Though you're right, demon Covers...are pretty much very like [Legion], with the souls and the...now I kinda wonder if there might be a connection to be written into the description of the legacy. Hmm.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:18:15-07:00","id":193693,"title":"","content":"Made this after playing Dragon Age. Not sure if any good, but here it is: <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mage Legacy: The Tranquil</b></span><br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"><i>Humanity is flawed. Why have ourselves garner power when we know not how to wield it?</i></div> <br /> With magic, there is power, but with power comes either the desire for more, or the fear of what one has become. From the latter was born the Tranquil.<br /> Rumor abounds that the legacy began during the Salem Witch Trials of 1692. Newly indoctrinated mages became fearful of drawing the attention of hunters to themselves and their families, but were also afraid of somehow justifying the horrendous executions committed in the name of God and the Puritan church.<br /> Through the study of the Prime and Mind Arcana, Thaumaturge Susan Locke found a way to not only suppress her magic, but make herself immune to it. But while this made her invulnerable to all covert (and some vulgar) magic, and seem to become ignored by abyssal manifestations, it also muted her ability to feel emotion, dream into the Astral Realm, and worse, cast vulgar spells of any sort.<br /> The Consilli, as a whole, does not condemn the Tranquil for their choice, but many either show pity or tragic sympathy for them, throwing away much of their talent for the sake of regaining the relationships they once had with the rest of society. The Adamant Arrow sees them as members still under their protection, as they are still Awakened and able to perceive magic, while the Mysterium is fascinated by the Legacy, wondering whether it was another way towards reaching Supernal enlightenment by rejecting power. The Guardians LOVE the Tranquil, as they are completely incapable of being touched by the Abyss, or manipulated by enemy mages, but in stark contrast, the Silver Ladder HATES the legacy, seeing it as a cowardly choice of action to deny what is within one's rights to have. As for the Free Council? They see the Tranquil with mixed feelings, some feel they are sympathetic to sleepwalkers, and are therefore good mediators, while others see them as a joke, having removed their ability to feel any emotion, and therefore lost their humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Any<br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Tranquil, (vulgar) Slack-jaws<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Tranquil usually wear simple and plain garb, the better to be overlooked. Many remain the way they looked before joining the legacy, save now with an expressionless face, and blank-staring eyes. Many take on the attire of monks or priests, and create shared, monastic sanctums with one another, usually becoming guardians to dangerous artifacts due to their immunity to abyssal influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Restrain from using magic for a specific period of time, meditating in silence, fasting.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments: </b><br /> <br /> <b><i>1st: Rite of Tranquility</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Gnosis 3, Prime 2 (primary), Mind 1,<br /> Upon joining the Tranquil, the mage becomes immune to covert spells that target her. She is not immune, however, to the effects of vulgar spells, or spells that manipulation the environment to attack her. Also, the Tranquil loses any dots she has in the Dream merit, and cannot purchase them again. She cannot cast vulgar spells, and gains a -3 to all social rolls due to emotional detachment.<br /> <br /> <b><i>2nd: Peace with the Void</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Gnosis 5, Prime 3<br /> At this level of training, the Tranquil has learned how to confuse the Abyss by becoming &quot;uninteresting&quot;. Manifestations ignore her unless she invokes a paradox, and even then, only physical attacks can affect her.<br /> Optional Arcanum: Mind 3<br /> Staring into the jaws of the Abyss can drive anyone insane, no matter how jaded they are. But the Tranquil have learned to strengthen their sense of sanity, and thus gain a +3 against acquiring derangements.<br /> <br /> <b><i>3rd: Magical Null</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Gnosis 7, Prime 4<br /> The Mage can now create and maintain a zone of anti-magic, making dampening all attempts to cast spells equal to -1 per success on a Presence + Composure check. This aura must be maintained by concentrating, and requires 10 minutes per 5 feet expansion, the maximum radius being 20 ft. This ability does not destroy abyssal manifestations, or impede, it merely weakens spell casting or the use of magical items. It does not affect artifacts.<br /> Optional Arcanum: Mind 4<br /> If the mage has enough training in the Mind Arcanum, she can focus her aura onto a specific subject, telepathically muting a number of mages attempts to cast spells equal to her Gnosis. This still requires concentration, and only works if the targeted mage fails to ward off the spell with mind or prime magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T12:06:11-07:00","id":193832,"title":"","content":"Not a clue what your source looks like, as I've never played Dragon Age; these are strictly Mage thoughts, Mr Paraduo.<br /> <br /> Immunity to covert spells is absolutely overpowered. A shielding effect that reduces any covert casting die pools sounds fine. I'd toss in something like Supernal Vision to bump the power back up.<br /> (Alternately, make this the third attainment and fiddle with it.)<br /> <br /> I like that second one, except for the nearly complete immunity to Manifestations. Again, that's overpowered.<br /> A round of complete immunity to them for a willpower? That works. Maybe expand the list to include abyssally empowered effects..<br /> The ability to counter the attacks of such things by spending a willpower to burn through their time remaining (or essence) could be interesting.<br /> I'd probably go with a Soul Shield that includes this &quot;ignore me, Abyss&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> That third one would be a lot simpler if they could simply concentrate to create a field effect that impedes by Prime. The Mind optional doesn't really fit the mechanics of mage, though. On the other hand, a Mind/Prime suppress casting effect could make some sense. Basically, a Counterspell Primal or Supernal Dispellation effect as an AoE or multiple targets could do similar things.<br /> <br /> I'd consider Spirit as the optional and folding the Mind effects into the main line a bit more, or the reverse. That way, you could toss in effects like &quot;Abyssal Essence boils off in the area every round. The duration of a Manifestation reduces, instead.&quot; and &quot;Counter the powers of abyssal spirits&quot; and that sort of thing. If you go with a mind conjunctional, the &quot;ignore me&quot; thing could apply to anyone hostile, say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T13:57:17-07:00","id":193948,"title":"","content":"Well, they lose access to Vulgar spells altough having Mind that's not that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:48:41-07:00","id":193992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=193832#post193832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a clue what your source looks like, as I've never played Dragon Age; these are strictly Mage thoughts, Mr Paraduo.<br /> <br /> Immunity to covert spells is absolutely overpowered. A shielding effect that reduces any covert casting die pools sounds fine. I'd toss in something like Supernal Vision to bump the power back up.<br /> (Alternately, make this the third attainment and fiddle with it.)<br /> <br /> I like that second one, except for the nearly complete immunity to Manifestations. Again, that's overpowered.<br /> A round of complete immunity to them for a willpower? That works. Maybe expand the list to include abyssally empowered effects..<br /> The ability to counter the attacks of such things by spending a willpower to burn through their time remaining (or essence) could be interesting.<br /> I'd probably go with a Soul Shield that includes this &quot;ignore me, Abyss&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> That third one would be a lot simpler if they could simply concentrate to create a field effect that impedes by Prime. The Mind optional doesn't really fit the mechanics of mage, though. On the other hand, a Mind/Prime suppress casting effect could make some sense. Basically, a Counterspell Primal or Supernal Dispellation effect as an AoE or multiple targets could do similar things.<br /> <br /> I'd consider Spirit as the optional and folding the Mind effects into the main line a bit more, or the reverse. That way, you could toss in effects like &quot;Abyssal Essence boils off in the area every round. The duration of a Manifestation reduces, instead.&quot; and &quot;Counter the powers of abyssal spirits&quot; and that sort of thing. If you go with a mind conjunctional, the &quot;ignore me&quot; thing could apply to anyone hostile, say.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Tranquil in Dragon Age are Mages who had their connection to The Fade (source of magic and the dream world) severed. This renders them incapable of using magic directly, but at the same time makes them immune to possession, mental influences, and allows them to work with the otherwise poisonous Lyrium (which is used for enchanting magical effects into mundane objects. Some choose to become Tranquil willingly, others have it forced upon them, but it cuts off their ability to feel any sort of emotion or to experience dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:15:13-07:00","id":194007,"title":"","content":"<b>Followers of Merlin</b>: The legendary Merlin was said to be one of the wisest, most powerful wizards in history, who's tutorship was the responsible for raising Kings into power, such as Arthur. He was also said to be half demon, possessing an Incubus for a father. The Followers of Merlin are a Mastigos Legacy who seek to become all knowing, much like their role model. They crave knowledge even at great personal risk and spend their time hunting down occult lore and meditating on the nature of the universe. Over time, a Follower of Merlin can become one of the most well informed scholars or the most insightful philosophers in the world. Their insatiable hunger for knowledge has lead them to studying the Arcana of Time because it often takes a life time to accomplish true understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Weather Witches:</b> This female exclusive Legacy of Thyrsus have dedicated their magic to harnessing control over the weather. Their enemies are met with blasts of lightning, gale force winds, freezing cold, scorching heat, and torrential downpours as they unleash the destructive forces of nature upon them. The Weather Witches have begun to study the Arcana of Forces such as cold, heat, electricity, air, est.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T17:46:37-07:00","id":194147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=194007#post194007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Weather Witches:</b> This female exclusive Legacy of Thyrsus have dedicated their magic to harnessing control over the weather. Their enemies are met with blasts of lightning, gale force winds, freezing cold, scorching heat, and torrential downpours as they unleash the destructive forces of nature upon them. The Weather Witches have begun to study the Arcana of Forces such as cold, heat, electricity, air, est.</div> </div> </div> </div>This ground is covered by an Acanthus legacy in Tome of the Watchtowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T18:31:34-07:00","id":194175,"title":"","content":"Awww. Well actually it's not surprising the idea was already made. But still, thought I put my own spin on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T02:25:18-07:00","id":194456,"title":"","content":"Also, is curious that the followers of Merlin are Mastigos when the man himself is the poster boy for the Achantus Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T06:41:20-07:00","id":194603,"title":"","content":"Well half demon, driven by a pursuit of knowledge and improving of the mind, had a fondness for education. Seems like a Warlock to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T06:54:36-07:00","id":194607,"title":"","content":"Guided peoples\u2019 fates and lived his life backward (by some accounts, at least); sounds like an Acanthus. Warlocks tend to be less enamored with educating and more interested in confronting. Also, Merlin\u2019s ancestry is as often cited to be fae as demonic; the latter representation arguably has as much to do with those who were revising the Arthurian myths recasting anything \u201cpagan\u201d as \u201cof the devil\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T10:55:00-07:00","id":202247,"title":"","content":"I've got one I've been mulling over for the past week. No name yet unfortunately.<br /> <br /> This particular legacy is inspired by quite a few sources, the Chalice Compact of Toronto, Summoners, Proximi and the Tremere. The basic philosophy goes something like this: Once you have Awakened only Archmastery or Ascension can get you back into the Supernal, or so the rumors go. On the other hand, Sleepers transcend the Abyss with surprising frequency (Depending on your views) and come back filled with Supernal power, a newly Awakened. What if the process of simply sending a soul to the Supernal to learn the absolute Truths that it contains could be harnessed? If you think it's so crazy it'll never work then consider this, according to some ancient theories the soul is naturally Supernal anyways, possibly a microcosm of the entirety of the Supernal realms which is why it contains such vast power enough to even create immortality as the liches of the Tremere have. So everyone, all Sleepers at any rate, though tainted by the Abyss, have a sympathy to the Supernal that could potentially be exploited. Another ancient teaching says that souls which pass on move to Stygia, or perhaps elsewhere in the Supernal realms, no one knows for sure of course, and then after that something happens and it comes back, reincarnated. Mages of this legacy take a great deal of interest in these ideas, and also the ability to summon beings from the Supernal to the Fallen to learn from them. Beings from the Supernal Realms usually have an alien mindset that's difficult to understand fully, and souls are a mystery, but ultimately they're housed in humans and humans are much easier to understand. So if you can acknowledge the possible validity of the fact that souls can and do travel to the Supernal and back, then it should be possible to use magic to synthesize a similar process and glean knowledge from them.<br /> <br /> The practices of these Mages lead to a tendency to cultivate Sleepers as Allies or Retainers, and appear to empower the Sleeping Soul with a glimmer of the glory of the realms Supernal. They appear to be benevolent, and in some ways they might even actually be. On the other hand a closer look at them would reveal that this is truly exploitative, enslaving the soul to their whims in their quest for knowledge and then discarding the burned out husks when they are no longer of use.<br /> <br /> Do these Mages actually succeed in sending souls to other realms? It's a question open to interpretation with no clear answer. Their power is unquestionable, the methods that they use to gain it bears fruit, but like so many they are simply blindly following their own philosophies and assumptions in the Darkness. Because of the fact that Mages have limitations in understanding and sympathy to the Supernal realms imposed on them by being stuck on one Path this Legacy seeks followers from all Paths to broaden the depths of its collective knowledge. It's a Legacy most likely to crop up in the Mysterium and the Seers of the Throne, one because of the knowledge that can potentially be gained and the other because it's a model of the rule of the Exarchs over their Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Attainment 1: Gnosis 3: Death 2: Like a Tremere Lich these Mages can steal the soul of a Sleeper following the rules for Sever the Sleeping Soul. However, they roll Manipulation+Persuasion+Death, though not always the case these Mages are likely to try and seduce their victims into eagerly giving up their souls in exchange for power and understanding beyond the scope of regular Sleepers. Additionally they are capable of creating a Soul Jar as per the spell. With this trapped soul they are able to add half (rounded down) its remaining Integrity as bonus dice on Resonance study rolls. The Mage may only maintain possession of a number of souls this way equal to his dots in the Death arcanum, and any soul that reaches 0 Integrity becomes impossible to use any of the attainments of this legacy on.<br /> <br /> Optional Space 2: With this the Mage is able to subtly manipulate the sympathies of the soul to its original owner so that the two don't even notice that they're separated. If the Sleeper is given custody of the Soul Jar with his or her own soul in it then other than the original Degeneration for soul loss she suffers no further ill effects and does not continue to degenerate as long as she keeps the Soul Jar on her person. Separation from it induces an automatic Degeneration check. This technique is far from perfected, as long as the Sleeper's soul remains outside of its natural housing then the Sleeper may not raise his Integrity by any means. Finally, the Sleeper may use his own soul inside of the Soul Jar to perceive Resonance and scrutinize it with a number of bonus dice equal to half his remaining Integrity. If his soul's Integrity is lowered to 0 one way or another he receives none of the benefits of this or any other attainment.<br /> <br /> Attainment 2: Gnosis 5: Death 3: This is pretty much the cornerstone of the Legacy, allowing the Mage to open a gateway to the Supernal and rather than summoning something from it sending a soul stolen with the first Attainment into the Supernal. This is an extended action and follows all of the same rules as the rules for summoning, including the possibility of an Abyssal intrusion with a couple exceptions. The Mage does not need extra successes for the presence of Sleepers and bringing the soul back for study effectively closes the gateway without risk of an Abyssal intrusion. Where exactly the soul goes, and why it experiences the changes it does are up to speculation. What is known is that the soul appears to go to the Supernal realm (or something close to it) for which the Mage has a sympathetic connection, in other words the realm of his Watchtower. There is no known way to send the soul to a different realm and it's because of this inherent limitation that the legacy seeks out Mages from all Paths in order to broaden its understanding of the Supernal realms. A soul sent in this manner automatically loses a point of Integrity. It is possible to simply leave a soul stranded in the Supernal by closing the connection on it before it has returned. What happens to the soul after that is completely unknown as none that has been abandoned in this manner has ever been recovered. Once the soul has been brought back it is changed, the subtle arcana of which it is composed that resonates with the Path of the Mage that sent it is prominently on display and if closely studied can reveal secrets and knowledge unknown to other Mages. Additionally this experience enslaves the soul to the one who sent it, he may now send it out or cause it to obey in a manner similar to a Familiar in Twilight. The soul however is unlike a familiar in that it has no numina, influences, no traits or skills, etc in the way that souls normally are. What it is capable of though is serving as a way of spying, information reminiscent of the Path subtle arcana of the Mage that sent it becomes imprinted on it during its travels and may be observed by the Mage upon its return. It also serves as a sympathetic connection for the Mage to cast through as a Familiar can, any magic so cast that threatens Paradox forces the soul to check for loss of Integrity.<br /> <br /> Optional Space 3: If the soul is returned to its jar and the Sleeper who originally possessed it then the Sleeper gains a benefit from the experience as well. Because the soul's journey to the Supernal was heavily influenced by the understanding and Path of the Mage who sent it he becomes a Sleepwalker in regards to that Mage only. This is a boon and a curse, he can witness magic and remember it, but only from the one Mage. Every other Mage treats this &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; as a normal Sleeper and incurs Paradox and Disbelief as usual. Even though he has some protection from the powers of the Quiescience if the Mage who owns his soul incurs Paradox and he is present to witness it then a Degeneration check on his Integrity will occur.<br /> <br /> Attainment 3: Gnosis 7: Death 4: At this level the Mage has refined and honed his techniques, increased his understanding and can more fully utilize the powers of the souls that he controls. He may use a stolen soul to establish a pseudo-Demesne or Annulity. This follows the usual rules for such things, the soul stone is actually the soul jar in which the soul is contained. These places of power though are sadly very temporary, the Mage must still check for Paradox on Vulgar spells inside of the Demesne, if the Paradox succeeds then the soul will automatically suppress it and automatically lose a point of Integrity.<br /> <br /> Optional Space 4: The Sleeper who has custodianship of the soul jar containing his soul returned to him finds that after his soul's sojourn into the Supernal it maintains a link with that Supernal realm. He may obtain the Blessings of a Proximi that is aligned to the particular realm to which his soul was sent. The rules for the use of these Blessings remain the same, but whenever they are used they incur a degeneration check for loss of Integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T07:57:10-07:00","id":202927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=188015#post188015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure what to do with regard to <b>Changeling</b>. Maybe an Acanthus-based Legacy with a talent for oneiromancy?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I had a huge write-up for a Legacy like this that I was about to post, when the browser crashed. I should know by now to only edit large posts in Notepad or something.<br /> Anyway, the <b>Storytellers</b> were an Acanthus Mind-focused Legacy focused on guiding others and shaping the world by communicating through dreams (the power of the Narrative).<ul><li>The first Attainment was a combined Emotional Urging and Perfect Moment (M:tA pgs 207 and 152) so their words would have the weight needed to recruit new agents. Optional Arcana was Forces or Matter for Instill Subliminal Message (GotV pg 194). (Gnosis 3, Mind 2 (Primary) and Fate 2, opt Forces 2 and/or Matter 2)</li> <li>Second Attainment was to communicate through Dreams with their agents, used for briefing and debriefing, optional arcana was Time for Prophetic Dream (TotM page 28). (Gnosis 5, Mind 3, opt Time 3)</li> <li>Third Attainment was for the Dreamscape to become as much a headquarters as possible, with actually bringing people into various Oneiroi, being able to dream up equipment, and guarding against intrusion. Optional arcana was Fate to sanctify and break Oaths.</li> </ul><br /> Whether or not Sleepers would remember the dream conferences could be played with to make actual Sleeper cells, they might not even know they were working for someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T08:38:27-07:00","id":202970,"title":"","content":"I'm really liking your weird pseudo-liches, Mrmdubois. Quite an interesting take on a Reaper Legacy. My only suggestion about them is to maybe change the optional second and third attainments' prerequisites to be Prime instead of Space, as I feel they fit thematically with that Arcanum better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T09:18:58-07:00","id":203006,"title":"","content":"I used Space more as a sign of the increasing sympathetic dependency the Sleeper has on the Mage who is influencing him via his Attainments. For instance the first Attainment screws with the sympathetic link of a Sleeper with his own soul letting him fake still having it in him, the second attainment allows the Sleeper to act as a Sleepwalker but only for the Mage who used the Attainment on him because of the web of sympathies between the Sleeper, the Mage, and the Mage's Supernal Realms (Or wherever that soul is actually going), and the third attainment is of course simply strengthening and refining the power of those bonds even further. <br /> <br /> So, I don't think I'd change it personally, and Space could use the love, but if you felt Prime was more appropriate and ended up using this Legacy yourself I wouldn't have any problem with it. A strong argument for Prime could definitely be made.<br /> <br /> Glad you liked it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T10:42:28-07:00","id":203062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=203006#post203006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used Space more as a sign of the increasing sympathetic dependency the Sleeper has on the Mage who is influencing him via his Attainments. For instance the first Attainment screws with the sympathetic link of a Sleeper with his own soul letting him fake still having it in him, the second attainment allows the Sleeper to act as a Sleepwalker but only for the Mage who used the Attainment on him because of the web of sympathies between the Sleeper, the Mage, and the Mage's Supernal Realms (Or wherever that soul is actually going), and the third attainment is of course simply strengthening and refining the power of those bonds even further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when you put it that way, then I really can't say anything else about the matter. I like it <i>even more</i> now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:09:23-07:00","id":204124,"title":"","content":"Did Tamers of Blood ever get a good write up anywhere? I've had a rendition rattling around in my head trying to incorporate everything Dave has ever said about them, but I'm not sure it's worth putting down on paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":".  Eh, here's my pitch anyways. 07-21-2014, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:27:56-07:00","id":204224,"title":"","content":"Just because someone else wrote something up doesn't mean a good alternative isn't welcome.<br /> If you think it's a good start, unique take, or whatever else makes it worth sharing, go for it.<br /> <br /> Same goes for alternatives for official legacies: If the original is good, a new take expands on that; if it's bad, the new one could replace it.<br /> <br /> The only unwelcome things, as far as<b> I'm</b> concerned, are ideas that basically do nothing unique and interesting. Even if it <i>sucks</i>, a legacy might include some neat ideas to scavenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:55:19-07:00","id":204272,"title":"","content":"The Tamers of Blood are largely unknown and fairly notorious where anyone has heard about them. They have an intimate understanding of Sympathetic connections, generally they talk about it in terms of family. Blood is thicker than water, family first, these are their ideals. Families can be wonderful, wholesome and nourishing, but they can also be warped and twisted, stunting growth. Those related to you can be your greatest source of help in reaching your greatest potential and they can also be your worst enemies manipulating you for their own ends. Some say you can't choose your family, the Tamers of Blood know better. The fact that a family can go either way is one of the biggest hindrances to the Tamers of Blood. The good ones just want to be able to help those closest to them, the bad ones get suspicion cast on the rest of them. It's true after all, their attainments allow a high level of control over those they're Bonded to, and therefore can be abused.<br /> <br /> Many Tamers fall somewhere on the periphery of the Awakened society. Seers don't have a problem with them for the most part because the Attainments can easily be used to further their ultimate goal of oppression, but the family unit itself is too small a focus for the globally minded Seers most of the time. The Pentacle on the other hand hears about the bad apples and worries about the Tamers being Left-Handed. Like any Tamer legacy they can be found in any Order in very small numbers, but the ones who gravitate to them the most often are the Guardians and the Arrow. The Guardians because it can give them greater control over their labyrinths and the Arrow because it can allow them to select some of those they've dedicated themselves to protecting and giving them a greater level of security. Silver Ladder sometimes join and use the Attainments as a way to keep tabs on Proximi and to ease the process of keeping the lines pure. Free Councillors might join in order to Bond with Sleepers they have attachments to that they're unwilling to forsake simply because they have Awakened. Just as frequently the Tamers are Apostate or Nameless building up cults of personality or fear. Because of their Attainments the Tamers are able to frequently operate via middlemen which can make them very elusive targets for enemies.<br /> <br /> To take advantage of any of their Attainments the Tamers of Blood require a ritual in which they and the person they are bonding to each take a point of lethal damage and exchange their blood. This ritual must be engaged in voluntarily, there might be coercion involved in getting that voluntary consent, but they have to be aware of what they are doing (Though not necessarily of all the consequences) and able to say yes of their own free will. This is important, if it's ignored the ritual will simply fail to create the appropriate bond. The exact technique varies, the blood can be consumed, or the wounds can be pressed together to force the blood to commingle. Some really forward thinking Tamers even go ahead and do blood transfusions. The lethal damage from the ritual must be allowed to heal naturally, and always leaves a scar as part of the process. I don't think there should be an upper limit on the number of people that a Tamer can Bond, but I do think that if they're not doing it for cabal mates then anyone who is Bonded should be represented by Merit dots appropriately. Allies, True Friend, Retainers, Mystery Cult Initiates, maybe even Contacts can all be appropriate, but it shouldn't be free. I think that with these two limitations, the necessity of voluntary involvement and the requirement for representing the Bonded with Merits can cut down on making this legacy too ridiculous. The merits can also help determine the kind of familial social focus the Tamer wishes to embody. Further limit on their power is that they can exercise their Attainments on only one given individual at a time, and for the Optional Attainments Resistance is allowed.<br /> <br /> All Tamers of Blood are bonded not only by the mentor/apprentice bond of a Legacy, but also by the Bond created and used by the Legacy itself. Experiencing the bond oneself, and having its influence exercised upon you is how the Attainments are passed on. This allows for a very closely knit and insular Legacy that has very regular internal communication. Of course, depending on one's Mentor/Apprentice relationship this can be just as oppressive as the worst Tamer relationship with any of his Bonded. The Tamer at least has some means of fighting back.<br /> <br /> Note: Many of the spells you can use to affect yourself seem to be constructed in such a way that with a dot higher you can affect someone else. I assume then that the inverse is also true. Because of the fact that I place requirements on Bonding and who you can be Bonded too in order to limit the reach of this legacy and because the Tamers are supposed to be able to use their Attainments on Bonded as easily as on themselves there are some Attainments which will appear to be a dot lower than they are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Attainment 1: Gnosis 3: Space 2: Upon the successful completion of a Bonding ritual the Mage and the Bonded share an Intimate Sympathetic connection. If for whatever reason some level of anonymity was desired and true names or the like were not shared it does not negatively impact the strength of this connection. Furthermore, this Bond does not wane over time from lack of use, though typically they see quite a lot of use. These Bonds can be concealed, or frayed as per normal but they will regenerate or reappear regaining one step of strength per dot in Space per day. The Mage who created the bond may relinquish it, at which point it will proceed to operate as normal. The Mage may now slip into the senses of the person he has bonded with as an instant action using Presence+Empathy+Space. This is similar to Scrying but operates only through the senses of the Bonded, the Mage sees what they see, feels what they feel, etc. At Space 3 this duration becomes Prolonged, at Space 4 it may use the Advanced Prolongation factors.<br /> <br /> Optional Life 2: The Tamer once slipped into the senses of a Bonded may exercise some influence over him. The effect is similar to Body Control or Control Autonomic Functions and successes on an Instant action Manipulation+Persuasion+Life roll can be spent towards effects similar to either of these spells, the roll can be contested by the Bonded as normal. This can be a great boon, granting the Bonded the ability to heal small injuries more quickly, regulate his breathing, ensure a sound night's sleep or a feeling of satisfactory fullness after a good meal. The positive effects of this Attainment can even justify the Bonded being able to buy dots in Physical Merits as the Tamer tweaks their bodies in small, subtle ways to make them hardier, healthier individuals. On the flip side it can be a curse, the Bonded can't sleep, can't feel comfortable, constantly sneezes all at the whim of another. Of course the Mage can benefit himself as well, quelling hunger, resting peacefully, being more alert, etc.<br /> <br /> Attainment 2: Gnosis 5: Space 3: The Tamer becomes metaphysically closer to the Bonded whose senses he has slipped into. With an Instant action of Presence+Subterfuge+Space he may assume the Sympathetic connections of the Bonded. This allows him to mask his true identity when casting a Sympathetic spell, it also can mask the location of origin of the spell appearing to originate from either the Tamer or the Bonded at the discretion of the Tamer. Particularly cruel Tamers will use their Bonded as unwitting catspaws, while more benevolent ones will attempt to lure the enemies of their Bonded to them in order deal with them in person. Paradox if it occurs is outside the scope of the Legacy's control for now and has a tendency to appear at whichever location it can harm the most. As a side note, though the sympathetic connections might conceal who really cast the spell the Resonance of it can still give the Tamer away. As a result many Tamers study Prime as well in order to further mask their casting.<br /> <br /> Optional: Life 3: The Tamer may Trigger the Lizard Brain in the Bonded he has slipped inside of, or himself. He rolls Manipulation+Persuasion+Life as an Instant action which is contested by Resolve if the Bonded wishes. I probably don't need to get into the ways that this can be used to benefit or manipulate someone. <br /> <br /> Attainment 3: Gnosis 7: Space 4: The Tamer co-locates into the body of the Bonded and Space warps him slightly to fit within the confines of that body, generally by shrinking the Tamer if need be in certain dimensions. This Attainment cannot be used to create a violent collision between two bodies occupying the same space, though further use of Space magic could. While the co-location is Transitory as the spell and requires an Instant action and a Presence+Expression+Space roll penalties to the roll can be used to increase the duration slightly. At Space 5 this can be Prolonged as normal. The greatest use of this Attainment of course is that the Mage may conceal his presence almost perfectly and cast spells as if they were at Sensory range. This allows him to exert a significant amount of influence in protecting or manipulating his Bonded or those around the Bonded. As per the co-location spell the Mage may Reflexively choose where to end it. If he chooses to end it at the location of his Bonded he appears next to him.<br /> <br /> Optional: Life 4: The Tamer not only co-locates into the Bonded he can use him to act in a fashion similar to the Human Minion spell. The roll is Manipulation+Persuasion+Life and is contested by Resolve+Gnosis if the Bonded wishes. The Bonded might not want to fight it, being fully one with the Tamer can come with benefits. If they cooperate then the Mage may aid physical actions the Bonded takes as if the Mage had chosen to use an Assist action and had rolled successes equal to his dots in Life. The Bonded also gains access to any of the Fighting Style Merits the Tamer possesses if the Tamer chooses to share them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T21:30:11-07:00","id":204651,"title":"","content":"I had a <i>terrible </i>idea today:<br /> <br /> <b>Wonder Team Sparkle Force</b><br /> Order: Free Council<br /> Path: Obrimos<br /> Nicknames: Sparkle idiots, Wonders<br /> <br /> Although invented by Free Council mages, the Council, on the whole, considers them an embarassment. Some Guardians actively hunt them down and kill them as living violations of the veil.<br /> <br /> It is extremely difficult to be sure whether or not these individuals are being serious or not, but they claim, in all earnestness, that they have been chosen by some celestial body as a patron to fight evil. Only related lineages ever claim the same patron, so they seem to be coordinating on some level. They <i>do</i> act mightily to fight the Lie, as a rule, though they have really idiosyncratic definitions. Whether or not they are sane, they <b>are </b>receiving direction that coordinates them and makes them further their patron's goals---usually in ways compatible with Destroying Followers of the Lie.<br /> <br /> They dress up in gaudy clothing, and call on their patron's powers in showy and overt ways. When multiple claim the same patron, they call on different ascpects. The Lunar Team is six strong and have a member for Waxing, Waning, Half, Crescent, New, and Full. The Solar Trio is Dawn, Noon, and Dusk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1st: <i>Flash Dance</i><br /> Reqs: Spirit 2, Forces 2</b><br /> The Nimbus of the Wonder adds color, tones, and textures that are very cheerful to represent their patron. If they represent a specific aspect, the changes specifically reflect that..<br /> The character may activate this attainment by calling out to their patron for the power to transform. Beginning this is an Instant Action which unveils their Nimbus, and grants them the same effects as using a Dodge action. The transformation takes two rounds after this to complete.<br /> A Wonder may perform one transformation per dot of Spirit before they must recharge by some sort of communion with their patron. The effect lasts a scene, though can be extended for a Willpower.<br /> <br /> From initial activation until the transformation is complete, a defense raises which converts hostile energies that are directed at or near the Wonder into a map of the Nimbus, creating a phantasmagoria of color and cheery tones. The effect is quite flashy, provided attacks are coming in. Treat this as Armor rated equal to Forces.<br /> The energies released into the Nimbus apparently act as some sort of mystical effect, which empowers the patron. The Wonders believe that they can recieve direct intervention with enough of a display.<br /> <br /> The effect provides the patron and/or any of it's related servants essence as if the effect is an example of their type. This is not creating or converting essence, though, as much as generating it through an appropriate mundane act. Much in the same way, sufficient energy must be converted by the shield to have any appreciable effect. Storyteller's discretion.<br /> <br /> Any time the Wonder Dodges, the defensive effect and Nimbus return for that round in addition to the normal effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prime 2:</b> Even hostile spells are affected by the strange defense field effect. Subtract Prime from hostile spells or attainments while dodging.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2nd: <i>Cleansing Celestial Prism</i></b><br /> <b>Reqs.: Spirit 3, Forces 3</b><br /> While &quot;Transformed&quot; the Wonder can already Dodge to defend against most forms of harm, but this attainment takes that a step farther: Their patron's protection from spiritual threats is granted at any time they are Transformed. This applies Numinous Shield exept that it costs Willpower to use.When Dodging, there is no cost.<br /> <br /> When countering Numina, the effect seems to channel the essence either to the patron or any servants nearby. This attainment activating also counts as an event that attunes a location to the patron.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prime 3:</b><br /> The Nimbus gains partial solidity, allowing Sleepers to sense it. The resonance of the area is dramatically pushed towards the Patron. Treat whatever occurs in the scene because of the Wonder as occurring once per level of Prime. This literally multiplies the rate at which the effect takes hold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>3rd: <i>Star Beam</i><br /> Reqs. Spirit 4, Forces 4</b><br /> The Wonder calls on their patron to dish out some sort of damage. This is an attack spell, and almost always fires a glowing symbol of the patron.<br /> <br /> The specifics are chosen when the power is learned, though it's possible to change this power by visiting the patron. The effect will deal harsher damage to the specific foes that the Wonder is &quot;called to fight.&quot;<br /> Grant Materialize to an ally of the Patron, a fetish weapon (usually ranged) appears upon transforming, the Wonder may use Blast, or some other effect are all possible.<br /> <br /> (Resolve + <i>Expression</i> + Spirit to attack?) (Ed: Yep, you're right Proindrakenzol, that just works better than Composure)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prime 4:</b><br /> The character can shatter spells with their Star Beam, per Supernal Dispellation. Activate using Presence + Intimidation + Prime as an Instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":".  Fixing it, 'cause that's important to the welfare of humanity. 07-22-2014, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T00:32:25-07:00","id":204767,"title":"","content":"I'd go with Resolve + Expression for the dice pool an a weapon rating of Spirit bashing for the third attainment.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the name of the Moon, I will punish you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T00:39:04-07:00","id":204770,"title":"","content":"A mage I have in a Dark Ages chat game has been developing the following Legacy, meant for interactions with the Hedge and such. It's a bit of a niche, but it works for games where it might come into play.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Children of the Thorns</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mages aren't supposed to be in the hedge. That's what nearly any Changeling thinks that knows what they're dealing with when they see some crazy human studying a goblin fruit with an eery stare. Most mages happily agree with this sentiment, the risks of the thorns far outweighing the rewards. However, a choice few Acanthus feel an odd sort of sympathy with the hedge, for one reason or another; perhaps they Awakened near or past a gateway, perhaps they learned much of their own magic by studying changelings, or maybe they've seen a bit of the bounty found within; tokens, oddments, and goblin fruits, amongst an infinite number of unique locations and mysteries.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Any spellcaster quickly learns that the Hedge is one of the most dangerous realms a mage has access to, however. Even the Shadow, Underworld, and Astral can generally be considered 'safe' when one is dealing with packs of Briar Wolves that aren't responding to a disciple's Life magic, or upon feeling the terrible sense of loss when the thorns rip out a portion of their very Soul. Those that can find a way to not only deal with these threats, but to attune themselves to the realm that births them, however, may find a niche no other mage can possibly follow.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Primary Arcanum:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Life</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Parent Path: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Acanthus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Appearance:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Survivalists tend to be in outdoorsy clothes a lot, though on a minimalist approach (They don't often carry around a lot of equipment), but also have minor bits of the hedge decorating them; a square of a briar wolf's pelt hanging off a belt, for instance, or a necklace made from Hedgebeast ivory (Although in either case, these trophies are usually gained from self defense, not a tendency to hunt the creatures wantonly).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There's also a supernatural aspect to their appearance; their nimbus uncloaks and affects the surroundings when they're in the hedge. This isn't quite the same as a Changeling's Wyrd affecting the hedge, or even how a low Humanity Vampire affects it, but it still makes them a bit more obviously 'inhuman' to others in the Realm.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Nicknames:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Tattered Druids, Hedge Survivalists, Those idiot wizards (usually by changelings)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sample Oblations:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Spending an hour in the hedge, eating goblin fruit, studying an oddment, trifle, or token.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">First Attainment:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Survival Instincts</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Requirements:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Gnosis 3, Life 2, Fate 1, Prime 1, Survival 2, 'Hedge' Specialty in either Occult, Survival, or Investigation.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Effect:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The mage gains an instinctual understanding of the odd flora and fauna of the place, and can, with an instant action, inherently determine what a Goblin Fruit or Oddment's effect would be on him (Goblin Fruits, per Equinox Roads, affect mages like they were changelings). This requires a Wits + Survival + Life roll, and an exceptional success is needed to determine more discrete details, like infection from spores or discerning between two very similar hedgefruits that do different things. Since this becomes an innate ability, not a spell, it is not limited in dice pool by a mage's Wisdom. The mage also becomes better able to handle these fruits to begin with; treat his effective 'Wyrd' as half his Gnosis (round up) when determining the number of them he can carry.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Similarly, his connection to the fauna means he can detect nearby hobgoblins and other fae nearby him; similarly to Sense Life, but attuned to Fae, the mage can sense any creature of Glamour within Gnosis*2 yards of himself, as well as their relative location within that space. For piercing obscuring effects, assume a Potency equal to the mage's Gnosis + Life.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Optional Arcanum:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Fate 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">By combining basic knowledge of Prime with a connection the same threads of Fate that interweave through the Wyrd, the mage becomes able to protect himself, to a small degree, from the Thorns of the Hedge. Like Changelings, they instead lose a bit of power whenever the thorns would reach for the soul; 1 mana is lost per hour spent in the thorns. However, if they run out of mana, their Wisdom begins to be stripped away as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> ______________________________________________<br /> <br /> <br /> For the 2nd attainment I was considering either essentially taking a Kith (similar in scope to the transformation that Children get, I figure) and/or being able to grow Goblin Fruits and similar flora as per the perfecting spell equinox roads mentions. The optional would've been Fate 3 to open Gateways that have a Key.<br /> <br /> For the third, I was figuring (Gnosis) rolls per scene in the hedge would benefit from rote action, at the player's choice. Fate 4 as an optional would then grant the ability to channel Glamour (Via sacramental chain's equivalent).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T12:43:37-07:00","id":205240,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well, yeah, with the Life primary, having them gain features akin to a kith would be interesting. Something that helps them actually navigate the realm would also be very useful. I do like the idea of Key for the second attainment optional.<br /> <br /> With Fate 4, Life 4, an effect to banish the tearing of the thorns for a number of scenes seems interesting. (Roughly analogous to an Amnion in Dreamtime)<br /> Alternately, and related, the attainment could grant them some ability to create paths and waypoints in the Hedge, though costing Willpower and Glamour. This could also grant a moment's respite, and would still require power expended.<br /> <br /> This would fit the more fae-like relationship with Fate that Mages have than the Changelings, and still require expenditures of power to remain in the Hedge. (I'd prefer that Mages who figure this out would do so in a manner that is different than that of Changelings.<br /> <br /> One thing that might serve is using Sympathy rules somehow, as part of the scheme. Magi who achieve a certain level of familiarity with a region of the hedge cease to be seriously harmed by it, and even come to navigate it simply, since that story becomes old hat, and newer challenges await. Not sure exactly how to run with that theme, just now, but I like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Re: the Tamers of Blood:<br /> I'd consider shifting away from Space as the primary, and moving towards Mind.<br /> Yes, normally only Space can build up bonds of Mystical Sympathy, but Mind and Life <i>do</i> present <i>reasonable</i> ideas of how to link to something. &quot;My blood&quot; and &quot;My friend&quot; fit Life and Mind, respectively, and certainly fit mystical (and literal) notions of Sympathy. A legacy could tap that, even if Supernal magic divides things a bit differently.<br /> (The Familiar bond is a precedent of using Spirit to create a tight sympathetic bond.)<br /> <br /> You'd need rules for how these bonds work. I was thinking exactly as natural bonds, except the link improves them Indefinitely by one step. The effective Sympathy is maintained at a level higher, so even severing the bonds with magic never fully works, and an Intimate relationship leads to &quot;Sensory&quot; connection. Not <i>literally </i>Sensory, but no penalties for casting. This would also make an emotional bond between the parties more obviously reasonable.I was thinking that a blood tie could allow a character to cast on the linked party as if on himself, but with any sympathy penalties.<br /> <br /> I think the link should be bidirectional and not severable until a later attainment, so even Tamers of the Blood don't <i>lightly</i> become blood of someone else. At some point, it seems to me that they should be able to link two other parties by blood, and just their own. Rules for severing blood ties should also be present, and make them of potential cross-over interest.<br /> <br /> This would make mental projections reasonable, which could use the normal rules. If you want the projection at the second attainment, though, I was thinking that the projection itself could bear any sympathy penalties on all actions, including sensory input, but qualify as fully present otherwise. If you have that Sensory link, no penalty exists.<br /> <br /> Just some notions. I like the rough shape of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T12:57:13-07:00","id":205247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=205240#post205240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: the Tamers of Blood:<br /> I'd consider shifting away from Space as the primary, and moving towards Mind.<br /> Yes, normally only Space can build up bonds of Mystical Sympathy, but Mind and Life <i>do</i> present <i>reasonable</i> ideas of how to link to something. &quot;My blood&quot; and &quot;My friend&quot; fit Life and Mind, respectively, and certainly fit mystical (and literal) notions of Sympathy. A legacy could tap that, even if Supernal magic divides things a bit differently.<br /> (The Familiar bond is a precedent of using Spirit to create a tight sympathetic bond.)<br /> <br /> You'd need rules for how these bonds work. I was thinking exactly as natural bonds, except the link improves them Indefinitely by one step. The effective Sympathy is maintained at a level higher, so even severing the bonds with magic never fully works, and an Intimate relationship leads to &quot;Sensory&quot; connection. Not <i>literally </i>Sensory, but no penalties for casting. This would also make an emotional bond between the parties more obviously reasonable.I was thinking that a blood tie could allow a character to cast on the linked party as if on himself, but with any sympathy penalties.<br /> <br /> I think the link should be bidirectional and not severable until a later attainment, so even Tamers of the Blood don't <i>lightly</i> become blood of someone else. At some point, it seems to me that they should be able to link two other parties by blood, and just their own. Rules for severing blood ties should also be present, and make them of potential cross-over interest.<br /> <br /> This would make mental projections reasonable, which could use the normal rules. If you want the projection at the second attainment, though, I was thinking that the projection itself could bear any sympathy penalties on all actions, including sensory input, but qualify as fully present otherwise. If you have that Sensory link, no penalty exists.<br /> <br /> Just some notions. I like the rough shape of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've ever seen any of the hints dropped about Tamers of Blood then it's supposed to be Space primary. Of course, it's also a legacy that's been around a long time, I'm sure someone has mutated it. I did think about making the attainments a two way street, but if it was it would be too simple to throw off any suspicion of being Left-Handed. I may end up changing it to the link being pretty much permanent on either end though because I agree I don't want them bonding with just anyone. On the other hand, they can bond anyone, and then ignore or use the link at their discretion anyways, bothering to sever it at all is simply a good faith gesture. Thinking over what I've got there it definitely needs to be smoothed out. <br /> <br /> In fact, with the Space primary thing, it's tricky overall. The Legacy is noted for body control, but it can also be used to to mess with things like the Vinculum from Vampire. I decided to go the indirect route, the Tamer can keep tabs on the Bonded with the first attainment, with the second he can actually screw with the Vinculum sympathy (or any other) by assuming the connection himself and from there severing it or going vampire hunting (and after using the first attainment he probably knows who the vampire is), with the third attainment he doesn't even have to alert the vampire to his presence, he just pops inside of the Bonded's body and then nukes the vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T14:47:18-07:00","id":205355,"title":"","content":"(Well, I'm trying <b>not </b>to be argumentative, here, in case it seems that way.)<br /> <br /> I consider the brief descriptions as what mages <i>think</i> they know about any given legacy, and guidance as to themes, so I'm up for changing anything as long as the results would still seem fitting. If a legacy is known to create and manipulate Sympathy, the assumption it's a Space thing makes sense. (<i>Most</i> magi wouldn't have even heard this much, and deeper research could reveal, shucks, maybe it <i>isn't</i> Space, so I'm comfortable with such a shift.)<br /> <br /> Switching to Life as the channel that establishes the link instead of Space (in a manner vaguely similar to a Familiar, through blood ties) makes it the perfect <i>Conjunctional</i> arcanum. Making Mind Primary cleans things up fairly well. When I sketched it out, mostly following your outline, I used Life as both Optional and Conjunctional arcana, and declared that they can target their linked others as if targeting their own body, though with Sympathy penalties. Their control over their personal physiology, then, also represents manipulation of that of their linked bodies, as well. This grants access to more powerful effects through Life as a direct consequence, but doesn't make these the attainments themselves, which I like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just because a legacy is left-handed does not mean that the legacy is evil, intrinsically or otherwise. Going with powers that are clearly sinister is one approach, but not the only one.<br /> <br /> Imagine a pre-Free Council conflict between the Tamers of the Elements and Diamond cabals. Some of the Tamers of Blood might well apply their attainments to root out Guardian infiltrators and to assassinate Silver Ladder dignitaries. (not to mention, remove any particularly successful Adamantine Arrow generals or champions and extract any useful secrets from the Mysterium) That's a fantastic way to get yourself declared Left-Handed, even if <i>they started the fight</i>. It's also a great way to save your allies and friends.<br /> <br /> A Lichtor abruptly has a change of heart, and declares the mage war over. Investigation reveals his beloved <i>Sleeper</i> daughter explaining to him that the mage war will lead to ever more tragic deaths, so he needs to end it. Unsurprisingly, he dedicates himself to hunting down the Tamers of Blood. Was that maneuver clearly evil? It prevented loss of life.<br /> <br /> Of course if you have the <i>ability </i>to kill, you are probably going to attract those who <i>want to</i>.<br /> <br /> If this isn't an intrinsically nasty thing, one interesting line of thought is in how the various lineages either embrace, reject, or regulate the darker aspects of their legacy.<br /> As old as they are supposed to be, there could be martial, philosophical, peace-maker, and family building branches. The Tamers may well accept that the Left-Handed forms exist, possibly calling them the &quot;Tainted.&quot; (&quot;Bad Blood&quot; and &quot;Black Blood&quot; have a good ring to them, too.)<br /> <br /> <br /> As I implied, I like harvesting ideas. I was tossing you some to play with since you gave me some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":".  clarity, of course. 07-22-2014, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T15:48:12-07:00","id":205411,"title":"","content":"Nah, I appreciate the feedback. I don't think I'd want to change it from Space/Life mostly because it's an interesting challenge and I really like Space and feel it didn't get done enough justice in any of the books. Just for instance, the number of books which don't try to do anything new with Space at all is deplorable in my opinion. On top of that, I don't think too many people would disagree if I said Mind is basically one of the strongest arcana, and although I also really like Mind it gets its due in a lot of Legacies and spells already.<br /> <br /> I think the primary attainments I came up with are interesting and mechanically sound enough to leave them be for the most part. It's the Life stuff I'm having the most trouble with. I'm currently toying with the idea of expressing &quot;body control&quot; that the Tamers are known for as the ability to switch Physical Skill and Attribute dots around by draining them from a Bonded and adding them to the Tamer and also allowing for the reverse to happen so a Tamer could create a super-Bonded by moving his own Skills and Attributes into the vessel. That could be the first and second Optionals respectively. The third Optional I'm pretty happy with, but might be hard to justify from the way I think about the Legacy in general since I can't think of terribly many situations where a Mage would puppet his own body with magic. I also have an additional idea for allowing damage to be shared among the Bonded and the Tamer similar to the Rose of Eden legacy, but that might be kinda bland since that's less in theme with &quot;body control&quot; and Life can manage to accomplish a lot more interesting things.<br /> <br /> I believe it should be a double-edged sword. It's not inherently Left-Handed, but the way the Attainments have been developed should stand as the kind of thing that can do potentially great good and great harm. For instance, with the Space stuff I've got up there, the Tamer could be either spying on his Bonded pretty much whenever he feels like it, and interfering to manipulate and control them like the meat/blood puppets they are. It's also set up so that they can be highly aware of what's happening to these people who are supposed to be so important to them so that they can better protect them. So yeah, while I'm totally with you on the fact that perhaps some Mage was just a jerk and started prosecuting them as Left-Handed, I'm also of the mind that maybe that jerk of a Mage was -right-. I'm not going to outright answer the question myself, that's for individual players and STs to do, but that means that I should create a setup where it's possible that it could go either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T20:22:49-07:00","id":205576,"title":"","content":"Cool.<br /> Okay, well, I <i>do</i> agree that Mind is so versatile it has vast utility which has, yes, lead to a pretty grand focus on it in legacies and so forth. I <i>also</i> agree that Space has been a bit under represented in legacies, not so much by its absence as by its lack of breadth. Find me a Space legacy that doesn't do more than one of: Untouchable, Create Threads, Scry, Destroy Threads, Ward, Ban, Teleport. There probably are some, but, yeah, I feel ya.<br /> <br /> That said, I still have trouble seeing this as the best example for that.<br /> <br /> Still, within your stated preferences, lemme think:<br /> <br /> This detaches from your outline a lot, mind, but I'm spinning different stuff, here.<br /> <br /> Obviously, &quot;Body Control&quot; is a stretch with Space, but not with control of Blood. Life and Mind are the obvious, though you could argue a weird take on Space <i>could</i> maneuver an object.<br /> <br /> Life is critical to the attainments, since Blood <i>is</i> the medium.<br /> <br /> <b>Space 2, Life 1: 1st: </b>Perhaps make the tie to blood obviate the need for a name, entirely. Thataway, if you get some blood, you got 'em, having both an Intimate connection and not <i>needing</i> any name.<br /> That's creepy right there, without any separate blood tie mojo.<br /> Toss in the (possibly not even unique) ability to treat a blood relation <i>as</i> the individual's blood, albeit directionally, and it gets worse. That is, each step of descent is two levels weaker, while the connection to a parent is only one level weaker. brothers and Sisters lose three: One to parent and two to their child. This indirection should apply the name penalty if any stage is unknown..(Or any one whose blood you don't have on your person. Wording of all this matters.)<br /> First attainment could track this stuff and see all blood ties in play. Make this expressly <i>not</i> require the physical presence of such individuals to assess the links with Interconnections, and such relational magics. Possibly require direct sight of blood, however, at least until higher skill levels.<br /> <br /> That's an attainment worth having though it's essentially passive.<br /> <br /> <i>ed:</i> There is an idea: The blood connection improves the sympathy by one step, up to and including Sensory. This merely offsets the name penalty, but whoo, that's nasty. Sensory means you no longer need a scrying window and the extra arcana dot to affect the target. Yeah, <b>that</b> should be 2nd or third attainment stuff, I'm thinking, but I <i>like</i> it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2nd: </b>Bump the blood tie mojo to Space 3? Certainly allow this to create new ties, though I think it should require the physical <i>exchange </i>of blood. The result would be a new, and fully legitimate blood tie that counts as every bit as close as parent to child.<br /> Maybe allow severing of existing ones, but this would need to be difficult, since, well, destroying that shouldn't be easy. This might not even be the right level for that.<br /> <br /> Blood ties share weak emotions when the links are strong enough. The strongest emotions leak through. I was thinking of mapping the Emotional Urging effect chart to emotional intensity experienced by either side, subtracting the levels of separation from that, and having that, if any levels remain, be the result of an Emotional Urging effect felt through the link. It's convoluted, though, so I'd probably just make a unique chart that covered the topic in broad strokes.<br /> <br /> Now allow uses of self-only effects through a personal blood tie, though otherwise still bear the normal restrictions.<br /> <br /> Make the effective link a level closer for the maximum level of attainment in the legacy. That is, when learned, the mage treats all existing blood ties as closer by two levels. On the third, improve by three.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Life 3:</b> Alternately, the control of blood could be used to do a few things. The ability to manipulate blood could include the ability to staunch any wounds as an Instant, or even Reflexive on their own pattern, action. They could also trigger or halt healing that occurs through the blood as an Instant action... maybe Concentration. Instead of Healing Heart and instant healing, though, this could simply activate that double-time healing merit. Similarly, though, they could get the ability to strangle tissues, reducing blood flow. Allowing them to apply their Life to all their Physical attributes as a penalty distributed as close to evenly as possible. Uneven amounts can be placed as desired.<br /> (Life 3 simply applies a -1 to all three physical attributes. With Life 4, they must have -1 in each attribute but are free to select one physical attribute to be a -2. Life 5 would allow two attributes at -2 with one of only -1. )<br /> The beginning of the manipulative blood mojo. Still, Life 3 can't do puppetry on a human just yet.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd: Sever natural bonds:</b> A target can be plucked from their heritage and the bonds of blood severed. This should be a serious undertaking with significant results. Not certain what all they are, but one of them could include mystical inheritance no longer considering the person an heir. Of course, the ability to pull shenanigans with Vinculii and the blood ties would be very interesting.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Mind 4:</b> Psychic Projection makes the control of another's body not part of the attainment, but well within their grasp. Picture: A private projection perceives a particularly pernicious provocation. Unwilling to permit probability to prevail, he promptly prevails to penetrate his party's psyche. No penalty for sympathy assessed, and no prohibition on Posession appears, as the attainment merely permits presence with rather than powers the overwhelming of the other person.<br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe there's something in that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Edit: </i>alternate notions for an outline:<br /> <br /> <b>1st: Blood Flows Through Generations</b><br /> The Tamer of Blood knows that blood is the life that flows from generation to generation. The insight granted by this is the ability to identify family relationships through the blood. This blood must still contain some life, which means it fades in hours. This living blood is critical to the powers of the legacy. After this, it becomes &quot;faded blood&quot; which loses potency each day. For each day after the blood faded, the effective sympathy reduces by one.<br /> <br /> Among the benefits of this, scrutinizing the Identity of a subject whose blood is perceptible (that is, normally, outside the body) inside sensory range adds successes on the roll equal to dots of Life. If such scrutiny achieves 5 successes, the character understands the identity quite fully. Should they examine a member of the same family, they will recognize the similarities. If they achieve 5 successes on a relation, they will be able to tell how closely related they are and, through magical insight, can even tell whether the relation flows through a subject's father or mother.<br /> <br /> When using blood as an intimate connection to a person, the die pool gains a +1 Sympathy bonus. Furthermore, the character may use the blood as Known sympathetic connection to anyone directly related to the source by blood. (Children and parents of the blood's owner, but not adopted family)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Life 2</b><br /> The life in blood may be preserved in a sealed vessel which can be a body. In a living host, the blood will reduce in vitality every week instead of daily. In an nonliving sealed container, the reduction occurs every other day.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd:</b><br /> The Tamer of Blood can use samples of blood to alter the blood ties between them. The subject must spend a willpower point or reflexively will resist the effect. The resistances stack.<br /> <br /> This can be used to have dramatic results, such as changing the very bloodline of a child to match his new adoptive family. This alters genetics.<br /> This can be worked into a blood-brother ritual to make two individuals count as brothers permanently, even without a change to parentage.<br /> Breaking such a tie is far from trivial, but even this is possible. Even a true son can be torn from his family tree.<br /> These tend to require Exceptional Success. This is the power that can tear out a Vampiric Vinculum.<br /> <br /> Faded blood now gains a grace period equal to Life in days. This applies to hosted blood. (in days, still. The host is what is degrading it, there.)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Life 3</b><br /> Tamers of Blood know that the blood is the life of the flesh, and can direct that flesh where they will. The Tamer must touch the blood of the subject. Then they can exert a rudimentary control over the flow of blood in the body of that subject. The character may reduce Physical attributes if the character stills the blood or may reduce Composure, Wits, and Presence, In either case, the reduction is evenly divided among the three attributes with the Tamer selecting where things fall if uneven. A number of dots equal to the Life rating are subtracted from the listed, with 1 dot in each of the other list gaining a +1. (but only up to their natural limits and not improving restoring health or willpower) At Life 3, this is a net transfer, but for each dot above that, the penalty grows. In addition to the attribute effects, the time to bleed out is doubled when blood is stilled and halved when quickened. Healing rates are doubled when quickened and halved when stilled, as well. Finally, with quick blood comes a quick temper. The quick blooded become edgy and temperamental. The slow blooded become depressed. (In 2e, this should simply become two Conditions: 'Quickened Blood' and 'Stilled Blood')<br /> <br /> Obviously, a Tamer may use this on their own blood.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd:</b><br /> Space 4<br /> Tamers of the Blood can see the life of blood. If the blood is within the vital phase, the Tamer treats the sympathy as improved by two steps, after other factors, such as a name penalty, are considered. This can improve the effective link to Sensory. The connection to a direct relative through blood is now Intimate and Known applies to grandparents, siblings, and grandchildren.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Life 4</b><br /> A Tamer of Blood can empower blood with an act of will. For 1 willpower, the Tamer may enhance a subject's blood, allowing them to heal at an accelerated rate. The subject converts one wound by one step per dot of Life. Aggravated to Lethal, Lethal to Bashing, Bashing to healed. The first conversion is instantaneous, but each further healing appears once each round following, always repairing the worst. It bears noting that Resistant damage is irrelevent to this ability.<br /> <br /> This effect also directly opposes any magical blood-affecting effects, so a subject could be cured of Quickened Blood, Stilled Blood, poison, a spiritually imposed bleeding effect, Vampiric Spoiling, or pretty much anything else. The character may intentionally leave Quickened or Stilled Blood in place, as that can aid in fixing things. This does not automatically cure all the conditions it applies to, though. (Insert appropriate rules for this. If the malady is carried in the blood, this can conceivably cure it. That said, it shouldn't be easy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 08-29-2015, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:38:07-07:00","id":206220,"title":"","content":"I had this idea and wanted to get it down, I might revisit it and add the fluff.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Moirai</b></span><br /> <i><b>&quot;To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose&quot;</b></i></div> <br /> <b>Primary Arcanum: </b>Fate<br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Thrysus or Moros<br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Fatespinners, Lifestealers, Fates<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment: Clotho<br /> Requirements:</b> Gnosis 3, Fate 2<br /> Persistent Fortune's Protection (M:tA, page 152) and Synchronicity (TotM, page 60)<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Thrysus, Life 2 - Body Control (M:tA, page 182)<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Moros, Death 2 - Final Sight (GotV, page 186)<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment: Lachesis<br /> Requirements: </b>Gnosis 5, Fate 3<br /> Thrysus: Bestow Exceptional Luck (M:tA, page 157) or Sense Strength and Weakness (GoG, page 72)<br /> Moros: Lucky Coin and Monkey Paw (both M:tA, page 155)<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Thrysus, Life 3 - Body Mastery (Myst, page 195, and GoG, page 32)<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Moros, Death 3 - Decay (M:tA, page 136) and Destroy Object (M:tA, page 139)<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment: Atropos<br /> Requirements: </b>Gnosis 7, Fate 4<br /> Forge Destiny (M:tA, page 159)<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Life 4 or Death 4 - One of the most oft-whispered powers of The Moirai is the ability to wholesale grant years life to the elderly, or punish the young and foolish with old age. Similar to Steal Lifespan (M:tA, page 146) and Grant Lifespan (L:tA, page 35), each success on the activation roll moves one year of life from target to target. If the target is willing, i.e., has signed a contract or otherwise agreed upon a number, the activation roll and mana cost is obviated, and the transfer occurs over the course of a scene. If the target is unwilling, the Moirai's activation roll is contested by the target's Stamina (+ Supernatural Trait, if they have it), and costs one mana per attempt. Any successful transfer of years happens immediately, shockingly, and painfully, dealing one resistant lethal damage per year stolen. If this kills the target, only as many years as damage inflicted is transferred.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T09:54:24-07:00","id":206241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=205240#post205240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, well, yeah, with the Life primary, having them gain features akin to a kith would be interesting. Something that helps them actually navigate the realm would also be very useful. I do like the idea of Key for the second attainment optional.<br /> <br /> With Fate 4, Life 4, an effect to banish the tearing of the thorns for a number of scenes seems interesting. (Roughly analogous to an Amnion in Dreamtime)<br /> Alternately, and related, the attainment could grant them some ability to create paths and waypoints in the Hedge, though costing Willpower and Glamour. This could also grant a moment's respite, and would still require power expended.<br /> <br /> This would fit the more fae-like relationship with Fate that Mages have than the Changelings, and still require expenditures of power to remain in the Hedge. (I'd prefer that Mages who figure this out would do so in a manner that is different than that of Changelings.<br /> <br /> One thing that might serve is using Sympathy rules somehow, as part of the scheme. Magi who achieve a certain level of familiarity with a region of the hedge cease to be seriously harmed by it, and even come to navigate it simply, since that story becomes old hat, and newer challenges await. Not sure exactly how to run with that theme, just now, but I like it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The character that created the Legacy (as mentioned, it's being ICly developed) has the Homeward Bound merit and a few trinkets that allow him to make basic navigation rolls. For a more general legacy, I could definitely see something along the lines of creating waypoints with the attainments, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T14:07:33-07:00","id":206517,"title":"","content":"Okay, to be honest, I've not read a Changeling book in five years or so. Hence the lack of detail on those suggestions.<br /> <br /> Even with the ultimate GPS available, <i><b>I</b></i> would prefer to have a personal capacity to navigate without one, just in case. What happens if the guy loses the trinkets? That's a challenge he'd face if he ever gets the attention of one of the Fair in a game of mine, since it's an interesting thing to see, and, well, they can make it happen.<br /> <br /> A Legacy could <i>require</i> learning those merits, with attainments that enhance them into something spiffy. Forging paths through the Hedge would certainly qualify as &quot;interacting with the Hedge,&quot; so it was a suggestion of a specific sort to consider. A Fate/Life and possibly also Prime sort of deal where you can do some Hedgespinning could be nice. Oaths that allow more of the Changeling take could be interesting. (Of course, the Mage version was bland, so replacing that might oughtta just be a houserule.)<br /> Way I see it, Legacies are at least as much about enshrining various lessons learned into a cohesive package to pass on as they are about taking those lessons and making new powers out of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The shtick of a specific Kith is generally not so powerful that calling that the second attainment would break things, as far as I recall.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:40:43-07:00","id":206673,"title":"","content":"<b>Speed Kings:</b> Blazing around the city at speeds that would make a physics professor go on a rampage, this Mastigos legacy is comprised of drag racers, parkour runners, athletes, and anyone else who enjoys the rush of moving rapidly through the world. Few things are as exhilerating to them as feeling the wind rush through their hair as they race across roof tops, up the side of buildings, and leave motor vehicles in the dust! By taking up training in the Arcana of Forces, they are able to vastly improve their maneuverability by controlling such things like friction, wind resistance, kinetic energy, weight distribution, and so on. It is said that some Speed Kings are able to move so blindingly fast, the human eye becomes incapable of tracking their motion, providing an effect similar to that of a teleportation!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Girl Squad:</b> Cute, strong, and disturbingly erotic, this all female legacy of Obrimos are monster slayers who use their holy magic to hunt down and eliminate vampires, demons, evil mages, and the like. Their signature magic allows them to switch their clothing with magical battle armor and summon weapons to their aid, but comes with a rather embarrassing side effect. In between conjuring and dismissing their battle armor, they are temporarily naked as their clothing swaps out, exposing themselves to others who may be around. They have taken up additional training in Space Arcana, which is the source behind their ability to conjure and dismiss weapons and clothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T01:29:49-07:00","id":206824,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm learning Ruby on Rails, and chose as a learning project a website to create legacies and collect variations. (It's actually a very nice level of complexity, pedagogically.) The placeholders I put up a couple days ago: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Sparkle Warriors</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">This is a happy little legacy that focuses on rainbows, glitter, and unicorns. As a result, most people cannot stand them. The Free Council is divided on whether they serve the Lie or are a force opposed. Time will tell.</td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Hot Foot</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">By focusing their mystical art on their feet, they learn to move at ludicrous speeds. Forces primary, they also add in Time and Space to their manipulations. A very odd group, who are hard to beat in a race, that's for sure. fun.</td> </tr> </table></div> I find this pretty funny.<br /> <br /> (Yes, obviously, it was making placeholder attainments for them that lead to my goofy nonsense above.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:45:23-07:00","id":208149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=206517#post206517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, to be honest, I've not read a Changeling book in five years or so. Hence the lack of detail on those suggestions.<br /> <br /> Even with the ultimate GPS available, <i><b>I</b></i> would prefer to have a personal capacity to navigate without one, just in case. What happens if the guy loses the trinkets? That's a challenge he'd face if he ever gets the attention of one of the Fair in a game of mine, since it's an interesting thing to see, and, well, they can make it happen.<br /> <br /> A Legacy could <i>require</i> learning those merits, with attainments that enhance them into something spiffy. Forging paths through the Hedge would certainly qualify as &quot;interacting with the Hedge,&quot; so it was a suggestion of a specific sort to consider. A Fate/Life and possibly also Prime sort of deal where you can do some Hedgespinning could be nice. Oaths that allow more of the Changeling take could be interesting. (Of course, the Mage version was bland, so replacing that might oughtta just be a houserule.)<br /> Way I see it, Legacies are at least as much about enshrining various lessons learned into a cohesive package to pass on as they are about taking those lessons and making new powers out of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The shtick of a specific Kith is generally not so powerful that calling that the second attainment would break things, as far as I recall.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Homeward bound is in Grimoire of Grimoires, it's essentially his 'last ditch'. What it does is this: no matter what realm you're in, it points you home. Not necessarily a safe way, but a short and direct way that will work. Still, if he does get the third attainment, it might be worth enhancing it a bit further in the way you suggested.<br /> <br /> As for hedgespinning, my ST glared at me when I suggested that. I need to up my prime if I want to make magical items, heh. Or ask a Changeling nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T06:16:33-07:00","id":208213,"title":"","content":"I've got a few Legacy ideas, but I've never really liked the way that Legacies worked, mechanically. I don't like Vampire, but the way that Bloodlines work in fluff and mechanics is just so perfect to me. I've been getting ideas for Legacies, but haven't really done anything with them. I'm sort of waiting for more info on how they'll work in FWC. I have an idea for a Legacy that's essentially Magical Girls, because grimdark WoD magical girls is a fun concept to me. I also had a Legacy I was tempted to create way way back when I was actually getting to play Mage that was a Moros Legacy that focused on shadowsculpting and Spirits. If I recall (I lost my notes years ago) they had speaking with ghosts/spirits as an Attainment, then they could use Shadow Sculpting as their second Attainment, and give ghosts or Spirits bodies of shadow for a scene.<br /> They were basically born of my desire to play a Moros with Spirit. Because I want to deal with ghosts AND spirits... without being a Thrysus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:40:11-07:00","id":208298,"title":"","content":"<b>Viewers of Chaos:</b> The most miniscule act can have dramatic, far reaching consequences. That is the essence of the Chaos Theory, and it is the philosophy that the Viewers of Chaos follow. An Acanthus Legacy, they use their powers to view the fates of others and take note of how changing even the tiniest little incident can drastically alter the course of events that unfold. Contrary to what you might believe, the Legacy is not inherently evil, they are simply curious to see how their actions affect the world around them. Sometimes these changes are beneficial, and sometimes they are disastrous. For the Viewers of Chaos, the joy of their craft lies in watching the events unfold, not about their eventual outcome. The Viewers of Chaos have begun to study the Arcana of Space, which allows them to alter their environment from a distance, as well as plant and remove objects and people from the locations they wish to manipulate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bayou Brujah:</b> From taming alligators, to turning people into frogs, the Bayou Brujah (otherwise known as Swamp Witches) are a Thyrsus Legacy who choose to live in the marshes, swamps, bogs, and bayous, defending the murky waters and overgrown foliage from all those who would bring them harm. As a society of swamp based Shaman, the Bayou Brujah have a strong connection to voodoo rites and practices including the forging of cursed dolls and other less familiar activities. In addition to their standard Arcana of Life and Spirits, they have also begun to study Death, giving them such terrifying abilities as reanimating zombies from those who meet their gruesome end among the swamps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T06:24:09-07:00","id":212387,"title":"","content":"Writeup of the Disciples of Rathma<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Disciples of Rathma</span></b></span></span></b> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Death is not the end. Death can never be the end.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Death is the road. Life is the traveller. The soul is the guide.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">- Sri Chinmoy</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Most consider Life and Death to be eternal enemies. Mutually exclusive states of being. Forces in fundamental opposition to one another. Enlightened in equal measure by sleeper science and certain sleeper cultures, the Disciples of Rathma know that this is wrong. Where others see conflict, the Disciples see symbiosis. Two forces codependent on each other and driving each other forward. Life begets death, Death begets Life. Without this unending circle there would be no progress, only stasis and entropic decay.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Disciples of Rathma as a Legacy arose not long before the Nameless War It was born amidst new scientific findings in biology at the beginning of the 20th century and certain sleeper cultures\u2019 view of life and death as being so intimately entwined as to basically being the same. With each generation that passes species improve themselves molded by the forces of natural selection and necessity. Life overcomes, life adapts, but only through the fires of death that get rid of the old can this evolution take place. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So the Disciples ask: what if you could turn yourself into a furnace of evolution? Make yourself able to evolve, without needing to die. Control death and life such that small parts of your being continuously die and are reborn, improved and adapted. </span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Disciples of Rathma seek to understand and master the balance of life and death. Once true mastery is achieved, it is said, a Disciple will be able to enter a spiral of Selfevolution. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">To reach this point, a Disciple of Rathma starts by becoming truly aware of the cycle of life and death around them. Once they are aware, they adapt their body using this knowledge, reaching a balance between true death and being alive, becoming able to evolve themselves </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The unique viewpoint on the relationship between the Life and Death Arcana means both Thyrsus and Moros often find themselves attracted to the Legacy. The different viewpoints both Paths provide to the Legacy can lead to conflict, but in a typical Free Council approach this is seen as more of a chance than a problem. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Disciple of Rathma\u2019s founder was Rising Sun, a member of the cabal of the Black Mast, one of the original founding cabals of the Free Council. Originally from Zanzibar, the Black Mast eschewed the traditional form of Sanctum. Instead they lived on a Dhow that travelled the trade route that goes from India, along the coast of East Africa, down to Tanga. Rising Sun had always been curious and inquiring, and the cabal\u2019s travels provided her with access to all manner of cultures and lore. Interested in both religions and science, Rising Sun happily merged sleeper beliefs about the nature of life and death with Darwin\u2019s theory of evolution to create the Disciples of Rathma legacy. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Theme</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Science and Discovery between Life and Death</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Parent Path or Order:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Moros or Thyrsus, Free Council</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Nickname:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Boneseers, Corpsewalkers, Seeders (new, first used around the turn of the millenium)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Appearance:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Many Disciples of Rathma emulate dress and style of sleeper groups focused on the life/death duality and the erosion of the borders between them. Many like to dress like stereotypical Necromancers or take after the looks of spirits and gods of life and death found in sleeper cultures. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Background:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The Disciples of Rathma draw members that are inquisitive, willing to question established knowledge and often have equal interest in science and the occult. Experimenting with one's own body, improving oneself and broadening what it means to be human is a central part of the Legacy, and members are often extraordinarily driven and adventurous individuals. Many have a background in medicine or biology coupled with an interest in the occult.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Organization:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> There are normally two teachers per student, one Thyrsus and one Moros, though the legacy\u2019s low numbers mean one is often only marginally involved and might live far away. Also, there is often a visible rift between the Thyrsus and the Moros that make up the Legacy, but as the unity of Life and Death is one of the core beliefs of the Legacy\u2019s members there are also many that actively try to foster working together. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Suggested Oblations:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Ritual Trance induced by careful use of dangerous poisons, activities with the aim of improving oneself (training, learning something new, etc), helping with a birth or death and watching the process with the first attainment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Concepts:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Researcher into matters of Life and Death, travelling Medicine Man or Wise Houngan/Mambo, explorer of the Underworld, researcher of the Undead, mad scientist experimenting on themself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Attainments:</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Similar to the Celestial Masters\u2019 relationship with Forces &amp; Matter, both Life and Death can be the Legacy\u2019s Primary Arcanum, depending on the Willworker\u2019s Path. Moros tread Life as the Primary Arcanum, Thyrsus Death.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>1st: The Struggle for Life</i></span><br /> Prerequisites:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Gnosis 3, Death 2, Life 2, Occult 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The first lesson a Disciple learns is open their perceptions, to feel Life and Death in all their forms interacting around them, permeating their surroundings. This attainment provides the a Disciple with an always on version of the Life 1 Spell Sense Life, but the Disciple can also feel the Undead (including Ghosts in Twilight) and any corpse that has been dead for less than the Disciple\u2019s Life Arcanum in days. If successes are required to notice someone, treat the Disciple as having rolled their Life Arcanum in successes. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Additionally, the Disciple can activate Speak with the Dead towards any Ghosts that enter the Spell\u2019s Safety Radius as an instant action.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>2nd: Experiments on Human Hybridization</i></span><br /> Prerequisites: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Gnosis 5, Death 3, Life 3, Athletics or Medicine 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">After adapting their perceptions, the second step for a Disciple of Rathma is to accept the unity of Life and Death as a part of them. By understanding how their body carries both, the Disciple of Rathma is able to integrate them more fully within themselves. They balance the two forces\u2019 power over their pattern, becoming neither fully dead or alive. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This Attainment replicates the spell Corpse Flesh. The dicepool to activate the attainment is Medicine + Stamina + Death. At Death 4 Life 4 the attainment no longer has a set maximum duration. The Disciple of Rathma basically always decides themselves if they want to to be under the Attainments effects.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>3rd: The Origin of Species</i></span><br /> Prerequisites: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Gnosis 7, Life 4, Death 4, Medicine 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">At this point, the Disciple of Rathma becomes able to actively evolve themselves, easily adapting to changing circumstances.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This attainment allows the user to change themselves, as with the spells Transform Self and Two Faces, but the mage never needs to roll to get features right. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Activating this attainment is an extended action that takes 10 minutes. The Mage gains one feature per activation and cannot have more activations than the lower of their Life and Death running at the same time. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If the second attainment is active when the third is used, the list of possible features extends beyond just normal biologically possible features to a few specific ones related to Death and the Undead. The exact extend of possible changes using this is not yet known, as Disciples are still discovering new ones. Known ones are the ability to draw sustenance from eating ectoplasm, do photosynthesis in the unnatural light of the Underworld or smell ghostly Anchors.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 07-30-2014, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:36:16-07:00","id":212873,"title":"","content":"Just thought of a Legacy who uses their magic to facilitate a form of reincarnation. Haven't written anything, the idea just came to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T21:30:23-07:00","id":213140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=212387#post212387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>3rd: The Origin of Species</i></span><br /> Prerequisites: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Gnosis 7, Life 4, Death 4, Medicine 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">At this point, the Disciple of Rathma becomes able to actively evolve themselves, easily adapting to changing circumstances.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This attainment allows the user to change themselves, as with the spells Transform Self and Two Faces, but the mage never needs to roll to get features right. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Activating this attainment is an extended action that takes 10 minutes. The Mage gains one feature per activation and cannot have more activations than the lower of their Life and Death running at the same time. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If the second attainment is active when the third is used, the list of possible features extends beyond just normal biologically possible features to ones related to Death and the Undead. The Mage might for example grant themselves the ability to draw sustenance from eating ectoplasm, do photosynthesis in the unnatural light of the Underworld, or smell ghostly Anchors.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Works pretty well up to this third guy. I like the idea of adding ghostly additions to the feature set. That's pretty clever, but it isn't very firmly described, and could use some narrowing down. This is already a very nice and flexible attainment before you toss in the undead features, so it doesn't need further breadth for power level. (Just theme) I suggest coming up with one or so &quot;undead feature&quot; that is an activated ability, like Devouring the Slain or something, that can be added as a feature when undead. Alternately, a short list of features that can be added but without further options could work.<br /> <br /> I like the idea, but it's overly vague. It <i>could </i>be interpreted as anything up to and including the ability to drink blood for Vitae and physical Disciplines. Not what you meant, I'm sure, but a way of interpreting &quot;related to Death and Undead&quot; none the less.<br /> <br /> (You ever play Heroes of Might and Magic 4, perchance?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 07-30-2014, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T01:38:30-07:00","id":213281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=213140#post213140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Works pretty well up to this third guy. I like the idea of adding ghostly additions to the feature set. That's pretty clever, but it isn't very firmly described, and could use some narrowing down. This is already a very nice and flexible attainment before you toss in the undead features, so it doesn't need further breadth for power level. (Just theme)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the comments!<br /> When I originally made the Legacy it was for a game that I don't expect to ever get to Gnosis 7, so that last attainment was just made as a tool for my ST to give his NPCs some cool and unique tricks. It seems that I missed this one when reworking the Legacy for public consumption and use by PCs. I'll try to rebalance that.<br /> It shouldn't allow you to do anything with vitae and a specific list of possible mutations might be the best way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (You ever play Heroes of Might and Magic 4, perchance?) </div> </div> </div>loooong time ago, honestly don't remember much.<br /> <br /> Edit: Rewrote it a bit, is that better? I can't think of any other cool and thematic features at the moment, so it's just those three for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 07-30-2014, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T14:07:18-07:00","id":213956,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that description does a good job of framing the power levels. Much improved.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't like the mechanics of most of these, but they seem a place to start for some more ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>Spectral claws</b> (+2L) that affect both material and twilight.<br /> <b>Stillness of the Grave:</b> The character with this trait can double the time he needs between breaths by activating undead metabolism in areas that are inactive. This removes any penalty due to personal shaking or instability while the character holds his breath. This grants a bonus of +2 to resistance traits that attack such susceptibilities, such as choke holds.<br /> <b>Rigourous Grasp:</b> The character gains the ability to lock their grip without needing to expend energy to maintain it. This improves effective Strength and Stamina by 1 for purposes of maintaining a hold or pin. (Technically, this could be done with just Life, since Mollusks do this.)<br /> <b>Ablation:</b> Some superficial skin can rot, providing the character the ability to slip free of bonds and holds much easier. The ability itself causes no harm, but <i>using</i> it causes a Bashing level unless an Exceptional Success is achieved on the escape.<br /> <b>Driven:</b> Will or magic drives an undead creature beyond natural limits. This feature taps that to drive the body beyond its normal limits. Gain a health level that lasts until the undead state is removed. This power allows one health level of damage to be healed as if Bashing,regardless of actual severity. This can only be used once per scene and once per activation of the Dead Flesh. While this feature is active, the character also reduces wound penalties by 2.<br /> <b>Ear of the Tomb:</b> The character has the ability to challenge ghostly concealment effects with his basic senses. Success on perception must exceed the concealment. If the character has another roll that can penetrate the effect, roll that with the 8,9,10-Again qualities, rather than rolling twice. <br /> <b>Quiet Mind:</b> The character can voluntarily dampen his mind as an Instant mental action. The result is the same mind as a Quicken Dead spell creates. The character may issue a single event or time-limit that restores consciousness, or their mind returns at the end of the attainment. While invoking, the character sets up actions per commands to a revenant (&quot;Zombie&quot; see the spell M:TA pp140-1) or simply be still. In this suppressed condition, their mind is dead, and cannot be targeted. Act committed in the dead state are easier to rationalize, granting a bonus die on degeneration checks.<br /> If so desired, this can also be activated when meditating, in which case the character's mind can, in fact, be targeted per standard rules, just not through their body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> HOMM4 had an expansion character who was Gauldoth the Half Dead... a Life/Death caster... it just reminded me of this, vaguely. That guy's combat shtick was Summoning. He had an undead arm he could use to manipulate ghostly or material things that would kill the living... that sort of thing. The fluff side was actually more fitting than the in-game aspects. (Just idle curiosity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T14:10:17-07:00","id":213957,"title":"","content":"It's not that far stretched though, Katsunim Tsuukya from Summoners has a Third Attainment which is basically, &quot;Gain any numina you can justify your totem spirit having.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T17:11:09-07:00","id":265820,"title":"","content":"<b>Order of the Vibrant Soul:</b> This legacy of the Mastigos focuses on internal power. By combining magical talent with their emotional spectrum, they can improve the effectiveness of their spells, and over time they learn to harness the emotions of others to even greater effect! They have begun to study the Arcana of Prime, learning to harness magic in its purest form.<br /> <br /> <br /> Attainment 1 - <b>Strength from Within:</b><br /> Requirements: Gnosis 3, Mind 2, Prime 2<br /> <br /> The Mage is able to harness their own emotional state to enhance the power of their spells. If the Mage is feeling an emotion that would normally be attributed to the effect the spell is intended to produce, they gain a +2 when casting it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Attainment 2 - <b>The Bonds we Share:</b><br /> Requirements: Gnosis 5, Mind 4, Prime 3<br /> <br /> The Mage no longer has to fight his battles alone. With this attainment, he can now draw upon the combined emotions of those around him. However, they must all share the same emotion as the one he is attempting to invoke for the spell, and their participation must be willing, meaning he can't draw power from an enemy. Every person who lends their strength to the spell provides an additional +1 on attempts to cast it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Attainment 3 - <b>Hopes of Those Who Came Before:</b><br /> Gnosis 7, Mind 4, Prime 4<br /> <br /> Upon reaching this attainment, the mage no longer requires living beings to supply the emotional power for their magic. They can now harness the emotional resonance that lingers in places strong with it's connection. The site of a great war may hold strong hatred, fear or sorrow. A whore house may hold great pain, lust, or regret. A child's playground may hold joy, freedom, or whimsy. All of these being just some possibilities. When casting a spell that draws upon an emotion that the area might possess, the mage is able to gain <i>up to a total </i>of +1 to casting equal to the location's size.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately because the area is not actually a living being, it can not replenish the emotions that linger there on its own. For each + the mage draws upon, the emotional power for the area is depleted by an equal amount in size. When the emotional resonance reaches 0, the location is dried up and the mage can not harness it again for quite a while. The emotional energy is replenished at a rate of 1 size each year (though not exceeding the locations size) if the location continues to see regular use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>The following is a list of examples for possible combinations, but is by no means a complete list.</i><br /> <br /> Offensive - Anger, Pain, Love (for another), Despair<br /> <br /> Defensive - Fear, Love, Pride, Mercy<br /> <br /> Transportation - Joy, Free Spirited, Impatient, Terror<br /> <br /> Transformation - Rejection, Uncertainty, Whimsy, Disgust<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T15:34:20-07:00","id":268579,"title":"","content":"<b>The Celestial Covenant</b><br /> This Legacy was created by a Mormon Obrimos in order to reconcile his religion's teachings on marriage and the family with the demands of Magehood. Members of the Covenant can marry Sleepers and have children with much less difficulty than other Mages, and the Legacy is popular with Mormons, Evangelical Christians, Orthodox Jews, and members of other religions that place a strong emphasis on marriage and reproduction. Merely spending time with one's nuclear family counts as an oblation, and your family can learn your Shadow Name and even witness vulgar magic without ill effects. One drawback is that one's life cannot be extended past a century. The highest Attainment of the Legacy ensures that in the event of a Mage's death, one of his children will Awaken.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T20:53:44-07:00","id":268740,"title":"","content":"<b>The Hands of Atlas</b><br /> <br /> <i>When I raise up this stone, sister, I raise up my soul.</i><br /> <br /> This legacy was founded by an illiterate Libertine Ecstatic in the early 20th century, who worked as a pig-iron hauler at a steel mill before his Awakening. Unable to participate in the more intellectual discussions of his peers, he decided to develop a mystical practice doing the only thing he had ever really excelled at: picking heavy things up and putting them down. Though mocked at first, his contemporaries began to find themselves in awe of how he ritually transformed this simple labor into a reflection of Supernal power's capacity to transform reality. One day, as he set down the last load of his shift, he turned to find a seasoned Adamant Arrow warrior bowing humbly before him, asking to be taught. And so the Legacy began its dissemination to the present day.<br /> <br /> Parent Path/Order: Thyrsus Libertine or Arrow<br /> <br /> Nickname: Lifters<br /> <br /> Appearance: The Hands of Atlas are generally quite muscular, and tend to have rather calloused hands. They prefer sturdy boots and clothing that shields their skin from the sun while not constricting movement.<br /> <br /> Background: Many Lifters are blue-collar workers or body-builders, but some are mages who have spent a considerable portion of their careers doing what they perceive to be un-fulfilling office work, and who look to embrace a lifestyle where the product of one's efforts is considerably more visceral.<br /> <br /> Initiation: An apprentice must spend an entire week working from sun-up to sun-down, hauling heavy objects or doing some other physically strenuous activity, and stopping only when their mentor signals them for momentary rests, water breaks, or meals.<br /> <br /> Organization: Lifters tend to form gangs who rally whenever a project appears that requires the efforts of more than one of them. Other than the customary deference of apprentice to master, Lifters view one another as equals, and while jests are often made amongst each other accusing one member or another of laziness, they are loathe to comment on one another's relative competence to outsiders, asserting that each does &quot;the best she can.&quot;<br /> <br /> Theory: Lifters believe that as they move things where they need to go, and pick up the stones that have been torn down, they slowly bring order to the Universe, and more perfectly align the Fallen and Supernal. When something is carried, it is transformed from its inert state- it gains potential energy, and its relationship with the rest of the world can be redefined to something more ideal.<br /> <br /> Oblations: Helping someone move, lifting weights, working as a day-laborer, carrying a cabal-mate an extended distance<br /> <br /> Yantras: Holding the subject over one's head provided it weighs at least as much as a backpack full of books +1 or +3 if the spell lasts only as long as the subject is lifted and the subject weighs at least as much as the caster, stacking stones or other heavy objects +2.<br /> <br /> Attainments: (Primary Arcanum: Forces) A newly initiated Lifter can tell how heavy something is at a glance, and where its center of gravity is with a touch. A student can reduce an object's weight as long as they are bearing it themselves. A master can lift things and move them with the slightest touch, levitating objects even if they themselves are not standing on the ground. (Secondary Arcanum: Life) A newly initiated Hand of Atlas can increase their own endurance; a student can heal themselves and others of injuries gained through physical labor, and a master can heal at an accelerated rate simply by getting back to work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T03:28:06-07:00","id":268903,"title":"","content":"The Hands of Atlas seem quite interesting, Ghost Turtle. I like their concept a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:31:29-07:00","id":269305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=268903#post268903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hands of Atlas seem quite interesting, Ghost Turtle. I like their concept a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! When I've tried to design legacies in the past, I usually started with their philosophy and then attempted to extrapolate practices. With the Hands of Atlas I did the reverse: I started with the activities the mage would undergo in search of Supernal Truth (picking things up and putting them down), and then tried to consider what sort of world-view would develop from doing that a lot, studying it closely, and contemplating its symbolic significance. This also made thinking about Attainments a lot easier, since you just pick things that facilitate what the mage was doing already.<br /> <br /> Initiation and Oblations ended up becoming key to thinking about the Legacy, because the former is what you do to start being a member, and the latter is what you continuously do as a member. For whatever reason I used to think of oblations as sort of in-theme side-quests that give you an optional reward for playing up your Legacy, but any Legacy member worth her salt (or at least the founder, whose stamp will be on the legacy forever) is going to be doing them as often as possible- they will be a key part of her magical lifestyle.<br /> <br /> I also just loved thinking up a legacy that was about becoming a transcendent mystical paragon by way of &quot;unskilled&quot; labor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","user":"GhostTurtle","date":". 09-30-2014, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T14:23:48-07:00","id":269501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also just loved thinking up a legacy that was about becoming a transcendent mystical paragon by way of &quot;unskilled&quot; labor. </div> </div> </div>Exactly, mage is filled to the brim with very cerebral Legacies and those that focus on the physical are usually some sort of mystic martial artists or uber gnostics that reject the flesh. Yours is unique and really stood out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T13:10:07-08:00","id":314784,"title":"","content":"<b>Cosmic Cultists:</b> A left handed legacy of Mastigos who adhere to the philosophy of Cosmic Indifference. Using their magic to consort with beings from across the stars, they study and refine Cosmicism in the hopes of transcending beyond the limitations of human comprehension. Most, unfortunately, are driven mad by their research, and they have practically no regard for human life when it comes to advancing their knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:31:37-08:00","id":423310,"title":"","content":"Hey, it's been a while since someone posted something here. I think it's still okay to post stuff here instead of making a new thread. If not, I apologize.<br /> <br /> THE AVERAGE ONES: Not so much a group of Legacies as a theme. These Legacies all are linked to a single Path, and their Ruling Arcana is that Path's Inferior. The group as a whole is made through focusing the Arcana through that Path's themes. I've only made two of five, so any suggestions might be useful.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Scions of Hades <br /> (Obrimos, Death)- Those who walk the path of the mighty believe in Order. Unfortunatly, death can be quite messy. These Obrimos seek to rectify this, becoming Kings and Queens of death like the chthonic deity from which they draw their name, bring reward and punishment as they desire.<br /> \u2022???<br /> (Mastigos, Matter)<br /> \u2022??? <br /> (Moros, Spirit)<br /> \u2022Dream Breeders<br /> (Thrysus, Mind)- This legacy seeks to understand the Astral as an ecology, studying Astral Entities in their natural environment, and even creating them whole-cloth at the highest levels.<br /> \u2022???<br /> (Acanthus, Forces)<br /> <br /> MISCELLANEOUS LEGACIES<br /> <br /> \u2022Neptune's Scions(???, Forces): Created as a contrast to the Tamers of Rivers, they focus on the Sea, an aggressive, capricious force that can give and take life with equal ease. Their Attainments should focus on making them better at sailing, aquatic navigating, <br /> and generally living around the oceans they so revere. <br /> \u2022Children of the New Dawn(Any, Prime with Mind Optional): A very rare and niche Legacy, they are open to all Paths and Orders, but only recruit Redeemed Awakened Prometheans. Their Attainments allow them to mimic some of the traits they once bore without the crippling downsides of being one of the Created. For example, one of their Attainments would allow them to flare a fake Azorothic Radiance, making them able to detect and be detected by the Created, as well as notice the &quot;burns&quot; which mark a body that once bore the Divine Fire(that is, the Redeemed). The optional Attainments primarily focus on resisting(or, more sinisterly, inflicting something like) Disquiet. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Shepherds of the Living Soul(Moros/Silver Ladder, Mind): Founded by a Silver Ladder monk, this group seeks to protect others by identifying and healing the mental and emotional problems of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Goofed on the name 02-28-2015, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:56:00-08:00","id":423334,"title":"","content":"The word &quot;Annunaki&quot; is already used for some major abyssal entities, do you ignore it or it was voluntary ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:22:46-08:00","id":423367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=423334#post423334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word &quot;Annunaki&quot; is already used for some major abyssal entities, do you ignore it or it was voluntary ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Er, didn't know about it. I chose the name because they were gods that judged dead souls in Babylonian myth. Any suggestions for a less... &quot;Charged&quot; name?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking of which, do you have any thoughts for the Moros, Mastigos, or Acanthus Legacies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:05:58-08:00","id":423481,"title":"","content":"Maybe another gods who are similar ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:35:41-08:00","id":423497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=423367#post423367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Er, didn't know about it. I chose the name because they were gods that judged dead souls in Babylonian myth. Any suggestions for a less... &quot;Charged&quot; name?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking of which, do you have any thoughts for the Moros, Mastigos, or Acanthus Legacies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe make them &quot;The Heirs of Hades&quot;*? Or &quot;Scions of Anubis*&quot;? Both gods had a role in judgement of the dead, had a structured system and were considered the kings of their realm.<br /> <br /> *Before Osiris supplanted him. But I avoided Osiris due to the whole Promethean angle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 02-28-2015, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:41:16-08:00","id":423501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=423497#post423497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make them &amp;quot;The Heirs of Hades&amp;quot;*? Or &amp;quot;Scions of Anubis*&amp;quot;? Both gods had a role in judgement of the dead, had a structured system and were considered the kings of their realm.<br /> <br /> *Before Osiris supplanted him. But I avoided Osiris due to the whole Promethean angle</div> </div> </div> </div>Those work. I'll go edit it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T17:16:55-08:00","id":423578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=161412#post161412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Pit Baiters</b>: These are Fate workers who attempt to curse the Abyss, tying it up in Supernal Mandates and driving it back. If the Supernal defines 'What Is' then the Loom of Fate defines the patterns of everything. Paradox is where 'What Cannot Be' is getting tangled up in the Loom. Baiter attempt to fix that by cursing the darkness--thus binding it. Paradox rolls are manipulated as these magi try to weave them out of the world. Fate primary. Considered reckless, at best, but they do have their successes. For now, they are not deemed Left Handed.</div> </div> </div> </div>More Please!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5202-hotchepsoot","name":"HotChepSoot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:40:09-07:00","id":437700,"title":"","content":"If I were to post a full writeup instead of just a short description, could I get some constructive criticisms? Would that be permissible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5305-theravis","name":"Theravis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:28:25-07:00","id":437743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theravis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=437700#post437700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to post a full writeup instead of just a short description, could I get some constructive criticisms? Would that be permissible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do it, dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T22:16:55-07:00","id":438046,"title":"","content":"The Black Avengers: A left handed Moros legacy, these angsty mages usually face their Awakening during a young age. Recruited from the ranks of goths, emos, punks, and others who are looked down upon by society, they typically have a bleak outlook on life, if not outright disdain for it. Recognizing the inevitability of death, they have no regard for the lives of others, unless those lives are important to them in some way. Taking pleasure in the suffering of those who have wronged them, their unique form of magic focuses on the use of curses, inflicting lasting torment upon their victims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:42:09-07:00","id":438814,"title":"","content":"This has been bouncing around in my head for at least a year now, so I figured I'd try to write it up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keepers of the Sacred Frequency</b> (Left-Handed, Obrimos, Free Council)</span><br /> <br /> Extra Arcanum: Mind</span><br /> <br /> Energy is what really makes up the universe; all matter is merely condensed energy. Mages are aware of many forms of energy that Sleepers have yet to discover, from the upwellings of Supernal power at Hallows to the more mundane but equally scientifically inexplicable patterns of Ley Lines that cross the globe. The Free Council wonders if the laws of physics in the Fallen World apply in some form to supernatural forces as well as natural ones; is the ephemera of the Shadow merely a more rarefied form of energy than what's found across the Gauntlet? Is there any truth to the metaphor of the Supernal Realms being &quot;above&quot; the Fallen, and is there a &quot;gravity&quot; that draws magic down from above?<br /> The answer to these questions, actually, is no: Physics may have one set of things to say about the connection between Matter and Forces, but the Supernal World's laws say different things entirely. The Supernal is not &quot;above&quot; the Fallen because &quot;direction&quot; in the Supernal world is conceptual at best, and may not truly exist outside of Pandemonium, the realm which includes Supernal definitions of all spatial relationships.<br /> A Seattle Obrimos who used to call herself Ceres found all this out the hard way in the 1990's. A professor of conventional physics before Awakening, she joined the Free Council and set out to prove indisputably that the laws of science explored by Sleeping truthseekers mirrored the governing principles of the Supernal world. Ceres studied for four years, making constant bold claims to local mages that she was approaching &quot;an understanding of the true laws of nature undreamt-of by the generations of magi who chased after the scraps of Atlantis,&quot; while showing little to no hard progress on proving her theories. The local Council was impressed by it, even appointing her emissary to the Consilium. Everyone else thought it was a crock of shit, and they turned out to be right. Frustrated by her lack of progress, Ceres sought out ancient lore of the sort she would've theatrically turned her nose up at in public, and reached back to the Aether, calling an Angel to the Fallen World to answer her questions. Well, she didn't like the answers she got. The Cherub of the Golden Key was compassionate; it explained as plainly as it could that her quest was futile; the laws of the Fallen were <i>not </i>the laws of the Supernal, and never had been. The Cherub told Ceres that her ego had backed her into a corner with the rest of the Consilium; it said it understood that after her decades of studying the laws of the world, Awakening and recognizing her own ignorance had frightened her, and it expressed sympathy for the suffering and sleepless nights she had put herself through trying to prove a theory that simply was not correct. It extended a hand past the borders of the summoning circle, and offered Ceres another glimpse of true knowledge, if she would take it.<br /> And Ceres grabbed the angel by the forearm, took her athame in hand, and slit the Angel's wrist.<br /> As divine fire poured from the wound, Ceres held the shocked and dying Cherub fast. This goddamn thing wasn't an <i>angel, </i>angels <i>helped </i>people! Telling her to give up was not <i>helping! </i>This being was a messenger of false prophecy, and if she had really called it down from the Aether, then the gods of the Aether were liars and frauds. She survived the outpouring of cosmic energy that came with the death of the Angel, and waited patiently at her summoning circle, leaving her conduit to the Supernal open until she felt something from the Abyss writhe its way in. Even then, she needed to call on the power of Forces to communicate with the thing, which took the form of a radio signal emitting from the point in the air where the &quot;false&quot; angel had appeared. It identified itself as the Sacred Frequency. It said it was drawn by Ceres' strong will and the &quot;courage&quot; she showed in taking the life of one who dared to deny her truth, and this, in its way, was true. It said it could show her the truth she was looking for, if she would prove it in the mortal world as an agent of the Sacred Frequency. Ceres accepted the bargain and in an instant, her mind and soul were no longer her own. The Sacred Frequency blended radio waves and her brain waves, letting her access both the signals of a station broadcasting nearby and the thoughts of everyone tuned into it. She saw visions of a great structure somewhere between a cathedral and a radio control tower, and masses of people, tuned into its signal, walking through its great doors, to...what? To unity. To add their signals to the Sacred Frequency, and to transcend. Taking a new shadow name (&quot;AM,&quot; both for the radio frequency band and for the &quot;new dawn&quot; she believes she will bring to mankind), Ceres fled her Consilium and set off in search of broadcasting enthusiasts. These days, she appears to web developers, HAM radio hobbyists (the ones that are still around), and any Obrimos frustrated by conflicts between their beliefs and the Aether's black-and-white delineation of right and wrong (or true and false). As with many Left-Handed Legacies, initiates rarely know what they're getting into until they take an Attainment, at which point the Sacred Frequency hums in their minds and souls and it may be too late to ever sever the connection.<br /> <br /> With their natural power over the Forces of the universe augmented by Mind magic, Keepers of the Sacred Frequency learn first to hear radio signals in their thoughts. Then, they learn to send their thoughts to follow those radio signals, broadcasting an emotion across a large area or even implanting thoughts into a listener's mind. The ultimate goal of the Legacy is to establish a network of the broadcasting cathedrals they dream of across the world, until all of mankind is in tune with the thought of their Abyssal god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T13:28:02-07:00","id":438859,"title":"","content":"That's both glorious...and horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:28:07-07:00","id":438898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=438859#post438859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's both glorious...and horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thank you! ^.^ I blame my best friend in 6th grade reading Stephen King's &quot;Cell&quot; and telling me all about it-I'm a huge King fan but have always avoided reading Cell because the cover of the first printing (the cell phone in a pool of blood reflecting a burning city off the screen) terrified me as a child. The original concept was Scelesti who hijacked cell phone control towers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T16:41:19-07:00","id":439046,"title":"","content":"This is the first draft of a legacy I've been toying with. First, it gives the Arrow another legacy, because really? 4 legacies, one of those Left-Handed? Second, it's a combat-focused legacy that isn't combat-exclusive like the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind or the Perfected Adepts.<br /> <br /> The Sworn Companions<br /> <br /> In Ancient Greece, the shield, not the sword or spear, was the symbol of war. The Sworn Companions understand this truth: The heart of warfare is to protect and defend, not for the purpose of destruction. These warriors are dedicated to the defense of a person, place, thing or group.<br /> <br /> Arcana: Space, (optional) Life<br /> <br /> Oblations: Standing watch over a place or person, meditation on vows, training regimins<br /> <br /> Names: Companion, Hetairoi, Knight, Shield, Mook (Perjorative)<br /> <br /> Special: Must possess the Oathbound merit. If they are not currently under an oath, all attainments cease to function.<br /> <br /> 1st Attainment: Semper Intenti- Space 2, (Optional Life 1), Gnosis 3<br /> The Companion is permanently under the effects of Space 2 Scry, and Space 1 Finder towards the target of their oath. If they have life 1, they also gain the effects of Life 1 Healer's Trance toward their oaths target. However this only tells them whether the target is totally healthy or not unless the Companion takes the time to concentrate.<br /> <br /> 2nd Attainment: Semper Paratus- Space 3, (Optional Life 2), Gnosis 5<br /> The Companion may open a portal to their charge as a reflexive action for the cost of 1 Mana. With Life 2, they receive an always-on Life 2 Organic Resilience. This armor stacks with any other mage armor, but not Organic Resilience.<br /> <br /> 3rd Attainment: Semper Armati- Space 4, (Optional Life 3), Gnosis 7<br /> The Companion gains a Pocket Dimension, per the spell, that may only be used to store weapons and armor, including their ritual tools. They may spend an instant action and 1 mana to retrieve or stock any arms or armor to and from this pocket dimension, and if they choose to retrieve armor, they may choose whether it is summoned near them, or already worn.With Life 3, the Companion gains their Life Arcana in extra dots of physical attributes. They may redistribute these spare dots by spending one mana and an instant action. This stacks with Honing the Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5305-theravis","name":"Theravis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T10:59:50-07:00","id":442824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theravis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=439046#post439046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first draft of a legacy I've been toying with. First, it gives the Arrow another legacy, because really? 4 legacies, one of those Left-Handed? Second, it's a combat-focused legacy that isn't combat-exclusive like the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind or the Perfected Adepts.<br /> <br /> The Sworn Companions<br /> <br /> In Ancient Greece, the shield, not the sword or spear, was the symbol of war. The Sworn Companions understand this truth: The heart of warfare is to protect and defend, not for the purpose of destruction. These warriors are dedicated to the defense of a person, place, thing or group.<br /> <br /> Arcana: Space, (optional) Life<br /> <br /> Oblations: Standing watch over a place or person, meditation on vows, training regimins<br /> <br /> Names: Companion, Hetairoi, Knight, Shield, Mook (Perjorative)<br /> <br /> Special: Must possess the Oathbound merit. If they are not currently under an oath, all attainments cease to function.<br /> <br /> 1st Attainment: Semper Intenti- Space 2, (Optional Life 1), Gnosis 3<br /> The Companion is permanently under the effects of Space 2 Scry, and Space 1 Finder towards the target of their oath. If they have life 1, they also gain the effects of Life 1 Healer's Trance toward their oaths target. However this only tells them whether the target is totally healthy or not unless the Companion takes the time to concentrate.<br /> <br /> 2nd Attainment: Semper Paratus- Space 3, (Optional Life 2), Gnosis 5<br /> The Companion may open a portal to their charge as a reflexive action for the cost of 1 Mana. With Life 2, they receive an always-on Life 2 Organic Resilience. This armor stacks with any other mage armor, but not Organic Resilience.<br /> <br /> 3rd Attainment: Semper Armati- Space 4, (Optional Life 3), Gnosis 7<br /> The Companion gains a Pocket Dimension, per the spell, that may only be used to store weapons and armor, including their ritual tools. They may spend an instant action and 1 mana to retrieve or stock any arms or armor to and from this pocket dimension, and if they choose to retrieve armor, they may choose whether it is summoned near them, or already worn.With Life 3, the Companion gains their Life Arcana in extra dots of physical attributes. They may redistribute these spare dots by spending one mana and an instant action. This stacks with Honing the Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool legacy. It reminds me of the Votary of the Ordained, a guardian legacy (<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Votary_of_the_Ordained\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Votary_of_the_Ordained</a>). Not the same, as their goal is to protect a person of great destiny from having it changed or demolished, but some of the abilities are similar and would be a good guide.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attainments<br /> <br /> Being a Votary of the Ordained requires that a mage be intimately familiar with the Mysteries of Fate. Space and Life or Matter are also advantageous. Most Votaries are well-muscled, large and healthy, with a strong knowledge of how to apply natural forces effectively, though some maintain the sanctity of their charges by utilizing more subtle means.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st Attainment: Soldier of Fortune<br /> <br /> Pre-Requisites: Gnosis 3, Fate 3<br /> <br /> The first Attainment allows the Votary of the Ordained to dedicate himself to a single charge of his choice, whether a person, place, or object, in a variation of the Fate Arcanum's oath spells. If the charge is a living being, it does not have to be aware of its new status, or even be willing to become a charge.<br /> <br /> Once the mage has declared his charge and spent one Mana to seal his intent, from that point on it is the Votary's sole responsibility to see that his charge meets its true fate. Generally, younger Votaries of Fate take on charges with simpler needs (guarding the asp that would bite Cleopatra from its birth until the event) while their elders see to the difficult ones (protecting a scroll for 100 years to ensure that only the proper person learns its secret). Once the Votary of the Ordained has dedicated himself to a charge, he gains the benefit of an Intimate sympathetic bond with his charge at all times.<br /> <br /> Once the charge's fate has been met, the bond between the Votary and his charge dissolves. If the charge has another important destiny in the future, the Votary may re-dedicate himself to the charge. Otherwise, he is expected to find a new destiny that needs his assistance.<br /> <br /> For each scene in the story, the Votary gains the benefits of the Fate 2 Exceptional Luck spell on dice roll per dot he has in the Fate Arcanum, although this benefit must be used to protect the charge or ensure that it meets his ordained destiny.<br /> <br /> Optional Arcanum: Space 1<br /> <br /> The Votary gains the benefit of the Space 1 Finder spell with respect to his charge, as long as he is within a number of miles equal to his Gnosis from his charge. If his charge is a location, he instead gains the effects of the Space 1 Omnivision spell as long as he is within that location.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2nd Attainment: Doctoring Fate<br /> <br /> Pre-Requisites: Gnosis 5, Fate 3<br /> <br /> The Votary can also fool others about the nature of his charge's destiny. As long as he is in the same room as his charge or, if his charge is a location, within it, he becomes instantly aware if someone is using supernatural perception to judge the nature and strength of his charge's fate. He may reflexively dim or misdirect this person's awareness as if he had already cast the Fate 3 Occlude Destiny and Fabricate Fortune spells at a Potency equal to his rating in the Fate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> If the Votary has Life 2 and his charge is a person, he gains the ability to purge poisons from his charge's body, similar to the Life 2 Purify Bodies spell. Make an instant Stamina + Medicine + Life roll.<br /> <br /> Optional Arcanum: Space 2<br /> <br /> The Votary may, as an instant action, view his charge, wherever it might be. This is similar to the use of the Space 2 Scrying spell, but it requires no roll or Mana expenditure.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3rd Attainment: Fate Defends Itself<br /> <br /> Pre-Requisites: Gnosis 7, Fate 4<br /> <br /> When someone threatens the Votary's charge, this level of Attainment in the Legacy allows the guardian to hinder that threat's every action with fate itself. The cords of destiny act to prevent the intruder's victory, causing her to stumble over nothing and catch her knife in her coat. The Votary can inflict an aggressor with a massive streak of bad luck, as if she were subject to the Fate 5 Great Curse spell. The Votary's player rolls Resolve + Intimidation + Fate as an instant action, and she must spend one Mana per use, although the effect is covert rather than vulgar. She can increase the number of targets affected by suffering dice penalties to her roll, per the rules for Target factors.<br /> <br /> If the roll is successful, the target(s) suffers a -1 dice penalty per dot of the Votary's Fate Arcanum; this penalty only applies to those attempts by the target(s) to affect the Votary's charge. The effect lasts for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> Optional Arcanum: Space 3<br /> <br /> The Votary may choose to summon his charge to him through use of the Space 2 Apportation spell. If the charge is a location or person, he may not use Apportation at all but may instead instantly take himself to his charge through the Space 3 Portal spell. Neither of these requires any roll. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:33:20-07:00","id":442965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theravis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=439046#post439046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first draft of a legacy I've been toying with. First, it gives the Arrow another legacy, because really? 4 legacies, one of those Left-Handed? Second, it's a combat-focused legacy that isn't combat-exclusive like the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind or the Perfected Adepts.<br /> <br /> The Sworn Companions<br /> <br /> In Ancient Greece, the shield, not the sword or spear, was the symbol of war. The Sworn Companions understand this truth: The heart of warfare is to protect and defend, not for the purpose of destruction. These warriors are dedicated to the defense of a person, place, thing or group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for teaching me something about history I never knew. Also, I love that their third attainment basically gives them access to hammerspace.<br /> <br /> Neither of these are fleshed out the way my last Legacy was, but here are two more ideas I'd be happy to flesh out if people like them (I may do so regardless)<br /> <br /> <b>The Socialites: </b>This sarcastically-named clique of Free Council Mastigos may be the first Mages to seek Supernal correspondences in the &quot;digital world;&quot; specifically, by using Forces to charge computers and code with Mana, they translate their Mind magic to social media. They are in particular intrigued by the way widespread social networking has changed cultural ideas about privacy, and about identity-is a man who lies about his name, face, and age, but finds a new community who accepts him under these false pretenses <i>just </i>lying, or is he changing supposedly immutable truths about himself through an act of will, reinforced by the good faith of those &quot;around&quot; him in cyberspace? Most of the experiments of this legacy (those recorded and published openly for the rest of the Free Council to read, that is) tend toward elaborate attempts at &quot;Catfishing&quot; or other juvenile social experiments such as leaking a celebrity's nude pictures and then changing the way Sleeper pop culture feels about the leak through mass manipulation of the blogosphere. However, there are rumors that the Socialites have created functioning &quot;trinary&quot; computers that approach true artificial intelligence <i>without </i>the use of magic, or discovered a way to manipulate &quot;Digital Sympathy,&quot; gaining a real connection to Sleepers or other Mages through online interactions with no need for anything as crude as a drop of blood or lock of hair. These rumors are part of the reason you won't find too many willworkers with active Twitter accounts.<br /> <br /> <b>The Colony: </b>This Left-Handed Thyrsus Legacy was born when an unknown Shaman of ages past did something unthinkable to Mages of the Diamond Orders: he called to the gods of the Primal Wild and, rather than attempting to hunt them as predator, outwit them as prey, or contract with them as equals, he bowed to them, offering his soul's sworn oath of fealty to any great Beast or Totem that had need of him, with no request for power in return. This strangely selfless ritual called to Queen Bee, whose servants work, fight, and die for her with no thought of their own personal gain. She touched his soul, and took him through the twisting combs of her hive, showing him how her colony moved its many bodies with one mind to keep harmony. The Shaman understood that highly individualized human minds were getting in the way of mankind's harmony with nature, and of the Fallen's harmony with the Supernal. He understood how he could fix this, and sought other Mages quietly until he found another Shaman seeking truths of the Primal Wild. He showed her the way, and the nameless Mage and his apprentice became a Colony of two. Mages of The Colony gain an affinity with Mind magic, despite being uniformly Thyrsus, and two or more who come together truly do act as one. Those at the highest levels of Attainment can further spread their hive-mind to animals, other Mages, or even Sleepers in their vicinity, eventually creating an entire small ecosystem that moves together governed by one mind-imagine a zoo where one of the visitors walks into the tiger cage fearlessly and is devoured without raising an arm to defend himself, for he knows that the tigers are hungry and have not eaten well. Later, the same tigers will allow other people to pick over the remains of the devoured man, and find his unscratched wallet or diamond wedding ring, because the tigers know that the humans can use these objects to obtain food to eat and good wood to make fire with.<br /> Mages of The Colony have the potential to become some of the most powerful Thyrsus in the world, but the price they pay for this power is freedom; Queen Bee feeds them her honey, and buzzes in their ears every night as they dream. She tells them her wishes for the Fallen World, and her wish is The Colony's command. Even if they remembered they could defy her, they would not-the &quot;individual&quot; identities of their souls have been stripped away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T14:02:55-07:00","id":443081,"title":"","content":"You don't really need to put trinary in quotes, ternary computers (aka trinary computers) are a real thing that actually exist.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of The Colony, a non-Abyssal hive-mind intruder is a fun idea. And the execution and write-up really pique my interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T19:57:22-07:00","id":443646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=442824#post442824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool legacy. It reminds me of the Votary of the Ordained, a guardian legacy (<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Votary_of_the_Ordained\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Votary_of_the_Ordained</a>). Not the same, as their goal is to protect a person of great destiny from having it changed or demolished, but some of the abilities are similar and would be a good guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are pretty similar. I've also been considering a Spirit or Mind variant that focuses on defense and inspiration, a sort of &quot;Band of Brothers&quot; idea over supernatural guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5305-theravis","name":"Theravis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T20:11:08-07:00","id":443666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuatreVingts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=442965#post442965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for teaching me something about history I never knew. Also, I love that their third attainment basically gives them access to hammerspace.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The Greeks confuse the heck out of me for that reason, because they named their troops after what shield they carry. This leads to issues when you have 5 different kinds of Peltasts, who are all skirmishers, and then Royal Peltasts, who are heavy armored infantry. As for the 3rd attainment.... That was the idea, but the real issue was limiting use. As one of my players pointed out: &quot;Tanks are made to hurt people, so take a tank wherever you go!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5305-theravis","name":"Theravis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T09:22:48-07:00","id":444391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=443081#post443081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...trinary computers) are a real thing that actually exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Am I old, are we living in the future, or is it both??<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=443081#post443081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really like the idea of The Colony, a non-Abyssal hive-mind intruder is a fun idea. And the execution and write-up really pique my interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I liked the idea of Supernal gods that Atlantean magic didn't interact with, because Atlantean Magical Theory/Theology is all about bootstrapping yourself up to the Supernal to deal with its inhabitants as an equal.<br /> There's a Dreamtime entity in <i>Night Horrors: Unbidden </i>that could probably serve a similar story function, but hive-minds are categorically underrepresented as a class of antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T09:43:42-07:00","id":444428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuatreVingts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=444391#post444391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Am I old, are we living in the future, or is it both??<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For your reading pleasure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternary_computer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternary_computer\" target=\"_blank\"> Ternary computer - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternary_computer\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternary_computer </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T23:45:21-07:00","id":447226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=444428#post444428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For your reading pleasure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternary_computer\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternary_computer</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well...that makes trinary (sorry, &quot;Tremary,&quot; gonna have to train myself out of that one) computers seem a good bit less mysterious and wonderful. I confess, my knowledge of the term comes from <i>Ascension </i>and from Ned Vizzini's <i>Be More Chill </i>in about equal measure. On the other hand, I know none of my potential players have the computer knowledge to call me on that, so it could still be useful as a plot device, or be something that a member of my newly-minted clique of Awakened social media nerds throws in the face of a PC. (&quot;Um, 'trinary?' What do you even think that means?&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T15:00:51-07:00","id":449804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HotChepSoot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=423578#post423578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More Please!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'll post what I got on this one. 'Tis extremely rough, so any polish is welcome. I am unlikely to haunt this site much for a while, though. <br /> <br /> <b>The Pit Baiters</b><br /> Fate (Death, Prime)<br /> <br /> This would be a legacy that practices Fate magic in an attempt to learn how to use Fate and Luck to bind and control the Abyss.<br /> <br /> They see some of their applications of their art as &quot;cursing&quot; the Abyss and making it less likely to affect the world. As far as these see it, the Supernal Realm defines what is possible, while the Loom of Fate defines what is. The Abyss represents what isn't and cannot be. If appropriately handled, then, the forces of Are Not can be carefully handled be weaving carefully and ending the trouble so caused. Paradoxes are snarls in the weave of reality, which a dedicated weaver can go back and repair, but is better served by preventing initially...<br /> <br /> <i><b>1st: Curse the Darkness</b></i><br /> <i>Fate Prime</i><br /> The mage tries the primary force of the legacy, and curses the Abyss with the power of Fate.<br /> The mage uses an action, and rolls Fate + Resolve + Composure. Each success affects one Paradox roll. Affected Paradox rolls are reduced by this caster's Fate rating. The range is sensory to the mage at the time of the casting. The mage cannot select the affected spells, just the Paradox rolls in the scene.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the mage can either reduce or increase the penalty to their own casting rolls caused by Paradox successes by up to their Fate rating. This does nothing to mitigate the effects of the Paradox in any other way. Spells still flip out of control or breaches in reality still form, etc., but the penalty imposed on the mage's magic is reduced after the Paradox is calculated. Generally, this means that they reduce the spell effect, preferably removing it. This must be declared before the results are finalized. Once the targets of havoc are declared, it's too late... (unless that's a temptation we'd <i>like)</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>2nd: Forging the Bane of Darkness</b><br /> Fate Prime</i><br /> The mage may craft a Spindle of Fate, which is alternately known as a Paradox Ward. This item may be any device wrought from iron or silver. Items could also be crafted from both. The functional structure must be pure iron or silver, and have been worked with hand tools. The creation of this item requires a mana.<br /> <br /> The mage must hold the device in their hand to use it. Only with such a device in hand can the mage use this attainment. This further limits useful shapes, but otherwise the device can be essentially any item. A ring could be worn and still count as held. <br /> <br /> The mage must use an action to empower the item in hand, and only one such device may be empowered by the mage at any given time. While the device is held in a hand and lifted up, the Abyss shrinks back. This subjects any Abyssal creature in direct line of sight and within sensory range to a penalty to all rolls equal to the caster's Fate dice. This also reduces all Paradox pools by one die within sight of the object. Both caster and the area affected by any spells cast must be within line of sight of the Paradox Ward for this effect.<br /> <br /> Those strongly tainted with the power of the Abyss, such as Tremere cursed liches and vampires, are affected by the curse as would be any other.<br /> <br /> (It's reasonable that Havoc would usually not target the character, too, but I haven't thought of any good system for that. Maybe just declare it so. )<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>3rd: Striking the Heart of Darkness</b></i><br /> The mage's Paradox Wards now strike out at the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The device now deals lethal to any Abyssal creatures on a touch equal to the creator's Fate. If the device is a weapon, the mage may add Fate to the extant equipment bonuses.<br /> <br /> It is rumored the Fourth Attainment is similar to the spell Swarm of Locusts, which renders Paradox much simpler to deal with.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the theme much better than these mechanics, though. I didn't come up with anything particularly evocative of the &quot;binding up the abyss in rules&quot; aspect I was looking for. Got me a migraine today, so I'm not even going to try to tackle this, now. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T16:08:37-07:00","id":450968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuatreVingts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=447226#post447226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well...that makes trinary (sorry, &quot;Tremary,&quot; gonna have to train myself out of that one) computers seem a good bit less mysterious and wonderful. I confess, my knowledge of the term comes from <i>Ascension </i>and from Ned Vizzini's <i>Be More Chill </i>in about equal measure. On the other hand, I know none of my potential players have the computer knowledge to call me on that, so it could still be useful as a plot device, or be something that a member of my newly-minted clique of Awakened social media nerds throws in the face of a PC. (&quot;Um, 'trinary?' What do you even think that means?&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>What about substituting the ternary computer with an <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Analog_computer\" target=\"_blank\">analog computer</a> that has gained full sentience/sapience due to its non-discrete nature and thus ability to produce non-discrete results such as varied emotions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:36:41-07:00","id":451984,"title":"","content":"I've had a huge interest in psi since...well, I don't even remember when it started any more, since I was a kid. Probably dates back to my early X-Men fandom some time in the early-mid 80s, but might go back further. Ascension makes this both easy and hard (paradigms model anything, but a model of pure mental manifestation is tricky for balance reasons), but in Awakening, it's just plain easy, thanks to Legacies. Without further ado, a bare-bones version of the Psychonauts (based on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychonautics\" target=\"_blank\">the practice of Psychonautics</a> as a path to psychic ability, not the video game -- though it's a <i>great</i> game):<br /> <br /> <b>Psychonauts</b> (Free Council, Mind, Optional: Forces):<br /> Psychics are real (note: see Second Sight). They are an objective Truth of the world, people who transcend the Lie through direct gifts rather than rituals. Often it is also a curse, but psychic ability is, to followers of this Legacy, an example of the Lie's vulnerability -- people <i>strive</i> for Truth, become living conduits of Truth, even wield the Truth as a weapon. Though seen as the odd stepchildren of science by some Libertines, the Psychonauts point to the undeniable (to Awakened) existence of Second Sight, and use it to transform themselves to mirror this model. Psychonauts, or mindwalkers (sometimes derisively called Scanners or brain-divers), take this transformation seriously, and their culture is strongly inclined to ethical use of their abilities. This isn't to say that they're immune to corruption -- far from it, some terrible Fallen have come from their Legacy -- but rather that they police themselves fiercely, given the abuses a telepathic Legacy is capable of.<br /> <br /> The primary Sphere is Mind, for its astral insights and telepathic communion; while Psychonauts are supportive of mediums, they're still Libertines, and their psychic model connects them to the Mysteries of humanity, not other Realms. When sh*t gets real, their Optional Attainments draw on the Symbol of mind over matter for telekinesis, shielding, and even manipulating heat for &quot;thermokinesis,&quot; roasting or chilling targets with equal facility. (The new five-rank model will allow for more abilities; I'm thinking one will be flight-via-levitation, but am divided between more straight-up pyrokinesis and the less-classical but no less valid electrokinesis.)<br /> <br /> Psychonauts view themselves as explorers, using their mental Attainments to seek humanity's magical potential within the minds of those they wish to liberate. However, they've gained a reputation within the Free Council as guardians and crusaders against the Lie, due to the useful mix of being able to read an opponent's actions, then counter them at range. Since Pyschonauts are typically even more offended by servants of the Lie than the average Libertine, they end up drawn to this role in spite of most mindwalkers' vocal objections to the contrary. A few embrace a role as adventurer-heroes, but they tend to be...odd, even for Psychonauts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:00:53-07:00","id":452146,"title":"","content":"What about the other types of psychics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:38:24-07:00","id":452183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=451984#post451984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> <