 of humanity, not other Realms. When sh*t gets real, their Optional Attainments draw on the Symbol of mind over matter for telekinesis, shielding, and even manipulating heat for &quot;thermokinesis,&quot; roasting or chilling targets with equal facility. (The new five-rank model will allow for more abilities; I'm thinking one will be flight-via-levitation, but am divided between more straight-up pyrokinesis and the less-classical but no less valid electrokinesis.)<br /> <br /> Psychonauts view themselves as explorers, using their mental Attainments to seek humanity's magical potential within the minds of those they wish to liberate. However, they've gained a reputation within the Free Council as guardians and crusaders against the Lie, due to the useful mix of being able to read an opponent's actions, then counter them at range. Since Pyschonauts are typically even more offended by servants of the Lie than the average Libertine, they end up drawn to this role in spite of most mindwalkers' vocal objections to the contrary. A few embrace a role as adventurer-heroes, but they tend to be...odd, even for Psychonauts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like it. Just an FYI, one of the new names of the Mastigos (in addition to Warlocks) will be Psychonauts in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:02:59-07:00","id":454521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=452146#post452146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the other types of psychics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainments only cover two Spheres. My Psychonauts are one type; there would clearly be others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:05:06-07:00","id":454524,"title":"","content":"Just wondering if you'd considered them.<br /> <br /> Since you seem to be going Mind and Forces, did you consider telekinesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T11:01:22-07:00","id":454608,"title":"","content":"I have one, but it's quite silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T11:23:30-07:00","id":454652,"title":"","content":"EDITED NOW<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T18:32:16-07:00","id":455152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=454524#post454524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering if you'd considered them.<br /> <br /> Since you seem to be going Mind and Forces, did you consider telekinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Optional. TK, shielding, Thermo. (The new five-Attainment version will need some revisiting.)<br /> <br /> Freemind, I didn't know that, but I'm not going to worry about it for now since it's just a fan thing. If I run a full M:tAw campaign, I'll probably end up renaming them. (Really glad Mastigos aren't all about the demons any more. Temperance FTW! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T21:33:35-07:00","id":455367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=450968#post450968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about substituting the ternary computer with an <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Analog_computer\" target=\"_blank\">analog computer</a> that has gained full sentience/sapience due to its non-discrete nature and thus ability to produce non-discrete results such as varied emotions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was completely lost on what to do with this until the reference to analog synthesizers came along; speaking of which, I have a couple music-related Legacies I should dig up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=454608#post454608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one, but it's quite silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>POST IT POST IT POST IT","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:35:36-07:00","id":467253,"title":"","content":"<b>Scavengers of the Farthest Shore</b><br /><br /> Astral is an infinite realm full of wonders and horrors in equal measure. Unfortunately, accessing it isn\u2019t easy and taking its treasures back to the physical world is a sin against the very nature of reality. Greater still are the horrors and mind-bending waves waiting at the shore of the Ocean of Ourobors. Reaching the most distant shore is no small feat and many mages only risk it in the direst need.<br /> Being members of the Free Council, Scavengers of the Farthest Shore are explorers and visionaries fascinated with the grim mysteries of the Astral Ocean. They wish to study the strange creatures and phenomena washed ashore by the abyss and when possible to bring it to the real existence. As the detritus washed up is anything but the part of natural astral space, materializing it by this legacy doesn\u2019t constitute the sin against wisdom. However, a deliberate exposure of some horror that will inadvertently pollute and destroy the world around it is weighted separately.<br /> Mainly consisting of the Mastygos and Moros mages of the Free Council, the legacy was founded by a fan of Lovecraft and is under close scrutiny and can be declared left-handed after a serious enough violation.<br /> Oblations: Wondering on the seaside and collecting debris, taking care of fish or birds, crafting.<br /> Monikers: Abyss forgers, nightmare hoarders, smiths of the unreal.<br /> <br /> X marks the spot - Mind 1 + space 1<br /> Sacrificing a token of travel to the Ouroboros, mage can travel quickly to the ocean without mana or demence. Only halve the successes required.<br /> <br /> Nightmare Vault - Space 2 + Mind 3<br /> Collecting staff on the unreal shore is one thing, keeping it from killing yourself is another. Dipping a representation of walls in the black water the mage can build a reinforced vault in his mind to safely contain his spoils. Number of cells = Gnosis<br /> <br /> Undreamt of Forge<br /> At this final attainment scavenger may finally draw his treasures to the material world and channel their power, or if wishing so to take them out of his oneiroi, giving a permanent existence to items and spirits.<br /> Mind 4 + Matter 4, channel trophies contained in the cells through appropriate medium.<br /> Mind 4 + Spirit 4, summon the living things from cells as spirits<br /> Matter 4 + Spirit 4 + Mind 4, as spell chimerical conjuration, but no wisdom loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:42:00-07:00","id":663835,"title":"","content":"rescuing this from the old site:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>The Celebrants of Life</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Parent Path: Mastigos<br /> Parent Order: None<br /> Nickname: The Stepford Smilers, The Rejoicers, The Joyous, The Super-Happies, The Delighted, The Rictus Grins<br /> Philosophy: The true goal of life is to enjoy it.<br /> <br /> <b>The first attainment</b>: Enjoy the Moment<br /> Requires: Gnosis 3 Mind 2, Empathy 2 or Persuasion 2<br /> <br /> Imagine a legacy devoted to being happy. Sounds nice doesn't it? So do it. Be happy. Use the Arcana of Mind to <u>be happy</u>. All the time. No exceptions. NO EXCEPTIONS. Be happy even during the onset of nuclear winter. (It becomes close to, if not impossible, to change the emotions of a Stepford Smiler who has learned the first attainment from the state of perpetual happiness. Any power that would induce such a change must achieve more successes than the Delighted has dots in Mind. Even then, the duration becomes transitory)<br /> <br /> In fact, being so happy makes you want to share the joy with as many friends as you can, doesn't it? So use something similar to <u>Emotional Urging</u> to make as many as Gnosis+Mind people happy so long as you concentrate on them. For some odd reason people will sometimes pretend they don't want to be happy by rolling Composure+Gnosis vs your Presence + Intimidation+ Mind. You don't know why, but you'll cheefully play along with their mock resistance and &quot;force&quot; them to enjoy themselves. For some odd reason, people are especially likely to play this game after other people die. Isn't that weird?<br /> With optional Space 2 you don't have to be near people to make them happy. Isn't it wonderful?<br /> <br /> <b>The second attainment:</b> Happily Ever After<br /> Requires: Gnosis 5 Mind 3<br /> <br /> Even though you would happily devote yourself to simply staring at your friends or even random strangers and just concentrating on making them happy until you dehydrate to the point of unconsciousness, there are better ways to go about making people happy. Having learned how much you enjoy making people happy directly, it seems like a fun idea to be able to make them happy even when you aren't around, doesn't it? All you have to do is reach into their minds and forge a <u>Passion Link</u> between one topic and pure happiness.<br /> <br /> For some reason, other people allow their happiness to be all to fleeting, so you can help them capture their moments of happiness and hold onto them, experiencing them over and over in a single <u>Eternal Now</u>.<br /> <br /> <b>The third attainment</b>: The Joys of Yesteryear<br /> Requires: Gnosis 7 and Mind 5<br /> <br /> You probably weren't around to help cheer up your friends for your entire life. Luckily, as a mage, you can make it as if you were. Mucking about with Time can get delightfully complex, so instead you can just <u>Breach the Vault of </u><u>Memories</u> so that you effectively WERE there all the time making them happy.<br /> <br /> Other mages keep on being silly and avoiding actions that would make them happy because it would be &quot;Unwise&quot;. You know it's better to be happy though, so you can cheerfully <u>Suppress Wisdom </u>in both yourself and others. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","user":"Lareath","date":". 09-14-2015, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T22:08:25-07:00","id":663882,"title":"","content":"This is one of my Legacies from way back:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000099\">The Enlightened Noetic Collective</span></b><br /> <br /> &quot;Come friend, give up the painful illusion of individuality and join us in Unity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since the dawn of civilization people have banded together for everything from safety to friendship. Some say that humans are inherently social beings and that actions that have the most moral worth are those done for the greater good of the human community as a whole; that the needs of the many outweigh the needs of the few. Communalism, or the creation of intentional communities for social reasons, often drew from such collectivist thinking. During the revival of communalism in America during the early sixties, Nelson Henshaw, a college dropout who had majored in psychology and philosophy decided to establish a commune of his own.<br /> <br /> Using the social ideals of Marx, Buddhism's illusion of Self, and the rhetoric of New Age Noetic Sciences, Henshaw cobbled together the Enlightened Noetic Collective, a community built on the principle of connecting with the World Consciousness of humanity. Founding a community on an isolated mesa in the Southwest Unisted States, Henshaw was lucky enough to attract the right mix of people to make the place survive and even prosper.<br /> <br /> Though he didn't truly believe in his own preachings, Henshaw had the charisma to forge true converts, including his own daughter, Sophia. A by-blow from his dalliance with one of his disciples, Sophia grew up with collectivist thought almost literally with her mother's milk.<br /> <br /> The ENC was truly a cult of personality and would have dispersed upon Henshaw's sudden death in the eighties, except that his death also triggered Sophia's Awakening onto the Mastigos Path. Returning from her Astral Journey with visions of a unified humanity, Sophia pulled the shaken community together around her. Using her newfound Mind arts, she even managed to strengthen their beliefs in Unity.<br /> <br /> Due to the isolation of the community, Sophia was allowed to grow in power without the influence of other mages, an Apostate. She spent almost a decade strengthening her sympathetic ties to the community, both magical and mundane. When a young Mysterium mage came to the town to investigate what was suspected to be a newly forming Hallow, he was struck by the peacefulness and cooperation of the people in the little community. After staying awhile, he became entranced by the simple and earnest lifestyle of the commune. The Collective earned its first Awakened convert.<br /> <br /> The local Consilium is just beginning to worry about The Collective and its motives. They had long dismissed it as a small cult of an isolated Apostate and expected it to die out years ago. The apparent signs of prosperity have made some councilors wonder about its longevity. They don't know that The Collective now has a handful of mage converts and that the Sleeper community no longer induces extra Paradox on Collective magic (most Mind arts) because of how ingrained the philosophy has become in their community.<br /> <br /> Though cautious about expanding, the Collective's ultimate goal is the unification of all humanity and it has been slowly introducing subtle memes to that effect into the general populace. For the most part, the Collective tries to be persuasive instead of coercive, relying on super-enhanced Social Attributes and Skills to convert newcomers, but when all else fails or violence threatens the community, Sophia doesn't hesitate to bring the mind-numbing onslaught of the mental voices of an entire community to bear on an attacker. The Collective is a pacifist philosophy, believing that all human life is as one.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Mastigos, but any mage that joins the commune can join the Legacy.<br /> <b>Nickname: </b> Hippy<br /> Appearance: Members of the Collective dress plainly, realizing that the need to stand out from others is a selfish motive, a left over, painful reminder of solitary existence. For the World Soul, &quot;wearing&quot; different bodies is separation enough.<br /> <b>Background: </b>Members of the collective come from many different backgrounds, though those who profess a belief in New Age concepts find resonance with the philosophy and the dispossessed find comfort in the community. People from neighboring towns who have had an encounter with one of the charismatic Atman come away reeling with ideas of the promise of Unity. Many leave their homes soon after to join the Collective.<br /> <b>Organization: </b> All members of the Collective are valued equally, truly just another expression of the One. Though no one member, even Sophia, is regarded as more important, the Atman are the inner circle of the Collective, a handful of mages who have joined the Legacy and are believed to be closer to reaching the goal of true Unity with the One. When Sophia crafted her Legacy, she took the Shadow Name, Atman, the World Soul and bestows it to all Awakened who follow her soul path. After admitting a few mages into the inner workings of the Collective, Sophia has been forced to become a healer of minds or else the Collective would have disintegrated under the combined weight of multiple mental disorders. This is also on par with Collective philosophy, though, as the pains of individuality have to be shared to be healed.<br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Communing with another Collective member in meditation. Spreading the philosophy of Unity. Divesting oneself of the illusion of individuality.<br /> <b>Concepts:</b> Commune member. Disillusioned materialist.<br /> <b>Attainments:</b> Lessons learned from the Iron Watchtower convinced Sophia that all human consciousness is the expression of the same Universal Consciousness. These attainments came about in an effort to rejoin the scattered pieces of humanity. Mind is the primary Arcanum, but knowledge of Space is required as well, to strengthen sympathetic bonds to the point where masters of this Legacy are magically one person.<br /> <br /> <b><u>1st: One Mind</u></b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b> Gnosis 3, Mind 2 (Primary), Space 1<br /> At this level of Unity, the Collective mage learns to open his mind up to the conscious thoughts of fellow Collective mages. As per the Mind 3 effect, &quot;Telepathy&quot; on pg. 212, an Instant action lets a Collective mage open up a mental line of communication with any other mage that has achieved this Attainment. An &quot;Emotional Urging&quot; effect also fills the mage with feelings of peace and calm whenever he communes with another mage through this Attainment and allows mages to always be aware of the emotions of all other Collective members on the subconscious level. The drawback to this ability is that the mage also opens themselves up to the madnesses of other Collective members. When a mage gains this Attainment, he gains the Derangements of all other members with this Attainment as well as transmitting any Derangements he has along to the others. Joining the Collective can be quite traumatic to the unprepared mage, which is why Sophia and the Atman try to groom potential candidates very thoroughly before admitting them to the ranks of the Atman.<br /> <br /> <b><u>2nd: One Heart</u></b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 5, Mind 3<br /> Achieving this level of Unity allows a mage to tap into deeper levels of her fellow mages' consciousness. Mages with this Attainment can reflexively &quot;borrow&quot; the Virtue or Vice of any mage that has at least attained &quot;One Mind&quot; for the purposes of regaining Willpower. The mage can only use this the same number of times she would normally be allowed, though, once per scene for Vices and once per session for Virtues. The drawback of this Attainment is that anytime a mage that has attained at least &quot;One Mind&quot; makes a degeneration roll, the mage that has attained &quot;One Heart&quot; is also forced to make a degeneration roll. Fortunately, she only has to roll as if she committed a sin equal to her current Wisdom rating, no matter what level of sin the offending mage committed.<br /> <b><u>Optional Arcanum:</u> </b> Space 3<br /> With Space 3, mages of the Collective can transfer Willpower to each other at will. It takes an Instant action to mentally contact another mage to request the Willpower, and most Collective mages give permission (it is impossible to take the Willpower against the donating mage's will). Successes on a Composure+Empathy+Mind roll gives the maximum amount of Willpower a mage can recieve in a given 24-hour period.<br /> <br /> <b><u>3rd: One Soul</u></b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 7, Mind 4, Prime 1<br /> Mastering the Unity lays bare the very souls of the Collective to the mage. The sympathetic connections between members of the Collective has become so strong at this point that a mage can even make use of another mage's knowledge of the Arcanum. After taking an Instant action to establish a connection with a network of fellow Collective mages, a mage who has Attained &quot;One Soul&quot; can act as the primary caster in a Teamwork spellcasting action. A Composure+Empathy+Mind roll determines how many mages the Master can network in a scene and only mages who have attained &quot;One Mind&quot; can be a part of this gestalt. The benefit is that since the spell relies on the Imago of the primary caster, the contributing mages are allowed to use the dicepool for the Rote, whether or not they know the Rote and the primary caster can access the Arcana levels of all contributing mages even if she doesn't possess the knowledge herself. The drawback is that while a mage's Arcana are being used, he cannot cast any spells himself.<br /> <b><u>Optional Arcanum:</u> </b>Prime 3<br /> With Prime 3, a Collective mage can transfer Mana as she used to be able to transfer Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T22:13:23-07:00","id":663887,"title":"","content":"It breaks the rules of the power levels of the Attainments, but that's on purpose and includes drawbacks to compensate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:57:11-07:00","id":664550,"title":"","content":"I particularly remember those two last Legacies from a while back. Really nice work. Really, really particular, each one. The one Lareath reposted is truly (and cheerfully) terrifying. I have one question about the Atman, Ophidimancer. In the case of one of the Collective overcoming her own Derangement, if she was the source of that particular derangement in the Legacy, does that mean that everyone else will is cured aswell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T11:50:48-07:00","id":664574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=664550#post664550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I particularly remember those two last Legacies from a while back. Really nice work. Really, really particular, each one. The one Lareath reposted is truly (and cheerfully) terrifying. I have one question about the Atman, Ophidimancer. In the case of one of the Collective overcoming her own Derangement, if she was the source of that particular derangement in the Legacy, does that mean that everyone else will is cured aswell?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I hadn't thought of it, but yes, that sounds good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T03:56:49-07:00","id":665508,"title":"","content":"Then the Local Council are in for a surprise. Given the third attainment, even more so. Have you taken into consideration that they could very well fit into the Left-Handed Path?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T04:18:34-07:00","id":665516,"title":"","content":"Is the mention of 'the Unity' a deliberate reference or a fun coincidence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T06:12:52-07:00","id":665610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=665508#post665508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the Local Council are in for a surprise. Given the third attainment, even more so. Have you taken into consideration that they could very well fit into the Left-Handed Path?</div> </div> </div> </div>I deliberately put them in the grey. They are pacifist hippies, but they are also a brainwashing cult. They could very easily be a Left Handed Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=665516#post665516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the mention of 'the Unity' a deliberate reference or a fun coincidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering I don't get the reference, it's probably a coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T06:16:58-07:00","id":665620,"title":"","content":"It's the Iron Seal of Mind, the Exarch behind the Hegemonic Ministry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T06:33:22-07:00","id":665643,"title":"","content":"Though Unity appears much earlier in Sanctum and Sigil as the Hegemony stand-in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T07:33:30-07:00","id":665678,"title":"","content":"Ahh, that would be a coincidence then, since I wrote this legacy long before those books came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T19:17:27-07:00","id":667723,"title":"","content":"After discovering today a family of squid called Mastigoteuthidae, I want to write up a Mastigos legacy focused on transforming one's body to become one's &quot;true self,&quot; whatever form that may take (usually horrific).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T20:28:57-07:00","id":667748,"title":"","content":"Here's another one I wrote way back.<br /> <br /> <b>Heralds of the Divine Path</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Farewell, and may the gods grant that our Paths cross again!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Awakening is a mysterious phenomenon that is unpredictable, even to the most learned of mages. Even the researchers of the Mysterium cannot predict what kind of person is more likely to Awaken, and it has come to young and old, the educated and the illiterate. One thing that mages have in common with each other is that the Awakening pushes them to the edges of society. Their insights into the invisible truths of reality makes mages uncanny neighbors at best and many end up shunned by their former friends and family. Some strive to regain their place in society and feel the warmth of closeness with Sleepers. Others found that they liked the new perspective they had from being estranged. Beyond the edge of the firelight, they found a wider world, a more exciting world.<br /> <br /> The Heralds of the Divine Path are a brotherhood of mages that hail from those who feel a divine call to travel. Sailors, explorers, and vagabonds all feel this call and in all cultures gods of roads and journeys have arisen to explain this urge. Greco-roman cultures recognize Mercury, with his winged sandals, messenger of the gods and patron of thieves and merchants. In Africa Eshu, another messenger god, plagued travelers with obstacles in order to teach them valuable lessons. Hecate was worshipped as goddess of crossroads, the underworld, and magic, while in Japan, Dosojin presided over journeys, fertility, and childbirth.<br /> <br /> To the Heralds, life is a journey, a Divine Path that, if traveled fully, teaches and purifies the soul of the traveler. Obstacles in one's journey are meant to flense away impurities and in an alchemical transformation lead the traveler to the end of all Paths in Ascension.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Obrimos, though the Heralds are a sect of mages that are separate from any Order and can teach any mage that walks the Divine Path to be a Herald.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Travelers, Capital &quot;H&quot; Heralds<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Heralds are almost always dressed for travel and often carry insignias of whatever Order they are working for at the time. Many carry emblems or religious paraphernalia denoting the god of travel they worship.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Members almost always have had a wanderlust since before their Awakening. Traveling becomes a divine calling after Awakening, so even if they had been affluent before becoming mages they end up looking like road-weary travelers soon afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Little organization exists for the Heralds beyond the Master/Apprentice relationship. Powerful Fate magic leads a Herald to prospective members and their Paths intertwine long enough for the Master to teach the student and instill in them the ways of the Divine Path. All who travel in life must find their own Path. Meetings between Heralds are brief and perfunctory. Blessings are exchanged and then each Herald goes her own way, sure in her own Path and not willing to sully the honor of the other's Path by offering aid. All Orders commision Heralds for courier services because the oath of a Herald to deliver is only given if the Herald is willing to bind their Fates to the journey.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Praying to patron god or goddess. Trailblazing. Beginning a new journey. Completing an Oath.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attainments:</b></u> Heralds of the Divine Path are travelers at heart. Traveling is both a testing and a catharsis for Heralds. Though it would make sense for a traveling legacy to have Space as their primary Arcanum, Heralds would never try to shorten their journeys in any manner such as teleportation. They believe that the troubles they face along the way are the whole point of a journey. Instead they rely on their ability to find their fated Divine Paths.<br /> <br /> <u><b>1st: Herald's Oath</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 3, Fate 2 (Primary), Destiny 1<br /> <br /> Divine Path Heralds are in high demand as transporters and messengers. Mages of all Orders and even the Seers of the Throne know that a Herald can be trusted to see their charges to their destinations. This ability has a lot to do with this reputation. At this level of Attainment, a Herald of the Divine Path has enough faith in his own path to be willing to stake his own destiny on it. A <i>Swearing an Oath</i> spell can be cast as an Instant action without a roll, binding a Herald to the task at hand. This Oath allows the Herald to regain Willpower when actively pursuing the goals assigned as if the Oath were a Vice as well as allowing a reflexive Resolve+Composure roll to resist anything that would stop him from completing his task. While under the effects of this Oath, each success on a Resolve+Occult+Fate roll grants the Herald the 9-again rule to one roll made to avoid obstacles that would prevent him from reaching his fated goals. This Oath is dissolved when the Herald completes his task. Herald's do not give their Oath lightly.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Prime 2<br /> <br /> A Herald versed in the Prime Arcanum can also use the strength of his Oath to shrug off spells that would hinder him in his task. The Herald can reflexively roll Resolve+Composure to resist spells that would block him from his destiny. Each success acts as a success in a <i>Counterspell Prime</i> effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>2nd: Find the Path</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 5, Fate 3, Space 1, Destiny 2<br /> <br /> The Herald can sense the path that he is fated to take and is guided by a wisdom that transcends conscious intelligence. The mage meditates on his purpose or prays to the gods and just starts off in the direction that feels right. Fate guides the Herald's Path and each success on a Wits+Composure+Fate roll lets the Herald set one condition to the path found. For example, three successes would let a Herald find a path that is quickest, safest, and avoids detection. Each success also grants the 8-again quality on rolls that actively help the Herald in pursuing his tasks.<br /> <br /> Alternately, after casting an augury, each success on a Wits+Composure+Fate roll grants the Herald one cryptic clue aboutwhat lies in store on his or another's path.<br /> <br /> <u><b>3rd: Divine Gauntlet</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 7, Fate 4, Destiny 3<br /> <br /> It is true that Heralds have the reputation of being trustworthy in seeing messages and travelers delivered to their destinations, but they also have the reputation of making the lives of their charges <i>interesting</i> in wild and bizarre ways. To the Heralds, life is a journey that is meant to test and refine one's soul, an alchemical transformation that is meant to end in the perfection of Ascension. Experienced Heralds learn to accelerate this process, inducing tests of their mettle by drawing down their Destiny from the Supernal Realms. In an Instant action, a Herald with this Attainment makes an impassioned plea to the heavens, rolling Presence+Expression+Fate. Each success grants the Herald a point of the Destiny Merit and an opportunity to gain the rote quality on one roll while under the effects of this Attainment. The Herald's life from that moment takes on the quality of a partial Mystery Play, wherein every event has hidden meaning. Every point of experience gained during the Gauntlet gains an accompanying point of Arcane experience. Destiny twists and roils around a Herald on his Gauntlet and Fate or Time divinations meant to reveal the lesson of the Gauntlet fail automatically. The Storyteller is encouraged to make life very strange for the Herald and test him in ways meant to strike at his greatest flaws. The Divine Gauntlet is of indeterminate length, only ending when the Herald has learned an important lesson. The Bane that is gained from the increased Destiny should not be known and should haunt the Herald as part of the lesson. Heralds are not guaranteed survival of their Gauntlets and often lose things that are very dear to them. Fate does not spare loved ones.<br /> <br /> Heralds on their Gauntlets know that people around them are at risk for the bizarre and wild turns of Fate that plague them, and consequently give discounts for their services for the duration. The end of a Gauntlet is heralded by an Astral Journey wherein the Herald meets with his Daimon in the form of his patron Deity, the incarnation of his personal Divine Path.<br /> <br /> Heralds have been known to invoke the Divine Gauntlet in dire emergencies just for the Destiny and rote quality benefits, but such an insult of Fate is not forgiven lightly. The Gauntlets of these Heralds tend to be . . harrowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:38:12-07:00","id":668367,"title":"","content":"That's a cool legacy Ophid, Space is the first thing I think of when I think of magic travel but it wouldn't have made sense with your legacy and all. Hey, what would you add to ramp those two legacies up to 2e?<br /> <br /> Also just jotting some thoughts down here for a Faustian legacy...thinking Fate/Space right now. The idea is that the Mage is the &quot;devil&quot; in the bargain, it's about less about screwing others over (Though you could) and more about reaching higher via contract enforced cooperation. The process of joining the legacy involves signing up for a special contract.<br /> <br /> First attainment is probably something along the lines of an instant Fate Knowing when someone breaks a contract made by anyone in the legacy either the Mage or the contractee. This allows the legacy to crack down hard on anyone who tries a double cross and keeps their ranks honest (mostly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:19:12-07:00","id":668614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=668367#post668367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a cool legacy Ophid, Space is the first thing I think of when I think of magic travel but it wouldn't have made sense with your legacy and all. Hey, what would you add to ramp those two legacies up to 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm currently working on updating my Legacies to 2ed, but it's a pretty busy month for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=668367#post668367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also just jotting some thoughts down here for a Faustian legacy...thinking Fate/Space right now. The idea is that the Mage is the &quot;devil&quot; in the bargain, it's about less about screwing others over (Though you could) and more about reaching higher via contract enforced cooperation. The process of joining the legacy involves signing up for a special contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think about a Reaper Legacy that binds people into selling their souls in exchange for certain blessings?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=668367#post668367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First attainment is probably something along the lines of an instant Fate Knowing when someone breaks a contract made by anyone in the legacy either the Mage or the contractee. This allows the legacy to crack down hard on anyone who tries a double cross and keeps their ranks honest (mostly).</div> </div> </div> </div>As well as maybe being able to read someone's curses, blessings, geasa, and Destiny like the legalistic Fate lawyers they are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:47:29-07:00","id":668766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=668614#post668614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about a Reaper Legacy that binds people into selling their souls in exchange for certain blessings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did a legacy like that earlier on this thread with Death and Space. It rendered Sleepers more useful to the Mage and granted a sort of pseudo-Mage Sight, pseudo-Sleepwalker status and then an upgrade to a sort of Proximi to the Sleeper. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy/page6\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...m-legacy/page6</a><br /> <br /> This one would be broader and less obviously Left-Handed. It feels very Mastigos to me, delving into the possibilities both malignant and benign in making deals. I feel like while they deal with Blessings, Curses and the like it's kind of a byproduct of the deal itself rather than what they actually study. I also don't want to make the knowledge they can access too broad. I could see my way to including an Unveiling effect that marks studied targets as under binding mystical contracts or not though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-17-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:07:04-07:00","id":726534,"title":"","content":"I don't have it fully fleshed out yet, but I rather like a Mind legacy based on a sort of sacrifice of self to propel other people to greater wisdom through causing them to self-reflect. It would borrow somewhat from Evangelion in terms of &quot;you as you see yourself, you as others see you, and you as you'd see yourself if you met yourself&quot;<br /> <br /> Attainment 1: feel as the target feels (emotional urging on self that auto matches the target, but lose access to your own unless multithreading your thoughts)<br /> -optional Time component: not just as the target currently feels, but as the target <i>would </i>feel if viewing events from your perspective<br /> <br /> Attainment 2: remember as the target remembers (temporarily treat targets memories relevent to the situation as your own, but lose access to your own unless multithreading your thoughts)<br /> -optional Time component: compare what they remember to what they thought at the time it was happening<br /> <br /> Attainment 3: think as the target thinks (fullscale temporary personality rewrite on self, other than smoothing over confusion about different bodies and such. lose access to your own personality unless multithreading your thoughts)<br /> -optional Time component: not just who they are, but who they could have been had their life taken a different path<br /> <br /> note the constant references to multithreading thoughts, part of the sacrifice that allows this legacies to use higher level magic than normal in their attainments (much like certain left handed legacies) is the utter necessity of constantly keeping up a multithreading spell if they want to continue existing as a their own person. Especially because the attainments activate automatically regardless of their will","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:38:53-08:00","id":761635,"title":"","content":"Not sure if I'm doing it right since I've only been reading Mage for a few years, but I did have one idea, but I'm not sure how OP it is, though I do have ideas for adding weaknesses. It's actually a very simple and sought after concept.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Arcane Soul</b></u><br /> A Legacy first created by a Moros seeking Immortality, the &quot;Arcane Soul&quot; manages to tap into the essence of the Mages soul using a combination of Death, Life and Prime Arcana. The premise is thus, the Arcane Soul has discovered a way to &quot;Feed&quot; their soul Mana to extend their life, stopping the ageing process and granting resistance/immunity to illness and disease. The Legacy is incredibly difficult to acquire and maintain. Obviously, this would require very high ranks in the three mentioned Arcana, possibly 5 in each or higher, but I have considered the following factors for the Legacy.<br /> <br /> 1. A steady supply of Mana is required to postpone the ageing process. A personal Sanctum/Demensa and Hallow are practically essential.<br /> 2. The Soul of an &quot;Arcane Soul&quot; acquires a tremendous luminocity, I figure this could be a weakness as anyone using Mage Sight could detect and track the Mage at great range. This great luminosity could also enhance another Mages sympathy when trying to cast spells on the Arcane Soul, their Mana fed soul now a magnet for spells.<br /> 3. Immortality is much sought after, and conversely, others may see this as an abomination. Arcane Souls will often have to watch their back and guard their secrets well.<br /> 4. Vampires could see Arcane Souls as rivals. The Abyss may also take an interest in this Legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Feeding</b><br /> Arcane Souls must conduct a ritual of &quot;Soul Feeding&quot; from a source of mana, mainly a Hallow, which can take several forms, but often involves the Mage capturing and channelling Mana and &quot;processing&quot; it to be absorbed into their soul. When a Mage does this, it typically resembles the mage performing ritualized body gestures, like martial arts practices, but another form is like a form of meditation or like a form of Feng Shui. The mana visibly follows the Mages movements if they use a physical form of ritual, but in all forms, the Mana floats around and reforms, depending on the Mage. For example, a Moros mage performing their Soul Feeding could shape their mana into ghostly images or into transparent forms of matter that change shape before being absorbed. A Mastigos might cause their Mana to form into leering demonic faces, eyes of various forms or to cause visible distortions and ripples in space. The Mage must &quot;feed&quot; their soul every week or month, depending on the potency of the Mage, their processing technique, their focus, the quality of their Hallow, and so forth.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ethics of Immortality</b><br /> Many Mages have often debated the ethics of becoming immortal in the Fallen World, but the original idea behind the Arcane Soul, by it's Moros creator, was that the Mage wished to help Mages and Sleepers alike, and would choose to die when they felt they had done enough. Many would find it ironic that a Moros would seek immortality, but the creator of this Legacy posits that no matter how hard you try to elude Death, it will always find you, the Arcane Soul simply has a say in when. Such a Legacy could be abused and be no more than a would-be Tyrants means to an end, and so the secrets of the Legacy would be guarded well and taught only to those deemed worthy.<br /> <br /> <b>Not Indestructible</b><br /> An Arcane Soul is not indestructible, they do not age and do not easily fall sick, but they can still be killed by violence. Depending on the mastery of the Legacy, an Arcane Soul would still also require food and water and oxygen to breath, but a possibly exalted master of the Legacy could possibly require only the mana which feeds their soul. It could also be possible that an Arcane Soul of any level can stave of the need for physical sustenance if they feed themselves enough mana during their Soul Feeding, but a small portion at Soul Feeding would not sustain the physical body on it's own.<br /> <br /> <br /> If anyone has ideas on strengths and weaknesses I could apply to this Legacy, both in terms of lore and game mechanics, please share your thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:55:44-08:00","id":761644,"title":"","content":"It's not impossible, but it wild probably help you a lot (and those of us interested in giving advice) if you tried to develop attainments?<br /> <br /> Plus, do you want it in 1e or 2e format? For instance drawing mana into yourself in 1e is 3 dots if you're doing it as a spell instead of as a meditation at a Hallow. In 2e my guess is it would only be a 2 dot, maybe even 1 dot Prime effect.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry too much about weaknesses to start off with by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-09-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:00:02-08:00","id":761744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=761644#post761644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not impossible, but it wild probably help you a lot (and those of us interested in giving advice) if you tried to develop attainments?<br /> <br /> Plus, do you want it in 1e or 2e format? For instance drawing mana into yourself in 1e is 3 dots if you're doing it as a spell instead of as a meditation at a Hallow. In 2e my guess is it would only be a 2 dot, maybe even 1 dot Prime effect.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry too much about weaknesses to start off with by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I have not gotten around to the attainments yet, I was waiting for some input on the concept of the Legacy before I went further, it just took me a while to get around to registering here. I was mostly worried about a Legacy that makes you immortal being considered OP or in poor taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:53:39-08:00","id":761783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Proteus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=761744#post761744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I have not gotten around to the attainments yet, I was waiting for some input on the concept of the Legacy before I went further, it just took me a while to get around to registering here. I was mostly worried about a Legacy that makes you immortal being considered OP or in poor taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really not OP. The thing is that unless you're completely immortal except by your Achilles heel, then your immortality isn't going to have a big impact on the game because unless the chronicle takes a lot of big time jumps it just won't come up.<br /> <br /> That's part of the reason that the Tremere Liches are considered a subpar legacy mechanically speaking.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing that's been constant in nWoD is that immortality comes at a cost. If you're using mana to fuel your Pattern beyond its normal limitations an idea for that is that your legacy could be experts at finding and completely draining Hallows. Since Hallows are highly valued resources as fonts of mana and access points to the Astral that would give them an excellent reason to stay on the down low. That would be over and above normal Mage suspicion of immortals. It probably would also mean they need to be decent at getting into guarded territory in order to drain a Hallow, and also at getting from place to place because Hallows are not terribly common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T09:13:54-08:00","id":762352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Proteus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=761635#post761635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if I'm doing it right since I've only been reading Mage for a few years, but I did have one idea, but I'm not sure how OP it is, though I do have ideas for adding weaknesses. It's actually a very simple and sought after concept.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Arcane Soul</b></u><br /> A Legacy first created by a Moros seeking Immortality, the &quot;Arcane Soul&quot; manages to tap into the essence of the Mages soul using a combination of Death, Life and Prime Arcana. The premise is thus, the Arcane Soul has discovered a way to &quot;Feed&quot; their soul Mana to extend their life, stopping the ageing process and granting resistance/immunity to illness and disease. The Legacy is incredibly difficult to acquire and maintain. Obviously, this would require very high ranks in the three mentioned Arcana, possibly 5 in each or higher, but I have considered the following factors for the Legacy.<br /> <br /> 1. A steady supply of Mana is required to postpone the ageing process. A personal Sanctum/Demensa and Hallow are practically essential.<br /> 2. The Soul of an &quot;Arcane Soul&quot; acquires a tremendous luminocity, I figure this could be a weakness as anyone using Mage Sight could detect and track the Mage at great range. This great luminosity could also enhance another Mages sympathy when trying to cast spells on the Arcane Soul, their Mana fed soul now a magnet for spells.<br /> 3. Immortality is much sought after, and conversely, others may see this as an abomination. Arcane Souls will often have to watch their back and guard their secrets well.<br /> 4. Vampires could see Arcane Souls as rivals. The Abyss may also take an interest in this Legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Feeding</b><br /> Arcane Souls must conduct a ritual of &quot;Soul Feeding&quot; from a source of mana, mainly a Hallow, which can take several forms, but often involves the Mage capturing and channelling Mana and &quot;processing&quot; it to be absorbed into their soul. When a Mage does this, it typically resembles the mage performing ritualized body gestures, like martial arts practices, but another form is like a form of meditation or like a form of Feng Shui. The mana visibly follows the Mages movements if they use a physical form of ritual, but in all forms, the Mana floats around and reforms, depending on the Mage. For example, a Moros mage performing their Soul Feeding could shape their mana into ghostly images or into transparent forms of matter that change shape before being absorbed. A Mastigos might cause their Mana to form into leering demonic faces, eyes of various forms or to cause visible distortions and ripples in space. The Mage must &quot;feed&quot; their soul every week or month, depending on the potency of the Mage, their processing technique, their focus, the quality of their Hallow, and so forth.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ethics of Immortality</b><br /> Many Mages have often debated the ethics of becoming immortal in the Fallen World, but the original idea behind the Arcane Soul, by it's Moros creator, was that the Mage wished to help Mages and Sleepers alike, and would choose to die when they felt they had done enough. Many would find it ironic that a Moros would seek immortality, but the creator of this Legacy posits that no matter how hard you try to elude Death, it will always find you, the Arcane Soul simply has a say in when. Such a Legacy could be abused and be no more than a would-be Tyrants means to an end, and so the secrets of the Legacy would be guarded well and taught only to those deemed worthy.<br /> <br /> <b>Not Indestructible</b><br /> An Arcane Soul is not indestructible, they do not age and do not easily fall sick, but they can still be killed by violence. Depending on the mastery of the Legacy, an Arcane Soul would still also require food and water and oxygen to breath, but a possibly exalted master of the Legacy could possibly require only the mana which feeds their soul. It could also be possible that an Arcane Soul of any level can stave of the need for physical sustenance if they feed themselves enough mana during their Soul Feeding, but a small portion at Soul Feeding would not sustain the physical body on it's own.<br /> <br /> <br /> If anyone has ideas on strengths and weaknesses I could apply to this Legacy, both in terms of lore and game mechanics, please share your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok so you definitely have <b>what</b> you legacy does, now you need a <b>how.</b> Unlike Paths, Legacies do have a culture built into them, specific rituals and trappings encoded into the Legacy by the founder.<br /> <br /> Mrmdubois makes a good point about there being a cost to immortality. Among those will be the possibility of being labeled a Left Handed Legacy. They will certainly be classified as Liches, as is any Legacy that cheats death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:23:46-08:00","id":762394,"title":"","content":"If they're not required to kill people or reap souls then usually they'd only get branded Left Handed for political reasons (The 2nd most popular cause of &quot;bad&quot; Mages).<br /> <br /> He really doesn't have what they do down either though, it's all very vague right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:12:27-08:00","id":762441,"title":"","content":"Another source of mana can also be gained via sacrifice. Members of the legacy who get the mana to fuel themselves that way would definitely be Left Handed.<br /> <br /> I actually just had some ideas about Attainments, I'm thinking Prime/Life<br /> <br /> 1st spend a mana to Know the nearest and largest source of mana in m sensory range. Your dots in Prime count as Potency toward piercing any magical concealment. Life: You may add the Life arcanum to your Mage Sight for free and by spending a point of mana you may find sources of life that may be sacrificed for mans in the same way that the Prime par of this attainment functions.<br /> <br /> I need to detail this out more, but the last attainment would involve creating (Making) an empty clone body, if you put a soul stone into it then if you die the soul stone will anchor you to the clone body and bring you back. Of course since the last attainment takes Gnosis 8 you could maintain only 2 of these backups at a time. <br /> <br /> Some of the stuff I'm thinking of for the middle attainments are some control or protection methods to help with survivability and some limited shape shifting fueled by and to benefit more from making sacrifices for mana.<br /> <br /> The 4th attainment I'm toying with is kind of a play on the Tass spell Dave spoiled. You can turn yourself into a being of pure mana for the scene thus halting aging, the need to eat, sleep or breath. However to perform mundane tasks (Make a skill or ability check) you have to spend a point of mana or take a point of Bashing as this purified form is corrupted by the Fallen world. The Life optional would expand your transformative option a little bit by letting you turn your mana body into the form of something you had sacrificed previously which gives you cool extra abilities or enhances your ability to impersonate people whose mana resources you might be targeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-10-2015, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T21:32:51-08:00","id":762828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=158976#post158976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was about to delete them when I woke up this morning, thinking &quot;maybe this is a tad too extreme&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, the hatred that's targeted towards them is kind of the point. They're typically immature and disrespectful mages who most likely Awakened before they were old enough to truly comprehend what that entails. And no, it wasn't intended to be a joke, just like the Malkavian's weren't intended to be the jesters of Vampirism. This is a Gothic Horror game, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wasn't aware of the requirements needed to create / join a Legacy, but now that I do, I may be able to come up with better ones in the future. Though why do you say that The Supremely Focused wouldn't survive long enough to pass it on?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I apologize if the content I came up with was too extreme. I'm not sure the exact limits of what most player considers to be over the line when it comes to the mature themes of this game. I watched a gaming session for Werewolf, in which the PC's are attacked during a high-school shooting by spirit ridden assailants. I've also seen a Sabbat game session involving stuff that was straight up twisted, which I won't be repeating here.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e is quite different from 2e where legacies are involved. In 1e they're limited for dumb reasons while having ridiculous gnosis entry requirements. Why do you have to have gnosis 3 or 4 to just barely start your journey? Stupid. Why can't you have a legacy useful in direct combat? It's all about weak attainments focused on the investigation and social game....seriously? <br /> <br /> 2e is open season, you want to be a Fireball using, magic carpet riding, teleporter....Obrimos with a legacy that gives you Space as your third primary Arcanum. <br /> <br /> You start a gnosis 2 with any 1 or 2 dot spell effect possible and at gnosis 4 it's 3 dots, at gnosis 6 it's 4 dots, at gnosis 8 it's 5 dots.<br /> <br /> Don't be scared because legacy attainments don't get reach. So if you really want to go big you should either have most your legacy attainments as rotes or praxis if possible. Yeah, you risk paradox but you get reach. Seems like a decent tradeoff to me.<br /> <br /> Curious, why have an attainment with mana cost that's a simple variation of a typical Prime/Space alarm spell in the core book that doesn't cost mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 11-11-2015, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T21:47:17-08:00","id":762834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=762441#post762441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another source of mana can also be gained via sacrifice. Members of the legacy who get the mana to fuel themselves that way would definitely be Left Handed.<br /> <br /> I actually just had some ideas about Attainments, I'm thinking Prime/Life<br /> <br /> 1st spend a mana to Know the nearest and largest source of mana in m sensory range. Your dots in Prime count as Potency toward piercing any magical concealment. Life: You may add the Life arcanum to your Mage Sight for free and by spending a point of mana you may find sources of life that may be sacrificed for mans in the same way that the Prime par of this attainment functions.<br /> <br /> I need to detail this out more, but the last attainment would involve creating (Making) an empty clone body, if you put a soul stone into it then if you die the soul stone will anchor you to the clone body and bring you back. Of course since the last attainment takes Gnosis 8 you could maintain only 2 of these backups at a time. <br /> <br /> Some of the stuff I'm thinking of for the middle attainments are some control or protection methods to help with survivability and some limited shape shifting fueled by and to benefit more from making sacrifices for mana.<br /> <br /> The 4th attainment I'm toying with is kind of a play on the Tass spell Dave spoiled. You can turn yourself into a being of pure mana for the scene thus halting aging, the need to eat, sleep or breath. However to perform mundane tasks (Make a skill or ability check) you have to spend a point of mana or take a point of Bashing as this purified form is corrupted by the Fallen world. The Life optional would expand your transformative option a little bit by letting you turn your mana body into the form of something you had sacrificed previously which gives you cool extra abilities or enhances your ability to impersonate people whose mana resources you might be targeting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mana cost isn't needed given it's a heavy duty Prime attainment. Just make Life optional (likely 2-5) as extra options. Sacrifice shouldn't be needed unless it's a left hand legacy and gives you something seriously awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T01:13:42-08:00","id":762908,"title":"","content":"I said Life was the optional I was running with right now.<br /> <br /> Attainments cost a mana to activate now if I remember correctly from the devblog so it doesn't matter if it's heavily Prime based.<br /> <br /> I think the ability to shapeshift into things you've sacrificed actually is pretty awesome considering the actual reason a member of this legacy (As I've thought of it so far) commits a sacrifice is for mana to fuel their immortality. This is a cool extra benefit to sacrifice in other words. Plus, like I mentioned, if you're sacrificing people to gain your mana and to impersonate them that's Left Handed. It's Left Handed optional, because you don't have to be evil and sacrifice people and you'd still get great benefit out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T02:29:07-08:00","id":762947,"title":"","content":"Gonna try to get more organized and add in a few extra ideas.<br /> <br /> 1st: Prime: Spend a point of mana and pinpoint the location of the nearest and largest source of mana in sensory Range. Dots in the Prime arcana count as Potency towards piercing magical concealment effects.<br /> <br /> Life: Add Life to your Mage Sight for free. In addition the location of creatures within sensory Range that can be sacrificed for mana are also revealed. This doesn't reveal what type of creature they are, but does reveal the amount(s) of mana they can be sacrificed for.<br /> <br /> 2nd: Prime: Spend a point of mana and raise a Veil with a Potency equal to your Dots in Prime that helps to conceal your true nature. The Veil hides the mana in your Pattern and also activation of further powers such as other attainments or the casting of spells.<br /> <br /> Life: Spend the point of mana and take control of a target in a fashion similar to Trigger the Lizard Brain from 1e. <br /> <br /> 3rd: Arcane Soul's often find themselves needing to stockpile stores of mana to continue to fuel their existence. This attainment lets them create Tass (Use the spell Dave spoiled as the template).<br /> <br /> Life: I haven't had a good idea for this yet. Maybe something like he is more efficient at committing a sacrifice and receives double the usual mana from it.<br /> <br /> 4th: By spending a point of mana the Mage may turn himself into a hybrid of pure mana and his living form for a scene. This purified form does not need to eat, sleep, breath and does not age. Any mundane action that is undertaken by the Mage (I.e. requires a die roll) costs the Mage either a point of mana or causes a point of Bashing damage (Mage's choice). This attainment is considered by many members of the legacy to be the goal they truly seek. Unfortunately, the fact that the effect is short-lived necessitates a constant supply of mana to fuel it.<br /> <br /> Life: When the Mage turns into his purified mana form he also has the option of paying a point of mana to take the form of a creature he has sacrificed instead. This includes people if the Mage has turned to human sacrifice.<br /> <br /> 5th: Haven't had a good idea here yet. Maybe allow the Arcane Soul to extend his time in purified form while in a Hallow at the cost of Unmaking it. Seems sort of lame though.<br /> <br /> Life: The Mage may create comatose duplicate of himself. This is a living body and so requires further magic or mundane life support to maintain or it won't survive on its own. The body is usually a copy of the Mage's own, but there's no restriction on this. If the Mage places a soulstone inside his duplicate then if he should die his soul will anchor to the duplicate. He may then activate it to come back to life in the duplicate body. Because of the high level of Gnosis needed to access this attainment no Arcane Soul maintains more than two of these duplicates at a time. The soulstone from this process may be reused.<br /> <br /> I think overall this is a really good mix of investigator for what the AS are specifically interested in, some stealth and control to make it easier to sneak or manipulate themselves towards what they want, a way to ensure their future and to achieve actual short lived immortality and then finally a much longer lasting form of immortality. I've got a couple attainments in there that are basically dud space right now unfortunately. I need to think about them more.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the weaknesses of the legacy should be pretty readily apparent. The 4th attainment requires a lot of mana to maintain while also obviously being one of the most desired effects of the legacy. If they've managed to stockpile a lot of Tass they can keep it up for a while but eventually they'll run out unless they stay constantly on the search for more sources of mana. Hopefully, that puts some pressure on them to make ethically dubious choices, but you could also play a pretty lax AS who exalts in his purified form but stays in it for much more reasonable periods of time. Aside from that is also the temptation to commit sacrifices for increased breadth of power. Sacrifices are usually considered in poor taste, but they're allowed. Switch up to humans for the bigger amount of mana though and you will get hunted down (Especially since you can sacrifice a Mage for even more mana). The last attainment adds an additional cost to immortality in the form of soulstones. I actually really like this one because at Gnosis 10 a Mage might be able to manifest the final attainment of his legacy and ascend. So by seeking immortality in the Fallen the Mage is deliberately preventing himself from realizing his actual, true potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T05:38:56-08:00","id":763980,"title":"","content":"My apologies for not responding sooner. Anyway, I've read the suggestions and feedback on the framework for my Arcane Soul Legacy and I've been using it to adjust the concept and consider it's attainments, history and culture. I won't be posting it all just yet as I'm still working on it. As for Mrmdubois's ideas, the idea of attaining a &quot;Pure Mana Form&quot; does not fit my original intention for the Legacy, but I did consider that it could be it's own Legacy, possibly with links to the Arcane Soul legacy either as something vaguely related or something encountered by the Arcane Souls or as a divergent path of it. I like the &quot;Mana Leech&quot; idea, and considering the Pure Mana Form idea, what would a Mana Leech/Vampire see when they encounter a being made purely of mana? A mana Form Legacy could potentially come into conflict with a more Left Handed divergence of the Arcane Soul who steals and leeches mana.<br /> <br /> The most important thing I've concluded based on the input in this thread is different &quot;Tiers&quot; of Immortality and feeding through the Arcane Soul Legacy. Basically, a low-maintenance practice of the Arcane Soul Legacy merely stops ageing, simply sipping feeding the soul just enough to get by does not impart any additional effects, and such a Mage could potentially live as an immortal hermit if they have their own Hallow and Sanctum/Demesne are are careful and self reliant.<br /> <br /> The more they feed their soul at each feeding, the more benefits they gain, and therein lies the possibility for hubris and corruption, as an Arcane Soul who drinks deeply could become superhuman or almost god-like. I figure at it's greatest extreme, an Arcane Soul could drain Hallows dry, absorbing truly vast amounts of mana in a single feeding and becoming very powerful and allowing them to stave off death for extended periods before required to feed again. I've roughly brainstormed a few Tiers of feeding.<br /> <br /> 1. Minimal feeding. Ageing stops but otherwise require food, water and oxygen and sleep. Minor resistance to disease. Must feed lightly every few days.<br /> 2. Second tier of feeding. Ageing stops and become immune to disease. Food, water, oxygen and sleep are still required. Must feed moderately every week.<br /> 3. Third tier of feeding. Ageing stops, immunity to disease and physical needs no longer apply.(food, water, oxygen, sleep). Must feed on large amounts of mana every year.<br /> 4. Fourth tier of feeding. Ageing stops, immunity to disease and physical needs. Gain enhanced spellcasting. Must feed every 2 years. Inordinate amounts of mana required for feeding. Risks disrupting or depleting Sanctum defences. At this Tier onward the Arcane Soul gains &quot;Soul Luminosity&quot;, causing their soul to shine brighter than others and imparting some weaknesses.<br /> 5. Fifth tier of feeding. Ageing stops, immunity to disease and physical needs, enhanced spellcasting and physical and mental attributes. Must feed every 5 years. Vast amounts of mana required for feeding. A Hallow or Sanctum risks being destroyed completely.<br /> 6. Final Tier of feeding. Ageing stops, immunity to disease and physical needs, enhanced spellcasting and greatly enhanced physical/mental attributes, resistance to damage. Must feed every decade. Requires vast amounts of mana, such as from draining a Hallow dry.<br /> <br /> Besides these benefits based on feeding, Arcane Souls could gain abilities that allow them to potentially absorb some or all of a spells power, or in some cases, to drain the mana from living things that possess it, like a Vampire. I plan on writing up details on divergent forms of the Arcane Soul and a lot of drama in the Legacies history. Long story short, the original creator of the Legacy intended for it to be used for good, but over the years some have abused and distorted it, and the entire Arcane Soul spectrum suffers for it.<br /> <br /> Weaknesses from Soul Luminosity could involve things like being easier to see and track with spells and mage sight, making it harder to resist certain spells due to sympathy aquired by &quot;Locking on&quot; to the Arcane Soul's brightly shining soul.<br /> <br /> I have also considered the Tremere Liches as the arch-enemies of the Legacy, who find an Arcane Souls soul especially nourishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T08:13:52-08:00","id":764066,"title":"","content":"The problem, as I see it is what defines these feeding tiers? Are they modeled off of spell's? If so which ones? Is it just a side benefit of being in the legacy and not related to its actual attainments (An option I actually considered because of the low mechanical value of immortality, but rejected because I don't think legacies should work like that.)? If it is part of the attainments how do you justify it within the 13 practices, and fit it inside the 5 attainment limit? Also I think as you rise in tiers as you have them you should be required to feed more, otherwise maintaining immortality loses its sense of urgency. One Hallow every decade is hardly a sacrifice.<br /> <br /> By the way, what's the problem with a purified mana form? It nets you the benefits you're asking for, immunity to disease, age, physical needs, etc. it's just difficult to maintain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-12-2015, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T09:11:41-08:00","id":764118,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a couple 1e legacies (which I <i>thought</i> I posted on here or the last forum, but who knows?) that <i>relate</i> to that theme.<br /> <br /> Mine 'em for ideas, use 'em, ignore 'em. Whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Famished</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Their souls strive ever upward, but they find their body literally requires the touch of the supernal to survive.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Path:</b> None<br /> <b>Order:</b> Mysterium or Guardians of the Veil</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Free Council has a branch, as well. Investigations by the Guardians have no explanation; No breach of security or link to any known member ever surfaced. Apparently some Councilor spontaneously joined this legacy. That didn't stop the Guardians from attempting to contain that branch. FC Famished can expect to be hunted by even the Guardians who accept the legacy as valid.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Oblations:</b> Performing acts of refined creation, inspiring others through art or personal council; Helping someone find True love; Teaching the Mysteries</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1st: Sublimation</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Req.: Gnosis 3, Prime 2, Dream 2</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The need for higher things makes the famished soul lean on mana as a source of higher power. The Famished may, at any time, spend a mana to reconnect, momentarily, to the supernal. This expenditure normally lasts for a single action, but that can be an extended action. The act is known as &quot;refining&quot; the act, or &quot;empowering.&quot; Refining acts mundane or opposed to the supernal realms can still work, as it reveals them to be such.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">For each level of Dream that the Famished bears, the Famished must refine an act throughout the course of the day. Failure to do so causes <i>breathing</i>to fade in significance, requiring mana or suffocation. Refining breathing only lasts for a scene, until the requirement has been met. The character's personal deadline can be defined by the storyteller or the player, but remains fixed. Midnight is a reasonable choice. So are dawn &amp; noon.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Famished must refine the act of eating, or it provides no nourishment. Any scene in which the Famished eats without refining his consumption, the food passes on without being absorbed. The famished excretes as if they digested that meal while starving, but all nutritional value is lost. This does, obviously, count towards refinement in a day.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">To anyone who has had contact with the supernal, contact with the Famished invokes a lesser longing, as well. Essentially any use of the skill Empathy, for example, on one of the Famished automatically causes memories of the supernal to resurface in that user.</span> Famished using Expression trigger such things as well. The Famished always feels this; such contact shares it in a lighter form. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The cost of any supernal magic directed at the Famished increases by one mana. The caster is intuitively aware of the increased cost as part of forming their Imago, and may pay it, if they have the capacity to do so. If not, the spell automatically fails, and the caster takes a distraction penalty equal to the Dream rating of the target Famished for the rest of the scene as they are assaulted by scenes from their awakening or any other supernal experience. If a caster does pay the surcharge, the Famished is briefly refreshed, momentarily connected to supernal. This restores a willpower point or,if that pool is full, a point of mana, as a result.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Optional : Mind 1</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">If a refined action fulfills the Famished's virtue, the result restores a mana per point of Dream or rank of Prime, whichever is lower, as well as the normal willpower.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2nd: Osmosis</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Req.: Gnosis 5, Prime 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Attempts to contact the Famished Soul shares the need for supernal power before any other contact may be made. This strong draw means that any attempts to touch the Famished soul with active magic, which even includes scrutiny with Mage Sight, requires an increased mana cost. The cost increases by two mana or, when the Famished's soul itself is the target, by the Dream rating of the Famished.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Furthermore, whether due to some form of scarring or exercise, the Famished Soul is far sturdier than normal. Attempts to manipulate it are not merely more expensive, they are harder to accomplish. Any activation rolls made to target the Famished Soul are penalized by the soul's Dream rating.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Non-supernal contact transfers a similar need, sympathetically, as well. This is interpreted differently by different types of souls. The common theme is that the psyche of the affected one suddenly shares a need for a concrete connection to a higher nature or purpose.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prometheans associate this longing to the Magnum Opus; Vampires usually associate it to blood, because that is stolen life, though some of the more mystically minded may feel it as part of their magic. Others associate it with all the noble things that they lost, such as the sun. Werewolves generally link it to a patron spirit. The effect hits hard, though.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Without success finding something that excites the draw to the Supernal, these characters temporarily gain or exacerbate the derangement Depression, or other effect appropriate for needing to find a higher purpose. This is not an attack and is not perceived as one, but rather a sort of common feeling. If this impulse can be acted upon within a scene per dot of Composure, this effect never takes place. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Optional : Mind 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Any supernatural contact with the Famished's mind, soul, or emotions leads those who made the contact stuck with a lingering longing for higher things. This lasts a day per level of the Famished's Mind + the interloper's Intelligence.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The longing represents a need to feel higher things, beyond normal considerations. Failure to achieve success in touching the supernal costs a point of Composure each day, which heals as resistant Aggravated wound. Failure to even attempt to contact also deals a loss of Stamina. These are cumulative and lasting, but only a single event is required to allow healing. The problem is that the need is for a thing that may well be unrecognized by the one feeling it. Seeking is enough to avoid the worst of this, it's true, but success requires that a character find some sublime truth.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">For Sleepers and creatures unfamiliar with higher concepts, merely seeking out sublime art or religious experience can be enough, but it must be profound. Most is insufficient. True love certainly functions. Awakening is a distinct possibility from the search.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">For creatures with souls or spirits bound apart from the supernal in some way, such as werewolves, this requires that they seek insight from higher things. Quests deep into shadow to speak with celestial creatures certainly qualifies.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">For magi, this is actually simultaneously easier and harsher. For their partial knowledge of the truth leaves them only allowed to use quests for supernal truth, but they know exactly what it is that they crave.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">(Alternately: The mind is hardened, as well, requiring the extra mana be spent to manipulate the mind or emotions. Those that cannot spend mana are less affected, and may overcome the need instilled by spending a willpower.)</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3rd: Parched Soul</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Req.: Gnosis 7, Prime 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Unless the Famished has full mana, his soul draws it from around itself every round. This literally is <i>no </i>action on the part of the character and cannot be suppressed. The least resistant source is drawn from first. The Famished's Mana capacity is also increased by Prime + Willpower rating.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Resistances are defined as follows: (Use this as a guideline to define any types missed.)<br /> The effective resistance increases by one if not in direct contact, and then by a further one per yard away.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Free mana is the most available. Entering the area of a Hallow drains a point of mana and deactivates that ambient mana reduction when this effect is active. Tass and vessels made for sharing tass are next. These both count as having a resistance of 0, however. Artifact resistances are their rating -5, but this can be modified by the function of the artifact.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">After this is mana stored as part of patterns. Objects use their Structure as their Resistance, while Mages use their Gnosis. Ravens with this second attainment add their Dream to their Resistance. Sleepers with mana injected into their patterns have no resistance. Spells cast use their potency, but only mana spend funding them (and not the cost from this attainment or that used to suppress Paradox) can be drawn.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Optional Mind 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Mana and willpower are interchangeable when mana rating is full. The limits on which types can be spent per round and per action, but the a mana spent can be used as a willpower or vice versa.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Furthermore, whenever willpower is fully refreshed through a virtue, the Famished recovers a mana, and has the option of transforming up to his current (before recovery) pool of willpower into mana. (Limited, of course, by maximum mana capacity.)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Ravenous</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Ravens seek to align their souls to the Far Shores. By doing so, they pick at a scab on their souls\u2014their thirst for higher things. To quench this thirst requires that they use magic and mana in a way other magi cannot. This provides a form of power that most cannot duplicate, either, but it is dangerous..</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Oblations:</b> Gathering mana, transcendental meditations to seek higher truth. Literally, the act of finding links to higher truth and even gathering mana can qualify as a legacy oblation. The requirement is that the search is active and should reveal sublime truth, mana, or both. This means, among other things, that magi practicing their path oblations can roll for their legacy at the same time.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1st: Pangs</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Reqs. Prime 2, Dream 1, Resolve 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The hunger begins. The new raven must face their inner needs head-on before beginning this quest, which requires a strong Resolve. The hunger is for higher truth, and those needs are of a vastly higher priority than the mundane. The soul of the raven absolutely requires the touch of the supernal as a mortal requirement. This means certain mundane actions lose their significance unless refined by some tie to higher truth. As a result, the Raven must perform a refined action per level of Dream, each day, or they begin to suffer from a loss of their connection with the supernal, ceasing to benefit from the merely mundane. Each day of deprivation increases the severity, removing the benefit from a widening array of actions.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Eating is the first act to cease providing benefit without being refined. Then social contact. After that, sleep. Next, water. Finally, breathing. Should they somehow manage to survive, they degrade ever farther, losing mundane senses, and heat from anything but the sun.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The raven may still refine an act to gain benefit from it, even in a degraded state. Fulfilling the requirements for a day lead to the status walking back in severity by one step each day. A Raven thus finds their Dream a mixed blessing, given the rarity of opportunities to engage in sufficiently refined activities.<br /> (Option: Required refinements don't count against the daily total?)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Refining an act requires a tie to a sublime concept, but needn't require anything <i>mystical</i>. Eating provides a great example. Holiday feasts often qualify as something sufficiently profound, though many do not. That depends on the family and attitudes involved. If the Raven cannot achieve the required refinement any other way, a mana can be spent to sanctify it. Those with insight will notice the difference. If one spends the mana and achieves sufficient profundity, the mana is recovered.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The sight of a raven is keen to the Supernal, which functions as Supernal Vision with a potency equal to the Raven's Prime.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">When the dream of a higher reality is brought into the dream of the present, there is a keen moment of connection for anyone touched by it. The raven can grant a glimpse of his need to any other caster through a spell targeting his own pattern. The casting of a spell onto a raven requires that caster to reflexively pay a mana per level of attainment that the raven has achieved. (1 at 1st, 2 at 2nd, 3 at 3rd) The raven can suppress this effect as a reflexive action for a round, but not if the effect targets their mind or soul.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">It is unclear what effect this recollection would have on beings without memory of the higher plane or with the ability to actually visit it. Some posit those without a memory would simply be unaffected, while those who could visit would find themselves either affected as normal or affected with a strong urge to go back. The final answer is, of course, up to the storyteller.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Or, see the &quot;Famished&quot; above for some other thoughts.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2nd: Gaunt</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Reqs. Prime 3, Dream 3, Composure 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The raven's soul is tougher for its clear sight of its own nature and the longstanding trials it endures. The effect is a Soul Shield, but uses the raven's Dream rating as the penalty applied towards the die roll in question. The potency is equal to the mage's Prime.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Attempts to draw mana from the mage's reserve must overcome this penalty, as well, given the strong need the raven has for this connection above. This applies to all mana inside the mage's pattern, and cannot be ignored or suppressed, even when the raven is the party drawing it out. If the mage uses magic to draw and transfer from an external source to an external target, the penalty can be avoided, since the mana never enters the Raven's pattern.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Opt. Mind 3</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The raven's mind is protected as well as his soul. An effect equivalent to Mental Shield, except that it uses Mind as its potency, and Dream as the penalty to such attacks.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3rd: Vortex</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Reqs. Prime 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">When the raven lacks mana in their pattern, their pattern drains it automatically each round. One point per dot of Dream is drained from any given mana containers each round. This does not require an action, but is a standard part of their attainment. Mana is drawn from simplest source to most difficult. The difficulty is based on several factors. Tass and vessels for mana such as artifacts tend to give their mana up the most freely. The resistance of other mages is based on their Gnosis, while objects resist with their Structures. Ravens with the second attainment count as having Gnosis + Dream resistance.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The raven may suppress this effect with concentration when their mana is below maximum, or activate it as a reflexive action even when it is full. This is good for drawing mana into other objects without a spell required to pull the mana free or spending a penalty for combined spell casting.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The raven may also perform a number of Legacy oblations each day equal to Dream. All such oblations must, of course, be refined actions.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Opt Mind 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A raven can no longer regain willpower through any unrefined action. Fulfilling one's virtue provides a point of mana in addition to the refilling of willpower.</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">On refined actions, the raven can spend willpower and mana interchangeably. The raven remains limited to the normal mana limits per round and only one willpower can be spent per action, but the points can come from either pool. (A Raven with this attainment, a temporary willpower pool of 9, and the ability to spend 15 mana per round could take 9 of it from his temporary willpower pool. Only one of those could go towards a standard willpower benefit.)</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":".  Funky formatting finally fixed 11-12-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T13:09:20-07:00","id":884008,"title":"","content":"Right, it's been a few months, but since the core came out I figure people are going to want to dust this topic off. Speaking of which, here are a few Left-Handed ideas I had for antagonists:<br /> <br /> \u2022The Correctionalists: A well-intentioned (but still utterly monstrous) Mastigos Reaper Legacy that, uniquely enough, is less interested in the souls themselves and more the people they've reaped. More specifically, they use Death to both take the soul and then freeze their target's degradation, exploiting both a quirk of soul loss and their optional Mind Attainments to render people exhibiting &quot;unacceptable&quot; or self-destructive behaviors into model members of society. <br /> <br /> \u2022The Dorian Brotherhood: A group of Reapers who can actually use photography, video recordings, and other representational media to steal souls, using Death and Space in order to pull off a &quot;Dorian Grey&quot; sort of immortality, pushing off age, negative Conditions, and breaking points off to the decaying soul-pictures. <br /> <br /> \u2022The Arbiters of Death: A Reaper Legacy of insane &quot;advocates for the dead&quot; who hunt down people who have wronged or dead or who are &quot;unworthy&quot; of life, ripping out their soul, leaving the victim vulnerable to the Possession or Claiming attempts of ghosts the Arbiter has deemed to deserve a second chance at flesh. They then reforge these souls into &quot;living ghosts&quot;, enslaving them as punishment for their &quot;crimes&quot;. <br /> <br /> \u2022The Incarnate Will: A heretical Lich offshoot of the Silver Ladder, members of this Legacy believe that Mages are the nascent divine aspect of humanity, and use Mind not only to direct their worshippers as is their &quot;right&quot;, but also to further their goal to ascend into a Awakened soul clad in nothing but Astral power, a functional deity that &quot;guides&quot; humanity from inside their collective soul.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Cult of a Thousand Eyes: A Left-Handed Legacy that is none the less popular amongst Panopticon (and can pop up in the Guardians from time to time) that forms cults and then use Space to turn the act of worship into a sympathetic link, allowing them to use their followers as anchors and targets for their magic with ease, especially when borrowing their senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:53:16-07:00","id":916932,"title":"","content":"To paraphrase Diane Duane &quot;Fairest and Ascendant, greetings and defiance&quot;<br /> <br /> The Loyal Opposition embrace an unusual juxtaposition of stances: even as they ardently oppose the Exarchs, they honor the &quot;office&quot; which the Exarch's hold and will, to some limited extent, even obey commands from the Exarchs. The Exarchs may corrupt venal tyrants with disagreeable policies, but it is undeniable that they hold the Throne of Heaven, with rightful Lordship and Dominion over the entire Tellurian. Furthermore, some Loyalists even maintain that certain Exarchs, particularly the original ones, ought to be revered as heroes for protecting humanity from existential threats, sealing the Bound, and claiming the Throne for humanity. Despite this, the Loyal Opposition is nevertheless united in their <b>opposition </b>to the Exarchs. They just believe in giving the devil his due, and that rights and prerogatives of the office should not be abrogated.<br /> <br /> I haven't really figured out the <i>magic</i> aspect of the Legacy though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:26:03-07:00","id":917131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=762908#post762908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attainments cost a mana to activate now if I remember correctly from the devblog so it doesn't matter if it's heavily Prime based.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the rule is that if they cost any mana, that cost is reduced to 1. If there isn't a mana cost, then there's no cost for the attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:52:13-07:00","id":917320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=917131#post917131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the rule is that if they cost any mana, that cost is reduced to 1. If there isn't a mana cost, then there's no cost for the attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting is that on page 87, it is stated that &quot;Any Legacy Attainments based on spells that would cost 2 or more Mana require one point to use.&quot; Presuming that the table is exhaustive in listing the possible uses of mana, does this mean that Attainments that would normally cost 1 mana as spells cost zero mana? I believe Dave stated this in the original Legacies dev blog (or somewhere on the forums?), so I wonder if that statement remained the same or if Attainments based on spells that cost 1 mana also require 1 mana to use. If so, the sentence could have said &quot;cost 1 or more Mana&quot;, for clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 06-19-2016, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:23:00-07:00","id":918588,"title":"","content":"Custom Legacy: Spirit Tamers [Spirit, Fate,]<br /> Inspired by the Stories of the Aladdin\u2019s\u2019 lamp, Suleiman the Great, and even Pok\u00e9mon\u2019s, this legacy concentrates on collecting spirit or Crypted companions. [Requirements: Occult 2, Presence 2]<br /> Spirit 2: Bug Bottle \u2013 Mage can create permanent (Spirit #) spirit bottles that sustain spirit within in material world. Max bonded Spirit level Gnosis/2<br /> Spirit 3: Healer \u2013 Mage can heal his spirits.<br /> Spirit 4: Creating Loci \u2013 magi themselves count as a (Spirit# level) loci, but only for their bonded spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:56:42-07:00","id":990874,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it's not a necromantic legacy per se, and maybe it <i>should be</i>, but I'm performing the ritual anyhow.<br /> <br /> Here's the bare bones of a legacy I wrote in in 1e now in shiny 2e. Probably staple the meat on later.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Shinobi</b></span><br /> <br /> When the tengu taught us their arts, they showed us the power of controlling the inner shadows and elemental balance to control the world around us. We focused on the art of overcoming our weaknesses and releasing our inner shadow to overcome the world.<br /> <br /> Path: Mastigos<br /> Order: None, but it can be taught by certain clans<br /> <br /> Initiation: Intense training is required to begin to learn the proper arts. Without these arts, they will not be taught the family's secret art of Shinobi.<br /> <br /> <b>1st: Kagete<br /> Reqs. Death 1, Professional Training(Assassin) 1, Mystery Cult initiation(Shinobi) 2</b><br /> <br /> The bushi learns to focus the mind and blank out all the yang to become unbalanced towards yin, and so begin to call the darkness that is present. The shuttered yang can be used in controlled bursts to force the shadows to obey the bushi's will.<br /> <br /> Shadow Sculpting (Death 1, Casting Time)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Mind 1: </b><br /> Perfect Recall (Mind 1, Casting Time) --What's the point of spying if you forget what you learn?<br /> <br /> <b>2nd: Uzura Gakure<br /> Reqs. Death 2</b><br /> Suppress Aura (Death 2, Duration) --Meditation to engage, but the focus has lasting effects. Only works on self.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Mind 2</b><br /> Incognito Presence (Mind 2, Duration) --Activates when using suppress aura. Only works on self.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd:<br /> Res. Death 3</b><br /> Corpse Mask (Death 2, Living Subject, Casting Time) --Can be used to disguise a corpse. If the Shinobi happens to count, it does work on their own body.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Mind 3:</b><br /> Psychic Domination (Mind 2, Will, Casting)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>4th: Konoha </b><br /> <b>Reqs. Death 4</b><br /> Suppress Life (Death 2, Reflexive for Mana (2), Duration, Casting Time-&gt;Self Only) The shinobi may, while maintaining the meditative state, cast an effect that shrouds their pattern in Death.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Mind 4:</b><br /> Imposter (Mind 3, Duration, Casting) --Seeming like another for a period is critical to many missions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>5th: Sensu Gakure<br /> Reqs. Death 5</b><br /> The yang energies of the self can be directed away from one's current locus, allowing the physical form to pool and flow as shadow.<br /> Shadow Flesh (Death 4, Duration, Casting Time) --Melting into shadows is a useful tactic<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Mind 5:</b><br /> When projecting the yang energies, one let their perceptions travel with them.<br /> Psychic Projection (Mind 4, Duration, Casting) --Melting into shadows and sending one's consciousness roaming is extremely useful.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-23-2016, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:29:08-07:00","id":991335,"title":"","content":"Y'all have made a <i>lot </i>of custom Legacies ^_^<br /> <br /> Me, I've only made the one. I'll give the blurb and will stat it out if people are curious. <br /> <br /> <b>Patrons of the Palace: </b>A Fate/Mind Mastigos Legacy, Guardians of the Veil or Silver Ladder. Members of this Legacy, colloquially referred to as 'Greys', per Gris Eminence, take the view that the best way to ensure a stable and productive society is not to solve others' Vices, as a Concord of Serpents might, but instead to ensure that everyone is sufficiently competent to meet the tasks ahead of them, whether they wish their help or not. Their attainments enable them to see the incompetence of others with respect to important upcoming tasks, and they tend to pick a proteg\u00e9 that is woefully mismatched with the task requirements ahead of them. They gain proficiency with respect to their proteg\u00e9's task and have the ability to temporarily endow them with skills (or in a Left-Handed variant, strip them of skills). Of course, the ability to constantly see the failings of others around them tends to lead to an extreme bitterness or a controlling demeanor, and it's a much more self-sacrificing Legacy than initiates might believe. While a burgeoning Grey will swiftly be bombarded with favours they can easily spin into political clout, truthfully the senior members of the Legacy tend to become more apolitical, often dropping out of Orders all together to become an independent adviser, the classic hermit mentor archetype. Their initiation consists of entering the Oneiros of someone they hate or consider worthless, and reshaping it without magic to improve them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:30:42-07:00","id":991389,"title":"","content":"<b>White Reapers.</b><br /> A left handed path that is considered just this side socially acceptable that the guardians aren't trying to wipe them out. White reapers focus their efforts on the souls of inhuman supernaturals and work to cull their numbers and keep their populations in check. Or at that that is what they say publicly. They experiment with the souls of Ghouls, Vampires, wolf blooded, and Werewolves, along with the quasi souls of the Promethean. Everything that isn't human or awakened is subject to their cullings in an effort to further their understanding of souls, and to gain greater power. Because they view themselves as targeting humanity's enemies they feel they are more or less morally justified in what they do. Initiation requires that the reaper <b>not</b> be at wisdom 7+, gain two persistent mental conditions, and form a bond to a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:16:21-07:00","id":991527,"title":"","content":"Two Legacies that were inspired by the Nasuverse. The first is a Mastigos Prime Legacy that projects portions of their Oneiros onto the outside world. The second is a Moros Mind Legacy based around summoning mythological people and romanticized historical figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:08:51-07:00","id":991547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=991335#post991335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'all have made a <i>lot </i>of custom Legacies ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I posted about, what, five or six 1 ed. legacies? That's somewhere around a 5th to a 7th of what I've written up. I suspect I'm not unusual in holding back until someone requests something on a theme or just get in a mood to share one.<br /> <br /> I finally got around to porting some of those.<br /> <br /> The old model of '1st: see the thing and, generally, shield from it; 2nd: Start controlling it' mostly breaks down in 2e. With easy Mage Sight as a normal feature of all mages, making a 1st attainment an improvement which isn't superceded by the second dot attainment is tricky. I've been playing with ideas.<br /> <br /> Some of those:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Rely on Arcana Attainments for sensory perception, and use Legacy Attainments for other things.</i><br /> Provides an appropriate Knowing effect as Instant action.<br /> Grant some utility effect.<br /> <br /> <i>Grant the Unveiling effect at a high enough level to duplicate the effect sought. </i><br /> Reach for Casting Time and Advanced Duration are pretty much enough, since that means an Instant action places the effect for the rest of the day, <i>minimum</i>. That means one attainment level higher than than the casting level---usually the 2nd attainment---will suffice for an effectively always-on perception, and should something end it early, it's an Instant action to replace. Not quite as good as Indefinite perception + Reflexive replacement as many granted in 1e, but close, really.<br /> <br /> <i>Make do with an ability that is hard to dispel though hard to replace:</i><br /> Place reach into Duration and not casting time. Such legacies would need some sort of Oblation/preparation ritual to make sense, but it's an option. As soon as you hit Arcana 2, that puppy bumps up to all day. That attainment is a bit of dead weight until that 2nd arcana dot is achieved, since you get a scene sight for a scene of prep..<br /> <br /> <i>Upgrade Mage Sight: </i><br /> * <i>Penetrating:</i> Within the attainment's purview: If the mage has the ability to perceive some phenomenon, but without the ability to penetrate mystical concealment, such concealment now provokes a Clash of Wills based on the perception in use. (Whichever is strongest, plus one for each multiple after the first) If the mage already gets a Clash of Wills to penetrate concealment, that roll now adds automatic successes equal to the Arcana rating. (If the ability granting the option is a spell, this counts as stacking and burns through the effect per those standard rules.)<br /> * <i>Encompassing:</i> Limited, of course to the attainment's listed purview: The mage can perceive the phenomenon more easily. If some detail is normally only available through some Knowing effect, it becomes one of the forms of information available to Focused Mage Sight. If the property is normally only visible to a mage with an active Unveiling effect, it can be seen with Active Mage Sight. Finally, if the thing is normally perceived through Active Mage Sight, it becomes similarly clear to Peripheral Mage Sight. As the mage learns attainments that expand perceptions, the requirements may shift.<br /> * <i>Expanding:</i> Some legacies should provide a very different view than any normal spell or Mage Sight reveals. For example, unveiling the &quot;Chains/Puppet-threads of the Exarchs&quot; effect (whatever it was called) from <i>Reign of the Exarchs</i> would certainly qualify as something unusual to reveal to Mage Sight. There may <i>be</i> a way to cast the effect with basic magic, but it's not a general Attainment. A Legacy is a perfectly good place to add such an improvement. (Ironically, though, to keep parity with Arcana attainments, there is a case that these, too, should come at 2nd Attainment.)<br /> <br /> <b>Fals Lich</b><br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path</b>: Moros<br /> <b>Primary</b>: Mind<br /> <b>Order</b>: Free Council, Mysterium<br /> <br /> The group studies death and the undead to understand the lessons of mortality. They are focused on learning the secrets of the dead, be they secrets of the afterlife or simply how unliving can so freely manipulate the physical world in material ways. Vampires and ghosts are especial focuses of their interest.<br /> <br /> Initiation:<br /> Their general concept is focused on the necromantic aspect of the Moros Path, yet they have found how to teach those who would share their insights. It involves trust, of course, since they must kill and restore anyone who wishes to join them.<br /> <br /> Mystical Factors:<br /> <br /> Mortality<br /> A true immortal is *not* a being that simply won't die at a normal time, but one for whom Death does not *apply*. &quot;Killing&quot; an immortal god doesn't work, it simply renders them angry and weak. They don't actually die. That's a requirement of true immortality. Undead, like vampires, who can be destroyed are not living but still mortal. Death can eventually return and finish its work.<br /> <br /> Underworld:<br /> In the Underworld, Death is closer. Casting is as if one has a higher rating of Death, but only for Reach. This effect also applies to this Legacy's attainments. This isn't a free reach to apply flexibly, unfortunately, but a specific form of expansion that applies when in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>1st: Dead Eyes</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Mind 1</i><br /> <br /> Dealing with the dead is not a safe prospect. Their mental state is critical to monitor. In the cases of spectral death phenomena, mental state is largely definitional. Those who would study the dead to learn from them should learn to observe their minds.<br /> <br /> Fals Lich learned a way of observing the minds of the dead with the powers of Stygia.<br /> <br /> Mental Scan (Mind 1, Casting)<br /> In the Underworld, the minds are more clear, revealing brief related thoughts, per the reach option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Optional Death 1:</i><br /> <br /> The Fals Lich may perform a seance. (Technically, this can be any oblation for Moros that involve memory or communion with the dead or any ritual that would allow communiion with or summoning of the dead.) At the completion of the ritual, the Fals Lich may opena conduit o the Other Side, and Speak with the Dead. (Death 1, Duration)<br /> <br /> This effect can be cast on the Lich, specifically, or onto any marked area that the Lich is fully inside that is small enough to fit under the basic Scale of the effect. (At Death 4, this is a large room) Those inside the effect can speak with any ghosts also inside the effect.<br /> <br /> Scale must fit the ritual and a locally defined space.<br /> <br /> Duration may be cut off by the mage prematurely, which makes sense, given that it can last up to a week.<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, this can be cast in a scene and permits discourse with the dead without limitations of language. (That's two, count'em, bonus Reach... in exchange for the heart of the effect being useless)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2nd: Probing Gaze</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Mind 2</i><br /> The Fals Lich can examine a mind to see what it really is. Effectively, this is Know Nature. (Mind 1, Casting, Sensory)<br /> When used on a dead thing, however, Obsessions are revealed, as well.<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, the ability reveals Aspirations and Obsessions from anything examined.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Optional Death 2:</i><br /> <br /> Moros come back from the dead, wiser. The Fals Lich tap that symbolism to learn things about the dead closed to most magi. Through a ritual preparation of a body for death, the Fals Lich may wrap it in the Mantle of Stygia. This state, also known as &quot;wearing the Shroud&quot;, is a mystically significant event that shapes how reality treats the subject. On its own, the effect is a rather simple Suppress Life effect. (Death 2, Duration) This extends to all magical and mystical things, though, as the subjct counts as dead.<br /> <br /> A mage who has achieved this attainment can don or doff the effect reflexively once a round, to count and appear as dead or living however they desire, after casting the effect. This ability requires the full ritual, initially, and ends at the normal duration thereafter, but it isn't ended by simply choosing to be deemed living again for a time.<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, the mage can forgo the ritual and simply activate the Shroud as an instant action. The Shroud in the Underworld is a spectral-looking but literal thing. It dissolves if removed unless by one who with this attainment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>3rd: Cloak of Lead</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Mind 3</i><br /> <br /> The powers of Stygia can protect a mind. Any dead subject can have its mind protected, per Mental Shield. (Mind 2, Duration, Casting, Sensory) Moros do not intrinsically count, for purposes of this attainment, but the caster, vampires, and ghosts do.<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, any mind can be so protected.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Optional Death 3:</i><br /> <br /> Relationships to Death are clear to the any Death-aspected Mage Sight. With this attainment, those symbols cast a sort of inverted light that the mage can use to percieve the entire world. This acts as Nightvision while using an active Mage Sight that incorporates Death. (Forces 1, Casting, Duration, Protected from Extremes)<br /> <br /> Avernian and Graveyard gates are automatically visible to peripheral Mage Sight to a mage with this attainment. While this attainment is active, concealing either form of gate provokes a Clash of Wills. Graveyard Gates can be percieved at Sensory range. (up from 10') This sense is distorted, however, while the mage counts as living. Rolls are automatically successful, but must be made to home in as normal. If the mage counts as dead, Graveyard Gates are simply visible.<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, the spell permits Scrutinty through Focused Mage Sight to reveal any Keys for gates and laws for Realms. To use the latter, something symbolic of the Realm must be scrutinized. The safest thing is usually the boundary gate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>4th: One of the Boys</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: Mind 4</i><br /> <br /> The Fals Lich learns how to release Pneuma by performing a ritual passing. This is to say, the Fals Lich prepares the body to die. (As this implies, the attainment requires a living, physical body) Writing a will, making peace with people, or anything else symbolically important. If being used on another, the Fals Lich must participate in the preparations and the subject must, as well. Obviously, some might find the experience a bit intimidating.<br /> <br /> At the end, the Fals Lich symbolically indicates death. (Representationally &quot;killing&quot; the subject and actually killing the subject both work, but so does simply ending some representation of the subject's life.) The subject must release a breath during or after this point, which is what activates the effect.<br /> <br /> The subject frees from their physical form. Their body goes comatose (unless othe preparations were made to render it dead or something else.) as their mind moves free of physical constraints. This is Psychic Projection (Mind 4, Duration)<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, this may be cast as an Instant action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Optional Death 4:</i><br /> <br /> Those wearing the Shroud may be protected from the powers of the Dead or undead. This is an extended form of Ghost Shield. (Death 2, Casting, Duration, Extended to All Undead)<br /> <br /> In the Underworld, this protects against even physical attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>5th: Death's Mantle</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: Mind 5</i><br /> <br /> The Fals Lich can call on the authority of one who understands death. Only the true immortals are immune to this power. The Lich can command anyone else per Psychic Domination. (Mind 2, Casting, Any Action (2), Area) If the Lich wants the command to apply even if suicidal, they must add a mana when invoking this attainment.<br /> <br /> The caster may exempt himself and, optionally, everyone wearing the Shroud from a given command. He needs to use Fate to be more selective than this.<br /> <br /> The effects are far more lasting in the Underworld, improving the effect to Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Optional Death 5:</i><br /> <br /> When using the 4th attainment, the Fals Lich can imbue a subject's projection with Death. The result is a Ghost for the duration of that effect. This soul is a projection of the subject's will, and is created as a Rank 1 ghost that has the subject as a fetter. (Create Ghost, Death 5, Duration)<br /> <br /> If the subject is a mage, the ghost is created as a Ghost Mage (though still created at Rank 1) appropriate to that mage. The subject retains access to any supernal magic, but use of any that the ghost is incapable of using separates the two, injuring the ghost for a level of Lethal, and launching the subject's consciousness into the world as a psychic projection. If the subject can cast Psychic Projection, they can project from the ghost as a reflexive action, simply understanding how.<br /> <br /> At the end of the duration, the ghost form dissolves, and, if the mind of the subject remains inside it, it is returned to the body automatically. Otherwise, that is handled according to the projection effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-23-2016, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:18:07-07:00","id":991679,"title":"","content":"I have the clockwork utopians and the supervillains, either of which will be my first depending on which one I finish. Both need names. I was initially considering &quot;The Malfeasance Collective&quot; for the second, but I think it works best for a Cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:01:26-07:00","id":991739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=991527#post991527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two Legacies that were inspired by the Nasuverse. The first is a Mastigos Prime Legacy that projects portions of their Oneiros onto the outside world. The second is a Moros Mind Legacy based around summoning mythological people and romanticized historical figures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I MUST see these fleshed out! LOL, very much a Nasuverse fan here. And they'd make very good legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12527-thearcane","name":"TheArcane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12527_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:39:56-07:00","id":991756,"title":"","content":"Not sure what the Nasuverse is, but I do like the idea of a legacy creating Astral Verges and/or using the Dream to sculpt an area. I'd like to see how you handle that.<br /> <br /> As to the other, are these ghosts of people that never were or ghosts of people that never were <i>in our timeline</i>, because the difference could make for very different legacies and both could be fun to have in a game. Or are they even ghosts at all? I could see goetic conjuring, too, but that seems less Moros und more Thyrsus.<br /> <br /> If it is specifically pulling out the heroes that <i>ought to have been</i>, I could see either Obrimos or Mastigos for very similar approaches to the magic yet with extremely different attitudes. (This is the right way; How they <i>should</i> have been! vs. These are my heroes; They are the important ones. That they weren't is of no matter. Mere non-existence is simply a barrier to be overcome.) If your idea <i>isn't</i> that, I think I'm going to try writing that one up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T00:06:28-07:00","id":991760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=991756#post991756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what the Nasuverse is</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The body of work set in the modern-fantasy world setting created by Japanese author Kinoko Nasu as part of TYPE-MOON. It includes works such as <i>Fate/Stay Night</i> and <i>Tsukihime</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:51:09-07:00","id":991831,"title":"","content":"<b>The Tamers of Lightning</b><br /> <br /> A bolt of lightning is symbolic. It is a symbol of loss of ignorance. It also represents the punishment of humans from the Gods. In dreams, lightning is a symbol of a terrible event and negativity.<br /> <br /> As a divine manifestation it has been a powerful symbol throughout history, and has appeared in many mythologies. Drawing from this powerful association, the thunderbolt is often found in military symbolism and semiotic representations of electricity. .<br /> <br /> Lightning plays a role in many mythologies, often as the weapon of a sky and storm god. As such, it is an unsurpassed method of dramatic instantaneous retributive destruction: thunderbolts as divine weapons can be found in most mythologies. The most familiar thunderbolt weapon in the West was that of Zeus or Jupiter. His thunderbolts, manufactured by the cyclopic children of Gaia, were used to strike down impious criminals and divine opponents.<br /> <br /> The followers of this legacy strive the be like the symbols of lightning, destroying ignorance, heralding terrible events and, if need be, deal retribution. <br /> <br /> Punishers often have Just or Patient as Virtue and Pride or Wrath as Vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent path:</b> Mastigos<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Punishers, Teachers, Retribution<br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Spending an hour in a storm, Observing the area from a high vantage point, Getting struck by lightning <br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <br /> <b>- First: Touch Power</b><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> Emulates &quot;Influence electricity&quot;<br /> <br /> Optional: Prime 1<br /> Lighting reveals the truth and destroys ignorance, the Punisher gets the benefit of &quot;Pierce Deception&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>- Second: See Power</b><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 2<br /> <br /> The Punisher can sense all physical phenomena related to the presence and flow of electric charge. In other words she can sense lightning, electricity, magnetic fields, radio waves, etc.<br /> <br /> This emulates and expands upon &quot;Tune In&quot; but without the ability to listen in on transmissions.<br /> <br /> Optional: Space 1<br /> The Punisher gets a feeling of being high up in the air and seeing all on a flat plain. Get the benefit of &quot;The Outward and Inward Eye&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>- Third: Withstand Power</b><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 3<br /> Emulates &quot;Environmental Shield&quot; but in addition to the normal effects the Punisher becomes immune to all non-magical forms of lightning damage.<br /> <br /> <b>- Fourth: Join Power</b><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 4, Space 3<br /> This Attainment can only be used during a storm either natural or created with &quot;Control Weather&quot;. The Punisher is hit by lightning and disappears, seemingly evaporating. But the Punisher actually comes down in another lightning strike in the area of the storm, unharmed.<br /> <br /> Optional: Space 4<br /> For one Mana, the destination doesn't have to be in the same storm but could be in any storm on the planet. Or even a storm on another planet if desired. <br /> The ability to travel to other planets gives the legacy some fame among awakened astronomers. Some astronomers may join this legacy just for this Attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>- Five: Become Power</b><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 5<br /> Sources of electricity now heal instead of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T08:29:39-07:00","id":991859,"title":"","content":"Fourth attainment doesn't actually make sense,and neither does the part about planet hopping. I'm also not sure about starting the Optional stuff out with Prime and then switching to Space. The 5th attainment is iffy as well, typically you'd need to combine it with Life.<br /> <br /> Ok, so the 4th attainment. I recommend it being an Instant Call Lightning. Then the Optional becomes: If the Mage has Space 4 and strikes himself with Call Lightning he's able to teleport anywhere to which he has appropriate Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:23:54-07:00","id":991873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=991859#post991859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm also not sure about starting the Optional stuff out with Prime and then switching to Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like the swapping too much either but it's not against any rules. Besides it only asks for one Prime dot.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=991859#post991859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth attainment doesn't actually make sense,and neither does the part about planet hopping.<br /> Ok, so the 4th attainment. I recommend it being an Instant Call Lightning. Then the Optional becomes: If the Mage has Space 4 and strikes himself with Call Lightning he's able to teleport anywhere to which he has appropriate Sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of an Instant Call Lightning.<br /> So how about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth: Join Power</b><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 4<br /> Once a scene the Punisher may cast an Instant &quot;Call Lightning&quot; regardless of the current weather conditions.<br /> <br /> Optional: Space 4<br /> When the Punisher hits himself with &quot;Call Lightning&quot; he will disappear, seemingly evaporating. But the Punisher actually comes down in another lightning strike in any location to which he has appropriate Sympathy and that could reasonably be hit by lightning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=991859#post991859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 5th attainment is iffy as well, typically you'd need to combine it with Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>A tamer legacy is supposed to become one with their element(or understand they always were one anyway), being healed by it was a my way to show this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:26:34-07:00","id":991875,"title":"","content":"There's no reason to limit Call Lightning to once a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:37:19-07:00","id":991878,"title":"","content":"A lightning bolt is supposed to deal 10 bashing damage (page 224), can't be avoided and Call Lightning can hit multiple targets. Using it every turn seemed a bit op.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:58:43-07:00","id":992557,"title":"","content":"I feel bad that I keep coming up with ideas and never fleshing them out with mechanics, but in my defense I am not good at math or balance. <br /> <br /> Anyway, here are some of the other concepts I've had:<br /> <br /> - A Mysterium/Acanthus counterpart to the clockworkers who work more on imposing order on the cosmos itself using the metaphor of clockwork. <br /> <br /> - Basically just the Virtual Adepts but a Free Council legacy. Experiencing in a schism between modern hackers and those who still want to wear black trenchcoats and carry katanas and call people &quot;chummer&quot;. <br /> <br /> - Adamantine Arrow knights who advance in the ranks by crafting a set of mystical transdimensional powered armor. They also have their base in a massive astral UFO modified into a battleship monastery, which has an unfortunate tendency to catch on fire and rip holes in reality if it spends too long in the real world. Structured as a knightly order. Also, if crossovers exist, they're Integrators and they have a Changeling auxiliary. Another idea I had for them is that they start manifesting an image of their armor as part of their nimbus when they cast spells upon joining the legacy, and advancing in it is based on &quot;filling in&quot; that image with actual physical armor. <br /> <br /> - An Acanthus legacy of storytellers whose attainment attuned them to the Wyrd and ultimately makes them True Fae. That is, if changeling exists in their world. If it doesn't, then they just turn into something that's very much like the True Fae. <br /> <br /> - Gunslinger mages. Because of course. <br /> <br /> - A Free Council legacy who style themselves as adventurers and science heroes but are in fact hopelessly corrupted and mostly work as hitmen, mercenaries, and thieves for hire within the mafia-like structure of the FC. They work closely with the Society for the Propagation of Peril and Doom and the OSI to pair up arches. <br /> <br /> - Flesh-hating cyberneticists who want to turn everyone into robots. Their Attainment lets them modify bodies without having to use Life (which joining the Legacy prevents them from learning).<br /> <br /> - Adamantine Arrow luchadors. Because come on, who doesn't want to be a magic luchador? Plus, the whole thing luchadores have with keeping their identities secret fits perfectly with Shadow Names. <br /> <br /> Actually, wouldn't it be cool if joining a legacy had major drawbacks or limits, like joining a Bloodline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-25-2016, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:30:36-07:00","id":993008,"title":"","content":"I'm currently working on a legacy for my character in a chronicle I'm playing in. None of the established legacies really suit him. He's a Mystagogue Mastigos with a focus on Space, but given his shadow name is Escher, I thought that artistic use of Space would make more sense than the way the Reality Stalker legacy approaches the arcanum. Expression is likely going to be the main skill and Alter vector is going to be the final attainment. I've thought about having the fourth attainment be one that allows him to spend a dram of mana instead of reaching in order to cast at range. I also think that either the first or second attainment should give him easy and quick access to knowledge of his surroundings. Given the potential for information overload, another attainment will likely be a copy of one mind two thoughts so that he can handle the influx of knowledge without losing himself in it. <br /> <br /> It's only bare bones right now, but until we have another game session it's probably not going to be developed further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:02:09-07:00","id":993052,"title":"","content":"Some half-baked ideas:<br /> <br /> Qataya Enkiak - Moroi who follow the ancient Sumerian alchemical inspirations who attempt to mix the earthly and unearthly in order to transmute dead matter into life and sickness into health. (Life, attainments could include Cleanse the Body, Accelerate Growth, Create Life...)<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Treatise - A relatively new Legacy of Obrimoi that see the universe as an exactly precise machination. Utterly preoccupied and fascinated with the nature of cause and effect, paradoxes, and providence. (Time, attainments could include perfect timing, acceleration)<br /> <br /> Bridgewrights (Pontifeces) - Thyrsi worshipers of the spirits in all things, particularly those that inhabit natural barriers like rivers, mountains, chasms, etc. Like the animist priests of old, a Pontifex believes that these boundaries are meant to be respected and crossed very carefully. (Space, attainments could include ground-eater, ban, alter direction)<br /> <br /> Bloomer - Mastigoi who seek to tap into the collective intelligence of humanity, astral voyagers attempting to connect to and learn from all consciousness. (Mind, with optional Fate. Attainments could include telepathy, universal language, enhance/gain skill)<br /> <br /> Any interest in seeing any of these fleshed out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:50:13-07:00","id":993110,"title":"","content":"Well, you certainly don't need that for a fourth attainment, Falcon777 since that's already the Space 4 Arcana Attainment. If Space is primary, you'd already have this ability. An ability to use some specific forms of spatial warping as sensory range would be reasonable. Another point, of course, is that a character might want to start focusing on space and time warping, making all of this the secondary part of the legacy.<br /> <br /> Some useful ideas:<br /> Space 3:<br /> <i>Ban </i>and <i>Co-Location</i> both fit well.<br /> Space 4:<br /> <i>Alter Direction</i> requires a Reach to curve, so for your purposes it's a pretty good 5th.<br /> Honestly, though, the last three attainments could all be <i>Co-Location</i> with different Reach permutations.<br /> <br /> Warp(3) and Collapse(4) could fit, too, if you want to make things somewhat martial.<br /> <br /> Something akin to the following spread could work, but you'd likely want to tweak how it all works a whit to make it fit your theme:<br /> 1st: <i>Inward and Outward Eye:</i> (Sp1=1 Reach: casting) Instant action for a few rounds of warpy sight.<br /> 2nd: <i>Ground Eater</i>: (Sp1=2 Reach: casting, duration)<br /> 3rd: <i>Ban:</i> (Sp3=1 Reach: duration) This is activated by whatever pseudo physical act actually warps the space.<br /> 4th: <i>Co-Location:</i> (Sp3=2 Reach: casting, duration)<br /> 5th: <i>Alter Direction:</i> (Sp4=2 Reach: curvy, duration)<br /> <br /> or even:<br /> <br /> 3rd: The mage gains the ability to bend space with (involved scene-long-ish thematic action). The result is <i>Co-Location</i> with a prolonged duration.<br /> 4th: Extends the 3rd attainment, granting it the option to make two locations map to each other, provided both sides are straight lines. If the mapping is clean enough, the co-location is visible to all.<br /> 5th: Line or curve, the only detail about the mapping required to fit is that they fit tangentially at the spatial joint.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Kvark:<br /> <br /> That Bridgewright legacy might well pick up Lying Maps, too, depending on whether they intend to mislead anyone. An attainment that lets them awaken the spirit of a place or, heck, imbue a place with an effect the Genius Loci or governing spirit can use could be interesting. A variant on Fetish that lets them create a sympathetic link to a place and use its powers while present, or tie a location as a Familiar would be interesting, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-25-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:06:12-07:00","id":993116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993052#post993052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some half-baked ideas:<br /> <br /> Qataya Enkiak - Moroi who follow the ancient Sumerian alchemical inspirations who attempt to mix the earthly and unearthly in order to transmute dead matter into life and sickness into health. (Life, attainments could include Cleanse the Body, Accelerate Growth, Create Life...)<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Treatise - A relatively new Legacy of Obrimoi that see the universe as an exactly precise machination. Utterly preoccupied and fascinated with the nature of cause and effect, paradoxes, and providence. (Time, attainments could include perfect timing, acceleration)<br /> <br /> Bridgewrights (Pontifeces) - Thyrsi worshipers of the spirits in all things, particularly those that inhabit natural barriers like rivers, mountains, chasms, etc. Like the animist priests of old, a Pontifex believes that these boundaries are meant to be respected and crossed very carefully. (Space, attainments could include ground-eater, ban, alter direction)<br /> <br /> Bloomer - Mastigoi who seek to tap into the collective intelligence of humanity, astral voyagers attempting to connect to and learn from all consciousness. (Mind, with optional Fate. Attainments could include telepathy, universal language, enhance/gain skill)<br /> <br /> Any interest in seeing any of these fleshed out?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, specially the Qataya Enkiak <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:29:18-07:00","id":993126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993110#post993110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you certainly don't need that for a fourth attainment, Falcon777 since that's already the Space 4 Arcana Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Space 4 attainment is the ability to spend one mana to get the Advanced Scale Factor, not changing range from Touch/Self to Sensory or Sensory to Sympathetically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:37:49-07:00","id":993134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993110#post993110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you certainly don't need that for a fourth attainment, Falcon777 since that's already the Space 4 Arcana Attainment. If Space is primary, you'd already have this ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the greater attainment of Space allows the mage to spend a point of mana instead of reaching in order to get the advanced scale factor (which, by the way, is pretty cool too). <br /> <br /> However you definitely hit the spot about Co-location: it is easily a strong contender for the fourth and fifth slots. The main reason I haven't put it down is that for me that spell needs lots of reach to do well, which puts it down as a fifth attainment at minimum. Also, given the fact that access to sensory range magic seemed necesary and that the fourth attainment slot seemed like a...equivalent level of learning to the greater attainments of the arcana, I didn't feel like I could put sensory range as the third attainment with Co-location aa the fourth. I...might be able to convince my ST about letting me do that, but there's a good chance that the game won't even get far enough for him to become a master, let alone develop his own legacy into the fourth and fifth attainment levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:42:53-07:00","id":993139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993008#post993008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently working on a legacy for my character in a chronicle I'm playing in. None of the established legacies really suit him. He's a Mystagogue Mastigos with a focus on Space, but given his shadow name is Escher, I thought that artistic use of Space would make more sense than the way the Reality Stalker legacy approaches the arcanum. Expression is likely going to be the main skill and Alter vector is going to be the final attainment. I've thought about having the fourth attainment be one that allows him to spend a dram of mana instead of reaching in order to cast at range. I also think that either the first or second attainment should give him easy and quick access to knowledge of his surroundings. Given the potential for information overload, another attainment will likely be a copy of one mind two thoughts so that he can handle the influx of knowledge without losing himself in it. <br /> <br /> It's only bare bones right now, but until we have another game session it's probably not going to be developed further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than using Mind to Multitask you could perhaps use Fate to point out what parts of your enhanced view you should be paying attention to. Making a Space/Fate legacy could be fun! Alternatively, screw with your perception of Time so you can effectively study all areas of your warped spatial senses in the same time it takes someone to do a normal look-round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:51:39-07:00","id":993147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993139#post993139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather than using Mind to Multitask you could perhaps use Fate to point out what parts of your enhanced view you should be paying attention to. Making a Space/Fate legacy could be fun! Alternatively, screw with your perception of Time so you can effectively study all areas of your warped spatial senses in the same time it takes someone to do a normal look-round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, interesting! Both suggestions are valid. I probably will still use Mind if only because it means less investment in arcana that Escher doesn't have currently. However that Fate option is quite tempting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:21:35-07:00","id":993210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993116#post993116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yep, specially the Qataya Enkiak <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to tear this apart but here goes. I really struggled with whether to go Life/Matter or Life/Death but I like how it turned out in the end. I can be convinced to do it over again the other way, though. I suck at balancing this shit too so maybe someone else can come up with some good suggestions for how they'd do it.<br /> <br /> <b>Qataya Enkiak</b><br /> <br /> He kneels over the injured creature, muttering to himself something about shame and loss. His eyes betray an ancient optimism you won't find in his words. He moves to snap its neck, but the crunch gives way to sounds of ripping tendons and freshly exonerated sinew. The beast takes flight, leaving behind an odd man with a crooked smile.<br /> <br /> LIFE IS A PROMISE, DEATH ITS FULFILLMENT<br /> <br /> If it's oldest living practioners are to be believed, the Qataya Enkiak is a Legacy that dates as far back as ancient Sumeria. Indeed, the very name Qataya Enkiak literally translates to <i>The Hands of Enki</i>, the Sumerian god-alchemist who is responsible for the creation of man and all man's woes. In Sumerian mythology, Enki crafted the very first humans from the clay and earth, intending them to be servants for his fellow gods. The Qataya claim that this was the first and purest act of true Alchemy, and dedicate their lives to the craft of transmuting the human self. <br /> <br /> ORIGINS<br /> Parentage: Moros, any Order (though largely found in the Arrow)<br /> Background: Many of the Qataya were physicians or caretakers who spent a lot of time around the dead and dying, but used that time to help and to heal, e.g. doctors, nurses, soldiers, and priests<br /> Appearance: No one physical trait binds the Qataya together, except maybe a tendency to have a thousand-yard stare.<br /> <br /> DOCTRINE<br /> Prerequisites: Life 2, Medicine 2, and Occult 2<br /> Initiation: The aspiring <i>Qatu</i> must be in a position to determine if a sentient creature lives or dies, and make that decision on their behalf. <br /> Organization: Qataya follow a master-apprentice model of informal organization, with one in each pair serving as the tutor and another the pupil until training is complete, after which each will seek to take on a new pupil. <br /> Theory: The Qataya all accept the duality between life and matter and see death as the gateway from the former to the latter. A Qatu will spend their lives pursuing the perfection of physical and biological matter, ultimately hoping to transmute a soul between the two.<br /> <br /> MAGIC<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Life<br /> Yantras: Succeeding on a medicine roll (+2), honoring the dead (+1), witnessing the birth of an animal (+3)<br /> Oblations: Healing the wounded, putting an animal out of its misery, consoling the grieving<br /> <br /> ATTAINMENTS<br /> First: The Alchemist's Eye - As per Life 1's Analyze Life, but can also decipher the material composition of a living entity. Works on the undead. Optional: Matter 1 - Automatically activates Mage Sight (Matter)<br /> Second: The Alchemist's Skin - As per Life 2's Body Control. Optional - Matter 2: If the Mage has matter of sufficient size and durability such as light metal, he can graft it onto the body in order to give an automatic +1/0 armor for the spell's duration.<br /> Third: The Alchemist's Flesh - As per Life 3's Knit. Optional - Matter 3: If the Mage has matter of sufficient size and durability, he can use the material to augment his healing. Instead of healing 2 bashing per Potency, Knit can heal 1 lethal. <br /> Fourth: The Alchemist's Bones - As per Life 4's Shapechanging, including optional Matter 4. <br /> Fifth: The Alchemist's Heart - As per Life 5's Create Life. Optional - Matter 5: The mage may sacrifice an item of durability up to 5. The resulting life form is a composite of organic and inorganic material with general armor equal to the durability of the sacrificed item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:36:22-07:00","id":993218,"title":"","content":"I have one that I've had the rudiments of an idea for, but this is the first time I'm actually trying to write it out in full. The Attainments are probably not terribly good, and it's probably not great for serious games, but I had fun coming up with it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Narrativists</b></u><br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Storytellers, Critics, Authors, Directors, Tropers, Pratchetts<br /> <b>Background:</b> Most Tropers come from creative backgrounds or backgrounds related to entertainment, usually being writers, self-professed &quot;auteurs&quot;, or media critics, but there's a surprising amount of diversity compared to other Legacies. The most important thing is a passion for media and entertainment, and compulsive need to study and break it down, decomposing narratives and fiction to the kernels of Supernal Truth contained within like a physicist breaking down matter to its most basic particles.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> While many would expect them to assume the role of &quot;hero&quot; in their lives, they're smart enough to know that sometimes, the hero dies, especially in the supernatural mystery world they all <i>obviously</i> live in. To the outside observer, they seem like slackers and idiots, preferring to stick to the sidelines and crack meta jokes, but this is really a fa\u00e7ade. If you think you've gotten the best of a Narrativist, rest assured that they've already arranged for an comeuppance for you. Some like to make asides to some unseen audience to throw others off, but that's <i>usuall</i><i>y</i> just an act.<br /> <u><b>Doctrine:</b></u><br /> <b>Path or Order:</b> Acanthus or Free Council<br /> <b>Arcanum:</b> Mind \u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics \u25cf\u25cf, and \u25cf\u25cf in any of the following skills: Computers, Expression, Science or Streetwise<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Directors must complete the narrative set in motion by their tutor<br /> <b>Organization:</b> Authors don't have a strict organization, but maintain a fairly tight-knit, albeit somewhat clique-y community of fellows. The advent of the internet has made communication between them much easier, although their tendency get sidetracked into arguments about the finer points of things like the reflection of the story of Christ in <i>Steven Universe</i> can occasionally be as much a distraction as it is helpful. That said, their actual reach and structure is pretty unclear, as they've developed a semi-magical lexicon that's nearly indecipherable to outsiders without magical assistance.<br /> <b>Theory:</b> Something of an expansion on the concepts of the Acanthus Path, Pretchetts believe that Truth is reflected by stories, and thus when stories are understood, so too can be Truth. Moreover, if stories are True, and the Fallen world reflects what is True, then the Fallen must therefor reflect elements of stories, and those elements can be toyed with, subverted and exploited. Like any enthusiast of entertainment, they know that stories get better when everybody understands them, so many take it upon themselves to pull apart and demonstrate these tropes and clich\u00e9s to others. After all, TV Tropes can Enhance Your Life.<br /> <b><u>Magic:</u></b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Mind<br /> <b>Yantras:</b><ul><li>Discussing media (books, movies, games, etc.) whose content and themes directly relate to the situation at hand: +1</li> <li>Explain the tropes and clich\u00e9s at work in the situation: +2</li> <li>Talk about things in terms that explicitly reference the fact that you're actually an RPG character: +1, +2 if it causes a negative social Condition (e.g. Notoriety as a total loon who thinks life is fictional)</li> <li>Explicitly a genre trope while exploiting it. (+2)</li> </ul><br /> <b>Oblations:</b><ul><li>Consuming a new piece of media</li> <li>Arguing about works of fiction with others</li> <li>Producing on fictional works of your own</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Attainments:</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (\u25cf) <b>TV Tropes Will Ruin Your Vocabulary:</b> You can speak in magically shrouded jargon that is comprehensible only to those within your Legacy. By switching to this jargon, anyone who would attempt to understand you would have to succeed on a Wits + Academics roll resisted by your Mind rating. This doesn't hide your speech from magical scrutiny any more than speaking in code, but it does make communicating with fellow Critics among Sleepers somewhat safer. You can't suspend the effect, and have to end it entirely in order to be understood easily.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Optional Fate </b>\u25cf:You can use your jargon to define the tropes surrounding others. You can discern information similarly to the spell Interconnections, which is conveyed to you as tropes of fiction.</div><b>(\u25cf\u25cf) Idiot Ball:</b> Sometimes a normally smart character makes an unexpectedly dumb decision to keep the plot going. For somebody watching a TV show, this is usually considered annoying and bad writing. For you, it's an opportunity. You can cause a target to make a mistake that benefits you without putting them directly in danger. This can be something like choosing to tell you their plan, giving you an innocuous but crucial object, or become distracted at a crucial moment.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Optional Fate \u25cf\u25cf:</b> You can spend 1 Mana to apply the Conditional Duration with an <i>improbable</i> condition.</div><b>(\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) Chekov's Gun:</b> A basic rule of fiction is that when you give focus to an object early on, it's probably going to come up again later. You can impose this rule on others, compelling the subject to use, take possession of, or destroy the object later in the Chronicle.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Optional Fate (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> By spending 1 Mana, you can dictate exactly how the subject is compelled to interact with the object, and under what conditions.</div><b>(\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) Medium Aware:</b> Every Mage says they know what's really going on in the world, but you <i>really</i> know what's going on. Once per Chapter, you can choose to break the fourth wall and speak to one of the players or the Storyteller directly. You can say anything you want, but the response will be only one sentence, and there's no guarantee that it will be useful or even relevant.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Optional Fate (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> You seem to know exactly what's about to happen, almost as if somebody with an omniscient perspective is telling you what's happening. You can Reflexively spend 1 Mana to know a single subject's next action before they take it.</div><b>(\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) Instant Expert:</b> Have you ever seen a show where somebody acquires a new skill or power, and masters it instantly? You can grant yourself dots in a Skill up to your Mind rating as per Gain Skill for a day.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Optional Fate (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> You are a true Renaissance Mage, seemingly knowing exactly what you need to know at any time. Once per Scene, you can Reflexively spend 1 Mana to change what Skill you've added dots to with this Attainment.</div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 10-27-2016, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:41:43-07:00","id":993223,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12157\" data-vbnamecard=\"12157\">Kvark</a> You need to assign Reach. The way it reads right now it has to be assumed that all of the attainments take a scene to activate and last for only a Transitory Duration at most. Which doesn't much matter for the healing attainment, but might for the others. The Optional Matter for the 1st attainment can be made better. Matter Mage Sight is free to a Moros anyway so you could give it a slight boost, maybe adding dots in Matter for spotting dead organic matter or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T00:39:49-07:00","id":993366,"title":"","content":"I do like the basics of the Quataya Enkiak, it maps well to my current character. I would rather the optional Attainments were based around Death though. I may give them a twist if you don't mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:17:47-07:00","id":993441,"title":"","content":"I'll rework it to be life death tonight for you. If you take a hand at it please post it here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T06:31:43-07:00","id":993468,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's really nice of you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ok, I'll post my version when it is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:58:24-07:00","id":993492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993210#post993210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ATTAINMENTS<br /> First: The Alchemist's Eye - As per Life 1's Analyze Life, but can also decipher the material composition of a living entity. Works on the undead. Optional: Matter 1 - Automatically activates Mage Sight (Matter)<br /> Second: The Alchemist's Skin - As per Life 2's Body Control. Optional - Matter 2: If the Mage has matter of sufficient size and durability such as light metal, he can graft it onto the body in order to give an automatic +1/0 armor for the spell's duration.<br /> Third: The Alchemist's Flesh - As per Life 3's Knit. Optional - Matter 3: If the Mage has matter of sufficient size and durability, he can use the material to augment his healing. Instead of healing 2 bashing per Potency, Knit can heal 1 lethal.<br /> Fourth: The Alchemist's Bones - As per Life 4's Shapechanging, including optional Matter 4.<br /> Fifth: The Alchemist's Heart - As per Life 5's Create Life. Optional - Matter 5: The mage may sacrifice an item of durability up to 5. The resulting life form is a composite of organic and inorganic material with general armor equal to the durability of the sacrificed item.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, redoing this:<br /> ATTAINMENTS<br /> First: The Alchemist's Eye - As per Life 1's Analyze Life, but works on the undead. (Reach assigned to be cast instantly). Optional: Death 1 - Can also see the health of the creature's soul per the Soul Marks spell.<br /> Second: The Alchemist's Skin - As per Life 2's Body Control. (Reach assigned to move duration to one scene). Optional: Death 2 - The subject embraces the boundary between life and death, and their body takes damage as if undead (downgrade lethal damage from kinetic attacks to bashing)<br /> Third: The Alchemist's Blood - As per Life 3's Knit (Reach assigned to allow for instant casting). Optional: Death 3 - The mage can accelerate the healing process using the life force of another living creature (including himself). Can choose to deal one lethal damage to another living creature in exchange for healing lethal damage instead of bashing.<br /> Fourth: The Alchemist's Bones - As per Life 3's Honing the Form (Reach assigned to change primary factor to potency and move to advanced duration of one scene). Optional: Death 4 - The Qatu first creates a void by killing a living creature (animal of size 2 or greater) and then fills the void with his own shadow. If such a sacrifice is made during the spellcasting ritual, the Qataya gains the ability to take on shadow flesh (per Death 4) for the duration of the attainment. He may switch between his physical form and shadow form as an instant action.<br /> Fifth: The Alchemist's Breath - The Qatu has mastered the art of creating Life where once there was none. Per Life 5's Create Life (Reach assigned to move duration to advanced, one scene). Optional - Death 5 - At the moment of creation, the Qatu can move a soul from a living creature into the newly created life form. Doing so does not require killing the original, however the original body immediately gains the Soulless condition. If this is done against someone's will it provokes a Clash of Wills. <br /> <br /> Still not 100% happy with it but I like it better than the original I put together. And I even actually assigned reach (thanks, Mr. Dubois!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:52:59-07:00","id":993519,"title":"","content":"2nd Optional Death attainment is unnecessary, Death already grants that effect as standard Mage armor. I'll have more useful critiques later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:56:35-07:00","id":993522,"title":"","content":"Feel free to suggest a replacement. I told you I suck at this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:02:53-07:00","id":993524,"title":"","content":"If the second optional attainment stacks with other mage armor it's far from unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:39:42-07:00","id":993541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993524#post993524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the second optional attainment stacks with other mage armor it's far from unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an idea, it could allow you to have Life and Death Mage armor active simultaneously, but I'd reduce the duration to Transitory in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:09:58-07:00","id":993554,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd rather it have some sort of sacrifice and keep the scene long duration. Something like deal 1 lethal damage to yourself or another to gain the benefits of the optional effect.<br /> <br /> Also, I realized that no one probably knows how to pronounce the Legacy name. Qataya Enkiak is pronounced Kuh (as in kaboom) Ta (as in tall) Ya (as in yuppie) Eng (as in bang) Key Awk (like awkward). The singular of Qataya in Sumerian is Qatu (Ka-Too), and the god's name is Enki (Eng-key).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:28:49-07:00","id":993566,"title":"","content":"Well, with Transitory Duration it'll still last between 2 and 10 (I think) turns. Enough for most combat. The cost would get in the mana to activate it if that needs to happen frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:40:53-07:00","id":993575,"title":"","content":"Well the attainment doesn't have an instant cast time so wouldn't transitory mean it lasts for 2-10 turns after the casting ritual is complete? Seems like an awful long time to cast a spell to prepare for short combat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe the optional component should be changed to, &quot;At any time for the Duration of the attainment, the Mage can reflexively activate death armor for two turns. This effect does not negate any other existing form of Mage Armor and may only be used once per scene&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:58:37-07:00","id":993687,"title":"","content":"If it's Mage armor stacking with another Mage armor (And I recommend only letting Life and Death stack since it's in theme for the legacy) then remember that any Mage armor activation is a Reflexive action as described in the arcana attainment section. They're not spells so Reach doesn't get spent at all. There's another opportunity to add a cost if you want, make the Death mage armor activation an Instant action instead of a Reflexive action when you're stacking it. That way you become highly protected, but it takes a bit of an opportunity cost to become that much of a tank.<br /> <br /> Ok, just finished reading the rest, and I noticed that on the 4th and 5th Optional Death attainments you didn't say how Reach were being spent. On the 4th one you can sort of cheat by &quot;combine casting&quot; the Life and Death parts so that while the Mage is under the effect of the Honing the Form (Which takes a scene to activate) he can instantly (de)activate Shadow Form during its Duration. This saves you the Reach for Instant Activation, and for Advanced Duration so you can spend it on something else. It also makes a sacrifice part of the scene long ritual for activating Honing the Form.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how useful the fifth attainment from Life or Death is, can you expand on their practical applications?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-26-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:11:01-07:00","id":993727,"title":"","content":"I've been playing around with a Prime legacy with some unusual attainments. It has a Zen flavor with a focus on subtle magic, but I'd like to know what people think of the mechanics side. Open to Free Council and Paternoster, all Paths. Probably requires Occultation and Composure to advance. They exclusively use Prime for Attainments.<br /> <br /> 1st: gain the persistent condition Insightful and one free dot of Occultation.<br /> 2nd: when using Universal Counterspell, your Clash of Wills has 8-again. Also, you may spend 1 Mana instead of a Reach to use Advanced Potency if your spell would not risk Paradox.<br /> 3rd: when you incorporate a legacy yantra into a spell, your spellcasting roll gets 8-again. You may spend 1 Mana instead of a Reach to cast at sensory range if your spell would not risk Paradox.<br /> 4th: you may regain up to your Gnosis in Mana from legacy oblations each day, and this Mana has a Quiet/Subtle Resonance. You may spend 1 Mana instead of a Reach to cast instantly if your spell would not risk Paradox.<br /> <br /> Possible 5th attainments: add Prime to spell control cap. Supernal Dispellation. Use Mana instead of Reach for all purposes if spell would not risk Paradox. Create magical dead zones. Rewrite a subject's Obsession, even one of the Mad.<br /> <br /> Insightful<br /> Your character has attuned herself through zazen to the principles of nonduality and no-mind and all that good stuff. Take +2 to Composure-based rolls.<br /> Beat: Gain a Beat whenever your character poses a question, riddle, or koan (whether esoteric or practical) that causes another character to reconsider a course of action and do something different.<br /> Resolution: once per Chapter, resolve this Condition to receive a &quot;sudden realization&quot; insight into a problem or question your character is aware of. This should take the form of a true statement related to the subject. Regain this Condition by spending an hour in sitting meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T02:17:43-07:00","id":993944,"title":"","content":"Ok, first try, very barebones:<br /> <br /> <b>ATTAINMENTS</b><br /> <br /> <b>First: The Alchemist's Eye</b> - Life 1: Analyze Life (Reach: Instant Casting). Optional: Death 1: Soul Marks (Reach: Instant Casting)<br /> <br /> <b>Second: The Alchemist's Blood</b> - Life 2: Purge Illness (Reach: Instant Casting) Optional: Death 2: Supress Life (Reach: Advanced Duration)<br /> <br /> <b>Third: The Alchemist's Flesh</b> - Life 2: Body Control (Reach: Advanced Duration and Lethal speed healing). Optional: Death 3: Devouring the Slain (Reach: Not counting towards daily Scourging)<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth:</b> <b>The Alchemist's Bones</b> - Life 3: Knit (Reach: Lethal and Tilt healing) Optional: Death 2: Soul Jar (Reach: bind soul to you or others, Lasting)<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth: The Alchemist's Breath </b>- Life 5 Create Life (Reach: Advanced Duration). Optional - Death 5: Create Ghost (Reach: Advanced Duration) Used as animating force for the body.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T10:35:01-07:00","id":994100,"title":"","content":"I like yours, much less complicated than what I was trying to do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:22:59-07:00","id":994152,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> was it intentional for all of the Death optional attainments to take a scene to activate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:25:28-07:00","id":994153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=994152#post994152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> was it intentional for all of the Death optional attainments to take a scene to activate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. It's the best way to spend the limited Reach. Most of the Life ones do too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-27-2016, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T20:26:38-07:00","id":994370,"title":"","content":"It's fitting for alchemy to take <i>at least</i> a scene for most things, so I prefer it slow like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:51:19-07:00","id":994616,"title":"","content":"It's possible (and probably likely) that I'm just misreading the source material, but I can't find where it talks about reach needing to be assigned for the optional effects. To me it reads like the optional effects are not separate attainments, they are modifications of the initial attainment and they would logically take effect whenever the primary attainment is cast, no? The only real example in the sourcebook doesn't really cover the specifics in this much detail. <br /> <br /> Regardless, my intention was for this to be a ritual-based Legacy and so using reach for things other than instant casting seems very appropriate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T09:59:52-07:00","id":994644,"title":"","content":"It can be either or, but they should kind of synergize. For instance, in the 11Q the final Matter attainment doesn't actually have anything to do with previewing the future. It's not even useful until you catch up the future you previewed. Then it's very useful for making sure you're ready for whatever the future had in store.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:21:21-07:00","id":994707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MRgK-k2mB94nzT4N8-FDGYNYIeXt5rLxD7jqyU546yM/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Wards of the Dark Mother</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZQ1PuDu5j9_D-eBsyoMMHXmqC007Toou204w-9JmWv0/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Hoard Keepers</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UFM_wVpNJMC4Ca0f9fHXq_FWe07arRdWf73hX_W3B5o/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Serpents of the Garden (plus bonus Seraphim of the Tree)</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rab-dzVyo9K8qgcTZx7Zqy9gCis557r1gMb9uoZlp3w/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Children of the Iron Wood</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T06:45:08-07:00","id":995174,"title":"","content":"Optional Attainments are like additional ones and have their own Reach. If you want both the Primary and Optional Attainment to work at the same time it can be done, but then you must be sure to make both work on the same activation time (either Scene or Instant).<br /> <br /> I think I might adopt this Legacy for my current character, although he is a Libertine, not an Arrow. I'm thinking Daimonomicon in the form of a cuneiform tablet. Old, long lost Legacy being reborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:57:50-07:00","id":995331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=995174#post995174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Optional Attainments are like additional ones and have their own Reach. If you want both the Primary and Optional Attainment to work at the same time it can be done, but then you must be sure to make both work on the same activation time (either Scene or Instant).<br /> <br /> I think I might adopt this Legacy for my current character, although he is a Libertine, not an Arrow. I'm thinking Daimonomicon in the form of a cuneiform tablet. Old, long lost Legacy being reborn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the clarification and for breathing life into the legacy with your character. Please let me know how it goes! I think the cuneiform tablet is a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T21:40:47-07:00","id":995954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=993134#post993134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the greater attainment of Space allows the mage to spend a point of mana instead of reaching in order to get the advanced scale factor (which, by the way, is pretty cool too).<br /> <br /> However you definitely hit the spot about Co-location: it is easily a strong contender for the fourth and fifth slots. The main reason I haven't put it down is that for me that spell needs lots of reach to do well, which puts it down as a fifth attainment at minimum. Also, given the fact that access to sensory range magic seemed necesary and that the fourth attainment slot seemed like a...equivalent level of learning to the greater attainments of the arcana, I didn't feel like I could put sensory range as the third attainment with Co-location aa the fourth. I...might be able to convince my ST about letting me do that, but there's a good chance that the game won't even get far enough for him to become a master, let alone develop his own legacy into the fourth and fifth attainment levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I somehow misread yours as Area. I don't know why. That's the <i>Time</i> attainment, then, so it's better than automatically superfluous, to be sure...<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW, <i>technically</i> Transient Stacking is quite explicitly only preventing the stacking of <i>spells</i> with an attainment, so such a ruling is to simply prevent game-breaking stuff.<br /> <br /> The low-grade, but free, vs. supercharged Mage Armor that they were playing with earlier in development might be what this sort of attainment unlocks, instead of straight stacking. That'd be pretty swank. You pick Death or Life, and get a low-grade persistent shielding effect, but one that stacks with Mage Armor of the opposite Arcanum should you activate it for a mana. That could be neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-31-2016, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T04:54:19-07:00","id":996026,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12157\" data-vbnamecard=\"12157\">Kvark</a> : I am working on a full write up of the Qataya Enkiak. I am trying to add Matter to the mix, maybe making the Attainments Life+Matter with Optional Death, or Life+Death with Optional Matter. Probably the first.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for this Legacy, I hope you like my take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:10:26-07:00","id":996045,"title":"","content":"I think Life+Matter with optional Death is appropriate. Some things that may help you thematically are that Enki was also the god of the waters and even though he created humans as slaves, he defended and protected them fiercely from the interventions of other gods, going so far as to betray his brother-god Enlil who, frustrated with humanity, wished to wipe out most of the humans.<br /> <br /> I would recommend maybe doing something for the Third Attainment like the following (per 1E tome of mysteries's):<br /> <br /> The Alchemist's Hands: Prerequisites: Medicine \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf or Occult \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf + Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> The alchemist manufactures material in the form of a salve, cream, or unguent, that can contain a spell effect whose primary arcanum is Life or Matter. The imprinted effect is triggered when the salve is rubbed on the target's body. Follow the rules for Imbue Item with the restrictions above. Deleterious effects against another creature invoke a Clash of Wills. Optional effect; Death (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - The primary arcanum can also be Death.<br /> <br /> This is a unique attainment not unlike Imbue Item that would allow the Qatu to create a salve that can heal wounds when rubbed on them, or an ointment that enhanced the sharpness of a blade when applied, etc.<br /> <br /> Just throwing ideas out there. Please let me know what you come up with!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 10-31-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:47:04-07:00","id":996357,"title":"","content":"<br /> All the talk of alchemy got me thinking. These aren't a coherent legacy, yet, but more some ideas on how to makes something like that. They probably would represent two or three legacies, and some might appear in more than one.<br /> <br /> <b>Matter 1, Prime 1: Brew Reagents: </b><br /> The alchemist can create chemical reagents that symbolically represent a supernal symbol. These symbols can be fluids or solids, decided at the beginning of the creation process. At Storyteller's discretion, though, that can be overridden by the supernal symbol itself. The Reagent itself is a Lasting effect, but without magic, symbols of things like Fluidity are naturally fluid. More often, the decision stands and the symbolism is simply weaker.<br /> <br /> This only works for symbols that fall under arcana that the mage knows, as he lacks the required underpinnings without that arcana knowledge. There are limits to the symbols possible with knowledge, as well, but the general rule is that any spell that the mage can personally cast can be thoroughly represented in this work. This resulting reagent can be used as a Yantra of a few forms, as a result, but is often used as a Sacrament or the basis of a Path tool.<br /> <br /> When a Reagent is used as a Sacrament, strong symbolism (normal) provides a Yantra Bonus of +3 while weak symbolisms only provides a +2. Used as a Tool, strong symbolism provides a +2 and weak provides the normal +1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Matter 2, Space 1: Multiplication of Virtue</b><br /> An Alchemist can create a supernally significant copy of any material object. This requires that alchemist have control over and possession of the object for the whole of the processing period. This result is a Reagent effigy, and is significantly similar to the original, but the mystical significance is Strong. (use Strong level of Sympathy and count the Reagent as a Material Representation) The object has temporal sympathy to its creation event, not to all times that its source was linked to<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional Time 2:</b><br /> The Reagent is a duplicate, albeit weaker, of its source. The reagent effigy counts as the object did at the time of its creation, save that all temporal sympathetic links are reduced by one step.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Matter 3: Brew Potion:</b><br /> <br /> The alchemist can create a material representation of an actual spell. This requires casting the spell as part of the process, as well as using Reagents appropriate to the spell. The result is similar to Hung Spell, but counts as a Matter spell cast onto the specific object.<br /> <br /> Activation is based on the form the object takes. The alchemist can choose one of the following forms: <br /> <br /> <i>Incense</i>, activated by burning; this targets the present location.<br /> <i>Lotion or oil</i>, activated by rubbing into skin or hair; this targets the owner of said skin and hair.<br /> <i>Potion or food</i>, activated by consumption;<br /> <i>Ash or Dust</i> activated by scattering in an area or on a subject<br /> <br /> If the material gets spread thin, it divides the activated successes between valid targets. If there are more valid targets than successes, the spell fails.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prime 3: Spell Reagent:</b><br /> The alchemist can mix up appropriate symbols of transitions and form that represent an entire working of a spell. This requires a Sacramental Yantra for each Arcana represented in the casting as well as one for each Practice. (Normally, this is merely two Reagents) As with the basic attainment, the alchemist must cast the effect as well as include material representations of every required element. This process requires a material representation of the target.<br /> (If it's desired that this be subject to change, that must be presented in a generic form and retained separate from the rest of the spell.)<br /> <br /> The result is a material representation of the spell that can be used as a powerful Yantra. Casting the spell using an appropriate Spell Reagent as a Tool grants 9-Again in addition to a Yantra bonus of +2. Using it as a Sacrament grants 8-Again and a Yantra bonus of +3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Matter 4: </b><br /> If a tool is created that represents a specific spell, it grants benefits to the casting of that effect. If such a tool is Imbued, it can now be made to empower the imbued effect.<br /> <br /> An Imbued Item can be enhanced in various ways, each of which increases the effective dot rating of the Imbued Item merit, should that matter, and each also requires its own symbols being incorporated into the item. For these benefits to apply, the target must be imbued into the item in a fixed manner. That means the item itself can be targeted or the area around itself could be, and these can apply, but not the person wearing the ring because that person could change. <br /> <br /> <i>Runed </i>(1, 2): (1) A Runed Imbued Item grants the benefits of using runes (+2) dice to the Imbued Item activation. (2) As (1), but this doesn't require drawing the runes and such to gain the benefit. These are part of the Imbued Item itself.<br /> <i>Sacramental </i>(1): A very specific sacrament is defined for the Imbued Item, which, when presented, empowers the next casting as it normally would for a mage. If the item itself is the Sacrement, the effect gains the Rote quality on the casting roll.<br /> <i>Stubborn </i>(2): Activating the Item costs an extra Mana, but the Duration is Advanced. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Death 5: Universal Solvent</b><br /> Pour this volatile liquid on anything not protected by magic and it dissolves, leaving only a Twilight echo of what once was.<br /> <br /> Living creatures killed by this will almost always leave a ghost behind, but never anchored to anything destroyed by the solvent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The idea of a pure Matter-based, albeit limited, Imbue Item would be pretty nifty. An armor that is cast by creating powerful potions of iron skin or something would be interesting. If alchemists got an attainment that allows them to grant any physically embodied spell Advanced Duration, they could mix that with potions to make things lke really long-lasting Love potions.<br /> <br /> Matter/Fate might even be able to grant conditional Advanced Duration for a modest mana, time, and effort cost. The ability to add Advanced and Conditional Duration to a non-Matter primary effect would be powerful and fit the mood, both. &quot;Give this to him, and he'll 'Sleep until True Love's kiss'. Now run along; I'm busy.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:36:10-07:00","id":997126,"title":"","content":"I am having way more problems to design the Attainments than previously expected. Specially the first and second. <br /> <br /> Third: a mix of Knit and shape matter. Makes flesh maleable as clay, useful for closing wounds and repair injuries. <br /> <br /> Fourth: Shrink and Grow<br /> <br /> Fifth: Transubstation flesh to clay, clay to flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:34:45-07:00","id":997156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=997126#post997126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having way more problems to design the Attainments than previously expected. Specially the first and second.<br /> <br /> Third: a mix of Knit and shape matter. Makes flesh maleable as clay, useful for closing wounds and repair injuries.<br /> <br /> Fourth: Shrink and Grow<br /> <br /> Fifth: Transubstation flesh to clay, clay to flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about the following?<br /> <br /> First Attainment: The Alchemist's Eye<br /> Prerequisites: Initiation, Life \u2022 + Matter \u2022<br /> The Qatu may investigate any living creature and determine information about it's health and vitals. Works as Analyze Life (Life \u2022), but the mage also gains forensic information about inorganic materials (clothing, prostheses, etc.), including the composition of such items. Optional (Death \u2022) - The Alchemist's Eye also works on corpses and the undead, and also reveals information about the health of a soul per Soul Marks (Death \u2022). (+1 reach for instant casting)<br /> <br /> Second Attainment: The Alchemist's Skin<br /> Prerequisites: Life \u2022\u2022 + Matter \u2022\u2022, Medicine \u2022\u2022 or Occult \u2022\u2022<br /> The Qatu has learned how to harden his skin with the earth in a way that does not interfere with the increased vitality from his life magics.<br /> While either Life Armor or Matter Armor is active, the mage may activate the other as an instant action. The duration of the secondary armor is determined on the Transitory scale, with one step per dot in the Armor's arcanum. Optional (Death \u2022\u2022) - The mage may also use Death Armor. However, only two armors may be active at one time.<br /> <br /> Third Attainment: The Alchemist's Hands<br /> Prerequisites: Life \u2022\u2022\u2022+ Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022, Medicine \u2022\u2022\u2022 or Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> The Qatu manufactures material in the form of a salve, cream, or unguent, that can contain a spell effect whose primary arcanum is Life or Matter. The imprinted effect is triggered when the salve is rubbed on the target's body. Follow the rules for Imbue Item with the restrictions above. Deleterious effects against another creature invoke a Clash of Wills. Optional effect - Death (\u2022\u2022\u2022) The stored spell's primary arcanum may also be Death.<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment: The Alchemist's Bones<br /> Prerequisites: Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Medicine \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> The Qatu has mastered the art of unlocking or restricting the Supernal aspect hidden within all life and matter. As per Shrink and Grow with the optional (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022) to allow casting on living creatures. (+1 Reach for advanced duration, +1 reach for Instant Casting). Optional (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Optional (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Qatu can access the latent mana in any living creature. As per Devouring the Slain (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) (+1 reach for instant casting, +1 reach for not going against the daily scouring limit)<br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment: The Alchemist's Flesh<br /> Prerequisites: Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Like Enki, who first molded humans out of clay, the Qatu has learned to transform inert matter into life and vice versa. Functions as Transubstantiation (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) with the optional (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) to allow transformation between living creatures. (+1 reach for advanced duration, +1 reach for instant casting). Optional (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) The mage may also transform living creatures or nonliving matter into and from the shadows. The subject of the The Alchemist's Flesh may take on shadow form per the Shadow Flesh spell (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022).<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe move the Third Attainment to the Second Attainment and put Knit in for #3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:22:31-07:00","id":997192,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know about any guides or guidelines for creating a custom legacy? Especially for the attainments. I know 2E has rules for legacy attainments, but it doesn't serve much as inspiration or advice on what good attainments might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:36:57-07:00","id":997202,"title":"","content":"I just kind of look at some spells that look fun and fill in the blank attainments with spells of the appropriate dot level, at least on the first draft.<br /> <br /> Here's a slightly more systematic way of thinking about it. The advantage of a legacy Attainment is: automatically succeeds without a roll, never risks Paradox, never risks Wisdom loss, can't be directly counterspelled, and doesn't count against spell control. So think of spells that would benefit from that.<br /> <br /> I suggest a mix of utility spells that would otherwise use up spell control slots (like stat boosts, dice tricks, and awareness enhancers) and a few big interesting setpiece effects that make the legacy interesting to players. I'm a big fan of the Eleventh Question attainment that uses Time/Matter to create a sympathy yantra from nothing, for example. Attainments are also a great place for &quot;mind control&quot; or binding spells that would otherwise risk Wisdom loss, like the Bokor or Thrice-Great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:48:39-07:00","id":997238,"title":"","content":"I'm looking to create a legacy for my Mastigos character with Prime (he already focuses on both Mind and Space so either works as Optional) and your example about a sympathetic yantra made me wonder if one attainment could be Invisible Runes (Prime 2) with Space 2 as Optional which allows the mage to create runes that works as a sympathetic yantra for the purpose of the sympathetic range attainment. Invisible Runes does not really seem like the best choice for a legacy attainment, but the optional makes it very worthwhile if it's viable and mechanically sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:52:35-07:00","id":997287,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a legacy they have an idea for but would like to see fleshed out? I rather like the challenge of putting these things together and would love some more practice.<br /> <br /> As for the question how to think about Legacy Attainments, I like attainments that provide truly unique possibilities or synergies for characters. I just drafted up a Legacy of Mastigoi that weave fate by communicating directly with the <i>Oneiropolis</i>, the place in the Astral Realms where unfulfilled dreams and ambitions reside. The first attainment is a dot in both Destiny and Dream. Nothing fancy, but thematically appropriate. The optional part of the second attainment is not a spell but the ability to use the Dream merit as an instant action and to apply half Dream dots to the potency of other attainments. My ideas probably need some balancing but generally that <i>kind</i> of synergy is the thing i like to see in Legacies (I can post this Legacy if anyone is interested).<br /> <br /> Take the Qataya example I just posted above. I'm thinking of redoing it so that none of the attainments have instant cast time, but that any of them can be applied as a spell per the third attainment. This would give the Qatu a unique way of storing spells to be instantly cast that would otherwise be ritual spells or attainments, something that usually takes Prime 4 to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:02:34-07:00","id":997294,"title":"","content":"I like your new notes on the Qataya, Kvark. I will work from there and see if I can polish them further. I do like the idea of most of the Attainments save, perhaps, the first) requiring a little ritual. It really fits the theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:47:32-07:00","id":997314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=997294#post997294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your new notes on the Qataya, Kvark. I will work from there and see if I can polish them further. I do like the idea of most of the Attainments save, perhaps, the first) requiring a little ritual. It really fits the theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I redid this so that all but the first and second attainment are rituals. I moved the crafting up to #2. Notably, these attainments can now explicitly be turned into salves to &quot;allow&quot; for instant casting using the Imbue Item rules, but otherwise they involve an alchemist performing a scene-long ritual.<br /> <hr /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Attainment: The Alchemist's Eye</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation, Life \u25cf + Matter \u25cf</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Qatu may investigate any living creature and determine information about it's health and vitals. Works as Analyze Life (Life \u25cf), but the mage also gains forensic information about inorganic materials (clothing, prostheses, etc.), including the composition of such items. Optional (Death \u25cf) - The Alchemist's Eye also works on corpses and the undead, and also reveals information about the health of a soul per Soul Marks (Death \u25cf). (+1 reach for instant casting)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second Attainment: The Alchemist's Hands</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Life \u25cf\u25cf+ Matter \u25cf\u25cf, Medicine \u25cf\u25cf or Occult \u25cf\u25cf</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Qatu manufactures material in the form of a salve, cream, or unguent, that can contain a spell effect or attainment effect whose primary arcanum is Life or Matter. The imprinted effect is triggered when the salve is rubbed on the target's body. Follow the rules for Imbue Item with the restrictions above. Deleterious effects against another creature invoke a Clash of Wills. Optional effect - Death (\u25cf\u25cf) The stored spell's primary arcanum may also be Death.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third Attainment: The Alchemist's Bones</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf + Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Medicine \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf or Occult \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Qatu has mastered the art of unlocking or restricting the Supernal aspect hidden within all life and matter. As per Shrink and Grow with the optional (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) to allow casting on living creatures. (+1 Reach for advanced duration). Optional (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): The Qatu can access the latent mana in any living creature. As per Devouring the Slain (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) (+1 reach for not going against the daily scouring limit)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth Attainment: The Alchemist\u2019s Blood</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf + Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Qatu has become an expert at mending the broken flesh. The Alchemist\u2019s Blood functions per Knit (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), with (+1 reach to heal lethal and +1 reach to advanced duration). Additionally, the Qatu may use physical material when using the Alchemist\u2019s Blood, and the subject will gain general armor equal to the Durability of the objects used (see Objects on p.223) for the Duration of the spell. Optional (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - If the mage desires, he may use the shadows themselves in lieu of physical matter. The shadows harden into physical form with Durability of 2, and the subject gains one dot to Stealth for the Duration of the spell.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth Attainment: The Alchemist's Flesh</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf + Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like Enki, who first molded humans out of clay, the Qatu has learned to transform inert matter into life and vice versa. Functions as Transubstantiation (Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with the optional (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) to allow transformation between living creatures. (+1 reach for advanced duration, +1 reach for transmuting multiple substances into a single substance or vice versa). Optional (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) The mage may also transform living creatures or nonliving matter into and from the shadows. The subject of the The Alchemist's Flesh may take on shadow form per the Shadow Flesh spell (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf).</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:14:55-07:00","id":997334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=997287#post997287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a legacy they have an idea for but would like to see fleshed out? I rather like the challenge of putting these things together and would love some more practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I wrote just earlier I'm looking to create a Prime legacy for my Mastigos, but I'm working from what my character needs (Prime as Ruling) instead of an actual legacy idea. I was thinking that I can fluff it up after creating at least one or two attainments.<br /> Speaking of which, I never got any criticism about my Invisible Runes/Sympathetic Yantra suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:41:43-07:00","id":997347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=997334#post997334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I wrote just earlier I'm looking to create a Prime legacy for my Mastigos, but I'm working from what my character needs (Prime as Ruling) instead of an actual legacy idea. I was thinking that I can fluff it up after creating at least one or two attainments.<br /> Speaking of which, I never got any criticism about my Invisible Runes/Sympathetic Yantra suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I love the idea. It makes sense and can even be thematically appropriate.If I were to do it, I would recommend crafting some sort of Legacy (Ruling Prime with Optional Space) around Leylines and finding/traveling between Hallows. There's a lot of fertile ground between sacred geometry and the Space arcanum to come up with some really cool attainments, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:54:18-07:00","id":997350,"title":"","content":"Good idea. The Obrimos in the group is the one who's focused on leylines and hallows thusfar, but mine has assisted in the mapping due to his high Academics and Cartography spec. I'll see if I can figure something out about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:57:59-07:00","id":997351,"title":"","content":"Check out the Tellurians if you can. It needs work, and an update obviously, but the base concept is pretty cool. Alternatively steal some ideas from the Celestial Orrery for messing with Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-02-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:16:26-07:00","id":997363,"title":"","content":"Character already has a cartography spec? That's perfect!<br /> <br /> Some sample attainments:<br /> <br /> Second Attainment: Prerequisites: <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf, Academics \u25cf\u25cf or Occult \u25cf\u25cf</span><br /> Sacred Geometry (Prime <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf) </span>with instant casting and advanced duration. The mage can perceive leylines and nodes, and feels a tug in the direction of the nearest node. Optional (Space <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf) - While Sacred Geometry is active, the mage gets the benefits of the Ground-Eater spell (Space \u25cf) when traveling in the direction towards the nearest leyline, or while traveling along leylines.<br /> <br /> Third Attainment: Prerequisites: Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Academics \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf or Occult \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Invisible Runes (Prime \u25cf\u25cf) with instant casting and advanced duration. The mage creates invisible runes that can only be revealed by Active Mage Sight. Optional (Space \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - The runes may be used as sympathetic yantra for purposes of the Space \u25cf\u25cf Sympathetic Range attainment.<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment: Prerequisites: Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, <br /> Geomancy (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with instant casting time and advanced duration.The mage may move leylines with ease and change the resonance of leylines. Optional (Space \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) Co-location - The mage may use the co-location spell with instant cast time and advanced duration. He may choose to co-located two regions with ley-lines to create a temporary node. Whether or not the node manifests into a Hallow is at the storyteller's discretion.<br /> <br /> I'll try to think of some more for you... </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:47:02-07:00","id":997383,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Kvark! Those look good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:06:11-07:00","id":997394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=997314#post997314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, I redid this so that all but the first and second attainment are rituals. I moved the crafting up to #2. Notably, these attainments can now explicitly be turned into salves to &quot;allow&quot; for instant casting using the Imbue Item rules, but otherwise they involve an alchemist performing a scene-long ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking good. I'd rather the Death optional attainments had to do with the soul, rather than shadows. I think I have a clearer idea now, I will post my version so you can tell me what you think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T06:40:48-07:00","id":997663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=997383#post997383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Kvark! Those look good.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Attainment: Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> When gaining mana from consuming tass, the mage gets an additional point of mana. Optional (Space <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf) - Consuming tass from a Hallow or channeling mana from a Hallow increases the sympathetic connection between the mage and the hallow by one step. This effect works only once per Hallow.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth Attainment: Prerequisites: Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf,</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hallow Dance (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with Lasting effects. The mage may activate dormant Hallows, particularly those resulting from his own intervention with leylines. Optional (Space \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) Teleportation - With instant cast time, the mage may use the teleportation spell to travel between any node or Hallow which he has created or from which he has channeled mana. He may also swap the location of two subjects with size difference no more than one at these locations.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 11-03-2016, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:29:54-07:00","id":998218,"title":"","content":"Some other ideas I plan on fleshing out:<br /> <br /> <i>Daydreamers - </i>Mages that aspire to greatness who are sought out by the <i>Oneiropolis</i>, the place in the Astral where unrealized fantasies and unfulfilled ambitions coalesce. They carry a piece of the Astral with them at all times and use it to craft their destiny in the fallen world. (Fate, Optional Mind)<br /> <br /> <i>Vox Auctoritatis - </i>A legacy started by a Guardian who manifested his authority through the power of his voice. Commanding, intimidating, and even imperial in nature, when these mages Speak, the whole of the Fallen World listens. (Forces, Optional ???)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:59:07-07:00","id":998247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=998218#post998218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Vox Auctoritatis - </i>A legacy started by a Guardian who manifested his authority through the power of his voice. Commanding, intimidating, and even imperial in nature, when these mages Speak, the whole of the Fallen World listens. (Forces, Optional ???)</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit, so the denizens of the Shadow heed their voice too? Mind, so word controls thought? Prime, so what is spoken becomes manifestly True?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:46:50-07:00","id":998278,"title":"","content":"I'd ask yourself if they're meaningfully different than the Bearers of the Eternal Voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:57:09-07:00","id":998283,"title":"","content":"Which source book is that in? Not familiar with that one! EDIT: Found the reference, for those interested, it's GotV (appropriately), pg 163. I don't own this book but will probably pick it up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 11-04-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:48:47-07:00","id":998614,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>The Pit Baiters</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Origins:</span></span><br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Obrimos. Members are primarily Silver Ladder, Guardians of the Veil, and Free Council for very different reasons. Mysterium is surprisingly well-represented because they are one of the places back-up Daimonomicons were stored when continuity of the legacy could not be assured. The heavy casualties and lack of focus on specific Order have left questions as to the origins.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Most members had someone die or be seriously damaged by a spell going awry or an abyssal intruder. Their backgrounds often overlap with those of Banishers, a detail which these are well aware of.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Mostly trends follow the parent organizations that a lineage is most aligned with. Silver Ladder tend to be immaculately groomed and dressed. Guardians tend to match their surroundings. Free Council tend to be flashier or comfortable, while the Mysterium members tend to be comfortable or academic.<br /> All of them, however, move like they are important. They have missions and their missions are important.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Doctrine:</span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Fate 2, Prime 1, and 6 dots in Occult and Academics (no fewer than 2 in either)<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> An individual member must seek out a significant example of a Paradox and mitigate it, returning to report their findings. The mission is fully monitored and the direct mentor is allowed to help. Initiates are sometimes shocked to discover that success or failure for initiation is in the learning from it. The report is the critical element.<br /> After discussing the results with the prospective student, the ranking members of the legacy discuss the findings with the student. If they are impressed, they take him to the safest and most well-guarded ritual space available to them and cast a powerful spell with the prospective student, to transform the prospective into an initiate.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> The Abyss Baiters see themselves as members of a high-risk, high reward society. They like to keep a close eye on members. This is both to prevent left-handed practicioners from cropping up, but also to back each other up when facing the incalculable horrors that they attract.<br /> Mentors are <i>expected</i> to introduce their various protegees to each other and their mentors and peers. It's common to host events to get to know each other.<br /> They try to foster a more filial than hostile arrangement, but mages are mages.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b><br /> They their art as tying up the Abyss in bands of supernally empowered fate, making it less likely to affect the world. After that, their goal is to repair the damaged section, removing the flaw permanently. As far as these see it, the Supernal Realm defines what is possible, while the Loom of Fate defines what is. The Abyss represents what isn't and cannot be. If appropriately handled, then, the forces of Are Not can be carefully handled by weaving carefully and ending the trouble so caused. Paradoxes are snarls in the weave of reality, which a dedicated weaver can go back and repair, but is better served by preventing initially... and most mages aren't such great and skilled weavers as to be able to make all the needed repairs.<br /> <br /> They figure that filling in the damaged weaves with proper ones can completely remove the gaps where threads are simply missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">1st: Weaving the Dark Thread</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The mage learns the primary force of the legacy, by tracking the trails of the Abyss in the world. This effect is largely via the Lie's interaction with the manifestations of the Supernal. When using Mage Sight of any sort, Paradox and abyssal phenomena can be spotted and examined.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Paradoxes that occur in the area, whether internalized or released, are visible to the mage.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Abyssal things trigger peripheral Mage Sight.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Lies are apparent as such to both Mind and Prime Active Mage Sights whenever active. If either must pierce supernatural concealment, it automatically scores successes equal to the mage\u2019s Fate dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">2nd: Scattering Shadows</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fate 2<br /> <br /> The mage can fight the myriad minor distractions of the Lie. The thousand gnats that drain the will and draining obstacles can be dispelled. This only goes so far, but it's a nice respite. The mage activates Quantum Flux with Advanced Duration equal to Fate.<br /> <br /> (Quantum Flux, Fate 1: 2 Reach: casting, duration)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Optional:</b> Prime 2</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fighting the darkness is easiest with illumination. Any lie is penetrated, of course, but this reveals information about the Lie, as well as informations about what is True.<br /> <br /> (Pierce Deception, Prime 1: 2 Reach: duration, insight)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">3rd: Cursing the Darkness</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fate 3</span><br /> The mage must study the target abyssal phenomenon or effect to determine the types of damage that it represents respecting the Supernal World. Through this careful scrutiny and probing, the mage comes to understand a means by which it can be contained and, ultimately, removed. The mage then ties the problem in carefully crafted bonds of fate to secure this ultimate outcome. <br /> <br /> The mage actually has little control over the specifics, but the Fate will make sure that the mage has a chance. Usually, a set of choices per dot of Fate appears, but this aspect is Withstood by Rank. If the effect is an active power, there is no Withstand, but a Clash of Wills is sometimes imposed. Against an Intrusion, the storyteller ought to pick a Withstand based on extent of the intrusion---Use the advanced Scale chart to set the Withstand.<br /> <br /> The stronger the mage's command of Fate, the simpler the requirements, the easier the path, or the sooner the result will appear.<br /> <br /> The Mage and Target both gain complementary Destinies. The key to this ability is that the mage learns a way to remove the target abyssal effect.<br /> <br /> Abyssally Tainted creatures always end up with a Bane imposed by their tainted power as a result. This converts the power into a vulnerability.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Prime 3<br /> <br /> Warding an area against the Lie is a useful tactic. Tne mage can spend a scene preparing a location to attune it with the heavens and to drive back the Lie. The result is that any casting that can use an Environment Yantra of the area gains the 8-again property. <br /> <br /> Abyssal things are decidedly uncomfortable, making Sleepers avoid the area.<br /> When the mage learns to create a symbol of the supernal, he may work that into a tool yantra and apply this attainment to that, as well.<br /> <br /> Should the mage desire to affect Abyssal creatures or powers when effecting a Ban with Space, this attainment permits the effect.<br /> <br /> (As Above, So Below, Prime 2: 2 Reach: duration, 8-again)<br /> <br /> (Previous edit was essentially: (Exceptional Luck, Fate 2: 2 Reach: casting, sensory))<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Optional:</b> Prime 3</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Warding an area against the Lie is a useful tactic. The mage can spend a scene preparing a location to attune it with the heavens and to drive back the Lie. The result is that any casting that can use an Environment Yantra of the area gains the 8-again property.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Abyssal things are decidedly uncomfortable, making Sleepers avoid the area.<br /> When the mage learns to create a symbol of the supernal, he may work that into a tool yantra and apply this attainment to that, as well, while inside this space.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">(As Above, So Below, Prime 2: 2 Reach: duration, 8-again)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">4th: Chain the Abyss</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fate 4</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The mage learns to craft a device from pure silver or another specially sacred material befitting the mage's watchtower. (individual parts must be pure, but the device can include multiple materials) This device is part of a pattern that repulses the untruth of the Abyss by sympathy to the mage's own Path and Watchtower.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The device can be anything that the mage can wield in two hands to something small enough to fit on the back of the mage's hand. Size matters very little, though the smallest it can be is a few inches in diameter.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">A mage may only retain one per level of Fate. The item may certainly be dedicated as a Path or Personal tool, but that's not required.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Abyssal and abyssally touched creatures who contact the device are affected by Grave Misfortune with Potency equal to the mage's Fate. The effect is an area.<br /> <br /> (Since there are loads of details weakening the effect, the following seems fair)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">While wielding the device, a mage may turn Abyssal powers away. This allows a Clash of Wills against any abyssal powers affecting the area projected. (maybe add/replace with Withstand 2)<br /> <br /> (Grave Misfortune, Fate 3: 2 Reach: casting, duration)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Optional:</b> Prime 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">By touching a Sleeper, the basic kernel of taint all sleepers bear can be pushed back and suppressed. This is not any sort of minor effect, either. It can last Indefinitely, given potent enough Prime.<br /> <br /> (Stealing Fire, Prime 3: Reach 2: duration, casting)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">5th: Naming the Nameless</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Fate 5</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The mage can twist fate around an abyssal creature and direct its behaviors, within limits.<br /> <br /> (Divine Intervention, Fate 4: 2 Reach: casting, duration)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Optional:</b> Prime 5</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">If the mage's device is placed on a weapon, that weapon can be used to slice through any layers of existence, from twilight and material on. To abyssal creatures, it counts as their Bane. (Note this is more specific: Abyssal creatures must be almost entirely impossible or a spirit with significant abyssal essence. Sleepers do not count unless extraordinarily infected.)<br /> <br /> (Ephemeral Enchantment: Prime 3: Reach 3: (2) Bane, duration)<br /> <br /> <br /> It is rumored the 6th Attainment could trigger Awakening or banish a powerful Acamoth back to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm still not thrilled with the attainments on this, but I consider it improved from the 1e version I wrote up. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:25:13-07:00","id":998721,"title":"","content":"2nd attainment Duration and Potency would both be determined by Fate since it's not a Combined effect. Since Potency is a secondary factor it'll never be more than 2.<br /> <br /> 3rd attainment not sure I see the point of the restriction on Exceptional Luck, Mages and Sleepwalkers can still be tainted.<br /> <br /> 4th attainment same as the second. Prime 4, it won't be a Lasting effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-05-2016, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T01:20:29-08:00","id":999119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=998721#post998721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd attainment Duration and Potency would both be determined by Fate since it's not a Combined effect. Since Potency is a secondary factor it'll never be more than 2.<br /> <br /> 3rd attainment not sure I see the point of the restriction on Exceptional Luck, Mages and Sleepwalkers can still be tainted.<br /> <br /> 4th attainment same as the second. Prime 4, it won't be a Lasting effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point on Potency from Fate. I originally wrote it as Fate with Prime conjunctions. Artifacts of editing, and all that.<br /> <br /> The only rationale for the limitation is the conceit of the legacy, namely that they have learned how to wrap abyssal effects in fate, which happens to allow cursing those using it, too. <br /> <br /> As to the effect being indefinite, well, I was actually debating between two things.<br /> 1. The device is Lasting, but the effect is cast during a fight. That would mean the magic is in the attainment and not the item. The valid target for the item simply has some extra rules.<br /> 2. The duration is primary, rendering the item effects nearly permanent, albeit considerably weaker. (low Potency, as you note)<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'd prefer something else, entirely. Something that emphasizes tying the lies and untruths up and limiting their abilities to act is needed, here. More than just Space get Ban-like stuff, now, so something like that might work better.<br /> <br /> Suggestions?<br /> <br /> I was actually hoping to get some wild ideas on how to model this.<br /> <br /> Actually, a mix of Time and Prime might be interesting, to allow reweaving snarls out of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 11-06-2016, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T05:18:32-08:00","id":999172,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my point was that you're limiting your curses from the 3rd attainment to the wrong group, Sleepers and vampires. Instead any Abyssally tainted person/place/thing should be valid targets since that's the actual thrust of the legacy. This would include Sleepers by default. I have no idea why you assume vampires to be related to the Abyss though, they're more likely aligned with the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> Anyway, why not use some kind of geas effect on the Abyss? Force Gulmoth to seek their own destruction, a Scelesti to purify himself, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:26:07-08:00","id":999433,"title":"","content":"Actually, that suggests the ability to target abyssal effects and apply Conditional Duration to them and adding Banes to the ephemera might be something. Instead of focusing on the patterns that are tainted, focus on the active broken force. Wouldn't be a straight spell, since nothing quite like that exists, but it would certainly fit the theme.<br /> <br /> Requiring a ritual to define how something may be destroyed seems fair. Something to permit the binding of an entity to a location or outside of one makes sense, too. Allowing the mage at some level to treat Paradox and abyssal stuff as valid conditions for a Ban seems good, too, but the rules for what that means probably deserve some attention.<br /> <br /> I've explained before why vampires are at least as abyssal as they are lower, but the short answer is (though, the distinction is mostly moot, anyway) they operate with powers that dominate the fallen world not from a lack of definition but from a nature that is literally in contradiction. Positionally, vampires are superior to fallen, and stealing one of the most sublime forces in a very pure symbolic way in order to gain this power over the fallen world.<br /> <br /> (Oh, it was never limited to tainted mages and vampires. &quot;As an instant action, the mage can curse a Paradox roll or anything bearing the touch of the Abyss. This <i>includes</i> Sleepers and Vampires but not true* Sleepwalkers and Mages.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:57:51-08:00","id":999444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=999172#post999172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, why not use some kind of geas effect on the Abyss? Force Gulmoth to seek their own destruction, a Scelesti to purify himself, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your Legacy <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> (though it looks like you mistakenly left a reference to Abyss Baiters instead of Pit Baiters in there), this idea of Mrmdubois's is pretty great and thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> Also, since so much of the legacy and the attainments revolve around affecting the abyss, it might be worth defining what exactly counts as abyssal or touched by the abyss, or is the idea to leave that to ST discretion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T17:53:52-08:00","id":999504,"title":"","content":"Can I get general or specific thoughts on a Legacy I'm working on? Either as to the flavor or the attainments or just in general:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=998218#post998218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Daydreamers - </i>Mages that aspire to greatness who are sought out by the <i>Oneiropolis</i>, the place in the Astral where unrealized fantasies and unfulfilled ambitions coalesce. They carry a piece of the Astral with them at all times and use it to craft their destiny in the fallen world. (Fate, Optional Mind)</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Daydreamers</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As she comes to the fork in the road, she pauses to reflect. She mutters in a language she has never spoken before or since. In seconds, she knows exactly which way she needs to go. She wonders, just for a moment, if this was the right choice before she chose it, or if it\u2019s the right choice now </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>because </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">she chose it. It doesn\u2019t matter, she knows the world is conspiring to take care of her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WHAT HAPPENS TO A DREAM DEFERRED?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is a place deep in the Astral Realm where faded aspirations and lost genius effervesce and coalesce. It manifests as a vast fluid of possibility, with rapidly changing form that engulfs and drowns out anything it touches. The ideas and memories within are diverse, but they share one thing in common: they seek instantiation and actualization in the real world. This place in the Astral Realms, called the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Oneiropolis</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, is the nest of dreams unfilled and ambitions unrealized. It subtly seeps into the waking world through the unconscious acts of all sapient creatures, yet it yearns to be acknowledged, to be unforgotten, and to be empowered. The Oneiropolis will latch onto certain mages, embedding a sliver of itself into their minds and weaving itself inextricably into their fates. It will then slowly, subconsciously, put ideas into the minds of the prospective Daydreamer guiding him towards an appropriate mentor and set fate into motion to arrange for a chance meeting between the two.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first references to the Legacy date back to early Greek history, in the first few centuries preceding the Common Era. It\u2019s unknown exactly whether the Oneiropolis reached out to the first Daydreamer, or if the founder of this Legacy instead stumbled across it in the Astral Realms. Regardless, almost all students of such matters agree that the meeting was not an accident (indeed, Daydreamer scholars might argue there are no true accidents). Daydreamers have been found scattered across all corners of the globe, brought together by apparent coincidences and inspired to seek each other out by arcane dreams or nightmares. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In more modern times, the Daydreamers are a rare but far-reaching collective of mages, with a great dedication to the pedagogy of their Legacy. Though they come from diverse backgrounds, almost all Daydreamers believe themselves destined for greatness (if they seek it) and so tend to be very involved in the world of mundane affairs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mystagogues have found a particular affinity for the Daydreamer, knowing that their riddled dreams and bewitched minds are usually the vessel for great Mysteries or obscure Truth. Most of the Daydreamers count themselves among the Mysterium and aspire to find their greatness within the Order\u2019s hierarchy. Select few other Daydreamers are drawn to the Free Council, whose belief that all of reality is magical resonates well with the Dreamer modus operandi, wherein they quite literally will often find magic in everything.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ORIGINS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parentage: Any Path, Mostly Mysterium or Free Council</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Background: The Daydreamers tend to be people of great vision and imagination (though not necessarily great success). The Daydreamers count many artists, scientists, and entrepreneurs among their Legacy. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance: Daydreamers come from all backgrounds and have no physical traits in common prior to joining the Legacy. It\u2019s been said that those that join end up appearing a little scatterbrained and skittish or otherwise \u201cnot all there,\u201d though anyone engaging in a conversation with a Daydreamer usually quickly realizes this is a superficial quality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">DOCTRINE</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate \u25cf\u25cf, Investigation \u25cf\u25cf or Expression \u25cf\u25cf, Destiny \u25cf, Dream \u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation: The mentor will guide the prospect through the Astral realms several times before finally diving into the Temenos and the Anima Mundi to see the Oneiropolis, who will impart the first Attainment. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Organization: All Daydreamers view themselves as equals before the Oneiropolis. This is not due to any sort of mind control or undue influence, but rather because the act of communicating with the Oneiropolis itself is very humbling. Daydreamer mentors consider pupils to be part of their life\u2019s work and dedicate great time and care to making sure that those under their tutelage embrace the Oneiropolis. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theory: Daydreamers believe themselves to be vessels of humanity\u2019s suppressed thoughts, unsubstantiated ideas, and forgotten memories. They do not have any sort of \u201cmission,\u201d but rather share a common drive-- to produce great works and become a greater part of the Oneiropolis. They borrow the ambitions and memories of others and use them to sculpt their own fates.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">MAGIC</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcanum: Fate</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: Succeeding on an Expression roll (+2), referencing a relevant work of genius (+1), completing a relevant research piece or artwork (+3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: Finishing a manuscript or a work of art, convincing someone to appreciate her works, traveling to the Astral to commune with the Oneiropolis, learning a new skill or practicing a new hobby</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1st Attainment: Waking Dreams</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage\u2019s mind becomes a beacon for the Astral, and the Oneiropolis can sing directly into it, subtly guiding her fate with bits and pieces of supernal truths. The mage\u2019s increases her maximum potential dots in Destiny and Dream by her Fate. She still needs to purchase these additional dots with experience, however.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Mind \u25cf) - The mage may use her Dream merit as an instant action without taking the time to enter a meditative state. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2nd Attainment: Whispers in the Dark</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate \u25cf\u25cf, Investigation \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf or Expression \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Destiny \u25cf\u25cf, Dream \u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage turns to the Oneiropolis for advice on how to proceed. The Oneiropolis responds in a combination of foreign memories, whispers, and strewn images that the mage interprets as an omen of where to go. This attainment functions as Serendipity (Fate \u25cf) with instant casting and the skill substitution reach.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf) - </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage becomes comfortable delegating certain tasks to the Oneiropolis, and grows more confident in his ability to interpret the resulting visions and dreams. In practice she gains the ability to use One Mind, Two Thoughts with instant cast time and advanced duration, as well as the reach to perform two instant mental tasks at once. This attainment can only affect the mage herself.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3rd Attainment: Conspiring Thoughts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Destiny \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Dream \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Oneiropolis watches out for its disciples and forges success through a chain of seemingly random events. This attainment functions as Shifting the Odds (Fate \u25cf\u25cf) with instant casting and advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - The mage communes regularly with the Oneiropolis inside and outside of her conscious state. She may use an effect similar to Dream Reaching (Mind \u25cf\u25cf) with advanced duration and the ability to be an active part of any dream, or to dream lucidly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4th Attainment: Hypnagogia</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Destiny \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Dream \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So great is the Oneiropolis\u2019s pull on the mage\u2019s Destiny that she can transform would-be failure into glorious success. This attainment mimics Superlative Luck (Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with instant casting time and advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - For the duration of Hypnagogia, the mage may mimic the effects of Enhance Skill with instant casting and advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5th Attainment: From Many, One</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Destiny \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Dream \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Mana</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure is no longer an option for the Daydreamer, nor is it something she has the time to tolerate. This attainment mimics Miracle (Fate \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with an instant cast time. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - The mage and the Oneiropolis are truly one, working together at all times. The mage can rely on the collective wisdom and intelligence of the Oneiropolis, and thus can use Augment Mind (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with instant casting time, advanced duration, and the ability to exceed the normal maximum attribute limit. This effect may only be used on the mage herself.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT log: Per Zombiecakes's feedback, replaced 3rd attainment with something less redundant.<br /> EDIT log #2: Expanded the flavor text.<br /> EDIT log #3: Changed first attainment (now uncaps dream and destiny by fate, instead of providing one free dot of destiny). Changed 3rd optional to more thematically appropriate Dream Reaching, changed flavor text of fourth attainment, and changed optional effect of 5th attainment to be mage-only.<br /> EDIT log #4: Replaced second optional attainment with something more balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 11-23-2016, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:02:08-08:00","id":999506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=999433#post999433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that suggests the ability to target abyssal effects and apply Conditional Duration to them and adding Banes to the ephemera might be something. Instead of focusing on the patterns that are tainted, focus on the active broken force. Wouldn't be a straight spell, since nothing quite like that exists, but it would certainly fit the theme.<br /> <br /> Requiring a ritual to define how something may be destroyed seems fair. Something to permit the binding of an entity to a location or outside of one makes sense, too. Allowing the mage at some level to treat Paradox and abyssal stuff as valid conditions for a Ban seems good, too, but the rules for what that means probably deserve some attention....</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand what you mean here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:01:12-08:00","id":1000004,"title":"","content":"Based on the conversations in the Vampire and Immortality thread, I'm wondering if there is stock in a Legacy that exploits the &quot;A Ghost is an Imprint of a Person&quot; property to use Ghosts as a stepping stone for AI. What Arcana (other than Death) might it be? End result would be creating Ghosts from still living people to use as the seed for AI, &quot;immortality&quot;, and &quot;human&quot; directed drones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:48:20-08:00","id":1000074,"title":"","content":"Forces probably since that's kind of the realm of software. Using a ghost as a copy of a person creates kind of a crappy copy though, you definitely suffer fidelity loss, flipped virtue/vice, limited drives, inability to &quot;grow&quot; without further mutations into monstrosity via the Underworld, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:58:11-08:00","id":1000080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1000074#post1000074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces probably since that's kind of the realm of software. Using a ghost as a copy of a person creates kind of a crappy copy though, you definitely suffer fidelity loss, flipped virtue/vice, limited drives, inability to &quot;grow&quot; without further mutations into monstrosity via the Underworld, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind too, probably? I feel that it's the more appropriate way to create humanoid constructs, by using magic to emulate the most versatile and complex consciousness we've ever seen( and can also control).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T19:02:28-08:00","id":1000084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=998218#post998218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Vox Auctoritatis - </i>A legacy started by a Guardian who manifested his authority through the power of his voice. Commanding, intimidating, and even imperial in nature, when these mages Speak, the whole of the Fallen World listens. (Forces, Optional ???)</div> </div> </div> </div>So I realized I've personally had enough of the strong Greco/Roman Mage influences and reshaped this into something of Nordic origin. By request, here is a half fleshed out version of this Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Askatalare</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">He is silent in this mediation. Indeed, he is silent in almost all negotiations these days. His words are precious to him, and he does not waste them on trivialities. The discussion begins to break down as his less reserved colleagues fling bitter insults at one another. Both sides fall silent as he pulls down the scarf covering his mouth; they are not fools that fear his voice, but wise men who fear his Truth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WHEN THE WHOLE WORLD IS SILENT, EVEN ONE VOICE BECOMES POWERFUL</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The traditions of the Askatalare date back to the Viking North, when mages of great power and stature were expected to demonstrate their strength both on and off the battlefield. The Askatalare, or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Thundertalkers</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, are comprised of men and women who demonstrate strength and composure equally well in combat as in negotiation. The Askatalare carry the weight of their most prized possessions, their voices, at all times. Knowing and respecting both the physical and metaphysical power of their sound, they are warrior-poets who seek to bring Truth to the Lie. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ORIGINS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parentage: Mostly Obrimos, Silver Ladder or Guardians of the Veil</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Background: The Askatalare are prominent in northern Europe, and many tend to be people who have demonstrated their skill in both combat and arbitration. Businessmen, lawyers, judges, mediators, doctors, and performers are all prime candidates for receiving the training the Askatalare require.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance: The Askatalare tend to cover their mouths when not speaking (or even when talking). They have great respect for their voices and take care to protect their mouths and their throats. It\u2019s not uncommon for an Askatalare to wear a scarf even in warmer weather, or a tie even on informal occasions. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">DOCTRINE</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf, Expression \u25cf\u25cf or Intimidation \u25cf\u25cf, Athletics \u25cf\u25cf or Firearms \u25cf\u25cf or Weaponry \u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation: The prospective Askatalaren is arranged to spar with increasingly senior members of the Askatalare. The combat is watched by local members of the Legacy, who usually stand in deafening silence in a circle around the combatants. Should the prospect be defeated or be victorious, he is scheduled to spar again. The initiation process is over when the prospect, instead of fighting, talks his opponent out of combat (through any combination of persuasion, intimidation, or expression). A prospect can go through as many as a dozen rounds of fighting before realizing that combat is not the correct solution to the initiation ritual.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Organization: Askatalare are diplomatic, usually electing local leaders based on perceived strength. As there are not too many Askatalare and they are regionally confined to northern Europe, elections are an informal process governed by vocal votes. Typically one or two members offers to mentor a new initiate, who will then receive increased training in the art of Aska Tal. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theory: The Askatalare are trained to craft their voice into a vessel for their magics. The Askatalare know that the voice is a unique weapon, in part because it doesn\u2019t have to be a weapon at all. The Askatalare seek out positions of power and then serve with righteous authority. They feel (and perhaps rightly so) that their training has prepared them to avoid most conflicts when possible, but to win any that may arise. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">MAGIC:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcanum: Forces</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: Singing or similar recitation (+2), de-escalating a conflict (+2), winning a battle of wits (+2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: Arbitrating a disagreement, meditation in absolute silence, singing as part of a chorus, abstaining from speech for extended periods of time</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Attainment: Voice of the People</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When speaking or screaming, the mage may increase or decrease the volume of her own voice by one step per the table on pg. 146.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Prime \u25cf) - Pierce Deception with instant cast time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second Attainment: Ear to the Ground</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf, Expression \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf or Intimidation \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The subject heightens her influence over sound dramatically. She gains the benefits of Receiver (Forces \u25cf) with instant cast time and advanced duration. Apply the Potency of this attainment as a bonus to dice pools involving stealth or avoiding ambush as appropriate. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Prime \u25cf\u25cf) - Words of Truth with instant cast time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third Attainment: The Obedient Voice</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage gains the ability to influence sound more directly. Functions as Control Sound (Forces \u25cf\u25cf) with instant cast time and advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - The mage\u2019s voice resonates with undeniable Supernal Truth. By spending a point of mana, the mage enchants her vocal cords for one scene. Her voice can be heard by creatures in all forms of Twilight (ghosts, spirits, angels, etc.). Her spells and attainments may now affect these beings provided they incorporate her voice as a primary element of the spell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth Attainment: Speak Truth to Power</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage channels sound into a roaring blast focused in one direction. Per the Telekinetic Strike (Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with instant cast time, and applies either the Deafened Tilt or Knocked Down tilt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - The mage may automatically attempt to resist any action, or spell that would prevent her from being able to use her voice. Any attempt, mundane or magical, to silence the mage provokes a Clash of Wills against her Gnosis + Prime. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth Attainment: Thunder without Lightning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage\u2019s voice is now a force of nature to be reckoned with. By shouting she induces an effect similar to Earthquake (Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) with instant cast time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) - At the mage\u2019s discretion, victims of this attainment also suffer one point of aggravated damage per Potency.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T13:16:58-08:00","id":1005076,"title":"","content":"I got asked to convert Tamers of Fire from the Legacies the Ancient book:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 1st Attainment: Respect the Flame<br /> Pre-requisites: Initiation (Forces \u25cf\u25cf, Athletics \u25cf, Expression \u25cf)<br /> The mage may use burn marks as a Dedicated Magic tool (yantra +2), whether these marks are on a foreign object or the mage\u2019s own body.<br /> Optional (Mind \u25cf): Mental Scan with Instant Cast Time<br /> <br /> <br /> 2nd Attainment: Touch the Flame<br /> Pre-requisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf, Athletics \u25cf\u25cf, Expression \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Influence Fire with instant cast time and advanced duration<br /> Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf): First Impressions with Instant Cast Time<br /> <br /> <br /> 3rd Attainment: Catch the Flame<br /> Pre-requsities: Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Athletics \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf or Expression \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Control Fire with instant cast time and advanced duration<br /> Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Emotional Urging with Instant Cast Time and Sensory Range<br /> <br /> <br /> 4th Attainment: Hone the Flame<br /> Pre-requisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> The mage pours energy into her target. This Attainment mimics the Thunderbolt spell with instant cast time.<br /> Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Augment Mind with Instant Cast Time and Sensory Range<br /> <br /> <br /> 5th Attainment: Become the Flame<br /> Pre-requisites: Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Custom Making Effect (primary effect: duration): As an instant action, the mage\u2019s body gives off incredible amounts of flame and heat. Everything within the area of effect centered on the mage takes one bashing damage per Potency, and anyone within melee range of the Tamer takes one bashing damage per turn for the entire duration. Flammable objects within the area of effect ignite, and nonflammable objects that take their Durability in heat damage also ignite. <br /> Optional (Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Psychic Reprogramming with Instant Cast Time and Advanced Duration<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:11:01-08:00","id":1005951,"title":"","content":"Relate to the Doctor Strange thread, but it seems more fitting here - has anybody made the sorcerers of Kamar-Taj who star there into a Legacy? After all, all of them has been taught by the Ancient One, save possibly for the Ancient One herself, under the same focus of magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:42:16-08:00","id":1005961,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about it myself. Some kind of Space/Prime legacy built around using artifacts, conjuring platonic forms, and accessing the mirror dimension is my thought. Probably replace the rings with a direct co-location attainment. Something like:<br /> <br /> 1st:<br /> Word of Command (instant - since they use Artifacts so much)<br /> Ground-Eater (instant - just because it's an iconic effect from the movie)<br /> <br /> 2nd:<br /> As Above, So Below (instant - good utility spell that could boost their legacy yantras)<br /> Ward (advanced duration - for sanctum defense without using up spell control)<br /> <br /> 3rd:<br /> Platonic Form (instant- due to Mana Break, costs only 1 Mana but object is treated as having [Potency] Mana)<br /> some sort of Space Weaving effect that recreates Ghost Gate, but accesses the Mirror Dimension instead of Death Twilight (instant)<br /> <br /> 4th:<br /> some sort of Prime Patterning effect that recreates Psychic Projection, possibly by turning into ephemeral Mana<br /> Co-Location (instant, stable portal)<br /> <br /> 5th:<br /> Apocalypse (instant, advanced duration)<br /> Pocket Dimension (advanced duration)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> The Mirror Dimension is a Space Emanation Realm with all attendant benefits. The movie does it justice much better than a written description from me could. Legacy practitioners access it to cast spells away from Sleepers, work complex Space magic without risking Paradox, settle disputes and train apprentices in private, and travel and spy on material places unseen.<br /> <br /> It has a way of fracturing and refracting and trapping the unwary. For every hour that a person spends in the Mirror Dimension, they must roll (Wits+Composure?) to keep their bearings or suffer a Condition such as Lost or Spooked.<br /> <br /> Mages can affect the Mirror Dimension using Space versions of the Matter spells Lodestone, Shaping, Shrink and Grow, Ghostwall, Annihilate Matter, and Ex Nihilo.<br /> <br /> Accessing the Mirror Dimension is slightly safer once the mage has Space 4 and can cast Alter Direction. Being able to redefine one's personal &quot;down&quot; is a lifesaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-21-2016, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:37:18-08:00","id":1006003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=999504#post999504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get general or specific thoughts on a Legacy I'm working on? Either as to the flavor or the attainments or just in general:<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure: some thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1st: I think you might extend both Dream and Destiny maxima by Fate rather than improve the merit.<br /> Optional can make Dream grant automatic successes according to Mind. Probably needs a separate attainment to turn it into an Instant action if you're going to do that, so your way is probably better as the first, actually.<br /> <br /> 2nd is good. The optional is excessively nice. Might make this add Mind as bonus automatic successes to uses of Dream.<br /> <br /> 3rd is good, too. Optional seems a bit off theme. Maybe something related to Dream Reaching or Emotional Urging and the inspiration.<br /> <br /> 4th seems to have a description a bit off theme. They don't seem to be <i>mastering </i>their fate, they seem to be guided around it. The *effect* is not bad.<br /> Optional is good.<br /> <br /> 5th optional: I'd consider adjusting it to something akin to &quot;Learning to trust the guidance of the Oneiropolis frees Daydreamer of the need to consciously think. This permits them to conjure their vision and the Oneriopolis provides a stream of guidance towards that goal. The result is Augment the Mind (Mind 3-3 Reach= Duration,Beyond Limits(2))&quot; Since that would need to be self-only, I'd probably convert that option into Instant casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:42:14-08:00","id":1006006,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:36px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Dreamspeakers</span></span><br /> <br /> To keep this briefer, I'll simply refer to the original in Legacies: The Ancient.<br /> For the most part, I'm just updating the parts that need updating.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Doctrine</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mind 2, Spirit 1, 4 or more dots across two or more the following: Academics, Empathy, Occult, Dream 1, Members must have shattered their inner Astral Barrier. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b><br /> Initiation requires the initiate's personal astral barrier to be removed. Initiation into the legacy creates a pressure that has one of only two outcomes: permanent removal of the individual's Astral Barrier or a breaking point. To overcome the internalized astral barrier requires going through a challenge to the normal limited worldview, and certain signs are well-known to prepare a soul for this legacy. <br /> <br /> Those who are already in the process of an Dreaming Awakening can be accepted and guided through to its conclusion essentially certain success. Encounters with the Dreamborn can sometimes trigger the Dreaming Awakening process. Mental breaks can launch people into these sink-or-swim mental challenges, as well, though not all mental illnesses are equivalent. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> The Dreamspeakers are tied to various specific cultures. These cultures have a wild variety of structures for organization. As a rule, the Dreamspeakers are extremely hierarchical, but in a familiy sense. The higher ranking members tend to be treated as respected elders of the culture that the specific group comes from. <br /> <br /> Between cultures, there is very little formal structured communication. The members' Order membership often overrides in such cases, since there is often strong enmity between twixt various communities that goes back centuries, especially between hidden medicine societies. <br /> <br /> The various incarnations of the legacy keep their own traditions and knowledge about initiations and Dreamborn. Almost any specific tradition will take the plight of a seeker lost in their Dreaming Awakening as a moral obligation, even if the subject is their enemy. (That said, some might *kill* certain sorts to resolve the problem, but they *do* resolve it.) This is one of the ways that can bring hostile rival traditions together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">1st: Dreamwalking</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> <br /> The Primal's Dream self is their true self. This was probably always true, but for Primals it becomes an unavoidable truth.<br /> <br /> Those who bear this attainment are always partially in the Dream. <br /> <br /> This has advantages and disadvantages. First, the only things that a Primal can do in one side without doing the same in both are sedentary things like sleeping or sitting.<br /> <br /> Primals need not meditate to enter the astral realms, already being in both, and do not, thus, require mana to pass the Astral boundary.<br /> <br /> Because the normal refreshing shock of waking out of the trance is no longer an option for them, however, the Primal has certain risks regarding their own Oneiros that other mages normally do not. Even more dangerous, they cannot simply will to wake up. When killed in the astral, the mage doesn't die, but their mind falls into a coma. <br /> <br /> This can sometimes lead to a vision of a Dreamborn and it often leads to death.<br /> <br /> A Primal can participate in Dream Shaping. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">2nd: Dreamform</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mind 2<br /> Primals understand the Astral as their native home. Attempts to navigate deeper or return are almost assured. Primals add successes equal to Mind when moving between strata or returning. The same benefit applies when navigating the various realms to return along the path trod, as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Spirit 2<br /> <br /> The Primal grows a protective skin around their soul. This applies to goetic powers and also reduces harm from any environmental hazards encountered in the Astral Realm by Spirit dots. This applies to the Exstatic Winds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">3rd: Dreamwings</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Mind 3<br /> As an Instant Action, the mage may Co-Locate his Aquaster astrally to any location to which the mage bears Connected sympathy. At the end of the effect, the mage may choose which location to remain in, and the Primal may cancel the effect reflexively.<br /> <br /> This actually involves visualizing and *symbolically becoming* something that can move rapidly, so it's possible to become a version of you that literally has functional wings. The cost of using the effect increases by 1 Willpower if the form doesn't fit one of the realms. If it doesn't really fit either, it still works if you pay 1 Mana, as well.<br /> <br /> Should the Primal wish to retain the characteristics after the effect ends, that requires a Dream Shaping roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Spirit 3<br /> <br /> Astral and spiritual phenomina blur to the bearer of this attainment. If the caster has the capacity to cast an effect that applies to one a type of ephemera (goetic vs. shadow), but has cast it to affect another, changing the choice is as simple as a reflexive action on the Primal's initiative as basic part of spell control. <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">4th: Host the Dreamborn</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Mind 4<br /> To use this attainment requirs a trip out to the Dreamtime where a Dreamborn lives. Convincing that dreamborn to aid the Primal is the next hurdle. A Mana and willpower are required to learn that Dreamborn's blessing. (Only one can be used at a time.)<br /> <br /> The limitations (self only and selected by picking a Dreamborn patron) are worth a reach or two, easily.<br /> (Augment Mind-Mind 3: 2 Reach: Casting, Duration, Multiple attributes)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Spirit 4<br /> <br /> The Primal can call a Dreamborn with whom they bear a pact to inhabit some acceptable physical vessel. <br /> (Rouse Spirit-Spirit 3=2 Reach: Casting, Duration(Not primary))<br /> <br /> The Dreamspeaker can strike this particular pact with a Dreamborn independently of the other, but often these are one and the same. The same requirements apply: mana and willpower to set the bargain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">5th: Dreameyes</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mind 5<br /> The Primal can pull his dream self closer to the physical and view the world of mental Twilight as his Aquaster, using all the same game traits it normally does. Using this effect is an extension of the fourth attainment.<br /> <br /> (~Psychic Projection: Reach 2, Duration, Casting)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Spirit 3<br /> <br /> The mage can send his personal dream self into the Shadow world or into the Twilight of spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's an approach to a 2e version.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:45:53-08:00","id":1006080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1006006#post1006006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Dreamspeakers</span></span><br /> <br /> To keep this briefer, I'll simply refer to the original in Legacies: The Ancient.<br /> For the most part, I'm just updating the parts that need updating.<br /> <br /> (abridged for quoting)<br /> <br /> Here's an approach to a 2e version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good work there. I see you've decided to make most of the Attainments add-ons to the mage template, rather than converting spells. This certainly captures the feel of Astral mediums and mediators, though I admit I haven't read the original content in Legacies: The Ancient so I can't comment much.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, how good would the various Traditions/Conventions/Crafts from Ascension would be as Legacies? Did anybody already convert them, canon or homebrewed? Or has the Translation Guide done a good enough job already, so should I buy it? I heard that some Legacies are effectively reimagined versions of them, like the Thrice-Great and the Thread Cutters - has anyone converted them into 2e?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T06:18:30-08:00","id":1006161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1006003#post1006003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure: some thoughts:</div> </div> </div> </div>These are great suggestions, thank you! I'll take them into advisement and re-edit the Legacy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:34:04-08:00","id":1006269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1006080#post1006080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good work there. I see you've decided to make most of the Attainments add-ons to the mage template, rather than converting spells. This certainly captures the feel of Astral mediums and mediators, though I admit I haven't read the original content in Legacies: The Ancient so I can't comment much.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, how good would the various Traditions/Conventions/Crafts from Ascension would be as Legacies? Did anybody already convert them, canon or homebrewed? Or has the Translation Guide done a good enough job already, so should I buy it? I heard that some Legacies are effectively reimagined versions of them, like the Thrice-Great and the Thread Cutters - has anyone converted them into 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thanks. The description &quot;Astral Mediums and mediators&quot; absolutely fits the original write-up, so that sounds promising.without breaking the new legacy rules overmuch. The three attainments and optionals from the original Awakening version are, more or less, mapped to the same effects here. There are some alterations, but are identifiably the same feel, I hope.<br /> <br /> There were not too many of the Ascension traditions that didn't get a legacy treatment in 1e. This narrowed their scope, as you might expect. Thus, some of the related concepts got more than one legacy.<br /> <br /> Akashics were the Physical Adepts and, sort of, the Demon Wind.<br /> Al-i-Bhatin were the Subtle Ones.<br /> Cult of Ecstasy were the Fallen Pillar, though Sphinxes, Pygmalian, Skald, and Walkers in the Mists could all fit, too.<br /> Euthanatos were the Thread Cutters but also fit the Logophages, Stone Scribes, and Daoine.<br /> Etherites and Void Engineers were the Free Fraggin Council and covered by many legacies like Imgaineers. (et alis)<br /> Etherites are particularly covered by Threnodists and Transhuman Engineers<br /> <br /> Hermetics <i>should</i> be multiple legacies. Notably the Thrice Great, Clavicularius, Uncrowned Kings, and House of Ariadne fit.<br /> Verbena were kinda covered by the Orphans of Proteus, Sodality of Tor, Daoine, Clavicularius, Walkers in the Mist, Fangs of Mara...<br /> The goths were kinda covered by the Free Council (magpie) and the Scelesti (nihilism).<br /> <br /> There were also user-created legacies to fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> @Kvark: You are certainly welcome, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T06:58:43-08:00","id":1006687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1006269#post1006269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Kvark: You are certainly welcome, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you again for your suggestions, I've edited several of them into the Legacy. I was wondering if you had any alternate suggestions for the optional 2nd attainment effect, as Dream no longer requires a dice roll to succeed in 2E I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:59:43-08:00","id":1007014,"title":"","content":"You are correct. Oops.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Maybe use the merit once per day per dot of Mind without needing to meditate? I dunno. It's not <i>that</i> much different from the spell Prophecy with a reach, so just removing the meditation/sleep requirement sounds valid. (<i>Some</i> limitation seems fair; maybe once per scene.) Nothing leaps to mind.<br /> <br /> Well, actually, something a bit like Serendipity, but cast using Dream might serve. (Limiting to the character's dream goals somehow seems reasonable, too)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T08:44:32-08:00","id":1007272,"title":"","content":"How about something like, &quot;The mage becomes comfortable delegating certain tasks to the Oneiropolis, and grows more confident in his ability to interpret the resulting visions and dreams. In practice she gains the ability to use One Mind, Two Thoughts with instant cast time and advanced duration, as well as the reach to perform two instant mental tasks at once. This attainment can only affect the mage herself.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:36:14-08:00","id":1007317,"title":"","content":"Makes sense to me. That would be one extra Reach with a restriction to self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T22:33:32-08:00","id":1007952,"title":"","content":"Does anybody have ideas for a Legacy of Tarot cartomancers? I can think of Yantras and Oblations fairly easily, but I can't think of any interesting Attainments for them other than &quot;really good at reading your future&quot; ones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:57:31-08:00","id":1008007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1007952#post1007952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody have ideas for a Legacy of Tarot cartomancers? I can think of Yantras and Oblations fairly easily, but I can't think of any interesting Attainments for them other than &quot;really good at reading your future&quot; ones</div> </div> </div> </div>How about, instead of going the divinations route, if it takes the &quot;This is now your Fate. You are the Chariot. Have fun with it, or else.&quot; approach?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:58:43-08:00","id":1008159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1007952#post1007952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody have ideas for a Legacy of Tarot cartomancers? I can think of Yantras and Oblations fairly easily, but I can't think of any interesting Attainments for them other than &quot;really good at reading your future&quot; ones</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tarot isn't just used to define the future, it's also used for meditation, communing with the dead or with spirits, etc. If I had to build a Legacy around this idea I would most likely try to do it by having the cards be a dedicated tool for her magics. Ruling Arcanum is Spirit, Optional Arcanum is Time. The Attainments could deal with summoning and coaxing spirits, with optional effects that would mimic divination, postcognition, Choosing the Thread, etc. If you want I can take a whack at putting it together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:07:53-08:00","id":1009271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1008159#post1008159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tarot isn't just used to define the future, it's also used for meditation, communing with the dead or with spirits, etc. If I had to build a Legacy around this idea I would most likely try to do it by having the cards be a dedicated tool for her magics. Ruling Arcanum is Spirit, Optional Arcanum is Time. The Attainments could deal with summoning and coaxing spirits, with optional effects that would mimic divination, postcognition, Choosing the Thread, etc. If you want I can take a whack at putting it together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, as an amateur reader myself, I stayed well clear of the spirit stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was picturing more of a Mind + Time combo, with Mind used for the meditation and &quot;communing with your own subconsciousness&quot; stuff. But Spirit sounds just as good!<br /> <br /> If you could take a whack, I'd be most grateful. I'm caught up in exams <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T00:20:32-08:00","id":1010544,"title":"","content":"Exams are still looming, but I've got myself caught up so much in this that I couldn't focus without letting it all out.<br /> <br /> So here's my take on the Clavicularius (well, at least their Attainments): <hr /><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>The Whispers Within</b><ul><li>The Attainment transforms the Solomonist's Goetia representing her Vice into an esoteric; a whispering presence that wades in the conscious mind, standing at that liminal point between the physical and the Astral. The esoteric can communicate with the mage and in turn be affected by her own Mind magic. The Vice-demon cannot supernaturally influence the Solomonist, for it is not yet Manifested in the physical world, but will constantly seduce her into acting on her Vice whenever an opportunity occurs. Resisting the temptation grants her a positive Condition such as Inspired or Steadfast, while succumbing into it gives her a point of Willpower as usual and imposes the Guilty or similar Condition. Should the esoteric be banished or discorporated, it submerges to the Oneiros and recuperates for a day, after which it reenters the Solomonist's psyche.</li> <li><b>Optional: Mind 1</b></li> <li>The Attainment emulates &quot;One Mind, One Thoughts&quot;, with Reach assigned to performing two tasks at the same time. The Solomonist and his Vice-demon work in tandem, but tasks undertaken by the latter will always reflect the Vice it was born out of. The demon will not tempt the mage until its task is finished, and thus the Solomonist does not gain additional effects for resisting or giving into her Vice.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>(Second Attainment)</b><ul><li>The Attainment emulates &quot;Gossamer Touch&quot;, with Reach assigned to advanced Duration. This Attainment only affects the Solomonist's own Vice-demon, allowing it to physically interact with entities in Spirit-attuned Twilight. Those Twilight entities may not be able to affect or even perceive the esoteric, depending on their capabilities. Also, the Solomonist herself and other mages may affect the Vice-demon with Spirit magic as if it were a spirit, as long as this Attainment is in effect.</li> <li><b>Optional: Mind 2</b></li> <li>The Attainment emulates &quot;Dream Reaching&quot;, with Reach assigned to allowing active engagement in the dream. This Attainment only affects the Solomonist himself, and when used always induces a lucid dream with both the mage and his Vice-demon as main actors. The contest between them is played out as Social Maneuvering with the demon using the same Attributes as the Solomonist, and where both start on Excellent first impressions with each other.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>(Third Attainment)</b><ul><li>The Attainment emulates &quot;Spirit Summons&quot;, with Reach assigned to giving the entity a single command. This Attainment only affects the Solomonist's own Vice-demon, counting herself Resonant for purposes of preventing Essence Bleed. If the mage has succumbed to the demon's temptations and indulged her Vice just before or as part of summoning the demon, it may be given complex commands. If the mage has resisted the temptation instead, she may instead choose to ignore the Withstand rating of the demon when summoning it. As the Vice-demon is now outside the Oneiros, the Solomonist is not affected by her Vice for the Attainment's Duration.</li> <li><b>Optional: Mind 3</b></li> <li>(still undecided)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>(Fourth Attainment)</b><ul><li>The Attainment emulates &quot;Bind Spirit&quot;, with Reach assigned to advanced Duration. This Attainment only affects the Solomonist's own Vice-demon she summoned with the third Attainment, counting herself Open for purposes of applying Manifestations on herself. She must still apply any prerequisite Conditions as normal when binding the demon to something or someone else. If the Solomonist has resisted the demon's temptations when using the third Attainment prior to using this one, she ignores its Withstand rating for this Attainment as well, and may give the demon a number of commands equal to her Mind dots without the need of spells or negotiation. As with the third Attainment, the mage is not affected by her Vice for the Attainment's Duration.</li> <li><b>Optional: Mind 4</b></li> <li>The Attainment emulates &quot;Psychic Projection&quot;, with Reach assigned to advanced Duration. When projected, the Solomonist's psyche wears his Vice-demon as armor, and scores automatic successes equal to his Mind dots when resisting or contesting mind-affecting powers attempting to influence him. However, during projection the mage loses one point of Willpower whenever he passes by an opportunity to indulge his Vice.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>(Fifth Attainment)</b><ul><li>The Attainment emulates &quot;Familiar&quot;, with Reach assigned to advanced Duration. This ignores the normal Rank limit on the bonded ephemeral entity. As with the third and fourth Attainments, the mage is not affected by her Vice for the Attainment's Duration.</li> <li><b>Optional: Mind 5</b></li> <li>Whenever the Vice-demon is outside his Oneiros, either from his Attainmens or other magic, the Solomonist enjoys the Vice-removing effect of &quot;Amorality&quot;.</li> </ul></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  EDIT: formatting 12-01-2016, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:58:50-08:00","id":1015878,"title":"","content":"Has there ever been a Legacy dedicated to applying the scientific method to magic, a la the Null Mysteriis from Hunter? Their Attainments could be based around not only the development of magical devices, but also around perfecting their capacity for reasoning and data gathering.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, is there a Legacy whose members embody the Jungian Archetype of the Trickster in some way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-11-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T16:29:20-08:00","id":1015890,"title":"","content":"Theoretically a lot of legacies can handle the &quot;employs scientific methods&quot; theme since it's pretty vague. Threnodists, Crypotologos, Reality Stalkers, Forge Masters, Transhuman Engineers, and Sphinxes, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:58:17-08:00","id":1016266,"title":"","content":"Here are some ideas for a Trickster Legacy. If anyone is interested in a full write up, please tell me.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Celebrants Of The Torn Facade</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Origins<br /> Parentage:</b> Acanthus<br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Jesters, Meddlers (Derogatory)<br /> <b>Background:</b> Most Celebrants have ties to movements in favor of free speech and civil rights. They can also be journalists and artists of various types who use their way with words to bridge the gap between common men and those who think of themselves as gods of Olympus.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine<br /> Prerequisites: </b> Mind 2, Expression 2 and one of the following at 2: Politics, Investigation, Persuasion or Subterfuge<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> The aspiring Celebrant must trick a leading figure of the Consilium into exposing their own foolishness and mistakes they\u2019d rather hide. Bonus points if they admit it and try fix these issues.<br /> <b>Theory:</b> Everyone Wears Masks, and perfection is the most ridiculous mask of them all. There is no use in being Awakened if you keep telling yourself lies about how superior and above misfortune you are. To prevent their fellow mages from becoming too serious and full of themselves, the Celebrants become satirists and practical jokers.<br /> <br /> <b>Magic</b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum: </b>Mind<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Symbols of mythological tricksters such as Coyote, Loki and Hermes (+1 or +2 if clearly visible), taboo-breaking fashion choices (+2), wisecracking (+1), mocking or destroying a representation of a scorned authority figure (+1 for a handheld representation or +2 for a detailed, life sized one), hidden compartments (+1), disguises (+1 if basic or +2 if complex)<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Pulling pranks, giving satirical performances, making oneself the comic relief, teaching unorthodox lessons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:03:25-08:00","id":1016435,"title":"","content":"I've created a couple so far:<br /> <br /> <b>The Strangers</b><br /> Mastigos Arrow/Guardians Fate Legacy about limiting and cultivating one's sympathetic connections, believing that sympathies have been at least partially influenced by Fate, and entwining the two a Mage can take personal responsibility for their own Destiny. Powers mostly relate to using Fate magic to shape what's in store for them, rather than simple manipulations of Luck.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sistershood of Hope</b><br /> Obrimos Ladder Fate Legacy, somewhat made in jest. &quot;Magical Girl&quot; Legacy about trying to find the &quot;Fate beyond Fate&quot;, seeing what Magic can manipulate as nothing more than subtle influences named &quot;Fate&quot; in some grand display of Ego. TRUE Fate is found in the Supernal and its will. Manifestations of Supernal power independant of an individual's will are messages from that realm itself, which the Sisterhood try to find, to interpret the will of that realm, and find their way home. Somewhat out of keeping with many more staunchly independant and self-assured Obrimos, however in truth each Sister is self-directed and few interpret each discovered omen the same way.<br /> <br /> <b>The Broken Men/The Burning Men</b><br /> Thyrsus Arrow Forces Legacy about finding solace from mental trauma in primal emotions, then channeling those emotions into manifestations of power. Created with a PC in my last game, for his 1860's war veteran character who realised the juncture after he entered an emanation relam near identical to the Supernal Realm which he awakened in. In modern times, it's derided as a Legacy that focuses on being unable to let go for the past and which relishes in an inability to seek mental health assistance. But for the time, it's quite apt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Accidentally posted early 12-13-2016, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:08:14-08:00","id":1016585,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Legacy: The Goetic Road</span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When I\u2019m building Legacies, I generally get really absorbed in the esoteric or philosophical parts of the idea. I then spend more than a few weeks wrestling with making the mechanics and philosophies meet in the middle. This particular legacy was an idea that began as a joke and after reading the setting for Los Angeles in the core 2e book really took off in my mind.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The entire attainment line is based on a home-brew thought of connecting the mage\u2019s soul to a Temenos realm, that winds up allowing their Attainments to do things that might not be considered conventional. I wind up abusing the \u201cMany Roads\u201d and \u201cStrange Attainments\u201d sidebars from start to finish, in an attempt to both keep the attainments as valid extrapolations from the legacy\u2019s practices/philosophies AND keep the legacy\u2019s attainments useful and fun. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">My goal is to, with these considerations in mind, attempt a legacy that is as close to canonically viable as possible, while avoiding game-breaking imbalances where I deviate from those guidelines. I\u2019m still working on it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Creation is Magical; Passion is Power</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Goetic Road (or \u201cSkinwalkers\u201d as they are known to the Awakened) embrace the truth behind the Libertine belief that Humanity is Magical. They grasp it more intimately than other mages do: They wear Humanity\u2019s thoughts and dreams like a totemic shaman wears an animal\u2019s skin, evoking the essence of sleeper belief through the metaphorical song-and-dance of playing the part. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">By forging a connection between their soul and the Temenotic Realm appropriate to their Focus, and invoking that reality within this one, these mages manage to integrate themselves and their magic into the fringes of Sleeper societies and subcultures, not just bypassing the Curse and breathing life into the fight against the Lie - but using the Lie against itself. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Sleepers live, bound by the Lie. While they do, they also dream, hope, envision, explore and create -- they invent gods, stories, mythologies, they reach for the heavens and believe. As if in response to their oppressed, mundane existences, they immerse themselves and fascinate themselves with their creations. Skinwalkers form their magic from those Sleeper thoughts and passions. Sleepers envision the magic for the Skinwalkers; the those on Goetic Road just harness it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">They blur the lines between the Truth and the Lie from both sides.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Origins</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Parentage:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mastigos,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Free Council</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Background</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> Many Skinwalkers hail from backgrounds of fanatic devotion, mortal occultism, piousness or devout fandom. Most of them relied heavily on their Focus for personal stability before Awakening; and find that incorporating their past selves into their Magic is more fulfilling than obstructing. All enter the Legacy drenched in a fascination with the magic inherent in humanity, and an appreciation for story, art, creation and imagination.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doctrine</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> Mind 2, Occult 2, and one of the following additional Skills at 2 dots or higher, as appropriate to their Focus: Expression, Socialize, Academics.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Organization</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> Skinwalkers don\u2019t really organize among themselves; though they occasionally form groups of similarly-Focused mages that loosely operate together or form cabals. Skinwalkers don\u2019t really view themselves as a group, or an organization. To them, it\u2019s just a practice of magic in and of itself, and individual practitioners owe nothing to one another beyond, perhaps, the norms between mentor and student.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Theory</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> The Skinwalkers believe that humanity\u2019s mythological creations bear magical truth. Progress toward enlightenment requires creative thought; the mage who bears this Legacy channels the creations of mortals to learn and command Supernal Truths. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">To do so, the mages a of The Goetic Road forge a special connection between a particular Astral Realm and their soul -- their namesake -- and uses it to begin the cycle of creation and empowerment, from sleeper to mage to sleeper again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Magic</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Ruling Arcana:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Mind</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Yantras</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> Quotes from the writings of the Focus (+1), Succeeding on an Expression roll for reenactment of scenes or stories from the focus (+2), verbally explaining the deeper meaning of an element of the Focus to a Dreamer (+1), collecting artwork or scriptures or fanfiction relevant to the Focus and the Spell [Note, this Yantra is the act of the Collection, and separate from anything collected] (+2), fanfiction or artwork (+1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Oblations</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> Studying the mage\u2019s Focus such as pouring over appropriate religious scriptures and attending appropriate Churches or binge-watching an appropriate show on the internet, attending conventions for their chosen Fandom such as church or gaming cons, artistic expressions within their chosen Focus such as biblical essays or fanfiction, pursuing an obsessive or otherwise unbalanced indulgence in the Focus, discussing the deeper themes and meanings of their Focus with other believers/fans.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Jargon</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> The mage\u2019s </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Focus</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> is the theme of sleeper culture that the Mage dedicates themselves to: Something like a specific religion, mythology, or fictional universe. They may practice Skinwalking with Catholicism, the Harry Potter universe, greek mythology, or conspiracy theorists. The Mage\u2019s Goetic Road leads from the astral realm of their Focus to their own soul.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Dreamers</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> are people who are dedicated to that Focus: devout believers or priests, professors of mythology, the fandom community for a show or book series, the author or actors, etc.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Mantles</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> are the characters, locations and objects prominent in the Mage\u2019s focus. The Mantle must be either recurring, named, or otherwise significant in the narrative: Unimportant or one-off characters are not Mantles. (However, if the ST approves, tropes within a fandom or religion that are common or memetic might be valid: a Star Trek focused mage could treat \u201cred shirt\u201d as a mantle.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Vessels</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> are people, places or things that share traits in common with Mantles from the mage\u2019s Focus: A detective might be a Vessel for sherlock holmes. A hippie might be appropriate for Jesus Christ. A motorcycle may be appropriate for Ghost Rider\u2019s bicycle. A bible may be appropriate for the Ten Commandment Tablets. How appropriate a Vessel is is ultimately up to the ST: A model of a specific object should be appropriate; but so should something that is of the same \u201ctype\u201d of object or person or place.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">1</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Remember When</span></span></u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> (Gnosis 2, Mind 1, Compelling. 1 Reach: Instant action. Limitation: Subjects. Benefit: ?)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This Attainment is the first blurring of the lines between sleeper fiction or mythology and the Fallen World by making characters and stories play out through vessels in the world around them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The mage calls a Mantle down their Goetic Road and projects it onto a Vessel; causing the Vessel to take a single action appropriate to the Mantle. This has effects similar to Coaxing the Spirits, but can be applied to sentient Vessels or appropriate locations as well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The actions taken must be appropriate to the original narrative of Mantle (which must in turn be appropriate to the Vessel). This means modeling events frequently enacted by the Mantle or significant events in the Mantle\u2019s story. For instance, a Vessel for a character who is characterized as food-loving and always hungry may be made to eat something. If that Mantle is not characterized as food-loving and hungry, though, the Mage may not force this action. </span></span><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Influence</span></span></u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> (Gnosis 2, Mind 2, Ruling. 1 Reach: Duration. Limitation: Subjects. Benefit: ?)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Mage may act as if they have Status dots equal to Mind in a Focus-relevant organization, when playing the part of activities relevant to their focus (an act that takes at least one scene to accomplish.) This Status does not function against non-Dreamers. If their focus is Catholicism; then they gain this whenever they make efforts to representing a priest, or angel, to members of a church. This Status only functions with appropriate Dreamers and/or Vessels.</span></span><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">3</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Community</span></span></u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> (Gnosis 4, Mind 3. Reach: Instant Action. Limitation: Subjects. Benefit: ?)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Mage may tap into a Dreamer\u2019s connection to the Astral Realm of their Focus; allowing them to ignore the Curse on a number of Dreamers equal to their Gnosis at once. The Mage may only make use of this Attainment for spells that are appropriate to their Focus; such as prophecy or biblical miracles for a Catholic-themed mage. This Attainment mimics the effects of Stealing the Fire; however the Dreamer does not suffer delayed reactions; they simply don\u2019t suffer reactions at all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">4</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Dream Come True</span></span></u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> (Gnosis 6, Mind 4, Reach: Duration. Limitation: Subjects. Benefit: Instant Action.)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When a Mage is in desperate need of an object, location or entity from their mythology of choice, this attainment allows them to call it down from the Astral and project it onto an appropriate physical vessel in the fallen world. For instance, the mantle of the Spear of Destiny can be cast upon a mundane Spear, the Arc of the Covenant can be cast into an appropriately revered or structured box. A preacher may be given the mantle of a Saint appropriate to his Virtue, his relationships, or his position in the church. A malicious mage may cast the Salem Court over a courtroom or town hall.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Mantle that is brought down onto the Vessel will embody itself in a narrative sense, not just in their actions and thoughts. Vessels bearing Mantles will play out the Mantle\u2019s story in subtle (and ultimately profound) ways; adjusted for the reality they find themselves in. Two subjects bearing the mantles of Cain and Abel will, over time, find a reason to murder each other if left to their own devices, for example. A vessel wearing Joan of Arc will eventually burn at the stake.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Mantle is a goetia of rank equal to \u00bd the Mage\u2019s dots in Mind, rounded up. The Mantle always has a ban of \u201cThe Mantle will suffer the narratively significant fates suffered by that which it represents within the Focus as soon as those fates become an option. The Mantle of Judas will be talked into betraying his best friend, the mantle of the Titanic will sink.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Mage may spend a point of mana for a Vessel to \u2018black out\u2019 for the duration of the Mantle\u2019s ride. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Vessel is granted the following condition:</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Condition: Mantle-Ridden</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The object, living being, or location is possessed by a goetic entity called the Mantle. The Mantle may use its Influences and Numena while controlling the Vessel. It is not safe from Essence Bleed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Entity may pay one Essence to empower any action it takes such that it gains an Exceptional Success on 3 successes rather than 5, so long as that action is a close enough approximation of an important success for the Mantle in it\u2019s original narrative. The Mantle of Sampson may Empower an action to kill a lion with it\u2019s vessel\u2019s bare hands, the mantle of Delilah may be empowered to ease a warrior\u2019s distrust.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mantles possessing Vessels have a great deal of control over their hosts. A Mantle controlling a Vessel can\u2019t make it do anything the Vessel isn\u2019t physically capable of doing, but it can turn switches on and off, fully control the body of a living being, open doors within its location\u2019s boundaries, etc. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Use the Mantle\u2019s attributes for mental actions (or physical actions where a Vessel does not have appropriate attributes, such as when possessing a car or a creepy basement), and the Vessel\u2019s physical attributes where appropriate. For a point of Essence, the Mantle may read the Vessel\u2019s mind.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">To ride a Vessel, a Mantle must stay imposed over the Vessel in twilight. This means that if the host touches the Mantle\u2019s Bane or is injured by a weapon made of the bane, the Vessel will suffer wounds to its Corpus.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Resolution</b>: Any method by which a person might be exorcised of a possessing Entity will work to remove the Mantle from the Subject.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Beat</b>: N/A</span></span><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">5</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fan Theories</span></span></u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> (Gnosis 8, Mind 5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This Attainment represents ultimate mastery of the Goetic Road between the mage\u2019s soul and the Astral Realms of their focus; and ultimately allows the Mage to begin to tinker with the details of their Focus.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Once the mage has successfully mediated to enter the Astral (or used any other method to accomplish Astral Travel), their travel abilities are drastically improved due to the strength of the connection their soul has to the Temenos Realm of their Focus, and the sympathies that they share with Dreamers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">They may opt to arrive in the Astral not in their own Oneiros, but the Temenos Realm of their Focus; and from here the Mage may open Irises (Keyed in a fashion appropriate to the mage\u2019s Focus, and of the Mage\u2019s design) between their Temenos realm, their own personal Oneiros, and/or the Oneiros of any Dreamer appropriate to their Focus. These Irises always open to the astral realm of the mage\u2019s Focus within the appropriate mindscape, and the Mage may choose to Key the Irises in a fashion appropriate to their Focus.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The mage could, for instance, meditate to enter the Astral and arrive in the Temenos Realm of Catholicism. He could then open an Iris to the Oneiros of a local priest, pious believer, or theologist; and choose to key the Iris to a rosary or saying three Hail Maries.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From this vantage, the Mage is equipped to begin enacting heavy-duty influence over his Focus. Many Skinwalkers theorize that as the Mage gains the power to influence the thoughts of Dreamers to influence the Astral Realm of their Focus; as well as influencing the Astral Realm to change the thoughts of Dreamers, they can combine trickle-down changes with trickle-up changes in order to heavily shape the Sleeper\u2019s creations and beliefs; in turn shaping that magic which they create and ultimately growing their Goetic Road to encompass anything they desire -- a potential, if very hubris-ridden and long-running, path to Ascension.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":12721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","user":"EvilSqueegee","date":". 12-13-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T20:25:41-07:00","id":1100314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160644#post160644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Body Thiefs:</b> Seer Legacy asociated with the Prelates of the Unity that achieve a sort of inmortality by living inside the bodies of slepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pleeeeeeeease, pretty please post these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T02:01:28-07:00","id":1100375,"title":"","content":"Man, its been a while since those. Well, I could try, but their mechanics worked due to the old Prelacy rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:35:56-07:00","id":1100856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1100375#post1100375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, its been a while since those. Well, I could try, but their mechanics worked due to the old Prelacy rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's not a problem. A little love here and there and BAM, updated to the 2nd edition rules.<br /> At least, I'll try to update it. The concept is too perfect for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T05:50:33-07:00","id":1101591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=159580#post159580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the original topic of the post, so as to actually contribute something other than analysis:<br /> <br /> <b>The Scavengers of the Farthest Shore:</b> A legacy of skilled Astral Travelers that is currently under scrutiny for left-handedness, the Scavengers of the Farthest Shore are fascinated by the various creatures and objects that wash up on the shores of the Ocean Oroboros. They believe that the twisted things that wash up on the shores are actually abyssal reflections or permutations of what has been lost within the Ocean's black depths over the ages - and that with proper study, fragments of the time before the abyss can be seen within their twisted forms.<br /> Obviously this legacy is prone to low-wisdom madmen who are easily tempted by the Abyss they study, but the legacy is difficult to detect... as part of their first Attainment is casting away the magical signs of their legacy into the Ocean Oroboros. Later attainments also involve casting parts of themselves into that same devouring ocean, but make them incredibly skilled Astral Travelers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was just re-reading this thread, and had to ask. Have you actually written a detailed description of this Legacy? I cannot stress enough how much i would absolute love reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T08:08:54-07:00","id":1101644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=160658#post160658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep: <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default5783-2.html?g=posts&amp;m=1173580#post1173580\" target=\"_blank\">link</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This link appears to be broken! Could you repost it? ^^<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T19:47:30-07:00","id":1107186,"title":"","content":"<b>Legacy: The Reforged</b><br /> <br /> <i>If the body is a temple</i>, say modern Reforged, <i>then the architect was half-blind and the construction crew was drunk</i>. Their ancient counterparts might not have put it quite so bluntly, but they would have recognized the sentiment: human flesh is heir to a thousand natural shocks, none of them pleasant and many of them all-too-easily fatal. <br /> <br /> Their roots allegedly trace back to Atlantean soil. Many martial disciplines employ the euphemism of \u201cbecoming one with\u201d a weapon to describe a state of intense mental focus, but the Reforged claim that the original meaning is quite literal: that the <i>Ungula Draconis</i> reshaped their bodies to match the keen edges of their blades and the enduring strength of their armor. In very modern nights, a nascent offshoot of the Legacy is developing within the Free Council, inspired by new developments in genetic engineering and \u201cwetware\u201d implantation.<br /> <br /> The Legacy\u2019s knowledge of angels &amp; demons is not extensive, but a string of ill-fated encounters have made them increasingly aware of the God-Machine as an entity capable of merging flesh and machinery in a way they don\u2019t understand (and certainly not to the empowerment of any humans involved.) To the God-Machine, the Reforged might be an irrelevant oddity\u2026 or It might be on the verge of becoming a Legacy-wide threat.<br /> <br /> <b>Origins</b><br /> <br /> Parentage: Moros, Adamantine Arrow or Free Council<br /> <br /> Background: Professional backgrounds as doctors, athletes, and soldiers are well-represented within the Legacy. The Reforged seek mages who a) demonstrate talent and inclination in the defense of others, and b) chafe at the limitations and weaknesses imposed by physical frailty. Where candidates display the former but not the latter, the Legacy wishes them well; they\u2019ll make good Arrows, even if they\u2019re not ready to recognize their full potential. If it\u2019s the other way around, the Legacy actively discourages them from applying; they have enough Left-Handed black sheep without adding more to the flock.<br /> <br /> Appearance: Inevitably among the most physically-fit of mages, the Reforged are never far from useful bits &amp; pieces of tech, weaponizable and otherwise.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Life 2; Athletics 1, Medicine 1, Science 1; at least one of Brawl, Firearms, or Weaponry 2<br /> <br /> Initiation: Save a life (usually, though not always, that of a Sleeper) from a source of violence or natural hazard requiring superhuman physical ability to overcome.<br /> <br /> Organization: Beyond the usual Socratic mentor-student dynamic, Reforged are expected to actively contribute to the defense of Sleepers against supernatural threats, usually in conjunction with their cabal and local Arrow chapter. The extent to which they owe that duty to Sleepers they feel are undeserving (<i>e.g. </i>a drunken brawl escalated into the murder of a werewolf\u2019s human family member) is a subject of hot debate and varies widely in application. <br /> <br /> Theory: Eternal truths of Life &amp; Matter bleed together with modern understandings of nanotechnology and medicine. They synergize, two parallel paths pointing towards the same goal: a vision of a humanity that stands unafraid in the darkness, torch lit and held aloft, on the cusp on conquering Death itself.<br /> <br /> At their best, the Reforged share philosophical tenets with the Perfected Adepts and with the Arrow at large. The Supernal is the Self; reforging the Self upon the anvil of one\u2019s Awakened will can bring one closer to the Supernal. Wise Reforged are conscious of the duty imposed by their capability; they owe it to humanity to stand, iron-fleshed, against deadly nightmares who would make human beings their chosen prey. From the Free Council\u2019s perspective, incorporating the fruits of modern ingenuity into the flesh is a proud declaration that Humanity is Magical, and that \u201cmere\u201d human technology can rival Awakened magic in flexibility and potency.<br /> <br /> At their worst, the Reforged lose sight of the fact that often, it is human frailty that lies at the root of human <i>empathy</i>. Experiencing the slings &amp; arrows of disease, hunger, and violence is more than just an impediment on the road to enlightenment; it\u2019s the touchstone that links witnessing such suffering with the desire to help alleviate it, because you understand what it feels like. The Legacy, to its shame, has turned out a fair number of mages who later turned to Left-Handed practices, cutting away their Wisdom with the same readiness as they would a genetic predisposition to cardiac disease.<br /> <br /> <b>Magic</b><br /> <br /> Ruling Arcanum: Life<br /> Yantras: Exceptional Success on an Athletics roll (+1); explaining a biotechnology concept to a layperson (+1); teaching self-defense techniques to Sleepers (+1); building fortifications or otherwise securing defenses (+2); discover new and important information about the God-Machine (+2).<br /> Oblations: Physical training; martial kata; cleaning &amp; assembling arms or armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <br /> <u>First: Warrior\u2019s Eye</u><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> As &quot;Heightened Senses.&quot; Potency [Life]; Duration one day or one week (Life 4). Casting time: one scene. Reach: Advanced Duration, additional spell effect (track by scent.)<br /> Optional: Matter 2<br /> As \u201cCraftsman\u2019s Eye.\u201d Duration [Matter] turns. Casting time: instant. Reach: instant casting, additional spell effect (understand utility, gain 8-Again.)<br /> <br /> <u>Second: Monk\u2019s Hammer</u><br /> Prerequisites: Life 2, Medicine 2<br /> As &quot;Body Control.&quot; Potency [Life]; Duration one day or one week (Life 4). Casting time: one scene. Reach: Advanced Duration.<br /> Optional: Matter 2<br /> As \u201cFind the Balance.\u201d Duration one day or one week (Matter 4). Casting time: one scene. Reach: Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <u>Third: Golem\u2019s Anvil</u><br /> Prerequisites: Life 3, Athletics 2, Science 2<br /> As &quot;Honing the Form.&quot; Potency [Life]; Duration one day or one week (Life 4). Casting time: one scene. Reach: Advanced Duration.<br /> Optional: Matter 3, Crafts 2<br /> As \u201cWonderful Machine.\u201d Potency [Matter]; Duration [Matter] turns. Unique limitation: target self only. Casting time: instant action. Reach: instant casting.<br /> <br /> <u>Fourth: Giant\u2019s Stance</u><br /> Prerequisites: Life 4, Medicine 3<br /> As &quot;Honing the Form.&quot; Potency [Life]; Duration one week. Casting time: one scene. Reach: Advanced Duration, additional spell effect (two attributes).<br /> Optional: Matter 4, Brawl 2<br /> As \u201cShrink and Grow.\u201d Potency [Matter]; Duration one week. Target: self only. Unique limitation: can only increase Size, not decrease it. Casting time: instant action. Reach: instant casting, advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <u>Fifth: Titan\u2019s Forge</u><br /> Prerequisites: Life 5, Athletics 3, Science 3<br /> As &quot;Honing the Form.&quot; Potency [Life]; Duration one week. Casting time: one scene. Reach: Advanced Duration, additional spell effect (three attributes).<br /> Optional: Matter 5, Brawl 3<br /> As \u201cColossus.\u201d The Reforged becomes living steel for the scene. Muscle, tissue, and bone become a material with Durability [Matter]. This Durability is added to the mage's Health and Armor; per the normal rules for Objects, this additional Armor does not apply against aggravated damage. The mage's unarmed attacks are now lethal weapons with damage rating [Matter]. Unless an attack deals aggravated damage, the mage is immune to the Arm Wrack and Leg Wrack tilts, no longer needs to breathe or eat, does not suffer wound penalties, and is immune to the Bleeding, Drugged, Poisoned, Sick, and Stunned Tilts. Reach: instant casting, advanced duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T11:16:34-07:00","id":1107375,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any ideas for something for Moros with Prime? Beyond the obvious thaumaturgical alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T15:37:47-07:00","id":1107430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1107375#post1107375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any ideas for something for Moros with Prime? Beyond the obvious thaumaturgical alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was developing one that was Moros with Prime as the Ruling and Death as an Optional but is is still in development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:59:00-07:00","id":1107483,"title":"","content":"I've been looking for some to flesh out our story, since there's some traveling and meeting of new mages. All I can think of for Moros is like Bokor, but with ghosts, or Bokor, but with golems.<br /> <br /> Wish the Left-Handed book went into more detail with scelesti legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T05:21:17-07:00","id":1107605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1107375#post1107375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any ideas for something for Moros with Prime? Beyond the obvious thaumaturgical alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hammering down people with the blunt truth of their loss so that they may move on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T06:58:50-07:00","id":1107620,"title":"","content":"Infusing ghosts with the truth of their former personality, given them sentience and vitality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T05:54:53-07:00","id":1109716,"title":"","content":"\u200bA technomage Legacy that seems to have gone horribly wrong. Or perhaps horribly right?<br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Origins</b><br /> <br /> You find yourself in a room in a Libertine lorehouse.<br /> <br /> There is a blackboard in the room.<br /> On it are written what seem like ideas, though without knowing the context of their project or projects it's hard to say. <br /> Much of what is written on it is faded. It looks like perhaps they didn't have enough space as many sentences seem to run over old ones.<br /> <br /> Some of the snippets you can make out read the following:<br /> <br /> &quot;Extend mind into more than just the one body? - What bodies?<br /> <br /> *Lots of crossed out ideas*<br /> <br /> Telekinetic limbs?<br /> <br /> Put one mind into multiple bodies? - But how can one mind (with Mind) run more than a few bodies?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">*There are a lot of network topology diagrams drawn on the board*</span> &quot;<br /> <br /> Below the board is a body. It seems to have died not too long ago. <br /> There is no evidence of struggle in fact it's like the body just stopped mid motion, slumped down and subsequently starved to death.<br /> Exploring the rest of the lorehouse you find more bodies. All who seem to have died in a similar manner.<br /> <br /> Some time passes as you investigate the lorehouse. You've found a Grimoire and in addition to some Rotes it seems to contain information on some, to you, unknown Legacy.<br /> <br /> Note:<i> I left it deliberately vague as to what happened to this Legacy. Maybe the servants the attainments allow you to create tend to go rogue? Maybe the attainments below are save but the mages you find studied dangerous variants of it? Maybe the Legacy is transhumanist and the bodies are there because their minds have been assimilated in the networks they created? There is no right answer I much prefer it to be a mystery.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Magic</b><br /> <br /> Parent path: Mastigos, Free Council<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 2, Computer 2 and two dots in any of the following Skills: Science, Crafts, Persuasion and Intimidation<br /> Initiation: ?<br /> <br /> Nickname: ?<br /> Yantras: Turning an electronical device to your purposes (+1), Turning a heretofore unknown device to your ends (+2), One or more of the servants you created are present (+1 for one to four, +2 for five to six, +3 for seven or more)<br /> Oblations: Setting up a network between devices, programming a device, establishing a chain of command among your servants<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <br /> <u>First: Brain-computer Interface</u><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> With this Attainment, the mage can read digital storage devices. This happens as though they were opened in the appropriate applications which means they are still read at human speeds. Reach is assigned to Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> This spell emulates &quot;Electronic Eye&quot; from the Free Council book.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 1<br /> The mage can bring up any memory with perfect clarity. This is identical to &quot;Perfect Recall&quot; with Reach to Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> <u>Second: Network Topology</u><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 2<br /> The mage can sense all physical phenomena related to the presence and flow of electric charge as used in data transmissions. In other words, she can see and understand radio waves, data streams, etc.<br /> <br /> This is identical to &quot;Tune In&quot;. Reach is Instant Casting and Duration<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 2<br /> &quot;One Mind, Two Thoughts&quot; with Reach to Duration and the ability to perform two mental instant actions.<br /> <br /> <u>Third: Multithreading</u><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 3, Computer 3 and two dots in a second Skill or three dots in a single Skill among the initiation Skill list.<br /> This Attainment creates an assistant made of telekinetic forces that can perform Extended physical actions for the mage like cleaning, cooking, lifting and moving, etc. Commands must be very simple and require the mage's oversight. <br /> By default the assistant has a Strength, Dexterity and Speed of 1. Potency may be added to one of these at the time of creating the assistant<br /> <br /> With &quot;One Mind, Two Thoughts&quot; the mage no longer needs to directly oversee the action since the mage can divide his attention. Though the mage still needs to be present. <br /> <br /> This Attainment emulates &quot;Autonomous Servant&quot; from 1st edition but also draws on the description of &quot;Telekinesis&quot; from 2nd edition. Reach is assigned to Duration.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 3<br /> The mage no longer needs to be present to guide the assistant as the mage has a telepathic connection to it. <br /> This is &quot;Telepathy&quot; with Reach to Instant Casting and Duration. This spell only works on your assistants but later also on your golems and AIs.<br /> <br /> <u>Fourth: Multiprocessing</u><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 4, Computer 4<br /> This spell animates a targeted force (fire, kinetic, light, etc.) to act in a live-like matter, a golem. This spell essentially grants the mage a retainer with dots equal to Potency. The golem field can include simple things like physical labor, combat, and other uncomplicated tasks.<br /> <br /> Note that the golem can only do tasks that is logically should be able to. A golem made out of fire can certainly injure and thus perform in combat but can't, for example, pick up a box.<br /> <br /> This Attainment emulates &quot;Golem&quot; from Matter 4 and follows its rules concerning Defense and abilities to follow orders but not health. With Reach to Duration.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 4<br /> When you have created a golem made from electromagnetic forces it may enter a computer and benefit from its systems. This has the following effects:<br /> - It may benefit from the computer's CPU and memory, this slightly increases the golem's complexity. The golem is still mindless but can now update its own orders. It can do this based on any pre-set conditions the mage gives it. So, for example: If attacked -&gt; defend yourself or If task complete -&gt; move to new location. Entire programs with long lists of instruction may be written for the golem, this is a Programming (Intelligence + Computer, extended action).<br /> - If both this golem and an assistant or another golem are under the effects of &quot;Telepathy&quot; to the mage they may communicate. This allows the 'computer golem' to update the orders of the regular golem, again programs may be written for this.<br /> - The golem has control over the computer and will use its programs and peripherals if it's ordered to do so.<br /> <br /> <u>Five: Expansion board</u><br /> Prerequisites: Forces 5, Two dots in a third Skill or three dots in two Skills among the initiation Skill list.<br /> The mage gains control of all electrical devices in the area and may control them as she pleases. The devices can perform any action that they would normally be able to perform.<br /> <br /> If the mage is connected with &quot;Telepathy&quot; to any golems they may focus on controlling the devices instead.<br /> <br /> This emulates Matter 1's &quot;Remote Control&quot; with Reach to Instant Casting, Duration, Scale, Sensory Range and the ability to perform complex and extended actions.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 5<br /> Going above and beyond assistants and golems now the mage creates a true artificial intelligence. With this Attainment, a Rank 1 Goetia is created. This entity, if also under the effect of &quot;Telepathy&quot; can communicate with, manage and update any golems also under the effect of your &quot;Telepathy&quot;, and will do so as commanded or as it otherwise believes to be to your advantage.<br /> <br /> This Attainment is identical to &quot;Psychic Genesis&quot; with Reach assigned to Duration.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:32:40-07:00","id":1109906,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Updated my character's legacy a while ago, but didn't get around to post the update here. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Disciples of Rathma</span></b></span></span></b> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Death is not the end. Death can never be the end.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Death is the road. Life is the traveller. The soul is the guide.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">- Sri Chinmoy</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Most consider Life and Death to be eternal enemies. Mutually exclusive states of being. Forces in fundamental opposition to one another. Enlightened in equal measure by sleeper science and certain sleeper cultures, the Disciples of Rathma know that this is wrong. Where others see conflict, the Disciples see symbiosis. Two forces codependent on each other and driving each other forward. Life begets death, Death begets Life. Without this unending circle there would be no progress, only stasis and entropic decay.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Disciples of Rathma as a Legacy arose not long before the Nameless War. It was born amidst new scientific findings in biology at the beginning of the 20th century and certain sleeper cultures\u2019 view of life and death as being so intimately entwined as to basically being the same. With each generation that passes species improve themselves molded by the forces of natural selection and necessity. Life overcomes, life adapts, but only through the fires of death that get rid of the old can this evolution take place. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There is a greater Supernal truth behind evolution. and the Disciples ask: what if you could turn yourself into a furnace of evolution? Make yourself able to evolve, without needing to die. Control Death and Life such that small parts of your being continuously die and are reborn, improved and adapted. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">To reach this point, a Disciple of Rathma starts by becoming truly aware of the cycle of life and death around them. Once they are aware, they adapt their body using this knowledge, reaching a balance between true death and being alive, becoming able to evolve themselves </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The unique viewpoint on the relationship between the Life and Death Arcana means both Thyrsus and Moros often find themselves attracted to the Legacy. The different viewpoints both Paths provide to the Legacy can lead to conflict, but in a typical Free Council approach this is seen as more of a chance than a problem. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Disciple of Rathma\u2019s founder was Rising Sun, a member of the cabal of the Black Mast, one of the original founding cabals of the Free Council. Originally from Zanzibar, the Black Mast eschewed the traditional form of Sanctum. Instead they lived on a Dhow that travelled the trade route that goes from India, along the coast of East Africa, down to Tanga. Rising Sun had always been curious and inquiring, and the cabal\u2019s travels provided her with access to all manner of cultures and lore. Interested in both religions and science, Rising Sun happily merged sleeper beliefs about the nature of <span style=\"font-size:14px\">life and death with Darwin\u2019s theory of evolution to create the Disciples of Rathma legacy. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Origins</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Parentage</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Moros, Thyrsus, Free Council, Mysterium, Adamantine Arrow</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Background</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: The Disciples of Rathma draw members that are inquisitive, willing to question established knowledge and often have equal interest in science and the occult. Experimenting with one's own body, improving oneself and broadening what it means to be human is a central part of the Legacy, and members are often extraordinarily driven and adventurous individuals. Many have a background in medicine or biology coupled with an interest in the occult.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Appearance</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Many Disciples of Rathma emulate dress and style of sleeper groups focused on the life/death duality and the erosion of the borders between them. Many like to dress like stereotypical Necromancers or take after the looks of spirits and gods of life and death found in sleeper cultures.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Nickname</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Boneseers, Corpsewalkers, Seeders (new, first used around the turn of the millenium)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doctrine</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Life 2, Medicine 2.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Initiation</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: The prospective disciple must go through metaphorical (and with magical assistance often literal) cycles of death and rebirth as a transformative experience.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Organization</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Originally,there were always supposed to be two teachers per student: One Thyrsus and one Moros. The legacy\u2019s low membership mean this practice has fallen out of favour. Also, there is often a visible rift in ethos between the Thyrsus and the Moros that make up the Legacy, but as the unity of Life and Death is one of the core beliefs of the Legacy\u2019s members there are also many that actively try to foster working together. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Theory</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: The Disciples believe that there is a greater truth behind the process of evolution. By perfectly balancing Life and Death in their patterns Disciples are able to rapidly evolve and with every challenge overcome by the perfect adaptation they take a step further on the path to enlightenment.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Magic</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Ruling Arcanum</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Life</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Yantras</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Using bodily processes or excretions in the casting (+1, +2 if this inflicts at least 1HL of Lethal damage on the Disciple), Using body modifications (+1), Succeeding at an Academics roll relevant to the Spell (+2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Oblation</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Ritual Trance in a near death state, activities to improve oneself through change (hard physical training, learning something that changes your view on something, exploring different modes of body or thought), helping with a birth or death (not necessarily human) and watching the process with the first attainment.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Attainment: The Struggle for Life</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The first lesson a Disciple learns is to open her perceptions, and develop a sense for Life and Death in all their forms interacting around her, permeating everything around her. The results can be overwhelming at first, but once the Disciple gets used to the change in perceptions it gives her an unmatched awareness of her surroundings. In its effect, the Attainment duplicates the spell \u201cOutward Inward Eye\u201d, in that within the attainments Scale factor the Mage reduces most attempts to surprise her by the living or the undead to a chance die, cast sensory-range spells on living or undead subjects she might not ordinarily be able to perceive, and reduce all penalties due cover, or concealment by the spell\u2019s potency. The Reach is spent on Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Optional</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Death 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The Disciple may also spend an additional 10 minutes activating the first attainment to enhance their ability to perceive the influence of Death and interact with it. This expands the attainment\u2019s perceptions to cover ghosts in twilight and their anchors, and even allows the Mage to speak with them as long as the ghost is capable of understanding a language she speaks. She can concentrate on a single ghost within</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">the area and determine its Rank, if it has an Anchor, and how many Anchors it has. This duplicates the effects of the spell \u201cSpeak with the Dead\u201d, with Reach spend on advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second Attainment: Perpetuation of Varieties</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Life 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">At this level, life\u2019s evolutionary adaptations become an open book to the Disciple. With but a moment of study she can discern the evolutionary adaptations the target has developed to interact with the world, hunt, hide, etc. The Disciple gets a general impression of all special abilities the target has and how they might be used. On mundane creatures this might tell him that an animal has especially sharp claws and the ability to see infrared light. On supernatural creatures this extends to a general knowledge of their supernatural powers, like supernaturally sharp sense of smell, mesmerizing eyes, a creature\u2019s ability to feel a target\u2019s thoughts, etc. When used to identify supernatural powers the Attainment is Withstood by the Creature\u2019s Composure, or Rank for Ephemeral entities. This Attainment does not work on beings that were custom built, like robots or the creations of the God Machine. Interestingly, and as of yet unknown to the Disciples, the Attainment can identify enhancements that are the result of an AI capable of recursive self-improvement adapting to outside stimuli.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This attainment works like a spell of the Knowing Practice, with 1 Reach spent on instant casting and 1 Reach on working on supernatural creatures. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Optional</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Death 2 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Now Capable of affecting the balance of Life and Death energy in her surroundings, suffusing her or a willing target\u2019s Pattern with the symbolisms of Death mutes her presence in the world. Activated by spending an hour meditating in a place of death or ritualy scarring the target, this Attainment duplicates the effects of the Spell Without a Trace with Reach spent on Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third: Man\u2019s Place in Nature</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Life 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">With this Attainment, the Disciple becomes capable of actively shaping a human target\u2019s body. She is not yet capable of changing a human it into a different species, but she can make it look like basically any other human. The attainment is activated by spending an hour in concentration and it works like the spell Many Faces, with Reach spent on Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Optional</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Death 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">At this point, the Disciple\u2019s ability to suffuse her pattern with the symbolisms of Death becomes so complete, that it hides her very essence and Aura from the world. The effect is so powerful, even strong revelatory magic has problems piercing it. Activated in the same way as the previous Death Attainment, this Attainment replicates the effects of the spell Suppress Aura with Reach spent on Advanced Duration and Advanced Potency.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth: Experiments on Human Hybridization</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Life 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Adaptation is central the hallmark of successful evolution, and the Disciples are its masters. With but a quick thought the Disciple can make her body or that of a willing target he touches evolve to fit her needs. Skin can become thicker, a tail could grow, teeth may become poisonous fangs. Whatever the Disciple needs, the body evolves to fulfil that need.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This Attainment works like the spell Transform Life, with Reach spent on Advanced Duration and Instant casting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Optional</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Death 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The next step for a Disciple of Rathma is to accept the unity of Life and Death as a part of them. By understanding how their body carries both, the Disciple of Rathma is able to integrate them more fully within themselves. Instead of having one overwhelm the other, they delicately balance the two forces\u2019 power over their pattern, becoming neither fully dead or alive. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Upon successfully activating this Attainment, and for the remainder of the Duration, the Disciple no longer suffers wound penalties, does not need to breathe and does not begin to bleed to death when all of her Health boxes are filled with lethal damage (see \u201cHealth and Healing\u201d in the Mage the Awakening 2e Rulebook, pp. 222-223). Likewise, she does not register as a living pattern to sensory magics (though Life Arcanum spells can still affect her and she doesn\u2019t count as a walking corpse for the purposes of the Death Arcanum), and perhaps most spectacularly, she can reattach severed pieces of her body with Life Arcanum healing (at the appropriate level for the type of damage sustained in losing the limb, or whatever other part was removed), so long as it is done before this Attainment\u2019s Duration expires.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Corpse Flesh [1 Reach Advanced Duration, 1 Reach Instant Cast, Adamantine Arrow p. 173]</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth: The Origin of Species</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Life 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">All life on earth started in the same origin. The connection to all the forms that original life has taken over the eons is there, in every human and animal, and fully at the Disciple or Rathma\u2019s command. With but a short act of concentration, the Disciple wills her body or that of a willing target to have taken a different path, to have evolved along another branch of the great tree. For the duration of the Attainment the body follows that act of will, transforming into any biota that has ever evolved or could realistically have evolved.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This attainment works like the spell Shapechange, with Reach spent on instant casting and Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Optional</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Death 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Most of the Disciples attainments take control of evolution, make it go along specific paths in a carefully controlled way. With this attainment, the Disciples mastery of Life and Death allows her to make it go wrong in the fastest and most horrible ways imaginable.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The Disciple flicks, spits, or shoots a small part of herself at the target, be it a fleck of blood or a gob of spit. If it hits, the targets gets infected with a terrible affliction. Living targets start to mutate quickly and painfully, as cancerous growths appear all over their body. On contact with unliving targets or ephemeral entities the small amount of living matter the Disciple attacked them with mutates itself, quickly growing roots of cancerous matter that brutally split apart the target like a tree\u2019s roots split a stone. Ephemeral entities especially are terrible to look at as veins of blood and flesh start quickly growing through their bodies, and entire areas start to slough off or break apart.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This attainment works like a direct damage spell of the Unraveling Practice, cast with Reach spent on Instant Casting and Advanced Duration. The attack uses Gnosis + Athletics or Firearms, and the Disciple can also use any delivery mechanism she evolved with the fourth attainment (like evolving the ability to shoot spikes at targets). The Attainment\u2019s damage is delivered at one hour intervals until the duration runs out.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-30-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:44:35-07:00","id":1113750,"title":"","content":"So... I remember reading a 1e custom Legacy written up a <i>loooong</i> time ago in one of those unofficial wiki/game resources pages, but can't find the page now. The idea was cool enough for me to want to reconstruct it from my incomplete memory, but I'm not familiar enough with legacy creation to think I'd be able to do so without some help.<br /> <br /> The Legacy was titled &quot;The Hive&quot; and their magical philosophy centered on the unity of all organisms as descended from a single organic source, known by legacy members as the Adam Kadmon. The optional Life attainments centered on controlling and mutating the forms of baser life forms to suit the purposes of the legacy member. The core attainments, however, were interesting in that they mucked with sympathy and gradually erased separation/distinction between legacy members - i.e. at a certain level one can cast spells on any fellow member as if you were casting on yourself, with no sympathetic range required, another level allowed easy sharing mana or wp with other members, etc. Weirdly, these attainments used Spirit instead of the more sensible Space or Mind. This would probably need to to change if converted.<br /> <br /> Does anyone think this Legacy deserves to be brought into the sunlight of 2e? If so, what order(s) (in your opinion) makes sense? I could see Silver Ladder for the idea of man's rightful dominion over other lifeforms, Mysterium for the creepy unity and connection to living magic, or Seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:20:00-07:00","id":1114010,"title":"","content":"Has anyone ever considered a legacy for Mastigos that accesses the Grave Dream of the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T23:54:51-07:00","id":1114075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvedulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1113750#post1113750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I remember reading a 1e custom Legacy written up a <i>loooong</i> time ago in one of those unofficial wiki/game resources pages, but can't find the page now. The idea was cool enough for me to want to reconstruct it from my incomplete memory, but I'm not familiar enough with legacy creation to think I'd be able to do so without some help.<br /> <br /> The Legacy was titled &quot;The Hive&quot; and their magical philosophy centered on the unity of all organisms as descended from a single organic source, known by legacy members as the Adam Kadmon. The optional Life attainments centered on controlling and mutating the forms of baser life forms to suit the purposes of the legacy member. The core attainments, however, were interesting in that they mucked with sympathy and gradually erased separation/distinction between legacy members - i.e. at a certain level one can cast spells on any fellow member as if you were casting on yourself, with no sympathetic range required, another level allowed easy sharing mana or wp with other members, etc. Weirdly, these attainments used Spirit instead of the more sensible Space or Mind. This would probably need to to change if converted.<br /> <br /> Does anyone think this Legacy deserves to be brought into the sunlight of 2e? If so, what order(s) (in your opinion) makes sense? I could see Silver Ladder for the idea of man's rightful dominion over other lifeforms, Mysterium for the creepy unity and connection to living magic, or Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Silver Ladder is big on the whole &quot;meritocratic strata of society&quot; thing, so all individuals joining to become one might not be what they prefer. The Mysterium and the Hegemony might indeed support such notions. Adam Kadmon (sounds better than &quot;the Hive&quot;) would be a Legacy with Thyrsus, Mysterium, and Seer parentage, with Space as their primary Arcanum and Life as the optional one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T02:19:47-07:00","id":1114093,"title":"","content":"This is a Legacy which one of my players, a Master of Mind and Adept of Prime, will take.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Architects of Truth</b></span><br /> The Architects of Truth are a Silver Ladder/Seers of the Throne Legacy focused on using Prime and Mind to manipulate the truth of the Fallen World.<ul><li>Parentage: Mastigos, Silver Ladder, Seers of the Throne</li> <li>Ruling Arcanum: Prime</li> <li>Yantras: Truthfinding (+1), opening the first Door in Social Maneuvering (+1), succeeding on a Persuasion check (+1, or +2 if the person was hostile to you in the beginning), planning the details of how to change Sleeper society (+2).</li> <li>Oblations: Public speaking; publishing an article; staging a protest; mingling with movers and shakers.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Origin</b></span><br /> The Legacy was originally developed by the Seers of the Throne to enhance their control over Sleepers and the Lie. It originated in the Hegemonic Ministry as a tool used to direct Sleepers towards whatever beliefs were required to keep them divided. It was created shortly after the Ministry's creation in the 17th century in Florence. The Legacy later found its way into the Silver Ladder as a similarly effective method of control, although to different ends. The Seers claim the Ladder stole it with soul theft, but the th\u00e9archs say a Seer defector brought them the Legacy. In the late 19th century when the Simulacrite cult defected from the Iron Pyramid and formed the Simulacrum Order, they took the Legacy with them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> The Architects of Truth believe that while Mages can temporarily enforce their will on the world, they can also change what is actually true about the world. This is the key to controlling Sleeper society, other mages, and even Ascension. Truthshapers engage in Truthfinding, obsessively studying individuals and groups to learn what desires, opinions, and facts emanate from them so that they might shape those into the correct ones.<ul><li><b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Persuasion 2, and one of the following additional Skills at 2 dots or higher: Politics, Empathy, Expression, or Subterfuge.</li> <li><b>Initiation</b>: The prospective Truthshaper must complete the task their tutor assigns. This usually relates to influencing the beliefs of a Sleeper population through means both magical and mundane.</li> <li><b>Organization</b>: The Architects of Truth work in cells within their Orders, usually in teams with clearly-defined roles. A small group of Truthshapers will plan out changes to Sleeper society and work to implement them, each one applying their specializations accordingly. The Legacy sometimes cooperates cross-Order to deal with supernatural threats or dangers to the Legacy.</li> <li><b>Theory</b>: A core activity of Truthshapers is Truthfinding. They observe or interact with individuals or groups in need of factual adjustment so that the truths in their own souls become resonant to those individuals. Activating any Mind Attainments require the Truthshaper to spend at least one Scene in Truthfinding with their target(s). Only one session is required; it allows the mage to activate some or all of the Legacy's Mind Attainments during that Scene.</li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attainments</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Truthseeking (1 dot)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation<br /> <br /> In order to define truth in the world, the Truthshaper must know how to seek it out. They gain the ability to instinctively uncover the truth of people and places. This Attainment emulates the &quot;Sacred Geometry&quot; spell with Reach spent to allow the mage to perceive whether or not they are in a Hallow. The mage always instinctively knows where ley lines and Hallows are.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Mind 1. To have influence over others, the mage must know their true desires. Even with casual observation, a Truthshaper can quickly discover what intent lies behind another's words and actions. This emulates the &quot;Mental Scan&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to Sensory Range.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Command Truth (2 dots)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites: Prime 2, Persuasion 3</b><br /> <br /> The Truthshaper learns the basics of usurping the truth of the Fallen World and replacing it with one of their own design. With a word, the Truthshaper commands Supernal phenomena to do as they wish. This emulates the &quot;Word of Command&quot; spell with Reach assigned to Instant Casting and Sensory Range. If the triggered effect requires Mana to be spent, the Truthshaper need only spend 1 Mana.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Mind 2. The Truthshaper's instinctual understanding of the Truths emanating from others allows them to be whoever they need to be in order to bend others to their whim. After Truthfinding the target for one Scene, the Truthshaper changes the truth of his own presence. This emulates the &quot;Alter Mental Pattern&quot; spell with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Alter Truth (3 dots)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 3. In addition to the Persuasion 3 requirement from the previous Attainment, the Truthshaper must increase the other Skill used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 3, or must attain 2 dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.<br /> <br /> The shaper's mastery over the usurpation of truth now extends to the altering of vast swaths of the Mundane. By spending about an hour studying the Ley Lines in an area, the Truthshaper can alter them for extended periods of time. This emulates the &quot;Geomancy&quot; spell with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration, allowing the Truthshaper to change the Resonance Keyword of Nodes or ley lines. The Attainment cannot move Ley Lines. However, when the Truthshaper alters a node or ley line, they themselves become Resonant with that ley line, a false extension of the new truth the Node or Line represents. A Truthshaper may also use this Attainment to simply become Resonant with a Ley Line or Node, and not alter its Keyword.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Mind 3. By forcefully projecting the truth that he creates in his soul outward, the Truthshaper can prepare other people to accept its reality. This spell emulates the &quot;Emotional Urging&quot; spell with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and Sensory Range. If the target is within range of a Node or Ley Line that the mage is Resonant with, the mage can bypass the Withstand of his target.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Annihilate Falsehood (4 dots)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Prime 4, Persuasion 4, and the other Skill requirements of the previous Attainment.<br /> <br /> The Truthshaper is no longer content to just temporarily change what is true. Opposing Supernal phenomena endanger the agenda of the Architects of Truth; spells that contradict the fabricated truths of the Truthshaper become falsehoods and can be destroyed. This emulates the &quot;Dispel Magic&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to Instant casting time, Sensory Range, and Lasting effect. The Truthshaper does not need to have dots in the component Arcana of the spells he's trying to dispel as long as those spells are within range of one of his Resonant Ley Lines or Nodes. Activating this Attainment costs 1 Mana.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Mind 4. Much like Supernal Truths that oppose the Truthshaper's agenda can be cast back across the Abyss, the facts, opinions, and beliefs of other people can be destroyed. This effect emulates the effects of the &quot;Befuddle&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to Sensory Range and Advanced Duration. It can only lower the target's Resolve or Composure. If the target is within range of a Node or Ley Line that the mage is Resonant with, the mage can bypass the Withstand of his target.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Create Truth (5 dots)</span></b><br /> Prerequisites: Prime 5. In addition to the Persuasion 4 requirement from the previous Attainment, the Truthshaper must increase the other Skill used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 4, or must attain 3 dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements, /or/ two dots in a third Skill from the list.<br /> <br /> With mastery over truth itself, the Truthshaper is able to fabricate truths ex nihilo. This emulates the effects of the &quot;Create Truth&quot; spell, except that the Truthshaper may pick any Resonance for the Hallow, even if it doesn't make sense for its location. He is also automatically Resonant with the Hallow. The Resonance-related bonuses of the lower-dot Attainments apply to the Hallow and any Ley Lines or Nodes it creates. Reach is assigned to Advanced Duration. Hallows created with this attainment do not generate tass, and only members of the Legacy can perform Oblations in them. Activating this Attainment costs 1 Mana.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Mind 5. The Truthfinding extends beyond instinct, automatically changing the Truthshaper into the person others need him to be in order to accept the truths he defines. This Attainment emulates the &quot;Social Networking&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T04:12:13-07:00","id":1114104,"title":"","content":"You might want to work on the Reach assignment for these attainments. For instance both parts of the first attainment take a scene to activate and the results are transitory. <br /> <br /> The second attainment has one too many Reach spent, you can either have it be Instant, or at Sensory Range, not both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T06:12:34-07:00","id":1114132,"title":"","content":"Word of Command is a Prime 1 spell. The Attainment requires Prime 2, which means you get 2 free Reach. I do agree that the Truthseeking attainment which emulates Sacred Geometry should maybe be instant cast instead of advanced duration. That way, the mage can just ping to find out if they're in a Hallow.<br /> <br /> The same argument could be made for the first Mind attainment. I originally had them as instant cast, but I switched to Sensory Range so that the mage could figure out stuff about the target before directly interacting with them, or not need to touch them. But I suppose you could rework the flavor to say &quot;with a handshake, the mage can use Mental Scan...&quot; or something to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T07:28:33-07:00","id":1114145,"title":"","content":"Word of Command, right, I got it confused with Words of Truth which is what I figured you'd want in that slot, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T08:59:59-07:00","id":1114174,"title":"","content":"Words of Truth is definitely a good candidate for the Legacy. The problem is that Words of Truth specifically involves things that are objectively true, and the point of the Legacy is to change what's &quot;objectively true&quot; (in the minds of the mage and Sleepers). This is why the higher level Attainments focus on screwing around with Ley Lines and Hallows, since they have powerful residual narrative effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T13:14:01-07:00","id":1119616,"title":"","content":"I really enjoy the guidelines on Legacy creation in the 2e core, and I'm going to try my hand at statting several concepts out. This is hopefully going to be the first in a series of &quot;pop culture Legacies&quot;, wherein I try to mimic the powers and flavor of a particular fictional supernatural character(s) using the Legacy rules. Feedback is <i>greatly</i> appreciated. Additional apologies if any of these concepts have been done as Legacies before. And thus, for your pleasure I present:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Cauldronists</span><br /> Nicknames: Sculptors, Midases (derogatory)<br /> Parent Path/Order: Moros or Mysterium or Free Council<br /> <br /> <i>Philosophy</i><br /> Many Mages believe that the gross material of the Fallen World is a shackle that binds them. They may seek to escape through projection of their consciousness to the Astral Planes and beyond, or chase the rarified magic of Prime for its to affirm and deny Supernal Truths. The Cauldronists know this, too, to be a lie. The stuff of which every rock and every human being is made up contains within it potential \u2013 it is the raw material which can in time be refined into precious treasure, both living and unliving. However, initiates of the Legacy are taught that there is constancy as well as change in the universe. Nothing new can be created without an investment of matter or energy (physical or mystical) from somewhere else.<br /> Cauldronists strive to attain mastery of the form and substance of inanimate matter, and of the intricate structures that determine their own body\u2019s Pattern. Legacy members meticulously experiment in search of a discovery that learned Cauldronists call the Sapphire Crucible. Outsiders who pick up scraps of legacy doctrine sometimes misinterpret the Sapphire Crucible as a physical artifact that must be located. In reality, the Crucible is understood as a perfected set of techniques that would allow the possessor to transmute matter with unlimited regard to scale or complexity, unlocking dominion over the foundations of the Fallen World, and perhaps Ascension itself.<br /> <br /> Legacy Skills: Science, Crafts, Athletics<br /> <br /> Appearance: Cauldronists tend to dress in practical, durable clothes, as their investigations can lead them into hazardous areas. More hubristic members may bear scars from rituals gone awry that they were unprepared to properly contain. Most Cauldronists carry pencil and paper, a smartphone, tablet, or some other method of quickly recording notes about supernatural phenomena and noteworthy objects and people they encounter.<br /> <br /> Concepts: Perfectionist architect, combat medic, gold-hoarder, experimental chemist<br /> <br /> <i>Magic \u2013 Primary Life, Optional Matter</i><br /> Oblations: Take apart and put back together a complex device or machine. Meditate while being exposed to a mild toxin or irritant. Analyze an object or compound unknown to you and record the alchemical formulae describing its composition.<br /> <br /> Yantras: Alchemical sigils drawn on or encircling the object being altered (+1), Cast while standing on an active ley line (+2)<br /> <br /> Attainments:<br /> <b>1<sup>st</sup>: Distillation \u2013 Matter 1</b> Before shaping the world, the Cauldronist must know what it is made of. By merely touching an object and spending a few moments analyzing it, the Sculptor may determine the materials of which the object is composed.<br /> As Discern Composition, with 1 Reach allocated to instant casting<br /> <br /> <b>Optional \u2013 Life 1 </b>To Cauldronists, biological entities are not fundamentally different in substance from the nonliving matter around them. With this attainment a Sculptor gains the ability to quickly learn details about an organism, though they must be able to both touch and observe the subject.<br /> As Analyze Life, with 1 Reach allocated to instant casting<br /> <br /> <b>2<sup>nd</sup>: Calcination \u2013 Matter 2</b>, <b>Life 2</b> The path of the Awakened often leads them into grave danger as they seek out the gods and monsters that hide within the Fallen World. With this Attainment the Cauldronist increases their chances of surviving such encounters. The Legacy member benefits from a persistent form of Matter Mage Armor that does not cost Mana to raise and lower, their will reflexively rearranging the molecules of skin and clothing alike to form a carapace that blunts the blades of would-be attackers. The mage must still lower this armor to benefit from any other Arcanum\u2019s Mage Armor.<br /> <br /> <b>3<sup>rd</sup>: Separation \u2013 Matter 3</b> This is perhaps the signature attainment of the Cauldronists (and one that lent them one of their sobriquets). With this level of mastery the Cauldronist may rearrange the configuration of matter to suit their needs, drawing energy from the Legacy conduit between their soul and the Supernal to effect the change.<br /> As Shaping, with 1 Reach allocated to allow shaping of gases, liquids, or solids + 1 Reach for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional \u2013 Life 3:</b> If the body is a Pattern, that pattern can be mended. The Cauldronist synthesizes alchemical catalysts within their own body, rapidly healing themselves or another from injury.<br /> As Knit, with 1 Reach for Instant Casting + 1 Reach for the option to heal Lethal Damage instead of Bashing.<br /> <br /> <b>4<sup>th</sup>: Conjunction \u2013 Matter 4</b> To know something inside and out is to know how to make or unmake it with ease. To the Cauldronist, destroying a steel door is as simple an alteration of matter as making a broken statue whole.<br /> As Nigredo and Albedo, with 1 Reach allocated to ignore Durability + 1 Reach for Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional \u2013 Life 4</b> By drawing on the extensive accumulated knowledge of the legacy, the Cauldronist sees the possibilities inherent in the basic form of an organism. Performing an elaborate alchemical ritual, the Sculptor may give a plant, animal or even another human traits from one or more organisms. However, any trait granted must be from a creature the Cauldronist has studied at some point using the 1<sup>st</sup> Attainment.<br /> As Transform Life, with 1 reach for Advanced Duration + 1 Reach for Indefinite Duration<br /> <br /> <b>5<sup>th</sup>: Coagulation \u2013 Matter 5</b> At this level the Legacy member\u2019s control over matter is complete. The Sculptor may create any nonmagical substance of the Fallen World, so long as they provide appropriate raw matter to exchange during the transmutation.<br /> As Transubstantiation, with 1 Reach allocated to use Advanced Duration + 1 Reach for Indefinite Duration<br /> <b>Optional \u2013 Life 5</b> To one who is close to the mystery of the Sapphire Crucible, even seemingly miraculous healings are possible. Elder members of the Legacy are sometimes sought out by the Awakened and the more knowledgeable among the night\u2019s other denizens for the chance to replace that which was lost.<br /> As Regeneration, with 1 Reach for Advanced Duration + 1 Reach for Indefinite Duration<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T15:40:55-07:00","id":1119648,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12051\" data-vbnamecard=\"12051\">Kvedulf</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bYou need to clear up the attainments somewhat, you have it as Life Primary, but you keep using Matter in the primary arcana slot for some reason.<br /> <br /> Life 2 doesn't actually do anything in the 2nd attainment<br /> <br /> Knit is a 3 dot effect of Life so you only have 1 Reach to spare either for Instant activation or for the ability to heal Lethal not just Bashing.<br /> <br /> Transform Life for the 4th attainment, you don't have enough Reach to have transformations passed on to the next generation so Indefinite may not be worthwhile, and it's also Potency primary which means you can't take the virtual dice penalties necessary to get to Indefinite Duration even if you do have the Reach. You might be better served making it Instant with Advanced Duration using the virtual dice penalties to get it to last as long as you can (I think either a month or a year) and then simply &quot;update&quot; the attainment on a subject you wish to keep transformed by activating it on them again before or just after its Duration expires.<br /> <br /> Fifth attainment you could charge a point of mana instead of Reach to hit the Advanced Duration table because this is a Matter effect, then you'd have a Reach left over for Instant as well as Indefinite (Note you can hit Indefinite here because Duration is the primary factor of Transubstantiation and gets a free factor bump), although you might consider going for the Reach clause so you don't have to work with conceptually pure substances. <br /> <br /> As for Regeneration, check the Potency costs, you may not be able to replace more than hands, feet, sensory organs and skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T12:29:42-07:00","id":1124433,"title":"","content":"Here's my attempt at writing a legacy. I originally envisioned it before 1e and it shows - I have completely no idea what could be the Fifth Attainment. Any ideas that could fit with the theme? <b>Die Wiederganger</b><br /><br /> <b>Other names: </b>Half-Dead, Zombies<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Most Adamantine Arrows consider undead to be useful foot soldiers and nothing more. One of them, a Mecklemburgian Moros later known as Draugr, become further interested in them. If Death normally means cessation of all living processes, does that mean revenants and ghosts die only a bit? Is revenant a human whose mind and ability to move have not been touched by Death Arcanum? Can the process be understood and harnessed to make him even more formidable in combat?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">The answer was a resounding yes \u2013 after years of research, Draugr finally found a way to partially change into a living corpse. By selectively ceasing his bodily functions during combat, he was able to ignore fatigue, pain and wounds that normally could be lethal. By dulling his mind, he could ignore fear and other distractions, becoming completely focused on his goal. Soon, the half-dead warrior became known and feared among the mages of Holy Roman Empire, many of whom wanted to know his secrets.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">When the Legacy was still young, it quickly became a subject of rumors. Plenty of mages hoped Draugr had found the secret of immortality (or, at least, Lichdom). Die Wiederganger objected \u2013 it\u2019s not that their founder didn\u2019t want to become immortal, it\u2019s just the method had proven to be unsuitable. It could temporarily stop bodily functions, but couldn\u2019t stave off aging and natural death. Unfortunately, not everyone believed them \u2013 soon, the Half-Dead had to deal not only with unsuitable apprentices trying to worm into their ranks, but also Reapers trying to steal their souls and take the secrets of partial death for themselves.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Trying to protect themselves and their secrets, the Legacy took drastic measures. Soul thieves were brutally murdered along with their cabals (or, sometimes, Consilia). Die Wiederganger also started to screen potential members very rigorously, admitting only proven Adamantine Arrows. Every single candidate had to prove they were dedicated to a cause greater than themselves before even being considered.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">This last requirement nearly spelled the end of the Legacy \u2013 when the Holy Roman Empire disbanded and got replaced by the German one, the Half-Dead embraced nationalism and willingly fought in Sleeper wars. This made them unpopular even among many other Arrows and made Guardians of the Veil furious. During the Great War, plenty of Zombies died in the trenches \u2013 most killed by artillery strikes, but some were assassinated by other mages. The last straw however, was World War II \u2013 a lot of Die Wiederganger openly supported the Nazi regime and were mercilessly hunted after 1945. Not willing to associate themselves with the \u201cNazi Legacy\u201d, German Consilia turned a blind eye when the Arrows trying to clean the Order\u2019s name, vengeful mages from neighboring countries and even occasional Reapers came knocking.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Ironically, it\u2019s the last ones that prevented the Legacy from going extinct. The formal structure of Die Wiederganger is gone, but their secrets lived on with mages who learned them from stolen souls. Some original members of the Half-Dead survived, but good luck getting them to teach you \u2013 their recruitment requirements got even harder than ever and include an oath of revenge on those who defiled the Legacy \u2013 which means not only the Reapers, but everyone they taught.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">While not Left-Handed, Die Wiederganger are pretty unpopular among the mages who know anything about their history. If you get inducted, chances are you either were taught by a Reaper or a literal Nazi. The latter is even worse, because it means you are oath-bound to pursue the former, which usually ends with two Consilia hating each other.</span><br /> <b>Background</b><br /><br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Moros, Adamantine Arrow Seers of the Throne (from Praetorian Ministry). Plenty of Reapers who stole the Legacy actually come from Mysterium.<br /> <b>Background: </b>Plenty of Zombies come from danger-related backgrounds. Soldiers are the most obvious candidates, although they no longer compose the absolute majority of the legacy. There is plenty of police officers, firefighters and lifeguards among the Half-Dead. At least one cosmonaut joined too.<br /> <b>Appearance: </b>Die Wiederganger frequently have various health problems \u2013 the ability to ignore pain, hunger and drowsiness at will means they tend to view their body as a tool and nothing more. The more they advance into the Legacy, the worse they look \u2013 it\u2019s easy to recognize them by pale skin and dark rings around the eyes. <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Death 2, Resolve 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> The prospective Half-Dead is symbolically brought on the verge of death and interred. Traditionally it meant being beaten nearly to death and buried. The original Wiederganger didn\u2019t mind high mortality, because it let them weed out \u201cunsuitable\u201d recruits. Today, only the remnants of the original Legacy bother with that method \u2013 most just give a recruit a controlled dose of toxin and put them into a coffin.<br /> <b>Organization: </b>Die Wiederganger used to have a loose hierarchy. The master was honor-bound to only introduce apprentices that was considered suitable, otherwise they risked shame and scorn from the rest of the Legacy. The prospective Half-Dead needed to be vetted by two other members. Otherwise they were free to do as they please. After the collapse of the Legacy, these rules are no longer observed.<br /> <b>Theory: </b>Death conquers all but the Mind. Life, however, can distract you and prevent from mastering Death. You can only free your Mind by giving up the parts of Life that hinder you. When you are able to do that, you become truly invincible.<br /> <b>Magic</b><br /><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Death<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Significant wounds (+2), carrying a memento of the cause the Half-Dead fights for (+1), lying motionless on the ground (+1), corpse paint (+1), sewing one\u2019s mouth shut (+2), although duct tape works too (+1)<br /> <b>Oblation: </b>Spending the night lying motionlessly inside a coffin, eating a meal consisting entirely of spoiled food (buttermilk, blue cheese or sauerkraut counts!), silent contemplation of the cause, hearing an elegy for yourself (a record is enough).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /><br /> <b>First: Know Death</b><br /><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiated<br /> To master Death, one needs to know it. By touching a body, the mage gets to experience its final moments. This duplicates the effects of \u201cForensic Gaze\u201d spell with +1 Reach applied.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 1<br /> Touching a living person lets the mage analyze traces of Death in their bodies. This works as weaker \u201cAnalyze Life\u201d spell, except that it only shows illnesses and Injuries (including Physical Tilts and Conditions).<br /> <b>Second: Dead Flesh</b><br /><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Death 2, Resolve 3<br /> The mage shuts down their bodily functions as if they used Death 2 \u201cSuppress Life\u201d. This doesn\u2019t actually make them dead, but lets them appear as such. Reach is used to knock the spell to Advanced Duration Chart.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 2<br /> The mage can slow their bodily functions as if they possessed Life 2 \u201cBody Control\u201d spell. This gives them the ability to slow their metabolism, breathing and heart rate, along with a natural armor. They can\u2019t, however, mend their wounds, mask their scent or get a bonus to initiative. Reach is used to knock the spell to Advanced Duration chart.<br /> <b><b>Third: Befriend the Grim Reaper</b></b><br /><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Death 3, Resolve 3, Stamina 3<br /> The Half-Dead becomes able to resist entropy in their bodies. They still receive damage, but they don\u2019t cause them to suffer that much. They may ignore wound penalties and Personal Tilts that wouldn\u2019t reasonably work on a zombie (for example, they could ignore Stunned, but stills suffer Arm Wreck after someone chops their hand off) \u2013 one Tilt per Potency. This is effectively the use of Shielding practice. Reaches are used for Advanced Duration and instant use.<br /> <b>O</b><b>ptional: </b>Life 3<br /> The Disciple of Life may also ignore limits their body puts on them, getting Life 3 \u201cHoning the Form\u201d. They may use them to increase their Stamina or Strength, but not Dexterity. The Reach is assigned to Advanced Duration.<br /> <b><b>Fourth: Second Chance</b></b><br /><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Death 4, Resolve 4<br /> Even death itself is not able to stop this mage. When the mage dies while this Attainment is active, they immediately turn into a free-willed revenant (as per Death 4 \u201cRevenant\u201d). It usually does everything to avenge their death or achieve the goal they tried before expiring \u2013 it remains active until this happens or for Duration of the spell. Reach is spent on Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Life 4<br /> Instead of dying and releasing a revenant into the world, the mage may choose to instantly mend their wounds as per Life 4 \u201cMend\u201d spell. The Reach is assigned to instant use.<br /> <b><b>Fifth: ???</b></b><br /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13425-gantolandon","name":"Gantolandon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:15:31-07:00","id":1125069,"title":"","content":"I like it! I have no idea about a fifth attainment either. Maybe something so that, if their body becomes too worn or they need to make a change, they can transfer to another dead body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:12:30-07:00","id":1125875,"title":"","content":"Honestly I could use some help designing a legacy...<br /> The legacy would be Primary Forces. End result is by the end of it you become a being close to the Dragons of Atlantis.<br /> Minor is death.<br /> <br /> Obviously this isn't going to start you off with fire breathing or even flying. But maybe a mighty roar. Using control sound to amplify your voice so that if deafens or stuns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:07:12-07:00","id":1125889,"title":"","content":"I know why you're going for this, but wouldn't a legacy based around becoming a pseudo atlantean dragon be more like Prime (supernal magic which the dragons embodied) and Life (Change into a dragon)? Forces and Death don't really tie all that well into atlantean dragons imo, especially Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T19:51:36-07:00","id":1126562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1125889#post1125889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know why you're going for this, but wouldn't a legacy based around becoming a pseudo atlantean dragon be more like Prime (supernal magic which the dragons embodied) and Life (Change into a dragon)? Forces and Death don't really tie all that well into atlantean dragons imo, especially Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me I think it would depend on how that person sees and understands them. For example if that person understood dragons to be forces of primal magic, of every arcana, that that dragons had different variaties and each was a force of nature, then understanding the existence of a death dragon wouldn't be that difficult. Though I agree...Life would be needed to make that physical change to the body. So I should think about it more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T02:32:34-07:00","id":1128372,"title":"","content":"Here is a Custom Legacy that I have been working on and I would like some feedback. I still have some Fluff writing to do but it is complete enough to start getting opinions on it. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Temponauts</b></span></span><br /> <b>The walkers in Time and Space</b><br /> (Fan crafted) \u2013 Homebrew</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Everything has a timeline, everything, and this timeline marks the Past, Present and the Future. The Past consists of everything that has transpired since the start of the timeline, the Present collects the building blocks of time to define the Past, and the Future is previously undefined present. Along this timeline there are markers placed to represent significant events. These events in turn mark the beginning of a sympathetic connection to that event, consequently starting another timeline. These timelines and connections hang off the original timeline like branches on a tree. It is this view of the fusing of a point in three dimensional space with a point in time that the Temponauts used to shape this Legacy, and is what they believe to be the basis of the Space-time Continuum. It is through the observation and manipulation of the Past that affects the Present and allows one to shape the Future, the key being the Spacetime point, and that is how magic is done.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Work In Progress</span><br /> <br /> <b>History</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Work In Progress</span><br /> <br /> <b>Origins</b><br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Mastigos or Free Council<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Time Bandit<br /> <b>Background:</b> Temponauts can come from any walk of life but most share a fascination with history, therefore many Temponauts are historians and collectors of ancient artifacts. These artifact can be anything, a book, fine art, an old arrowhead, the item itself is superfluous as long as it has a significant history. It isn\u2019t until after they have become awakened that these items have any true meaning or usefulness. The collections of a Temponaut is truly as site to see, that is if they allow you to get close enough to see it.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Temponauts are very inquisitive and tend to study everything. Lost in their train of thought they become distant to others and some would describe their preoccupation as absentminded. They are very protective of their collections and go to great lengths to keep them safe.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Gnosis 2, Time 2, Academics 2, Science 2.<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> The prospective Temponaut must acquire an item that is no less than a century old and then research its history and significance.<br /> <b>Organization:</b> Temponauts have regional leaders and a council to judge those that would step out of line. The regional leader is usually the highest ranked member of the Legacy. He takes on the role of judge and the council is the jury when a case of abuse is brought before them. They also have infrequent social gathering where they discuss or show off their latest acquisitions or discoveries, the host being the one with the most recent and significant find.<br /> <b>Theory:</b> Time is a playground vast and endless, but be careful what you leave in that playground. Never change the playground without first contemplating the outcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Magic</b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Time<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Historical artifacts (greater than a century old) +1, Ancient historical artifacts (Greater than three centuries old) +2, Two objects graphed together +2<br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Reading historical documents, Carbon dating objects, Walking through a museum, Giving a lecture on history.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Work In Progress</span><br /> <br /> <b>Primary:</b> Time, <b>Optional:</b> Space<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b> Strands of Spacetime<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> One of the first things that a Temponaut learns to do is to examine the strands of time. By examining a strand, he can discern when two strands crossed and how long they stayed intertwined. This is similar to the \u201cInspect Timeline\u201d spell. While inspecting a strand he must know the specific timeline he is looking for, as an example he can inspect Susan\u2019s timeline for the last time she was at the library but he couldn\u2019t look to see the last building she was in. By inspecting the libraries timeline he can then locate when Susan\u2019s timeline crossed it. He cannot tell what she did while at the library but he would be able to discern how long the strands stayed intertwined. This is a ritual casting with Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Space 2<br /> By overlaying a timeline onto a sympathetic connections utilized by space the Temponaut can view the times of significant occurrences associated with that connection. As an example while viewing a connection between a man and his wife the Temponaut can not only tell when the connection started but see when they had a fight that almost ended the marriage.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b> Witness Spacetime<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Time 2 and Academics 3<br /> After employing the Strands of Time attainment the Temponaut can use this specialized version of the \u201cDivination\u201d spell. The visions of the past automatically jump to the point identified by the Strands of Time and view just the amount of time that the two timelines were intertwined. This is an instant action with Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Space 2<br /> With Space 2 the Temponaut can tag a connection with a time stamp. This tag will allow the mage to use that connection as a Medium strength Sympathetic Yantra for both Time and Space spells. The mage may only have a number of active tags equal to his Space Arcanum rating. Anyone viewing the Connection or the Timeline of either subject can detect this tag with a Perception + Investigation skill roll and can remove it with a Clash of Wills, the Temponaut will receive automatic successes equal to his Space Arcanum rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment:</b> Falsify Spacetime<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 4, Time 3, Science 3<br /> At this level of proficiency the Temponaut is able to change what others perceive as the chain of events. With a specialized version of the \u201cFalsify Timeline\u201d spell he may veil any past event that he has seen with the Witness Spacetime ability. While this ability is in effect the witnesses will recall the Falsified chain of events and all recording devices will record a lasting recording of the falsified timeline. Example the Temponaut would be able to change<br /> <br /> 12:15 pm, Subject enters a bank.<br /> 12:16 pm, The bank gets robed.<br /> 12:17 pm, Subject exits bank.<br /> <br /> This could be changed to<br /> <br /> 12:15 pm, Subject enters a bank.<br /> 12:16 pm, Subject exits bank.<br /> 12:17 pm, The bank gets robed.<br /> <br /> This would not change the fact that the bank was robed or that the Subject was the one that robed it, but the witnesses would recall that the subject left the bank before it was robbed and the banks video surveillance would record the subject leaving before the robbery. Any attempt to discover the true timeline would cause a Clash of Wills and the Temponaut would score a number of successes equal to his Time Rating. This is an instant action with Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Space 3<br /> The Temponaut would be able to veil any sympathetic links that the subject may have to the Falsified Timeline with a specialized version of \u201cVeil Sympathy\u201d this would mask any connections that may exist with the even. This is an instant action with Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:</b> Rend Spacetime<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6, Time 4 and Academics 4<br /> With the ability to view timelines the Temponaut is able to throw his opponent a few turns into the future, maximum number of turns is the Temponauts time rating. This is similar to \u201cTemporal Stutter\u201d in that the Temponaut is able to shunt his victim into the future. This is an instant action.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Space 4<br /> Using Space in conjunction with the primary ability the Temponaut is able to cause his opponent great harm. By momentarily breaking the bond between space and time the Temponaut is able to create an effect similar to the \u201cCollapse\u201d spell. When the subject re-enters normal time he suffers Lethal damage equal to the casters space rating. This is an instant action.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b> Devour Spacetime<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 8, Time 5, Science 4<br /> This ability is the pinnacle of the Temponauts training and there most feared ability. This effect is similar to the \u201cRewrite History\u201d spell and may be performed one any timeline that has been witnessed with the Witness Spacetime above and rewrites the witnessed event. This is ritual casting with Advanced Duration and Infinite Duration costing one mana.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Space 5<br /> In conjunction with the base ability the subject also cut the threads associated with that event similar to the \u201cCut Threads\u201d spell. Any connections that were formed during the witnessed event in the base ability is severed. This is ritual casting with Advanced Duration and Infinite Duration costing one mana.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Unique spells created by the Temponauts.</b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inspect Timeline (Time \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Investigation, Occult.<br /> With this spell the strands of time are as visible as a clock upon the wall. The mage can inspect the subject\u2019s timeline for a known intersection. This will tell the mage when two known timelines crossed and how long they stayed intertwined with each other. The mage can see other timeline intersections but he would not be able to discern any information about that intersection. Unlike the spell Divination you are not viewing the timeline of the subject and therefore you would not be able to see what transpired during that time, however there is also no viewing speed so locating the intersection is instantaneous. You are able to discern the number of times that the two timelines crossed using potency as noted on the time table below. If either of the two the subjects has their timeline concealed then there is a Clash of Will to be able to inspect the timeline.<br /> <b>Add Space \u2022:</b> By adding the Space Arcanum you can also see if there is a connection between the two subjects.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> With this reach you do not need to know both subjects, you can use generalities in place of one of the subjects. Example: When did the restaurant receive its last delivery? When was the Last time the subject spoke to another person? This will reveal the number of times that the general condition occurred equal to potency. With potency two you would be able to tell the last two deliveries the restaurant received.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and Space \u2022:</b> With this you can search a timeline for unknown connection, this will reveal a number of connections equal to potency and allow you to follow those connections, similar to the base ability of Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Potency 1: The most recent.<br /> Potency 2: Within the Last hour.<br /> Potency 3: Within the Last Day.<br /> Potency 4: Within the Last week.<br /> Potency 5: Within the last Month.<br /> Potency 6: Within the last Year.<br /> Potency 7+: Every time the strands crossed.<br /> <br /> <b>Falsify Timeline (Time \u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Larceny, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> For the duration of this spell the Mage can Falsify the subject\u2019s action within the Timeline. If someone tries to view the subjects past it will provoke a Clash of Wills. If they fail the Clash of Wills then the Caster of this spell can send an altered image of events to the onlooker. This does not alter what really happened just what the onlooker perceives happened.<br /> If the onlooker Records this Falsified Timeline, in any fashion, the effects become lasting in that the recorded history remains even after the spell ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-16-2017, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:57:35-07:00","id":1129694,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Too complicated? Am I trying to do too many things at once?<br /> <br /> The Heirs of Heimdall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nicknames: The Crowned, Heathens (derogatory)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path/Order: Thyrsus/Silver Ladder</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Philosophy: </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Heirs of Heimdall, a young Legacy, take their name from the Norse god Heimdall; however, they do not seek to only emulate his aspects of protection and staunch determination, but his wise rulership as spoken of in the Song of Rig. A noble ruler, he led humanity into a golden age of peace and prosperity before his human body\u2019s death and the return of his divine soul to Asgard. The founder of the legacy, a Thyrsus calling himself Seidmann (the ancient Norse word for a magic-using male), was in his Sleeper life a follower of Asatru, Germanic neo-paganism, and sought to blend his religion with his chosen order, interpreting the gods as powerful archmages who had become Supernal symbols discernable even to the Fallen World. Not only that, but he was obsessed (as many mages are) with seeking immortality. Though he would later reconcile himself to the semi-impossibility of his quest, he did make some important discoveries and laid out three important precepts for his future legacy; firstly, that all places in the Fallen World have echoes in the Supernal, which draw them \u2018upwards\u2019, so to speak; secondly, that Space only has meaning in Pandemonium and the Fallen World, that in truth, all places--even including the Supernal Realms, the Abyss, and the Fallen World together--are actually one point; and thirdly, that a mage may so imbue a claimed area with his soul that he never truly dies, but instead brings that piece of the Fallen World and the Supernal Realms \u2018closer\u2019 by tying his Supernal soul to the Fallen land. Essentially, by claiming a piece of the world, the Heir, philosophically speaking, claims the whole world, and can draw out its natural divinity through just and fair rulership, emulating Heimdall, who gave himself to Midgard for its betterment. While some among the other orders, especially the Free Council, deride the Heirs as \u201cmad wizards in their towers\u201d, the Legacy is quite popular among Silver Ladder Thyrsus, many of whom regard it as the ultimate expression of the Precept of Thunder. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Legacy Skills: Occult, Politics, Expression</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance: As many Heirs are previous or current Asatru followers, they often affect long, \u201cviking\u201d beards if male, and usually intricately braided hair if female, as well as other markers such as Mjolnir amulets or, more commonly, horn amulets to represent Heimdall. They also often carry symbols of rulership, including staffs, rods, and even crowns if engaged in spellcasting. Otherwise, they are about as diverse as any other group of mages.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concepts: Awakened anarcho-monarchist, neo-pagan mystic, Silver Ladder elitist</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Magic \u2013 Space Primary, Spirit Optional</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: Patrolling one\u2019s claimed territory, actively mediating disputes between local spirits, improving the territory in some observable, definable way</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: Horns (musical ones) played during casting (+1), Cast while in one\u2019s claimed territory (+2) </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12723-react0rman","name":"react0rman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T18:10:49-07:00","id":1152346,"title":"","content":"I wanted to work with a legacy that played on superhero symbolism but placed the Mage at odds with the Pentacle. Could use some suggestions about making them more &quot;Left-Handed&quot;. Any critique is appreciated.<br /> <br /> ************************************************** *****<br /> <br /> True Believers (Left-Hand)<br /> <br /> Origins<br /> <br /> Parentage: Obrimos, Acanthus, Free Council<br /> Background: This Legacy has traditionally recruited members from those in heroic vocations; especially those went to war with the servants of the Seers in their Sleeper lives (e.g., noble warriors, heretical voices for change, whistleblowers). However, as their practices have come under more scrutiny, veteran Heroes no longer recruit prospective members but instead wait for those willing to accept the consequences of their calling to seek them out.<br /> <br /> Appearances: No two Heroes will ever look the same. As each Hero gains experience, they will cultivate a very specific outfit that calls on the symbolism of their Shadow Name. However, all Heroes maintain two idiosyncratic personas that represent their civilian and heroic natures. During formal and informal gatherings of the Legacy, it is considered uncouth to appear in one\u2019s civilian persona.<br /> <br /> Doctrine<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Prime 2, Persuasion 2, two dots in one of the following Skills; Craft, Investigation, Athletics, and Streetwise, one dot in the Shadow Name Merit.<br /> <br /> Initiation: The eager young Hero must patrol their protectorate, relying on only their wits and natural skills should the need for crime-fighting arise. Moreover, the Hero must intentionally spend each night patrolling locations where they believe servants of the Seers or some other supernatural manipulator are active. During this time, a veteran Hero will shadow the recruit as they patrol; looking for any hint of moral corruption or cowardice. Only when the recruit has found a suitably heroic and dangerous situation will the veteran intervene. If the duo survives the final conflict, the veteran will welcome the recruit into the Legacy. While in ages past the end of this ceremony would result in the recruit seeking out their own territory, the multitude of adversaries in the modern-era has led to multiple Heroes patrolling the same protectorate.<br /> <br /> Organization: All Heroes are expected to lead their own personal crusade against the Seers and those monsters that seek to oppress humanity. It is not uncommon though for a veteran Hero to take a junior member under their wing, or, for a group of Heroes to maintain an informal organization that they can call on to combat large threats. During times of monumental crisis, Heroes are expected to answer the call of the Legacy to face the threat as a unified front.<br /> <br /> Theory: It is common knowledge that there is no historical evidence connecting heroic legends with the activities of Mages, but isn\u2019t it such a curious thing that humanity continues to create heroes with powers beyond mortal ken? Most Mages write this Sleeper phenomenon off as little more than an escape fantasy. For Heroes, they believe that is the soul of humanity slipping through the Abyssal-taint; showing Mages a way to subvert the Abyss and become the heroes they were destined to be. Stories of cultural heroes and the colorful pages of comics are blueprints. Mask and origin stories are sword and shield against the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> <br /> Ruling Arcanum: Prime<br /> Yantras: Succeeding on a Persuasion roll related to the relevant spell (+2); declaring the evil deeds of your adversary (+1); explaining how your \u201cpowers\u201d work to a bystander (+1, or +2 if the bystander is a Sleeper); collecting evidence of your enemy\u2019s wrongdoing or weaknesses (e.g., photos, recordings) (+2).<br /> Oblations: Patrolling one\u2019s protectorate, Practicing the skills related to one\u2019s \u201cpowers\u201d, repairing and tending to the equipment and clothes tied to the heroic persona, pursuing and hiding one\u2019s secret identity, spreading rumors about Heroes.<br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> <br /> First: Staring into the Night<br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> The Hero becomes attuned to the Truth as they start their crusade to right the injustice that is the Fallen World. This Attainment replicates \u201cPierce Deception\u201d with Reach assigned to Instant Use. If this Attainment is attempting to pierce through supernatural concealment, it automatically scores successes equal to the Mage\u2019s Prime dots.<br /> Optional: Fate 1, Destiny 1<br /> Often in heroic stories, the narrative works to direct the protagonist towards their goals. By believing in their own heroic goals, the Hero gains intuitive insight into where they need to be to stop the forces of darkness. This Attainment replicates the \u201cSerendipity&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to Instant Use. It is used solely provide glimpses to what the Mage should do in the pursuit of justice. The Mage may use a dot from their Destiny pool to add the +1 Reach allowing the Mage to substitute any Skill of the same type to accomplish their desired goal.<br /> <br /> Second: Standing for Truth<br /> Prerequisites: Prime 2, Persuasion 3.<br /> The Hero is able to bring the light of heroic belief into the world with their words. This Attainment replicates the spell \u201cWords of Truth\u201d with Reach assigned to Instant Use. In Social maneuvering action, this removes Doors equal to the Hero\u2019s rating in Prime. This power is solely used to aid the Hero in bringing the truth out of villainous and to inspire the meek.<br /> Optional: Fate 2, Destiny 2<br /> The hyper narratives that surround heroic stories are filled with instances when the Hero plots the most opportune path amidst a chaotic situation. While the Hero is patrolling their protectorate, they find reality working for them to aid them in their crusade. This Attainment replicates the spell \u201cQuantum Flux\u201d with Reach assigned to Instant Use and Advanced Duration. This Attainment subtracts penalties equal to the Hero\u2019s Fate dots for a number of actions equal to their Fate dots.<br /> <br /> Third: Donning the Mantle<br /> Prerequisites: Prime 3, two dots in a second Skill among the initiation Skill list and two dots in the Shadow Name Merit.<br /> As their notoriety increases, the Hero finds that the symbols and tools tied to their heroic persona hum with the power of the Supernal. Carefully tending to and donning these symbols allows the Hero to call on their symbolism to greatly increase their power. This Attainment replicates the spell \u201cAs Above So Below\u201d with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and grating the 8-Again effect on spellcasting rolls. The Hero may dedicate a number of Yantra equal to their dots in Prime. The first Yantra dedicated must be their Heroic persona.<br /> Optional: Fate 3, Destiny 3<br /> Heroes often have access to equipment that exceeds the capabilities of mortal craftsmanship. Just as they dedicate Yantras to call on the power of their Heroics symbolism, the Hero can collapse destiny on an object to increase its capabilities to mythic heights. This Attainment replicates the spell \u201cMonkey\u2019s Paw\u201d with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. This Attainment can only be used to bless a piece of equipment that the Hero uses in their crusade. By spending a Destiny point for the duration of the Attainment, the Hero may access the +1 Reach option to allow the equipment bonus to exceed 5. The Potency of this Attainment is equal to the Hero\u2019s dots in Fate.<br /> <br /> Fourth: Facing front<br /> Prerequisites: Prime 4, Persuasion 4.<br /> When calling on the symbolism of their heroic persona, the Hero can push back the darkness in the souls of Sleepers. This allows the Hero to call on their powers without fear of Paradox within their protectorate. After patrolling their protectorate in their Heroic Persona, the Hero replicates the spell \u201cStealing Fire\u201d with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale. This ritual creates room-sized areas where Sleepers become Sleepwalkers when they enter. This Attainment only affects spells that call on the Hero\u2019s persona as a Yantra.<br /> Optional: Fate 4, Destiny 4<br /> By calling on the strength of their heroic narrative, the Hero may bring fate to bare on those who witness them in action. This Attainment replicates the spell \u201cSworn Oaths\u201d with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and giving the Hero awareness of when the Oath is broken. This Attainment is used to bind villains to change their ways and aspiring heroes to moral actions.<br /> <br /> Fifth: Breaking the Wall<br /> Prerequisites: Prime 5, two dots in a third Skill among the initiation Skill list, or three dots in the second and three dots in the Shadow Name Merit.<br /> At the height of their power, the Hero can now break a piece of the Lie\u2019s hold on the Fallen World. The Hero\u2019s protectorate now becomes suffused with the power of their heroic persona. This Attainment replicates the spell \u201cCreate Truth\u201d with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. The rating of the Hallow is equal to the Hero\u2019s dots in Prime; with a Resonance identical to the Hero.<br /> Optional: Fate 5, Destiny 5<br /> By this point in the story, the Hero knows that no matter the obstacle they are going to save the day. It isn\u2019t a matter of fate or destiny, but instead the inevitable effect that their crusade has on the Lie. With that awareness, the Hero can briefly push aside the Lie to make their desired outcome a reality. This Attainment replicates the spell \u201cMiracle\u201d with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. The Hero gains enough intercessions equal to their dots in Fate, but may only use them while in their heroic persona. The Hero may spend a Destiny point, a Willpower point, and a Mana point to access the +2 Reach form of this spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 11-11-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T19:00:55-07:00","id":1152359,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s no bad, but definitely doesn\u2019t strike me as Left-Handed.<br /> <br /> Also, Words of Truth has to typically be used on a subject other than the Mage casting it so it will require a touch or Aimed activation Range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T03:30:41-07:00","id":1152449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1152359#post1152359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s no bad, but definitely doesn\u2019t strike me as Left-Handed.<br /> <br /> Also, Words of Truth has to typically be used on a subject other than the Mage casting it so it will require a touch or Aimed activation Range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I definitely understand that. I think I just wanted to get the mechanics down before I fine-tuned the aesthetic. I just imagine them being an affront to Awakened societies desire to be secretive, but maybe that doesn't mean they have to be left-handed.<br /> <br /> Ahhh yeah I wasn't sure if the spell was affecting the words on the Mage's end or recipient's. I'll have look to see if there is something clever to switch in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T11:12:13-07:00","id":1152561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1152449#post1152449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I definitely understand that. I think I just wanted to get the mechanics down before I fine-tuned the aesthetic. I just imagine them being an affront to Awakened societies desire to be secretive, but maybe that doesn't mean they have to be left-handed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It does if they recklessly leave broken people behind, their sanity eroded by quiescence.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what liberal use of attainment #4 will do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 10-24-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T11:46:14-07:00","id":1152573,"title":"","content":"I just realized that the Hero legacy doesn\u2019t always do spell factors properly. For instance the 4th Attainment says it can affect a number of Sleepers up to dots in Prime, but it should be a number up to -4 (So 3) at Prime 5 as secondary factors like Scale determine their level of effectiveness by treating dots in the arcana as a pool of dice you can apply dice penalties to. I\u2019d redo it, use the secondary factor to increase Potency and accept that you can only make Sleepwalkers one at a time, but you can make them as often as you want since you can have an infinite number of attainment instances running in parallel as they don\u2019t take up<br /> Spell control. Reach could be spent on Instant and Advanced Duration. In practice it would probably look like the Hero greeting people in his protectorate and shaking their hand or brushing their hand as they help with a bag of groceries and placing the attainment on them. You\u2019d have to check in on them semi-regularly too to keep the effect up, at least once a year. This wouldn\u2019t work on Sleepers with a Resolve of 4 or higher though (They\u2019re exceedingly rare anyway though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:45:57-07:00","id":1153991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1152573#post1152573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized that the Hero legacy doesn\u2019t always do spell factors properly. For instance the 4th Attainment says it can affect a number of Sleepers up to dots in Prime, but it should be a number up to -4 (So 3) at Prime 5 as secondary factors like Scale determine their level of effectiveness by treating dots in the arcana as a pool of dice you can apply dice penalties to. I\u2019d redo it, use the secondary factor to increase Potency and accept that you can only make Sleepwalkers one at a time, but you can make them as often as you want since you can have an infinite number of attainment instances running in parallel as they don\u2019t take up<br /> Spell control. Reach could be spent on Instant and Advanced Duration. In practice it would probably look like the Hero greeting people in his protectorate and shaking their hand or brushing their hand as they help with a bag of groceries and placing the attainment on them. You\u2019d have to check in on them semi-regularly too to keep the effect up, at least once a year. This wouldn\u2019t work on Sleepers with a Resolve of 4 or higher though (They\u2019re exceedingly rare anyway though).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the late reply. I appreciate the critique. I definitely knew that the Spell Factors for that Attainment were a bit fuzzy. I figured that because this Attainment was only usable when spells utilized the mage's Shadow Name Yantra, that it would allow for some leeway. I originally imagined it being used only during combat and leaving bystanders broken from what they have seen after. I definitely like the idea that you have suggested. I","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:56:09-07:00","id":1153995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1153991#post1153991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the late reply. I appreciate the critique. I definitely knew that the Spell Factors for that Attainment were a bit fuzzy. I figured that because this Attainment was only usable when spells utilized the mage's Shadow Name Yantra, that it would allow for some leeway. I originally imagined it being used only during combat and leaving bystanders broken from what they have seen after. I definitely like the idea that you have suggested. I</div> </div> </div> </div>A different route you could go is to skip Advanced Duration and take Advanced Scale instead, and still use the dice penalties to bump up Potency. Then in a small room sized area around your Hero for up to 10 turns any Sleepers inside the Scale of the effect that aren't Resolve 4 or higher would be Sleepwalkers. They'd lose the effect if they move out of the area, and it's only a small room size that's affected so anyone outside the area would still be affected by Dissonance normally. Basically, it wouldn't be great on a busy city street, but in a back alley you'd be able to do pretty much whatever you wanted in a magical brawl.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could skip Instant activation, and use Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale to set up multiple small room areas contiguous to each other running with your attainment simultaneously via a scene long ritual and prepare a much bigger area of &quot;safe&quot; magic over time as Sleepers become Sleepwalkers when they wander into it. This would likely be the purpose of going on patrol in your protectorate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T15:04:37-07:00","id":1153997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1153995#post1153995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A different route you could go is to skip Advanced Duration and take Advanced Scale instead, and still use the dice penalties to bump up Potency. Then in a small room sized area around your Hero for up to 10 turns any Sleepers inside the Scale of the effect that aren't Resolve 4 or higher would be Sleepwalkers. They'd lose the effect if they move out of the area, and it's only a small room size that's affected so anyone outside the area would still be affected by Dissonance normally. Basically, it wouldn't be great on a busy city street, but in a back alley you'd be able to do pretty much whatever you wanted in a magical brawl.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could skip Instant activation, and use Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale to set up multiple small room areas contiguous to each other running with your attainment simultaneously via a scene long ritual and prepare a much bigger area of &quot;safe&quot; magic over time as Sleepers become Sleepwalkers when they wander into it. This would likely be the purpose of going on patrol in your protectorate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You my friend are a genius. I think both make sense for different Heroes depending on how they view their role in their protectorates. I'll get to work incorporating these into the write-up. Thank you for taking time to think and respond about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T17:44:46-08:00","id":1280215,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Eternal Soul Sentinels</span> </b><br /> <b>Other names</b>: Heralds of the End, Century Children, Could-Have-Been-Kings, Time Liches, Guardians of Forever<br /> <br /> The Sentinels originated at the end of time and are expected to pass the legacy BACKWARDS to their youth, once they achieve Time Mastery. They equate mentorship to the ancestry of the mind and thus their \u201clineage\u201d is those \u201cancestors\u201d that will exist in the future as part of the direct line of mentorship that propagated backwards to a given Sentinel. The \u201calpha member\u201d is the member the member fartherst back in time, whose chief duty is to achieve Time Mastery and continue the propagation backwards. There are also \u201comega members\u201d from collateral lineages that propagate the legacy forward in time.<br /> <br /> The Eternal Soul Sentinels believe they have been given a sacred charge to protect and pass backwards a sympathetic link to the \u201cEternal Dark\u201d. The Eternal Dark is not a specific date but rather a metaphysical point to which all timelines lead. It is the time at which the universe ends utterly, the silent cold darkness at the end of the universe after the last ray of background radiation passes by and nothing ever happens again. The Eternal Soul Sentinels hold that it is impossible to actually <i>pass</i> this point as doing so would merely mean it is later in time. Those who try to use the Sentinel's temporal sympathy to actually arrive at the Eternal Dark either use magic to carefully never pass the final threshold or never return. <br /> <br /> The actual nature of what that sacred charge IS and what will happen meta-when the Alpha Member reaches the earliest possible point though is a \u2026 complicated subject. Due to the acausal nature of the Legacy, multiple mutually exclusive versions of the founding of the legacy are all equally true. There are even multiple Ur-Ancestors. And that's <i>before</i> taking into account the distortions inherent in passing an oral history through an enormous game of Telephone played by secretive Time Master across multiple linguistic and cultural drifts. And the cross contamination as different branches and lineages of the legacy work together and communicate.<br /> <br /> By this point in time there are many jumbled together interpretations of the purpose of the legacy that nobody can really keep straight. One posits that history is wounded and the legacy will stitch together the wound in order to protect the Sleeping soul of the Fallen universe itself. Several speculate the entire Legacy is actually a Archmaster's cult for producing quintessence. Another is that a a horde of souls stolen from across all of time will sent climbing up the ladder formed by the legacy and into the Eternal Dark in a mass jailbreak from the Lie. Another is the exact opposite, that the future will feed souls into the past and reform the wheel of re-incarnation broken by the Abyss. There are dark rumors that the Could-Have-Been-Kings are meant to be the true secret rulers, the true Seers of the Throne, guiding history as they wish and \u201ctruly living\u201d unlike the \u201cflatliners\u201d that they mold like clay by controlling the timeline. Conversely some posit the immense amount of good an organization of Time Liches spread across all of time could do, not least of which is simply acting as a safeguard against extinction events.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the most daunting interpretation, and the one to which StrifeStalker subscribes, is that the Legacy is nothing less than a declaration of war against Quiescence and the Exarchs. Due to the nature of the legacy, it is possible that with enough meta-time every person to ever live will emerge from the changing tides of history stabilized from further alterations to the past by learning the second attainment of this Legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Origin</b><br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Moros, Adamantine Arrow or Silver Ladder<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: Devotion and mental resilience are key traits the Hands look for when recruiting potential immortals. Of particular interest is a strong belief in and devotion to something greater than oneself. Priests, cultists, social workers, sports coaches, and the like. Also important is an understanding and acceptance of mortality. For it is in passing that members achieve immortality, and most will die a thousand deaths before the changing past sets them on the path to achieve the fifth attainmen.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: Century Children often appear to be callously unsympathetic to the plights of others, offering only philosophical platitudes before moving onwards with a a relentless self assurance that can seem like cocky arrogance. The constant companionship of the End casts all things into into perspective and ever is a reminder of the ephmerality of existence. And as a result, many find their comfort in esoteric philosophy.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> Prerequisites: Time 2, Athletics 2 (members of this Legacy are bear within their souls a sacred trust and must be able to protect it by protecting themselves until they can pass it on). Occult 2, Two dots of Status or Mystery Cult Initiation (but not M.C. Influence).<br /> Initiation: The student must use a variant of Postcognition to trace the temporal sympathy of their mentor forward to the End and experience it until they naturally develop their own sympathetic connection to it. Mentor and student go through the rituals of the Second Attainment in order to extend the mentor's aegis across the moment of the student's initiation. The mentor then melds his own sympathetic connection to the End to that of the student's. and uses their third attainment to Perfect this sympathetic connection and also to animate the student's own shadow and feed it to them. Technically the student is now mystically initiated into the legacy at this point, but they haven't been socially initiated.<br /> <br /> The social initiation occurs as the mentor guides the student's awareness through time to \u201cvisit\u201d each \u201cancestor\u201d of their direct lineage of mentorship. During each \u201cvisit\u201d the mentor, student, and ancestor inspect eachother's sympathetic connections to the End for issues like Abyssal taint, and then coil copies of eachothers around their own. In this way the student's sympathetic connection to the End grows to be less like a thread and more like a thick rope of many threads woven together. Plus this acts as another layer of protection for rescuing members if events in the past undo their existence.<br /> <br /> The last step of initiation is for the mentor to \u201cdangle a hook\u201d for the student's own students to \u201cvisit\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b>: Due to the way the legacy propagates backwards in time, no real organization beyond mentor and student exists for the alpha terminus. Though if one's mentor decides to indulge in some extra recruiting, fellow legacy members might suddenly pop up<br /> <br /> <b>Theory</b>: One of the metaphors the legacy uses to describe its attainment is that of long icicles dangling down from the obsidian ceiling of an old lava cave long since gone cold. The dark obsidian roof is the Eternal Dark and the icicles dangling from the roof are the frozen lines of temporal sympathy which the legacy protects and grows backwards in time. This was inspired by an actual site in the northern reaches of Canada that is thus held to be sacred to the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Beyond that the legacy teaches that the universe itself is the divine corpse of a demiurge that, when confronted with an eternity of solitude, killed itself in a deific fit of suicidal despair. The Demiurge ripped itself apart and cast the fragments of its divinity across its body so that it can lie to itself that it is not alone. Thus every soul contains a divine spark and the Awakened are those whose sparks that have found fertile fuel to ignite into the blazing fire of Gnosis which shines with the light of Wisdom.<br /> <br /> The legacy acknowledges 4 different types of enlightenment: Corpse Law, Flame Law, Sword Law, and Blood Law. The enlightenment of Flame Law is understanding the blaze of one's own innate divinity. It is to know one's self is a self-imposed delusion without losing hold upon the substance of that delusion. The enlightenment of Blood Law is the links and interconnections of the world, binding oneself to the community and the flaming souls of others. The enlightenment of Corpse Law is found in the suicidal nihlism of the Demiurge and drawing upon the latent divine power soaked into the Demiurge's corpse. The enlightenment of Sword Law is found in the art of severing and cutting, which the Demiurge wielded upon itself .<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>: astronomy and contemplating the night sky, contemplating a growing icicle, researching potential inheritors of the legacy, studying the \u201cmentorship family tree\u201d and tracking your impact on your ancestors. Maintaining and studying one's own Constant Presence memoirs, as well as comparing them to the non-stabalized version.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b>:<br /> <b>First</b>: Final Breath<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation<br /> The Could-Have-Been-King's mana-infused breath billows out, fogged with the chill of his icicle. The cold congeals mana into one of his Imago and rimes it with ice, greatly prolonging the spell by preserving it and stretching it out along the lines of temporal sympathy towards the End. The Century Child spends 1 mana to apply the Advanced Duration reach to his spell or spell-like attainment<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Death 1<br /> Instead of infusing his Final Breath with mana, the Sentinel draws forth darkness of the End. He peers into his fogged breath and in its shape and movement sees Symbols representing how to bring a thing closer to its End. When used to inspect a married couple for instance, a Sentinel capable of seeing spatial sympathetic connections might see his breath overlay the number 3 onto his view of the wife's phone to symbolize that the couple's sympathetic bond might be ended by the revelation that the 3<sup>rd</sup> contact on her phone is her boyfriend. This Attainment is an Unveiling effect for how the subject could bring about the end of a given specimen, with Potency determining the number of revealed clues. An Int+Occult roll might be necessary to interpret its results and could potentially result in an Informed condition for ending the specimen<br /> <br /> <b>Second</b>: Frozen Blood<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Time 2 Athletics 3 or Occult 3<br /> The Eternal Soul Sentinel dances a rite honoring and symbolizing the celestial sphere. As each celestial object is honored, it is symbolically quenched and the dancer acts more and more like they are freezing to death. As the dance reaches its End, the dancer passes through paradoxical undressing, terminal burrowing, loss of consciousness, and then the final stillness of organ failure. By doing this, the chill inevitability of the End expands out from the Sentinel's lungs and into the bloodstream. The Sentinel becomes congealed in the time stream as if by a ritual casting of Constant Presence with Advanced Duration.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Death 2<br /> When performed at night, the Sentinel's sacred dance shifts and drags at the Earth's shadow (aka the dark of night) and (very locally) snuffs out the light of each celestial object as it is symbolically quenched. By the end of the dance, the dancer lies still within a collapsing sphere of darkness as thin streams of the Eternal Dark begin flowing within their veins. This enacts a variant of Suppress Aura with Advanced Duration. The Sentinel's personal aura and nimbus are dampened, with Mage Sight detects him as <i>not existing </i>even while mundane eyes see him fine. Magical attempts to see through the effect provoke a Clash of Wills. This effect can be spread to spells cast later for the cost of a point of mana and a Reach. His emotions become harder to read in general, imposing a -2 penalty on Empathy checks.<br /> <br /> <b>Third</b>: Cracked Skin<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Time 3, 3 dots in 2 of (Occult, Athletics, Status/Mystery_Cult_Initation) and 2 dots in the other<br /> The Sentinel's connection to the Eternal Dark develops to the point that it cracks open the boundaries of his skin and oozes out to affect the world. He speaks a sacred Mystery of the Eternal Dark, in which every word is silent. Then, as if they were blow-darts, he spits out these frozen silences to either bolster or undermine the strands of sympathy they stab into. This functions as a thrown touch-range Time version of the Web-Weaver spell, allowing the caster to strengthen or weaken an existing Temporal Sympathetic link<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Death 3<br /> Instead of solely the frigid temporal sympathy of his icicle, the Sentinel can also allow the umbral touch of the Eternal Dark itself to seep out into his sacred words. This functions as the Shadow Crafting spell, save that the animated shadows are silent (absorbing and blotting out any sound that tries to pass through them) and bitterly cold, leaving hoarfrost on any surface they touch. Due to the chill and being the metaphysical manifestation of the end of all things, prolonged contact with the shadows tends to be damaging to non-legacy members.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth</b>: Organ Failure<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Time 4 Athletics 4 or Occult 4<br /> The Sentinel curls his body slightly and then unleashes the coiled tension in a shove, as if hitting a volleyball or launching a package through zero g. But instead of space, the target is cast adrift through time as the mage uses his Icicle as a harpoon to tether a different temporal version of the target into reality. This functions as the Rewrite History spell.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Death 4<br /> Strengthened by enduring prolonged exposure to the end of all things, the mage's soul can linger and persist past the death of its mortal body. Upon death (or the temporary occurrence of such via the Time portion of this Attainment) it remains in the world as if kept in a Soul Jar formed of its own gnosis. The Sentinel still retaining his personality and ability to act, so typically he seeps his soul into nearby shadows he can manipulate and form into a body via the third attainment, surviving as a shadowy wraith similar to the spell Shadow Flesh. Despite his soul remaining fundamentally the soul of a human mage, the mage's mind is subjected to new drives and needs. Instead of more mundane food, the bared soul of the wraith hungers for mana with a startling intensity. The wraith body is never satiated and even when full the mage is forced to have \u201cDevour the mana of the living\u201d as an aspiration. Its hunger rips mana from the bodies of those injured by its animated shadows in an effect similar to Devouring The Slain. This form of lichhood is made all the more deadly by the fact that destroying the shadow body does nothing but inconvenience the invisible lingering soul. Some speculate that there is some form of kinship with the Strix.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth</b>: Oblivion<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Time 5<br /> The mage spends 1 mana or a dot of willpower and takes on the fundamental nature of the legacy, twisting time back upon itself as future changes past in act of simultaneous genesis and annihilation. The mage becomes one with his connection to the Eternal Dark and traces that connection back to a previous point in his own life time. This functions as a lasting/indefinite Corridors of Time spell.<br /> The fact that even the shadowy liches of the fourth optional attainment can use this attainment to unwrite their own death is what earns members of this legacy the title of Time Liches.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Death 5<br /> The mage spends a mana and unleashes the direct touch of the Eternal Dark upon a target viewed through the fog of the first attainment, washing the target with a wave of the most pure metaphysical Ending possible until the target ceases. This is sensory range advanced duration Unmaking effect that nigh inevitably brings about the end of the target, destroying it utterly if its Stamina (or equivalent Withstand) is not equal to or greater than the Potency (dots of Death) of this attainment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T13:49:14-08:00","id":1280399,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</a> , an Acanthus Legacy of master planners and strategists.<br /> <br /> Feedback is very much appreciated. Do the yantras make sense ? Do the attainments look useful ? Was the theme presented in a cohesive manner ?<br /> <br /> I wanted to make them into enlightened strategists. At the time I was reading more about Plato and the philosophies derived from his teachings, in order to get a stronger grasp on the inspirations for Mage. Stoicism seemed to resonate with the Arrows, especially when Marcus Aurelius stood out as both a philosopher king and great strategist. The fact that Wisdom was one of their core virtues was especially interesting: &quot;Are there any Legacies that tackle cultivation of Wisdom ? Seems not, that might be a cool theme to explore&quot;.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-28-2019, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T23:44:31-08:00","id":1287439,"title":"","content":"Here are the 3 Legacies I've made for the game I'm running:<ul><li>Priests of the Nekromanteion: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1269784-help-with-new-acanthus-legacy\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...canthus-legacy</a></li> <li>Gallizenae: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1269479-help-with-new-thyrsus-legacy\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...thyrsus-legacy</a></li> <li>Forge Masters: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1272145-yet-another-legacy-this-time-is-moros-time\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-is-moros-time</a></li> </ul>I'm particulary proud of the Priests of the Nekromanteion, the seem to me very well rounded and with enough back history to feel &quot;real&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","user":"Eleizel","date":". 02-13-2019, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T10:15:31-08:00","id":1292806,"title":"","content":"We made one, I suggested the concept and themes and KaiserAfini has been helping me with the details and attainments so I give you:<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1281000-help-with-custom-legacy-the-nizari\">The Nizari</a>: A Mastigos Legacy of assassins from the Guardians of the Veil inspired by the old assassins order in the midle east.<br /> <br /> Still working on a few details but it's mostly done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 02-28-2019, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T00:52:35-08:00","id":1293428,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This one has been completed for some time. It's a refinement of an earlier idea I posted in some other thread I can't find right now. Basically, you learn to control the darkness within and without for the sake of knowledge, secrecy, and control over others. In the end you become that very same darkness and rule your kingdom within the human soul forever.</span></span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disciples of Ahriman</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Origins</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parentage: Mastigos</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nickname: Secret Masters</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Background: An ancient tradition dating back to the height of Zoroastrian times created by a master known to adherents as the Deceiver. They weave their webs from the shadows, mastering the vices and failings of people with positions of power over politics or secret societies, seemingly for its own sake. Some among the Disciples speak of a &quot;Great Work&quot; conceived of by the Immortal Masters to bring the Legacy to a kind of mass ascension through mastery of the world.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance: The Secret Masters typically wear a variety of disguises to present themselves how they wish to their targets. They do their best to appear 'in character' in appropriate locations they have set up ahead of time to best enable their manipulative practices, but can look like pretty much anybody in everyday situations.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doctrine</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Death 2, Occult 2, and one of the following skills at 2 dots or higher: Empathy, Investigation, Persuasion, or Subterfuge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation: The Legacy seems to appear at random in seemingly unconnected mages at different places and times, who create a circle of apprentices and co-conspirators from there. When forced to speak the alleged truth, the original Disciple of Ahriman (a suspect title to begin with) will confess that the Deceiver came to them in a dream. It cares not for the sects of its students, seeking Mastigos from among the Pentacle, Iron Pyramid, and Nameless with no apparent rhyme or reason.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Organization: A master and a handful of apprentices. The Secret Masters are secret even to each other, with only the greatest of them knowing more than what they were meant to.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theory: Conceive. Conceal. Control. These three words define a way of life intended to give you the knowledge to understand others, the secrecy to protect yourself from them, and the means to make them do as you wish. To peer into human souls, master the darkness within them, and rule over the kingdom of demons which dwells there without anyone being the wiser. So it shall be with magic itself, for it too has a mind that may be controlled without its awareness - the road to Ascension.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Magic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcanum: Death</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: Disguising yourself as another (+1); Whispering a subject's failings and weaknesses in their presence (+1); Invading the subject's privacy to construct a map of their personality and relationships (+2); Organizing an ominous secret meeting with the subject at least a day in advance (+2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: Creating profiles of potential subjects; erasing evidence of someone's presence; selecting and putting on disguises; setting up ominous decor.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainment 1 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To control the mind and soul of another requires a Sovereign to first understand it. Through a scene of observation they gaze into the soul of another person to see the marks left on it over the course of their lives. This duplicates the Death spell &quot;Soul Marks&quot; at sensory range.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Mind 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The inner demons of others may be coaxed to whisper to the Secret Master about their strengths and flaws of character, their goals and dreams. This allows the main Attainment to also duplicate the &quot;Know Nature&quot; spell and reveal a subject's Virtue, Vice, Aspirations and Obsessions at sensory range. However, it will not reveal the subject's Mental or Social Attributes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainment 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Death 2, Occult 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The infernal shadows of human sin briefly expand their reach so that few might see their way through to the Secret Master behind them. With but a touch the shadows begin to spread. This duplicates the &quot;Deepen Shadows&quot; spell instantly with Advanced Scale.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Mind 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demons surrender information about more peripheral, immediate concerns in the souls of their people without much coaxing. In an instant the Secret Master may tune into this information from any individual they may directly perceive within their dim illumination. This duplicates the &quot;Mental Scan&quot; spell instantly at sensory range.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainment 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Death 3. In addition to the Occult 3 requirement from the previous Attainment, the Secret Master must increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The darkness of the human soul spreads to conceal the Disciple's true glory. They appear to be nothing more than another ordinary inmate of the black iron prison they will someday transcend. This duplicates the &quot;Suppress Aura&quot; spell instantly with Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Mind 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are no cues which will give away a Secret Master. They may disguise their surface thoughts and feelings so as to better obscure their true self from those they interact with. This duplicates the &quot;Alter Mental Pattern&quot; spell instantly with Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainment 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Death 4, Occult 4, and the other Skill requirements of the previous Attainment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">None may prove the guilt or even presence of the Disciple or his conspirators, because the darkness will reach out to consume the evidence. Nothing that could enable a forensic investigation to identify them is left behind for the duration. This duplicates the &quot;Without a Trace&quot; spell at sensory range instantly with Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Mind 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even the disguises become unnecessary for a Secret Master at this level of initiation. They may appear to be whomever they like from the perception of others, all the better to appeal to the secret counsel given unto them by the subject's inner demons. This duplicates the &quot;Imposter&quot; spell instantly with Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainment 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Death 5. In addition to the Occult 4 requirement from the previous Attainment, the Secret Master must increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 4, or must attain three dots in a second Skill from the list of possible requirements, or two dots in a third Skill from the list.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After a scene of meditation the mage's flesh is transformed into a three-dimensional shadow, incapable of interacting physically with the world except to speak, but all too capable of imposing her will on it with magic. This duplicates the &quot;Shadow Flesh&quot; spell with Advanced Duration, and with the expenditure of 1 Mana can be made to last Indefinitely.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Mind 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage's Shadow Flesh may shift into Mind-attuned ephemera. In this way they can bodily travel into the Astral Realms by combining the transformative meditation with a ritual for Astral travel. If their life comes to an end while in this form then the mage completes the transformation and becomes a tenebrous demon themselves, haunting the Astral Realms forevermore as an Immortal Master.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 03-03-2019, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}